hadiths[2656]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4448","Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, and Abu Muawiyah, Ubaydullah told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, assigned on the day of Khaybar to the horse two shares and to the man one share. And Abu Muawiyah said: He allotted to the man and his horse three shares: one share for him and two shares for his horse."
"4449","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus told us, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, he said: I saw a man come to Ibn Umar and ask him, and he said: He vowed to fast every Wednesday, and that fell upon the day of sacrifice or breaking fast. So Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah commanded fulfilling the vow, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us fasting the day of sacrifice."
"4450","Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of one."
"4451","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever frees his share in a slave is charged to complete his freeing with a just value."
"4452","Hushaym narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: We were with Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when he poured forth from Arafat to Muzdalifah, so he led us in Maghrib and went on, then he said: The prayer. So he prayed two rakas, then he said: So did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do in this place as I did."
"4453","Hushaym narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he passed by Abu Hurayrah while he was narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, he has a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial, he has two qirats, the qirat is greater than Uhud. So Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O Abu Hurayrah, look at what you narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So Abu Hurayrah stood to him until he took him to Aishah, and said to her: O Mother of the Believers, I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, he has a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial, he has two qirats. So she said: O Allah, yes. So Abu Hurayrah said: Planting young palm trees and dealing in the markets never kept me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I only sought from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a word he would teach me and a morsel he would feed me. So Ibn Umar said to him: You, O Abu Hurayrah, were the most attached of us to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the most knowledgeable of us of his hadith."
"4454","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Awn told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the pilgrim in ihram does not find the two sandals, let him wear the two khuffs and cut them below the two ankles."
"4455","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said told us, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, and Ibn Awn, and more than one, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: From where do we enter ihram. He said: The starting place of the people of Medina is from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the starting place of the people of Syria is from al-Juhfah, and the starting place of the people of Yemen is from Yalamlam, and the starting place of the people of Najd is from Qarn. And Ibn Umar said: The people analogized Dhat Irq to Qarn."
"4456","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Awn told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the pilgrim in ihram does not find the two sandals, let him wear the two khuffs and cut them below the two ankles."
"4457","Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd told us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am. Praise and blessing belong to You, and dominion, there is no partner for You. And Ibn Umar added in it: Here I am, here I am, and happiness to You, and good is in Your two hands, here I am, and desire and deed are to You."
"4458","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said told us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Ibn Umar, he said: We went early with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Arafat, among us one saying takbir and among us one saying talbiyah."
"4459","Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus told us, Ziyad ibn Jubayr told me, he said: I was with Ibn Umar at Mina, and he passed by a man while he was slaughtering a camel while it was kneeling, so he said: Make it stand bound, the sunnah of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4460","Hushaym narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid told us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when he poured forth from Arafat, then he came to Muzdalifah, so he prayed Maghrib and Isha, and when he finished, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did in this place like what I did. Hushaym said once: So he led us in Maghrib, then he said: The prayer, and he prayed two rakas, then he said: So did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do with us in this place."
"4461","Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said told us, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, and Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked what the pilgrim in ihram may kill. He said: He kills the scorpion, and the little mouse, and the kite, and the crow, and the vicious dog."
"4462","Hushaym narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib told us, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, that he heard his father say to Ibn Umar: Why do I not see you touch but these two corners, the Black Stone and the Yemeni corner. So Ibn Umar said: If I do, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Touching them both wipes away sins. He said: And I heard him say: Whoever circumambulates a week counting it and prays two rakas, it is for him like freeing a slave. He said: And I heard him say: No man lifts a foot nor puts it down but ten good deeds are written for him, and ten evil deeds are wiped from him, and ten degrees are raised for him."
"4463","Hushaym narrated to us, Ubaydullah told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, touch the Black Stone, so I never leave touching it in hardship nor in ease."
"4464","Hushaym narrated to us, more than one told us, and Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the House, and with him were al-Fadl ibn Abbas, and Usamah ibn Zayd, and Uthman ibn Talhah, and Bilal. So he ordered Bilal, and he closed the door upon them. So he stayed in it as long as Allah willed, then he came out. So Ibn Umar said: The first I met of them was Bilal, so I said: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray. He said: Here, between the two pillars."
"4465","Mutamir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qara and muzaffat, that drink be fermented in them."
"4466","Mutamir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to Friday, let him wash."
"4467","Mutamir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"4468","Mutamir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to place his mount across and pray toward it."
"4469","Mutamir narrated to us, I heard Burd, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None spends three nights but his will is written. He said: So I never spent a night after but my will is placed with me."
"4470","Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, he said: I saw Ibn Umar pray the voluntary prayer upon his mount wherever it faced with him, so I mentioned that to him, so he said: I saw Abu al-Qasim do it."
"4471","Mutamir narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that the livestock of people be milked except with their permission."
"4472","Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to combine the two prayers, Maghrib and Isha, when the twilight was gone. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to combine them when travel pressed him."
"4473","Uthman ibn Uthman, meaning al-Ghatafani, narrated to us, Umar ibn Nafi told us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza, and qaza is that the boy be shaved and part of his hair be left."
"4474","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan wrote to Ibn Umar: Raise to me your need. He said: So Ibn Umar wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support. And I neither ask you anything nor refuse a provision Allah grants me from you."
"4475","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The image makers will be tormented on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: Give life to what you created."
"4476","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, that Ibn Umar used to pray voluntarily upon his mount, then when he wanted to prostrate, he came down and performed witr upon the ground."
"4477","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: A man accused his wife. So he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, separated between the two brothers of Banu al-Ajlan, and said: Allah knows that one of you is a liar, so is there a repenter among you. So they refused, and he repeated it to them three times, and they refused, so he separated between them."
"4478","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar called for prayer at Dajnan, then he called: Pray in your dwellings. Then he narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to order the caller, so he would call for prayer, then he would call: Pray in your dwellings, on the cold night and on the rainy night during travel."
"4479","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever takes, or said: acquires, a dog that is neither harmful nor a livestock dog, two qirats decrease from his reward every day. So it was said to him: Abu Hurayrah says: and a farm dog. So he said: How would Abu Hurayrah have a farm."
"4480","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar, his son Abdullah ibn Abdullah entered upon him with his back in the house, and said: I do not feel safe that there will this year be fighting among the people, so you will be barred from the House, so if you stayed. So he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out, and the disbelieving Quraysh came between him and the House, so if I am barred from it, I shall do as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did. So he said: In the Messenger of Allah there was for you a good example. He said: I have obligated an Umrah. Then he traveled until when he was at al-Bayda, he said: I see their matter is only one. I make you witness that I have obligated a Hajj with my Umrah. Then he came and circumambulated for them both one circumambulation."
"4481","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw men and women perform ablution in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, all together from one vessel."
"4482","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what does the pilgrim in ihram wear, or he said: what does the pilgrim in ihram leave. So he said: He does not wear the shirt, nor the trousers, nor the turban, nor the two khuffs, except that he find no two sandals, so whoever finds no two sandals, let him wear them below the two ankles, nor the burnus, nor anything of clothes touched by wars or saffron."
"4483","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he said about Ashura: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fasted it and ordered fasting it, then when Ramadan was prescribed, it was left. And Abdullah would not fast it unless it coincided with his fasting."
"4484","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The two sellers have the choice until they separate, or it be a sale with choice. He said: And Nafi would sometimes say: Or one of them says to the other: Choose."
"4485","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit it riding and walking, meaning the mosque of Quba."
"4486","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prescribed the charity of Ramadan upon the male and the female and the free and the slave, a sa of dates or a sa of barley. He said: So the people afterward equated it with half a sa of wheat. Ayyub said: And Nafi said: Ibn Umar used to give dates, except one year dates were scarce, so he gave barley."
"4487","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raced between horses, so he sent what had been trained of them from al-Hafya, or al-Hayfa, to Thaniyyat al-Wada, and he sent what had not been trained of them from Thaniyyat al-Wada to the mosque of Banu Zurayq. Abdullah said: So I was a horseman that day, and I outran the people, the horse brought me to the edge of the mosque of Banu Zurayq."
"4488","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The month is twenty-nine, so do not fast until you see it, and do not break fast until you see it, and if it is cloudy over you, measure for it. Nafi said: So Abdullah, when twenty-nine of Shaban had passed, would send one who looks, so if it was seen, so be it, and if it was not seen and no cloud nor haze blocked his view, he woke breaking fast, and if cloud or haze blocked his view, he woke fasting."
"4489","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Nafi said: So I was told that Umm Salamah said: How about us. He said: A span. She said: Then our feet will show. He said: A cubit, add nothing to it."
"4490","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muzabanah, and muzabanah is that what is on the tops of palm trees be sold for dates with a named measure: if it increases, it is for me, and if it decreases, it is upon me. Ibn Umar said: Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted the sale of araya by its estimate."
"4491","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of habal al-habalah."
"4492","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you order us to pray of the night. He said: One of you prays two by two, then when he fears dawn, he prays one, and it makes odd what he prayed of the night."
"4493","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling palm trees until they ripen, and ears of grain until they whiten and are safe from blight. He forbade the seller and the buyer."
"4494","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar said: I saw in a dream as if in my hand was a piece of brocade, and I point with it to no place of Paradise but it flies with me to it. So Hafsah narrated it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Your brother is a righteous man, or: Abdullah is a righteous man."
"4495","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: All of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible. So the commander who is over the people is a shepherd and he is responsible for his flock, and the man is a shepherd over the people of his house and he is responsible, and the woman is a shepherdess over the house of her husband and she is responsible, and the slave is a shepherd over the wealth of his master and he is responsible. Lo, all of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible."
"4496","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he returned from a Hajj or a raid, when he rose upon high ground of the earth or an eminence, said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah, alone, there is no partner for Him, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful, returning, repenting, prostrating, worshipping, to our Lord praising. Allah kept His promise, and aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone."
"4497","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought it, meaning the lizard, so he neither ate it nor forbade it."
"4498","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Jews brought the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a man and a woman of them who had committed adultery, so he said: What do you find in your Book. So they said: We blacken their faces and disgrace them. So he said: You have lied, in it is stoning. So bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful. So they brought the Torah, and they brought a reader of theirs, one-eyed, called Ibn Suriya, so he read until when he reached a place of it, he placed his hand upon it. So it was said to him: Lift your hand. So he lifted his hand, and lo it shone. So he said, or they said: O Muhammad, in it is stoning, but we used to conceal it among us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered them both, and they were stoned. He said: I saw him lean over her, shielding her from the stones with himself."
"4499","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub told us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The people used to see dreams and narrate them to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: I, or he said: I hear, your dreams have coincided upon the last seven. So whoever of you seeks it, let him seek it in the last seven."
"4500","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar divorced his wife one divorce while she was menstruating, so Umar asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he ordered him to take her back, then wait until she menstruates another menstruation, then wait until she is pure, then divorce her before touching her. He said: And that is the waiting period that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, ordered that women be divorced for. And Ibn Umar, when he was asked about a man divorcing his wife while she is menstruating, would say: As for me, I divorced her one or two, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to take her back, then wait until she menstruates another menstruation, then wait until she is pure, then divorce her before touching her. And as for you, you divorced her three, so you have disobeyed Allah in what He ordered you of divorcing your wife, and she is separated from you."
"4501","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, in a marfu report, he said: Indeed the two hands prostrate as the face prostrates, so when one of you places his face then let him place his hands, and when he raises it then let him raise them."
"4502","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sells date-palms that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."
"4503","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut off for a shield worth three dirhams."
"4504","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I knew that land used to be leased at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for what is upon the water channels and something of straw, I do not know how much it was, and Ibn Umar used to lease his land in the era of Abu Bakr and the era of Umar and the era of Uthman and the beginning of the rule of Muawiyah, until at the end of it it reached him that Rafi narrates concerning that a prohibition of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he came to him, and I was with him, and asked him, so he said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade leasing cultivated lands, so Ibn Umar abandoned it and would not lease it, and when he was asked he would say: Ibn Khadij claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade leasing cultivated lands."
"4505","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Lo, let not the livestock of a man be milked except with his permission. Would any of you like that his storeroom be come to and its door broken, then what is in it plundered. For indeed in the udders of their livestock is the food of one of them. Lo, let not the livestock of a man be milked except with his permission, or he said: by his command."
"4506","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two rakahs before Zuhr and two rakahs after it, and two rakahs after Maghrib in his house, and two rakahs after Isha in his house. He said: And Hafsah narrated to me that he used to pray two rakahs when dawn breaks and the caller calls to prayer. Ayyub said: I think he said: light ones. And two rakahs after Jumuah in his house."
"4507","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not travel with the Quran, for I fear the enemy may get hold of it."
"4508","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your example and the example of the Jews and the Christians is like a man who employed workers and said: Who will work from the morning prayer until midday for a qirat each. Lo, the Jews worked. Then he said: Who will work for me from midday until the Asr prayer for a qirat each. Lo, the Christians worked. Then he said: Who will work for me from the Asr prayer until sunset for two qirats each. Lo, you are those who worked. So the Jews and the Christians became angry and said: We did more work and were given less. He said: Did I wrong you anything of your right. They said: No. He said: It is only My bounty, I give it to whom I will."
"4509","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque, so he stood and scraped it, or he said: scratched it off with his hand, then he turned to the people and was angry with them and said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is in front of one of you in his prayer, so let none of you spit in front of his face in his prayer."
"4510","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Ayyub said: I do not know it except from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever swears and makes an exception then he has the choice, if he wishes to go ahead with his oath, and if he wishes to turn back without breaking it, or he said: without blame."
"4511","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Pray in your houses and do not take them as graves. He said: I think he mentioned it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4512","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Bayan, from Wabarah, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: I circumambulate the House while I have entered ihram for Hajj. He said: What harm is there in that. He said: Ibn Abbas forbade that. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enter ihram for Hajj and circumambulate the House and between Safa and Marwa."
"4513","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade joining dates together while eating except that you ask permission of your companions."
"4514","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that he used to lick his fingers then say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You do not know in which of your food the blessing lies."
"4515","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"4516","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People are only like a hundred camels in which no riding camel is found."
"4517","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that they used to be beaten at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, if they bought food in bulk and tried to sell it on the spot until they brought it to their lodgings."
"4518","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him."
"4519","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Witr on the camel."
"4520","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu Amr ibn Yahya, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying on a donkey while facing toward Khaybar."
"4521","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave a horse in the path of Allah then found it being sold, so he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about buying it, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not take back your charity."
"4522","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not forbid her. He said: And the wife of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, used to pray in the mosque, so he said to her: You know what I like. So she said: By Allah, I will not stop until you forbid me. He said: Then Umar was stabbed while she was in the mosque."
"4523","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard Umar saying: By my father. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers, so if one of you swears let him swear by Allah or be silent. Umar said: I never swore by them after that, neither deliberately nor narrating."
"4524","Abu Mamar Said ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, he said: My father Abdullah ibn Umar, when a man intending travel came to him, would say to him: Come near that I may bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bid us farewell, saying: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds."
"4525","Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears, he forbade the seller and the buyer, and he forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy fearing the enemy may get hold of it."
"4526","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade shighar."
"4527","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man invoked lian against his wife and denied her child, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, separated between them and attached the child to the woman."
"4528","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muzabanah, and muzabanah is buying fruit for dates by measure, and grapes for raisins by measure."
"4529","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"4530","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Witr on the camel."
"4531","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade meeting goods before they are brought down to the markets, and forbade najsh, and said: Let none of you sell over the sale of another. And when the journey pressed him he would join between Maghrib and Isha."
"4532","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut down the date-palms of Banu al-Nadir and burned."
"4533","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina two rakahs."
"4534","Al-Walid narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab narrated to me, that Ibn Umar used to perform ablution three times three and would attribute that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4535","Al-Walid narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi the freedman of Ibn Umar, that Ibn Umar heard the sound of a shepherds pipe, so he placed his two fingers in his ears and turned his mount from the road, saying: O Nafi, do you hear. So I would say: Yes. So he went on until I said: No. Then he put down his hands and returned his mount to the road and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he heard the sound of a shepherds pipe, so he did like this."
"4536","Al-Walid narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, that Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to him, that Abu Qilabah narrated to him, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A fire will come out from Hadramawt, or: in Hadramawt, driving the people. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us. He said: Upon you is Sham."
"4537","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydillah ibn Umar narrated to me, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you eats let him eat with his right, and when he drinks let him drink with his right, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"4538","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what clothes the muhrim wears, and Sufyan once said: what the muhrim leaves of clothes, so he said: He does not wear the shirt, nor the burnus, nor trousers, nor the turban, nor a garment touched by wars or saffron, nor the two khuffs except for one who finds no sandals, so whoever does not find the two sandals let him wear the two khuffs and cut them until they are below the two ankles."
"4539","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar walking in front of the funeral bier."
"4540","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he opened the prayer raise his hands until level with his shoulders, and when he wanted to bow, and after he raised his head from bowing, and Sufyan once said: and when he raised his head, and most often he would say: and after he raised his head from bowing, and he would not raise between the two prostrations."
"4541","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit for dates. Sufyan said: Thus we memorized it: fruit for dates. And Zayd ibn Thabit informed them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted araya."
"4542","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, join between Maghrib and Isha when the journey pressed him."
"4543","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about what animals the muhrim kills. He said: Five, no blame in killing them on whoever kills them in the Haram: the scorpion, the mouse, the crow, the kite, and the vicious dog."
"4544","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ill omen is in three: the horse, the woman, and the house. Sufyan said: We only memorize it from Salim, meaning ill omen."
"4545","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: One whom the Asr prayer escapes, it is as if his family and his wealth were destroyed."
"4546","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, as a narration, and once he said raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"4547","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: A man saw that Laylat al-Qadr is the night of twenty-seven or such and such, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I see your dreams have coincided, so seek it in the remaining ten, in the odd ones thereof."
"4548","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Salim heard, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: By my father, by my father. So he said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: By Allah, by Allah, I never swore by them after that, neither deliberately nor narrating."
"4549","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"4550","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah gave the Quran and he stands with it in the hours of night and day, and a man to whom Allah gave wealth and he spends it in truth in the hours of night and day."
"4551","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Indeed Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."
"4552","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates, and whoever sells pollinated date-palms, the fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates."
"4553","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever of you comes to Jumuah let him bathe."
"4554","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while a man was admonishing his brother about modesty, so he said: Modesty is part of faith."
"4555","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed, and once he said: the entering into ihram of the people of Madinah is from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the people of Sham from Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn. He said: And it was mentioned to me, and I did not hear it: and the people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam."
"4556","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not forbid her."
"4557","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Kill snakes, and the one with two stripes and the tailless, for they seek eyesight and cause miscarriage. And Ibn Umar used to kill every snake he found, then Abu Lubabah, or Zayd ibn al-Khattab, saw him chasing a snake and said: House-dwelling ones have been forbidden."
"4558","He said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah read to me, al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Let none of you eat from the meat of his sacrifice beyond three days."
"4559","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked how the night prayer is performed. He said: Let one of you pray two by two, and when he fears dawn let him make odd with one."
"4560","Sufyan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling wala and gifting it."
"4561","Sufyan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not enter upon these people who were punished except weeping, and if you are not weeping then do not enter upon them, for I fear what befell them may befall you."
"4562","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the dabb lizard. So he said: I do not eat it nor forbid it."
"4563","Sufyan narrated to us, I heard it from Ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If a Jew greets you, he only says: Death upon you, so say: And upon you. And once he said: If the Jews greet you then say: And upon you, for they say: Death upon you."
"4564","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: If you are three then let not two converse privately excluding the third. And once he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade two men conversing privately excluding the third when they are three."
"4565","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to take the pledge for hearing and obeying, then say: As much as you are able. And once he said: He would prompt one of us: As much as you are able."
"4566","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The two sellers have the choice as long as they have not parted, or it be a sale with choice."
"4567","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he heard Ibn Umar, the son of his son Abdullah ibn Waqid: O my son, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at one who drags his lower garment in pride."
"4568","Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abdullah ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Awf, the mosque of Quba, praying in it, then men of the Ansar came to him greeting him, and Suhayb entered with him, so I asked Suhayb how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did when he was greeted. He said: He would gesture with his hand. Sufyan said: I said to a man: Ask Zayd: Did you hear it from Abdullah. And I was afraid to ask him. So he said: O Abu Usamah, did you hear it from Abdullah ibn Umar. He said: As for me, I saw him and spoke to him."
"4569","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Salim, from his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he returned from Hajj or Umrah or an expedition, and he rose upon high ground, said: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner has He, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable. Allah fulfilled His promise, and aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone. Returning, God willing, repentant, worshipping, praising our Lord."
"4570","Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, he said: Ibn Umar used to say: This is al-Bayda about which they lie against the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. By Allah, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not enter ihram except from beside the mosque."
"4571","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked about the night prayer, so he said: Two by two, and when you fear dawn then make odd with one."
"4572","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, he heard Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Let not the Bedouins overcome you for the name of your prayer. Lo, it is Isha, and they darken camels, or: away from camels."
"4573","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, and Hisham, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the dabb lizard. So he said: I do not eat it nor forbid it."
"4574","Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Nafi, Ibn Umar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the minbar, and when I saw him I hastened and entered the mosque and sat, and I did not hear until he descended, so I asked the people what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. They said: He forbade the dubba gourd and the muzaffat vessel to make nabidh in."
"4575","Sufyan narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muawi, he said: I prayed beside Ibn Umar and turned the pebbles, so he said: Do not turn the pebbles, for it is from Satan, but as I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do: he would move it thus. Abu Abdullah said: meaning a wiping."
"4576","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not travel with the Quran, for I fear the enemy may get hold of it."
"4577","I heard Sufyan say: He vowed, meaning to perform itikaf in the Sacred Mosque, so he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he commanded him. It was said to Sufyan: From Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar vowed. He said: Yes."
"4578","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he said: It is due upon every Muslim to spend two nights, having what he wills to bequeath, except his will is written with him."
"4579","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a detachment to Najd, so their shares reached twelve camels, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave us extra a camel each."
"4580","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, he said: We were with Ibn Umar at Dajnan, so he established the prayer then called: Lo, pray in the lodgings. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command a caller on a rainy or cold night: Lo, pray in the lodgings."
"4581","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever swears an oath then says: If Allah wills, he has made an exception."
"4582","He said: Sufyan read to me: I heard Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling habal al-habalah."
"4583","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Judan, from al-Qasim ibn Rabiah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of the conquest of Makkah while upon the steps of the Kabah: Praise be to Allah who fulfilled His promise, and aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone. Lo, the victim of intentional manslaughter resembling error with the whip or the stick, therein is one hundred camels, and once he said: the aggravated, therein are forty pregnant she-camels with their young in their bellies. Every inherited honor of Jahiliyyah, and blood, and claim, and once he said: and blood and wealth, is under these two feet of mine, except providing drink to the pilgrims and custodianship of the House, for I confirm them to their people as they were."
"4584","Sufyan narrated to us, Sadaqah heard Ibn Umar say, meaning from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The people of Najd enter ihram from Qarn, and the people of Sham from Juhfah, and the people of Yemen from Yalamlam, and Ibn Umar did not hear it, and he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The entering into ihram of the people of Madinah is from Dhu al-Hulayfah. They said to him: Then where is the people of Iraq. Ibn Umar said: There was none that day."
"4585","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Umar, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Touching the two corners erases sins."
"4586","Sufyan narrated to us, Amr said: Ibn Umar heard: We used to sharecrop and saw no harm in that, until Rafi ibn Khadij claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it, so we abandoned it."
"4587","Sufyan narrated to us, Amr said: Said ibn Jubayr heard, saying: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to the two invoking lian: Your account is upon Allah. One of you is lying. You have no way to her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth. He said: You have no wealth. If you were truthful to her, it is for what you made lawful of her private part, and if you lied to her, that is farther for you."
"4588","Sufyan narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Abu al-Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Umar, it was said to Sufyan: The son of Amr. He said: No, the son of Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he besieged the people of Taif and could gain nothing from them, said: We are returning tomorrow, God willing. The Muslims disliked that, so he said: Go forth in the morning. So they went forth to fight and were wounded, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are returning tomorrow, God willing. So the Muslims were pleased, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed."
"4589","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Salim, from his father, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If a slave is owned between two, and one of them frees his share, then if he is wealthy it is valued upon him with a value neither deficient nor excessive, then he is freed."
"4590","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ismail al-Shaybani: I sold what was on the tops of my date-palms for one hundred wasqs; if it increases it is theirs, and if it decreases it is theirs. So I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it, and permitted araya."
"4591","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Umar, between them Salim, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray after Jumuah two rakahs."
"4592","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when dawn brightened would pray two rakahs."
"4593","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met Umar during one of his journeys while he was saying: By my father, by my father. So he said: Indeed Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers, so whoever swears let him swear by Allah, otherwise let him be silent."
"4594","Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raced horses, sending what was trained among them from Hafya, and sending what was not trained among them from Thaniyyat al-Wada to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."
"4595","Sufyan narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, from Nafi: Ibn Umar set out intending Umrah, then they told him there was trouble in Makkah, so he said: I enter ihram for Umrah; if I am prevented I shall do as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did. So he entered ihram for Umrah, and when he had gone a little, while at al-Bayda, he said: The way of Umrah is none but the way of Hajj. I make Hajj obligatory, and said: I call you to witness that I have made Hajj obligatory, for the way of Hajj is the way of Umrah. So he came to Makkah and circumambulated the House seven times and between Safa and Marwa seven times, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do. He came to Qudayd and bought a sacrificial animal and drove it with him."
"4596","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar came to Qudayd and bought his sacrificial animal, then circumambulated the House and between Safa and Marwa, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do thus."
"4597","Sufyan narrated to us, Ayyub, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, from Nafi: I heard a man of Banu Salamah narrating to Ibn Umar that a slave girl of Kab ibn Malik was pasturing his sheep at Sal, death reached a ewe among them, so she took a sharp stone and slaughtered it with it, so he ordered him to eat it."
"4598","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Dhuayb, of Banu Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza, he said: We went out with Ibn Umar to al-Hima, and when the sun set we were shy to say to him: Prayer, until the whiteness of the horizon went and the darkness of Isha went. He alighted and prayed with us three and two, and turned to us and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do."
"4599","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: I accompanied Ibn Umar to Madinah and did not hear him narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except one hadith: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and jummarah was brought, so he said: Among trees is a tree whose example is like the Muslim man. So I wanted to say: It is the date-palm, but I looked and I was the youngest of the people, so I was silent. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is the date-palm."
"4600","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Umar witnessed the Conquest while twenty years old, with a refractory horse and a heavy spear. So Ibn Umar went to cut fodder for his horse, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Abdullah, indeed Abdullah."
"4601","Ibn Idris narrated to us: Imran, meaning Ibn Hudayr, informed us - and Waki, the meaning, said: Imran informed us - from Yazid ibn Utarid - Waki said: al-Sadusi Abu al-Bazari - he said: I asked Ibn Umar about drinking while standing, and he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to drink standing and eat while we were walking briskly."
"4602","Abadah narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar used to begin with the prayer before the sermon on Eid."
"4603","Abadah narrated to us: Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out lian between a man and his wife and separated them."
"4604","Abadah narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"4605","Abadah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being asked about water in open desert land and what frequents it of animals and beasts of prey, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the water is the amount of two qullahs it does not carry filth."
"4606","Abadah narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from his uncle Wasi from Ibn Umar, he said: One day I climbed above the house of Hafsah and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attending to his need, facing Sham and turning his back to the qiblah."
"4607","Ibn Idris narrated to us: Ubaydullah informed us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to sleep in the mosque, taking midday rest in it, while we were young men."
"4608","Ismail narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar acquired land in Khaybar, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his counsel about it, saying: I have acquired land in Khaybar; I have never acquired wealth more precious to me than it, so what do you command concerning it? He said: If you wish, withhold its corpus and give it in charity. He said: So Umar gave it in charity, not to be sold nor gifted nor inherited. He said: So Umar gave it in charity among the poor and kinsfolk and necks and in the path of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and the wayfarer and the guest; there is no sin upon whoever administers it to eat from it in a fair manner or to feed a friend, without accumulating wealth thereby."
"4609","Ismail narrated to us: Mamar informed us from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father: that Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi embraced Islam while married to ten wives, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Choose four of them."
"4610","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me, he said: Ibn Umar would sometimes lead us in the obligatory prayer with two or three surahs."
"4611","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is twenty-nine, like this and like this; if it is obscured from you, then decree for it. He said: And Ibn Umar, when it was the night of the twenty-ninth and there were clouds or haze in the sky, would begin the morning fasting."
"4612","Yahya narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us: my father informed me: Ibn Umar informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not deliberately time your prayer for sunrise nor sunset, for it rises between the two horns of Satan; when the edge of the sun has risen, do not pray until it has come out fully, and when the edge of the sun has set, do not pray until it has set."
"4613","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Day mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds: he will stand in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."
"4614","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to plant the spear and pray toward it."
"4615","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A woman shall not travel three except with a mahram."
"4616","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"4617","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us from his uncle from Ibn Umar, he said: One day I climbed upon the house of Hafsah and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attending to his need, with his back to the house and facing Sham."
"4618","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar: that he used to trot three and walk four, and he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it; and he used to walk between the two corners. He said: He used to walk between them only to make touching them easier."
"4619","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the dabb while he was on the minbar, and he said: I do not eat it nor do I forbid it. And the Prophet said: Whoever eats of this tree shall not come to the mosque."
"4620","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar: that he used to pray on his mount and perform witr upon it, and he attributed that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4621","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Hajjaj narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one whose Asr prayer is missed deliberately until the sun has set, it is as if his family and wealth have been taken away."
"4622","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-Amash from al-Minhal from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar: that he passed by people who had set up a live chicken as a target shooting at it, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever mutilates animals."
"4623","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated to us from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank will look into his dominion of two thousand years, seeing its farthest as he sees its nearest, looking at his wives and servants; and the highest of them in rank will look at the Face of Allah, the Exalted, twice every day."
"4624","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs from Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a great sin; is there repentance for me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have parents? He said: No. He said: Then do you have a maternal aunt? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then be dutiful to her."
"4625","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah he entered from the upper pass, and when he left he left from the lower pass."
"4626","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to count, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive and his companions were numerous: Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, then we would fall silent."
"4627","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us from Abi al-Zubayr from Awn ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah from Ibn Umar, he said: While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man among the people said: Allah is Most Great, great; much praise belongs to Allah; glory be to Allah morning and evening. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who said such-and-such? A man among the people said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I was amazed at it; the gates of heaven were opened for it. Ibn Umar said: So I have not abandoned them since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that."
"4628","Ismail narrated to us from Ayyub from Nafi, he said: When Ibn Umar entered the nearest part of the Haram he would stop the talbiyah; when he reached Dhu Tuwa he would spend the night there until morning, then pray Fajr and bathe, and he would narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that; then he would enter Makkah in the forenoon and come to the House and touch the Stone, saying: In the name of Allah, Allah is Most Great; then trot three circuits, walking between the two corners; when he came to the Stone he would touch it and say takbir, four circuits walking; then come to the Maqam and pray two rakahs; then return to the Stone and touch it; then go out to al-Safa from the greatest gate and stand upon it and say takbir seven times: three times takbir, then say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful."
"4629","Ismail narrated to us from Abd al-Khaliq, he said: I asked Said ibn al-Musayyab about nabidh, and he said: I heard Abdallah ibn Umar saying, near the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This - the delegation of Abd al-Qays came with al-Ashajj and asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about drink, and he said: Do not drink in a hantamah nor in a dubba nor a naqir. So I said to him: O Abu Muhammad, and the muzaffat? He thought he had forgotten, then said: I did not hear it that day from Abdallah ibn Umar, though he used to dislike it."
"4630","Ismail narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hakam narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the stallion's mating."
"4631","Ismail and Muhammad ibn Jafar both said: Mamar narrated to us from al-Zuhri - Ibn Jafar in his hadith said: Ibn Shihab informed us - from Salim from his father: that Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi embraced Islam while married to ten wives, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Choose four of them. When it was the time of Umar, he divorced his wives and divided his wealth among his sons; that reached Umar, and he said: I suspect Satan, in what he steals of hearing, heard of your death and cast it into yourself, and perhaps you will remain only a little while; by Allah, you shall take back your wives and take back your wealth, or I shall bequeath them from you and order your grave to be stoned as the grave of Abu Righal was stoned."
"4632","Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Salim from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote the book of sadaqah but did not send it out to his agents until he passed away, then he attached it to his sword. When he passed away, Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, acted upon it until he passed away, then Umar until he passed away. In it was: for five camels a sheep, for ten two sheep, for fifteen three sheep, for twenty four sheep, for twenty-five a bint makhad. My father said: Then an illness befell me in the gathering of Abbad ibn al-Awwam, so I wrote the remainder of the hadith, but I think I did not fully understand part of it, so I doubted the rest of the hadith and left it."
"4633","With this hadith in the Musnad, in the hadith of al-Zuhri from Salim, because he had collected the hadith of al-Zuhri from Salim, so he narrated it to us in the hadith of Salim from Muhammad ibn Yazid in full, and in the hadith of Abbad from Abbad ibn al-Awwam."
"4634","Muhammad ibn Yazid, meaning al-Wasiti, narrated to us from Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had written the sadaqah but had not sent it out to his agents until he died. He said: Then Abu Bakr brought it out after him and acted upon it until he died, then Umar brought it out after him and acted upon it. He said: Umar died on the day he died while that was attached to his will. He said: In it was: concerning camels, for every five a sheep until reaching twenty-four; when reaching twenty-five, therein a bint makhad up to thirty-five; if there is no bint makhad, then an ibn labun; when exceeding thirty-five, therein a bint labun up to forty-five; when one more, therein a hiqqah up to sixty; when more, therein a jadhah up to seventy-five; when more, therein two bint labun up to ninety; when more, therein two hiqqahs up to one hundred twenty; when camels are many, for every fifty a hiqqah and for every forty a bint labun. And concerning sheep: from forty, a sheep up to one hundred twenty; when more, therein two sheep up to two hundred; when more, therein three up to three hundred; when more after that, therein nothing until reaching four hundred; when sheep are many, for every hundred a sheep. Likewise, what is united shall not be separated nor what is separate united, out of fear of sadaqah; whatever belongs to two joint owners, they settle between themselves equally. No decrepit nor defective sheep shall be taken."
"4635","Ismail narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever frees a share - or said: a portion - belonging to him - or said: a partnership share belonging to him - in a slave, and he has wealth reaching his price by fair valuation, then he is fully freed; otherwise, what has been freed of him has been freed. Ayyub said: Nafi would sometimes mention in this hadith, and sometimes not mention it, so I do not know whether it is in the hadith or Nafi said it on his own - meaning his saying: then what has been freed of him has been freed."
"4636","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ayyub informed us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a campaign or Hajj or Umrah and ascended a high ground of the earth or an elevation, he would say: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great; there is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful; returning, repenting, prostrating, worshipping, praising our Lord; Allah has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone."
"4637","Ismail narrated to us from Yunus from al-Hasan from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not entrust a servant with subjects, few or many, except that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will ask him about them on the Day of Resurrection: did he uphold the command of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, among them or neglect it - until He asks him about his household in particular."
"4638","Ismail narrated to me, he said: Mamar informed us from Abdillah ibn Muslim, brother of al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abdillah ibn Umar from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging will persist with one of you until he meets Allah, Blessed and Exalted, with not a shred of flesh on his face."
"4639","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to me: Nafi informed me from Abdillah, he said: They used to trade food in bulk in the market, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to sell it until they moved it."
"4640","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Abdillah ibn Umar, he said: The people of Jahiliyyah used to sell the meat of the slaughtered camel for habal al-habalah - and habal al-habalah is when the she-camel gives birth to what is in her belly, then what she gives birth to becomes pregnant - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them that."
"4641","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, said: They mentioned a man entering ihram for Umrah then exiting - is he allowed to approach, meaning his wife, before he circumambulates between al-Safa and al-Marwah? So we asked Jabir ibn Abdillah, and he said: No, until he circumambulates al-Safa and al-Marwah. And we asked Ibn Umar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakahs behind the Maqam, and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then said: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"4642","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Sufyan: Abdillah ibn Dinar narrated to me: I heard Ibn Umar saying: While the people were praying Fajr in the mosque of Quba, a comer came and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has had Quran revealed to him tonight and been commanded to face the Kabah, so face it. So they turned around and faced toward the Kabah."
"4643","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall eat of his sacrifice beyond three days. And Abdallah, when the sun had set on the third day, would not eat of the meat of his sacrificial animal."
"4644","Yahya narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abi Salamah from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"4645","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"4646","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed us from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque is better than two thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."
"4647","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabanah - and muzabanah is fruit for dates by measure, grapes for raisins by measure, and wheat for standing crop by measure."
"4648","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The traitor will have a banner raised for him on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so son of so-and-so."
"4649","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"4650","Yahya narrated to us from Ismail: Salim Abu Abdillah narrated to me from Ibn Umar from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever follows a funeral until prayer is offered over it, he has a qirat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the qirat, and he said: Like Uhud."
"4651","Yahya narrated to us from Malik: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Two men from the people of the East came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and addressed, and the people were amazed at their eloquence, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, some eloquence is magic - or: Indeed, part of eloquence is magic."
"4652","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Mina two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr, and with Umar, and with Uthman in the early part of his rule, then he completed."
"4653","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Abdillah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make some of your prayer in your houses, and do not take them as graves."
"4654","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed us from Abdillah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trim the mustaches and leave the beards."
"4655","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Abdillah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah."
"4656","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me: Ibn Umar informed me: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night in Dhu Tuwa until morning, then entered Makkah; and Ibn Umar used to do that."
"4657","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. He said on the fourth: And those who shorten."
"4658","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of you but his seat is shown to him morning and evening: if he is of the people of Paradise, then of the people of Paradise; if of the people of Fire, then of the people of Fire. It is said: This is your seat until you are raised to it."
"4659","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man shall not make a man stand from his seat to sit in it; rather, make room and widen."
"4660","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rakahs before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two after Jumuah; as for Jumuah and Maghrib, in his house. He said: And my sister Hafsah informed me that he used to pray two light rakahs when dawn broke. He said: And it was an hour when I would not enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4661","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inspected him on the day of Uhud when he was fourteen years old and did not permit him, then inspected him on the day of al-Khandaq when he was fifteen and permitted him."
"4662","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar: that Umar asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us sleep while junub? He said: Yes, when he performs wudu."
"4663","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dealt with the people of Khaybar for half of what comes out of fruit or crop."
"4664","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two shall not converse privately excluding the third."
"4665","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The example of the keeper of the Quran is like the keeper of hobbled camels: if its owner hobbles it he retains it, and if he releases it it goes away."
"4666","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar: that two Jews committed adultery, so they were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered them stoned. He said: So I saw the man shielding her with himself."
"4667","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found Umar among riders while he was swearing by his father, and said: Do not swear by your fathers; let one who swears swear by Allah or be silent."
"4668","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hearing and obedience are upon a man in what he loves or hates, unless he is commanded to disobedience; if commanded to disobedience, then no hearing nor obedience."
"4669","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite a surah to us, and when he recited a prostration he would prostrate and we would prostrate with him, until one of us could not find room for his forehead."
"4670","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Prayer in congregation exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-seven."
"4671","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar: that some companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Laylat al-Qadr in dreams in the last seven, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see you have concurred on the last seven, so seek it in the last seven."
"4672","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me from Jurayj or Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Four traits I have seen you do that I have not seen anyone do. What are they? He said: I saw you wearing these sabti sandals; I saw you touching these two Yemeni corners, touching no others; I saw you not entering ihram until you place your foot in the stirrup; I saw you dyeing your beard yellow. He said: As for my wearing these sabti sandals, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear them, perform wudu in them, and prefer them. As for touching these two corners, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching them, touching no others. As for my dyeing my beard yellow, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dyeing his beard yellow. As for my entering ihram when my mount stands straight with me, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he placed his foot in the stirrup and his mount stood straight with him, enter ihram."
"4673","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah - and Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Ubaydullah narrated to us - from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a slave perfects worship of his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and gives sincere counsel to his master, he has the reward twice."
"4674","Yahya narrated to us: Malik narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to me from Salim from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began prayer he raised his hands level with his shoulders; when he bowed he did likewise; when he raised his head from bowing he did likewise, and when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, he said: Our Lord, to You belongs praise; and he did not do likewise in prostration."
"4675","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib: Uthman ibn Suraqah narrated to me: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not praying in travel before it nor after it."
"4676","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Abu Ishaq narrated to me from Abdillah ibn Malik: that Ibn Umar prayed Maghrib and Isha in Jam with one iqamah, so Abdillah ibn Malik said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is this prayer? He said: I prayed them with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this place with one iqamah."
"4677","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold, and he would place its stone toward his palm; then people took such rings, so he threw it away and took a ring of silver."
"4678","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A dream is one part of seventy parts of prophecy."
"4679","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he was standing at the door of Aishah, gesturing with his hand toward the East, saying: Tribulation is here, where the horn of Satan rises."
"4680","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar, he said: When Abdallah ibn Ubayy died, his son came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, give me your shirt to shroud him in, pray over him and seek forgiveness for him. So he gave him his shirt and said: Let me know. When he went to pray over him - meaning Umar - said: Allah has forbidden you to pray over the hypocrites. He said: I am between two choices: Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them. So he prayed over him, then Allah, the Exalted, revealed: And never pray over any of them who dies. He said: So prayer over them was abandoned."
"4681","Yahya informed us: Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) planted the spear to pray toward it."
"4682","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed the name Asiyah, saying: You are Jamilah."
"4683","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Zayd al-Ammi narrated to me from Abi al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the Mothers of the Believers a span in the hem; they asked for more, so he granted them another span, making it a cubit; they used to send to us to measure a cubit for them."
"4684","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Abi Rawwad: Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque, scraped it off and perfumed its place with khaluq."
"4685","Yahya narrated to us from al-Amash from Abi Salih from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you are three, two shall not converse privately excluding their companion. He said: We said: And if they are four? He said: Then it does no harm."
"4686","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Abi Rawwad from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not omit touching the Stone and the Yemeni corner in every tawaf."
"4687","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Ibn Dinar narrated to me: I heard Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you says to his brother: O disbeliever, one of them has borne it."
"4688","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Abdillah ibn Abi Labid narrated to me from Abi Salamah from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let not the bedouins overcome you over the name of your prayer, for it is Isha; they call it Atamah because they darken with camels for milking them."
"4689","Yahya narrated to us from Husayn: Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us: Sulayman, freedman of Maymunah, narrated to me, he said: I came to Ibn Umar while he was at al-Balat and the people were praying in the mosque. I said: What prevents you from praying with the people? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not pray a prayer twice in one day."
"4690","Yahya narrated to us from Malik: Nafi narrated to us from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drinks wine in this world and does not repent of it will be deprived of it in the Hereafter; he will not be given it to drink."
"4691","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi informed me, he said: I know it only from Abdallah: that al-Abbas sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to spend the nights in Makkah during the days of Mina on account of the water provision, so he permitted him."
"4692","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. He said: I said to Nafi: What is shighar? He said: A man gives his daughter in marriage and takes his daughter in marriage, and a man gives his sister in marriage and takes his sister in marriage, without dower."
"4693","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us: I heard Said ibn Jubayr saying: I was asked about the two who invoke curses - are they separated - during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr, and I did not know what to say, so I rose from my place to the house of Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, the two who invoke curses - are they separated? He said: Glory be to Allah, the first to ask about that was so-and-so son of so-and-so. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a man who sees his wife in indecency: if he speaks, he speaks of a grave matter, and if he stays silent, he stays silent over the like of that? So he was silent and did not answer him. Later he came to him and said: What I asked you about, I have been afflicted with. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed these verses in Surat al-Nur: And those who accuse their wives, until reaching: that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is of the truthful. He began with the man, admonished him, reminded him, and told him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I have not lied to you. Then he turned to the woman, admonished her, reminded her, and told her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. She said: By Him who sent you with the truth, he is indeed a liar. He said: So he began with the man, who testified four testimonies by Allah that he is of the truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he is of the liars. Then he turned to the woman, who testified four testimonies by Allah that he is of the liars, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is of the truthful. Then he separated them."
"4694","Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us: my father informed me: Ibn Umar informed me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the edge of the sun rises, delay prayer until it is fully visible; when the edge of the sun sets, delay prayer until it has set."
"4695","Yahya narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us: my father informed me: Ibn Umar informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not deliberately time your prayer for sunrise nor sunset, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."
"4696","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah: Nafi narrated to us from Abdillah ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman shall not travel three except with a mahram."
"4697","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Day mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds, he said: He will stand in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."
"4698","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan: Abdillah ibn Dinar narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Jews greet, they say: al-sam be upon you, so say: Upon you."
"4699","Yahya narrated to us from Malik from Abdillah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, similar."
"4700","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Simak ibn Harb narrated to me from Musab ibn Sad: that people visited Ibn Amir in his illness and began praising him, so Ibn Umar said: Yet I am not the least sincere of them toward you: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept charity from misappropriation nor prayer without purification."
"4701","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed Usamah over a people, and the people criticized his command, so he said: If you criticize his command, you have already criticized the command of his father. By Allah, he was indeed fit for command, and he was among the most beloved of people to me, and this son of his is the most beloved of people to me after him."
"4702","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan, Ibn Dinar narrated to me, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Aslam, may Allah grant it safety, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it, and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"4703","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, I heard Ibn Umar say: Quraysh used to swear by their fathers, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever would swear, let him swear by Allah; do not swear by your fathers."
"4704","Yahya narrated to us from Ismail from Abu Hanzalah: I asked Ibn Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both, about prayer on a journey. He said: Prayer on a journey is two rakahs. We said: We are safe. He said: The Sunnah of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4705","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said, my father said, and Yahya ibn Said once said from Umar, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed in the Jahiliyyah to observe itikaf for a night in the mosque, so he said: Fulfill your vow."
"4706","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When a slave is sincere to his master and performs worship of his Lord well, he has reward twice."
"4707","Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Those who make these images will be punished, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"4708","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade meeting traders on the way."
"4709","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, he said, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: When the supper of one of you is laid and the prayer is established, let him not stand until he has finished."
"4710","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Make the last of your prayer at night witr."
"4711","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib from his maternal uncle al-Harith from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar from his father, he said: There was a wife under me whom Umar disliked, so he said: Divorce her, but I refused, so Umar went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Obey your father."
"4712","Yahya narrated to us from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: When one of you is called to a wedding feast, let him come to it."
"4713","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar that Umar saw a striped hullah or of silk being sold, so he said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If only you bought this to wear on Friday or for delegations. He said: Only one who has no share wears this. He said: Then some hullahs from it were gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he sent to Umar among them a hullah. He said: I heard you say what you said, and you sent it to me. He said: I only sent it to you that you may sell it or clothe someone with it."
"4714","Yahya narrated to us from Abd al-Malik, Said ibn Jubayr narrated to us that Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray on his mount coming from Makkah to Madinah wherever it turned with him, and concerning it this verse was revealed: So wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah."
"4715","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever eats from this tree, let him not come to the mosques."
"4716","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Nafi informed me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: They used to trade food in bulk at the top of the market, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade them to sell it until they moved it."
"4717","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he returned from armies or expeditions or Hajj or Umrah, or when he overlooked a mountain pass or a highland, would say takbir three times and say: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable; returning, repentant, worshipping, prostrating, to our Lord praising; Allah fulfilled His promise and aided His slave and defeated the confederates alone."
"4718","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"4719","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water."
"4720","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys."
"4721","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, practiced wisal in Ramadan, so the people practiced wisal, and they said: You forbade us wisal and you practice wisal. He said: I am not like any one of you; I am fed and given drink."
"4722","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Let none of you sell over the sale of his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother, except that he permits him."
"4723","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Before you is a Hawd, between Jarba and Adhruh."
"4724","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the woman who joins hair and the one who has it joined, and the woman who tattoos and the one who has it done."
"4725","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Makkah from the upper mountain pass which is at al-Batha, and exited from the lower mountain pass."
"4726","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, from Muhammad ibn Suqah from Nafi from Ibn Umar: We used to count for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a gathering, him saying: My Lord, forgive me and turn to me, indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Forgiving, a hundred times."
"4727","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Fudayl, meaning Ibn Ghazwan, narrated to us from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Fatimah and found on her door a curtain, so he did not enter upon her, and seldom would he enter except he began with her. He said: Then Ali came and saw her concerned, so he said: What is with you. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me and did not enter upon me. So Ali went to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Fatimah was distressed that you came to her and did not enter upon her. He said: What have I to do with the world, and what have I to do with figured cloth. He said: So he went to Fatimah and informed her of the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said: Then say to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What do you command me with it. So he said: Say to her that she send it to the sons of so-and-so."
"4728","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Fudayl, meaning Ibn Ghazwan, narrated to us, Abu Duhqanah narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar, and he said: A guest came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to Bilal: Bring us food. So Bilal went and exchanged two sas of dates for a sa of good dates, and their dates were inferior, and the dates pleased the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: From where are these dates. So he informed him that he exchanged a sa for two sas, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Return our dates to us."
"4729","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter unless he repents."
"4730","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you is called to a wedding feast, let him answer."
"4731","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib asked permission of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to stay the nights of Mina at Makkah on account of his water service, so he permitted him."
"4732","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dealt with the people of Khaybar for half of what came out of crops or dates, and he used to give his wives every year one hundred wasqs and eighty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley. Then when Umar ibn al-Khattab stood, he divided Khaybar, and he gave the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the choice to have land allotted to them or to guarantee them the wasqs every year. So they differed; among them were those who chose to have land allotted, and among them were those who chose the wasqs, and Hafsah and Aishah were among those who chose the wasqs."
"4733","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar from his father, he said: We went early with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Mina to Arafat, among us the one saying talbiyah and among us the one saying takbir."
"4734","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a ring of silver, and it was in his hand, then it was in the hand of Abu Bakr after him, then it was in the hand of Umar, then it was in the hand of Uthman, its engraving: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4735","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man should not make a man leave his seat to sit in it, but make room and widen."
"4736","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it."
"4737","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us from Wabarah from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered killing the mouse and the crow and the wolf. He said: It was said to Ibn Umar: The snake and the scorpion. He said: That used to be said."
"4738","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that goods be met before they enter the markets."
"4739","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw in some of his raids a slain woman, so he forbade killing women and children."
"4740","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding women in ihram from gloves and the face veil and clothes touched by wars and saffron."
"4741","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you dozes in his seat on Friday, let him move to another."
"4742","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Salim from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever lies upon me, a house in the Fire is built for him."
"4743","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from Hanzalah from Salim: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw at the Kabah a wheat-colored man with lank head, placing his hand on two men, his head dripping or flowing, so I asked: Who is this. They said: Isa son of Maryam, or the Masih son of Maryam, and I do not know which of the two he said. And I saw behind him a red man with curly head, blind in the right eye, the one I saw most resembling him being Ibn Qatan, so I asked: Who is this. They said: The Masih, the Dajjal."
"4744","Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us from Sufyan from Ismail from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered killing dogs until we killed the dog of a woman who came from the desert."
"4745","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Fudayl, meaning Ibn Ghazwan, narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whichever man declares a man a disbeliever, then if he is as he said, otherwise it returns with disbelief."
"4746","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, Malik ibn Anas informed us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw in some of his raids a slain woman, so he disapproved of that and forbade killing women and children."
"4747","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abdullah from Sad, freedman of Talhah, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a hadith which, had I not heard it except once or twice, until he counted seven times, but I heard it more than that. He said: There was al-Kifl among the Children of Israil who would not refrain from any sin he did, then a woman came to him and he gave her sixty dinars on condition that he have intercourse with her. Then when he sat from her as a man sits from his wife, she trembled and wept, so he said: What makes you weep, did I compel you. She said: No, but this is a deed I never did, and only need drove me to it. He said: So you do this and never did it. He said: Then he got down and said: Go, the dinars are yours. Then he said: By Allah, al-Kifl will never disobey Allah again. So he died that night, and in the morning it was written on his door: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has forgiven al-Kifl."
"4748","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Asim, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If people knew what is in solitude, no one would ever travel alone at night."
"4749","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us from Yusuf ibn Suhayb from Zayd al-Ammi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wants his supplication answered and his distress removed, let him relieve one in hardship."
"4750","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us from Yazid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ibn Umar that he kissed the hand of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4751","Waki narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to me from Salim from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out from the house of Aishah and said: The head of disbelief is from here, whence rises the horn of Satan."
"4752","Waki narrated to us from al-Umari from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wisal in fasting, so it was said to him: You do it. He said: I am not like any one of you; I spend with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"4753","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Asim ibn al-Mundhir from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When water is the amount of two qullahs or three, nothing makes it impure. He said, and Waki said, meaning by qullah a large jar."
"4754","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Tribulation comes from here, from the east."
"4755","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was at this pillar, which was then a palm trunk, meaning preaching."
"4756","Waki narrated to us, Qudamah ibn Musa narrated to us from a shaykh from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No prayer after the rise of dawn except two rakahs."
"4757","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib and al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray two rakahs after Maghrib in his house."
"4758","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Tawbah al-Anbari from Mawriq al-Ijli, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Do you pray Duha. He said: No. I said: Did Umar pray it. He said: No. I said: Did Abu Bakr pray it. He said: No. I said: Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray it. He said: No, I think not."
"4759","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The parable of the Quran is like hobbled camels; if its owner attends to it, he holds it, and if he leaves it, it goes away."
"4760","Waki narrated to us, Said ibn al-Saib narrated to me from Dawud ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer at Mina, so he said: Did you hear Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: Yes, and I believed, so I was guided by him. He said: He used to pray at Mina two rakahs."
"4761","Waki narrated to us, Isa ibn Hafs ibn Asim narrated to us from his father, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both, he said: We went out with Ibn Umar and prayed the obligatory prayer, then he saw some of his children volunteering, so Ibn Umar said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman on a journey, and they did not pray before it nor after it. Ibn Umar said: Had I volunteered, I would have completed."
"4762","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar and from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Aishah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a lahd made for him."
"4763","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Mujahid from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited in the two rakahs before Fajr and the two rakahs after Maghrib twenty-odd times or ten-odd times: Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One."
"4764","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Layth from Mujahid from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took hold of part of my body and said: O Abdullah, be in this world as though a stranger or a passerby, and count yourself among the dead."
"4765","Waki narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to me from Yazid ibn Utarid Abu al-Bazara al-Sadusi from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to drink while standing and eat while walking in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"4766","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The keys of the unseen are five, none knows them but Allah: Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed Allah is Knowing, Aware."
"4767","Waki narrated to us, Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, Salim narrated to me from his father that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Only one who has no share wears silk."
"4768","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Ibn Rawahah to Khaybar to estimate for them, then gave them the choice to take or return, so they said: This is the truth; by this the heavens and the earth stand."
"4769","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade castrating horses and animals. And Ibn Umar said: In it is growth of creation."
"4770","Waki narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If people knew what is in solitude, no rider would ever travel at night alone."
"4771","Waki narrated to us, Thabit ibn Umarah narrated to us from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, so there is no prayer after dawn until it rises, meaning the sun."
"4772","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not aim your prayer at the rising of the sun nor its setting, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."
"4773","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted women to let down a span. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, then our feet will be uncovered. So he said: A cubit, and do not add over it."
"4774","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Among the best of your names are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman."
"4775","Waki narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No contagion and no omen and no hamah. He said: Then a man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what of a camel with mange so camels get mange. He said: That is decree; so who made the first mangy."
"4776","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad from Razin ibn Sulayman al-Ahmari from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a man who divorces his wife three times, then another marries her, and the door is closed and the curtain let down, then he divorces her before consummating with her: Is she lawful for the first. He said: No, until he tastes the little honey."
"4777","And Abu Ahmad, meaning al-Zubayri, narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad from Sulayman ibn Razin."
"4778","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he entered Makkah, said: O Allah, do not make our deaths therein until You take us out of it."
"4779","Waki narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us from Salim from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that images be struck, meaning the face."
"4780","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you hurry away from his food for prayer. He said: And Ibn Umar would hear the iqamah while eating supper and would not hurry."
"4781","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar narrated to us from Qazaah, he said: Ibn Umar said to me: I bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bade me farewell: I entrust to Allah your religion and your trust and the final deeds."
"4782","Waki narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us from Said ibn Hassan from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to stop at Arafah in the valley of Namirah. Then when al-Hajjaj killed Ibn al-Zubayr, he sent to Ibn Umar: At what hour did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, depart on this day. So he said: When that is, we depart. So al-Hajjaj sent a man to watch at what hour he departs. Then when Ibn Umar wanted to depart, he said: Has the sun declined. They said: The sun has not declined. He said: Has the sun declined. They said: It has not declined. Then when they said: It has declined, he mounted."
"4783","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Farqad al-Sabakhi from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to oil at ihram with unperfumed oil."
"4784","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Firas from Abu Salih from Zadham from Ibn Umar that he called a slave boy of his and freed him, then said: I have no reward for it equal to this thing I lifted from the earth. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever slaps his slave boy, his expiation is freeing him."
"4785","Waki narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Muslim al-Fazari narrated to us, Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to me: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not leave these supplications when morning came and when evening came: O Allah, I ask You well-being in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You pardon and well-being in my religion and my world and my family and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and secure my fears. O Allah, guard me from before me and from behind me and from my right and from my left and from above me, and I seek refuge by Your might lest I be seized from beneath me. He said, meaning collapse."
"4786","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Najrani from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a drunk man and flogged him the hadd. So he said: What is your drink. He said: Raisins and dates. He said: Each one of them suffices from the other."
"4787","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Abu Tumah, their freedman, and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Ghafiqi, that they heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wine is cursed in ten ways: Wine is cursed in itself, and its drinker, and its server, and its seller, and its buyer, and its presser, and the one for whom it is pressed, and its carrier, and the one to whom it is carried, and the eater of its price."
"4788","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Musa, Waki said we see he is Ibn Uqbah, from Salim from Ibn Umar, he said: The oath of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he would swear upon was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"4789","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Salim, meaning Ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar that he divorced his wife while menstruating, so Umar asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Order him to take her back, then let him divorce her pure or pregnant."
"4790","Waki narrated to us from Sharik from Abdullah ibn Usm, and Israil said Ibn Ismah, Waki said he is Ibn Usm: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In Thaqif is a destroyer and a liar."
"4791","Waki narrated to us from Shubah from Yala ibn Ata from Ali al-Azdi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Prayer of night and day is two by two."
"4792","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Asim ibn Ubaydullah from Salim from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers; it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"4793","Waki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed toward his camel."
"4794","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: While the people were in the mosque of Quba in the dawn prayer, a comer came to them and said: Quran has been revealed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he was directed toward the Kabah. He said: So they turned."
"4795","Waki narrated to us from his father from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Mujalid from Mujahid from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever disowns his child to disgrace him in this world, Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before the witnesses, requital for requital."
"4796","Waki narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib from his maternal uncle al-Harith from Salim from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order us to lighten, though he would lead us with al-Saffat."
"4797","Waki narrated to us from Hisham ibn Sad from Umar ibn Asid from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to say in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The Messenger is the best of people, then Abu Bakr, then Umar. And Ibn Abi Talib was given three traits, that one of them be mine is dearer to me than red camels: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married him his daughter and she bore him, and he closed the doors except his door in the mosque, and he gave him the banner on the day of Khaybar."
"4798","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Yazid ibn Bishr from Ibn Umar, he said: Islam is built on five: testimony that there is no god but Allah, and establishing prayer, and giving zakah, and Hajj of the House, and fasting Ramadan. He said: Then a man said to him: And jihad in the path of Allah. Ibn Umar said: Jihad is good; thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us."
"4799","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abu al-Yaqzan from Zadham from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three are upon mounds of musk on the Day of Resurrection: a man who leads a people and they are pleased with him, and a man who calls adhan in every day and night for five prayers, and a slave who fulfills the right of Allah the Exalted and the right of his masters."
"4800","Waki narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Tawil narrated to me from Abu Yahya al-Qattat from Mujahid from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The people of the Fire are magnified in the Fire until between the earlobe of one of them and his shoulder is a journey of seven hundred years, and the thickness of his skin is seventy cubits, and his molar is like Uhud."
"4801","Waki' narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ziyad, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ruqba and said: Whoever is granted a ruqba gift, it is his."
"4802","Waki' narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the house of Aishah and said: Disbelief is from here, from where the horn of Satan rises."
"4803","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was asked about water in the open land and the beasts and wild animals that come to it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When water is two qullahs, nothing makes it impure."
"4804","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet before me but he described him to his ummah, and I shall describe him with a description none before me has given: he is one-eyed, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, is not one-eyed; his right eye is as if it were a floating grape."
"4805","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever deliberately abandons Asr until the sun sets, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"4806","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bahir al-San'ani al-Qass informed us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-San'ani informed him that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at the Day of Resurrection as if seeing it with his own eyes, let him recite: When the sun is folded up, and When the sky splits asunder, and When the sky bursts open; and I think he said: Surah Hud."
"4807","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: When Hafsah became widowed, and she had been under Khunays ibn Hudhafah, Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, met Uthman and offered her to him, and Uthman said: I have no need of women, but I shall consider. Then he met Abu Bakr and offered her to him, and he remained silent, so Umar felt resentment toward Abu Bakr in himself. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to her. Umar met Abu Bakr and said: I had offered her to Uthman and he turned me down, and I offered her to you and you kept silent toward me, so I was angrier with you than with Uthman, who had turned me down. Abu Bakr said: He had already mentioned her matter, and it was a secret, so I disliked disclosing the secret."
"4808","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks it, let him seek it on the twenty-seventh night; and he said: Seek it on the twenty-seventh night, meaning Laylat al-Qadr."
"4809","Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantamah. It was said: What is hantamah? He said: The jar, meaning nabidh."
"4810","Yazid informed us, Husayn ibn Dhakwan, meaning al-Mu'allim, informed us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, that Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas attributed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: It is not lawful for a man to give a gift and then take it back, except a father regarding what he gives his child. And the example of one who gives a gift then takes it back is like the dog: it ate until it was full, then vomited, then returned to its vomit."
"4811","Yazid narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Amr al-Jumahi, from Abu Bakr ibn Musa, who said: I was with Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar when a caravan of Umm al-Banin passed with bells in it, and Salim narrated from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The angels do not accompany a party with a jingling bell among them. So see how many jingling bells are among these."
"4812","Yazid informed us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Siddiq, he is al-Naji, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you lay your dead in the grave, say: In the name of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4813","Yazid informed us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog other than a dog for crops, or livestock, or hunting, a qirat is deducted from his deed every day. I said to Ibn Umar: If it is in a house and I dislike it? He said: It is upon the master of the house who owns it."
"4814","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, Salim narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, concerning the dream of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Abu Bakr and Umar. He said: I saw the people gathered, then Abu Bakr stood and drew a bucket or two, and in his drawing there was weakness, and may Allah forgive him. Then Umar drew, and it turned into a large bucket. I never saw a genius among the people drawing his drawing, until the people watered their camels to satiety."
"4815","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The month is like this, and like this, and like this, and he clasped his thumb on the third."
"4816","Rawh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"4817","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clientage belongs to the one who emancipates."
"4818","Rawh narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, who said: Ibn Umar used to perform ablution three times, attributing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ibn Abbas used to perform ablution once, attributing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4819","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) halted at al-Batha' which is at Dhu al-Hulayfah and prayed there."
"4820","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, I heard Salim ibn Abdullah say: Ibn Umar would almost curse al-Bayda' and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram from the mosque."
"4821","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Nafi' informed me, that Ibn Umar used to say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing belong to You, and sovereignty; there is no partner for You."
"4822","Rawh and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd; Affan said in his hadith: Humayd informed us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Makkah with his companions reciting talbiyah; and Affan said: entering ihram for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes may make it Umrah, except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall one of us go to Mina with his organ dripping semen? He said: Yes, and the censers blazed. Ali ibn Abi Talib arrived from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I entered ihram with what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with. Rawh said: Then you have a sacrificial animal with us. Humayd said: I narrated it to Tawus and he said: This is what the people did. Affan said: Make it Umrah."
"4823","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine in this world shall not drink it in the Hereafter unless he repents."
"4824","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4825","al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people hoard the dinar and the dirham, trade by inah, follow the tails of cows, and abandon jihad in the cause of Allah, Allah sends down upon them a calamity and does not lift it from them until they return to their religion."
"4826","Aswad informed us, Isra'il informed us, from Fudayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha' prayer until those who pray had prayed, those awake had woken, those sleeping had slept, and those keeping night vigil had prayed tahajjud. Then he came out and said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would have commanded them to pray at this time, or this prayer, or something like that."
"4827","Rawh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both, that al-Abbas sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to spend that night in Makkah on account of the water-drawing duty, and he permitted him."
"4828","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, that Ibn Umar used to take a short nap at al-Batha', and mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that."
"4829","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anointed himself with oil that was not perfumed while in ihram."
"4830","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is unlawful."
"4831","Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"4832","Mu'adh narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, I heard my father say: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This authority shall remain in Quraysh as long as two of the people remain. He said: And he moved his two fingers, twisting them like this."
"4833","Mu'adh narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Utarid Abu al-Bazari, who said: Ibn Umar said: We used to drink while standing and eat while walking in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4834","Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muslim, a freedman of Abd al-Qays; Mu'adh said: Shu'bah used to say: al-Qurri; who said: A man said to Ibn Umar: What do you think, is witr a sunnah? He said: What sunnah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr, and the Muslims prayed witr. He said: Is it not a sunnah? He said: Quiet, do you not understand? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr, and the Muslims prayed witr."
"4835","Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: A man called out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What garments may the muhrim wear? He said: Do not wear the shirt, nor the turban, nor the hooded cloaks, nor the trousers, nor the leather socks, unless there are no sandals; if there are no sandals, then two socks below the ankles; nor any garment touched by wars dye; Ibn Awn said: Either he said dyed, or he said touched by wars and saffron; Ibn Awn said: And in the book of Nafi': touched by it."
"4836","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: I mentioned it to Ibn Shihab; he said: Salim narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Umar used to do that. Then Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd narrated to him that Aishah narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to permit women to wear leather socks."
"4837","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to me, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Tawus, who said: I asked Ibn Umar: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid nabidh of the jar? He said: Yes. Tawus said: By Allah, I heard it from him."
"4838","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except al-Masjid al-Haram, for it is better."
"4839","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a banner is raised for every treacherous one, and it is said: This is the treachery of so-and-so, son of so-and-so."
"4840","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: Let none of you seek out sunrise or sunset, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid that."
"4841","Muhammad narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it off, then turned to the people and said: When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit toward his face, for Allah the Exalted is before the face of one of you when he is in prayer."
"4842","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he put his foot in the stirrup and his camel stood upright with him, would enter ihram from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."
"4843","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out by the way of al-Shajarah, and used to enter Makkah from the upper pass and leave by the lower pass."
"4844","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he circumambulated the House in the first circumambulation, would hasten three circuits and walk four."
"4845","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the Qur'an is like hobbled camels: if its owner attends to them with their hobbles, he keeps hold of them, and if he releases their hobbles, they go away."
"4846","Yazid informed us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Quba' riding and walking."
"4847","Yazid informed us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Maghrib prayer is the witr of the daytime, so make the night prayer odd."
"4848","Yazid informed us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear dawn, pray witr with one."
"4849","Yazid informed us, Sa'id ibn Ziyad al-Shaybani informed us, Ziyad ibn Subayh al-Hanafi narrated to us, who said: I was standing praying toward the House with an old man beside me, and I prolonged the prayer and put my hands on my waist, so the old man struck my chest with his hand, a blow he did not spare. I said to myself: What has disturbed him about me? I hastened to finish, and there was a boy sitting behind him. I said: Who is this old man? He said: This is Abdullah ibn Umar. I sat until he finished, then I said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, what disturbed you about me? He said: It is you. I said: Yes. He said: That is standing akimbo in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid it."
"4850","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of Arafah; some of us said Allahu Akbar and some said talbiyah. As for us, we said takbir. He said: I said: How strange of you, why did you not ask him how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did?"
"4851","Yazid informed us, Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Wabarah: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the muhrim to kill the wolf, meaning, and the mouse, the crow, and the kite. It was said to him: And the snake and the scorpion? He said: That used to be said."
"4852","Yazid informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Umar, that a man bought date-palms whose owner had pollinated them, then disputed with him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the fruit belongs to its owner who pollinated them, unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."
"4853","Yazid informed us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, and Ishaq ibn Isa said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from al-Hasan ibn Hadiyah, who said: I met Ibn Umar; Ishaq said: He said to me: From which people are you? I said: From the people of Oman. He said: From the people of Oman? I said: Yes. He said: Shall I not narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes indeed. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a land called Oman, beside it, and Ishaq said: by its side, flows the sea; a Hajj from it is better than two Hajjs from other than it."
"4854","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed Khaybar to its people for half, and it remained with them throughout the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the life of Abu Bakr, and the life of Umar, until Umar sent me to divide with them, and they bewitched me so my hand became crooked, and Umar took it back from them."
"4855","Yazid narrated to us, from Hammam, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that Aishah wanted to buy Barirah, but her people refused to sell her unless the clientage would be theirs. Aishah mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy her and free her, for clientage belongs only to the one who pays the price."
"4856","Yazid informed us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, Nafi' narrated to us, who said: Ibn Umar felt cold while in ihram and said: Throw a garment over me. So I threw a hooded cloak over him, and he pulled it back and said: Would you throw over me a garment the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the muhrim to wear?"
"4857","Mu'adh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, who said: I wrote to Nafi' asking him: Was the invitation before fighting? He wrote back to me: That was in the beginning of Islam, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided Banu al-Mustaliq while they were heedless, their cattle being watered at the water, and killed their fighters, took their captives, and on that day took Juwayriyah bint al-Harith. Abdullah ibn Umar narrated this hadith to me, and he was in that army."
"4858","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khubayb, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, six years at Mina, and they prayed the traveler's prayer."
"4859","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer is like a tree whose leaves do not fall. What is it? He said: They said this and that but did not get it right, and I wanted to say: It is the date-palm, but I was shy. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the date-palm."
"4860","Yazid informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the night prayer two by two, then pray witr with one rak'ah at the end of the night, then stand as if the adhan and the iqamah were in his ears."
"4861","Yazid informed us, Isma'il informed us, from Abu Hanzalah, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer while traveling, and he said: Prayer while traveling is two rak'ahs. He said: We are safe, fearing no one. He said: The sunnah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4862","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People shall stand before the Lord of the worlds, for the greatness of the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted is He, on the Day of Resurrection, until sweat shall bridle men up to the middle of their ears."
"4863","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"4864","Yazid informed us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, that he narrated to them from Ibn Umar, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over the well of Badr and said: O so-and-so, O so-and-so, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? By Allah, indeed they now hear my speech. Yahya said: Aishah said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman, he erred; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: By Allah, indeed they now know that what I used to say to them is true. And Allah the Exalted says: Indeed you do not make the dead hear, and you do not make those in the graves hear."
"4865","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave and said: Indeed this one is now being punished on account of his family's weeping over him. Aishah said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman, he erred; Allah the Exalted says: No bearer of burdens bears the burden of another. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: Indeed this one is now being punished while his family weep over him."
"4866","Yazid informed us, Muhammad informed us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, who said: Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is twenty-nine, and he clapped his hands twice, then clapped a third time and clasped his thumb. Aishah said: May Allah forgive Abu Abd al-Rahman, he erred; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only kept away from his wives for a month, then came down after twenty-nine, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, you came down after twenty-nine. He said: The month is sometimes twenty-nine."
"4867","Yazid informed us, Isma'il informed us, from Salim al-Barrad, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever prays over a funeral, he has a qirat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is the qirat? He said: Like Uhud."
"4868","Yazid informed us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon this minbar, while forbidding people, when they enter ihram, what is disliked for them: Do not wear turbans, shirts, trousers, hooded cloaks, or leather socks, unless one compelled is forced to them, then let him cut them below the ankles; nor any garment touched by wars or saffron. He said: And I heard him forbid women gloves, the face-veil, and garments touched by wars and saffron."
"4869","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, that he narrated to them from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Selling fruit is not valid until its soundness is evident."
"4870","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Husayn, informed us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, who said: We were with Ibn Umar on a journey when he passed a place and turned aside from it. He was asked: Why did you do that? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do this, so I did it."
"4871","Yazid informed us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, informed us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, he was informed that a man informed him, from his father Yahya, that he was with Abdullah ibn Umar, and that Abdullah ibn Umar said to him concerning the tribulation: You do not consider killing anything. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding private conversation: Two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion."
"4872","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: While Ubayd ibn Umayr was preaching, with Abdullah ibn Umar present, Ubayd ibn Umayr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the hypocrite is like a sheep between two resting-places: when it comes to these, they butt it, and when it comes to these, they butt it. Ibn Umar said: That is not how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: Like a sheep between two flocks. The old man memorized it angrily, and when Abdullah saw that, he said: If I had not heard it, I would not have contradicted you over it."
"4873","Yazid informed us, Ibn Awn informed us, who said: I wrote to Nafi' asking him: What kept Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from raiding, or from the people when they raid, regarding calling the enemy before fighting them, and whether a man in the battalion may charge without his commander's permission? He wrote back to me: The sons of Ibn Umar used to raid, and he used to provide mounts, and he used to say: The best deed after prayer is jihad in the cause of Allah the Exalted. Nothing kept Ibn Umar from raiding except the bequests of Umar, young children, and much neglected property. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided Banu al-Mustaliq while they were heedless, watering at their livestock, and killed their fighters, took their captives, and took Juwayriyah bint al-Harith. Ibn Umar narrated this hadith to me, and he was in that army. They were only called in the beginning of Islam. As for a man, he may not charge against the battalion except with his commander's permission."
"4874","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two to converse privately to the exclusion of a third when there is no one else with them. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to make another man give up his seat, and said: When he returns, he has more right to it."
"4875","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you dozes in the mosque on Friday, let him move from that seat of his to another."
"4876","Yazid informed us, Muhammad informed us, from Nafi' and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, both narrated it from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five, there is no sin upon anyone for killing them: the crow, the mouse, the kite, the scorpion, and the vicious dog."
"4877","Yazid informed us, Muhammad informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qiblah and took a stick or a pebble and scraped it with it, then said: When one of you stands to pray, let him not spit toward his qiblah, for he only converses privately with his Lord, Blessed and Exalted is He."
"4878","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rak'ah at the end of the night."
"4879","Yazid informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Dajjal is one-eyed, as if it were a floating grape."
"4880","Yazid informed us, Asbagh ibn Zayd informed us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever hoards food for forty nights has disassociated from Allah the Exalted, and Allah the Exalted has disassociated from him. And whenever the people of a courtyard wake with a hungry man among them, the protection of Allah the Exalted is disassociated from them."
"4881","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that he disliked stipulation in Hajj and used to say: Is not the sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sufficient for you? He did not stipulate."
"4882","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, and Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lizard, and he said: I neither eat it nor forbid it."
"4883","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May I buy gold with silver? He said: When you take one of the two, your companion must not leave you while there is still confusion between you and him."
"4884","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Qays, informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: My father sent me to Ibn Umar, and I said: May I enter? He recognized my voice and said: O my son, when you come to people, say: Peace be upon you; if they return it to you, say: May I enter? He said: Then he saw his son Waqid trailing his garment and said: Lift your garment, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever trails his garment out of pride, Allah shall not look at him."
"4885","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you seek out prayer at sunrise or at sunset."
"4886","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"4887","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I have not ceased touching the two corners, in ease or hardship, since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch them."
"4888","Ma'mar said: And Ayyub informed me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, the like of it."
"4889","He said: And Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved in his Hajj."
"4890","He said: And Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4891","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah upon a camel of Usamah ibn Zayd until he halted in the courtyard of the Ka'bah, then called for Uthman ibn Talhah for the key, and he brought it and opened. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered with Usamah, Bilal, and Uthman ibn Talhah, and they closed the door upon them for a while, then opened it. Abdullah said: I hastened ahead of the people and found Bilal standing at the door. I said: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars. He said: And I forgot to ask him how many he prayed."
"4892","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the weak among the people to leave Muzdalifah by night."
"4893","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Malik, from Ibn Umar, who said: I prayed with him Maghrib three and Isha' two with one iqamah. Malik ibn Khalid al-Harithi said to him: What is this prayer, Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: I prayed it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this place with one iqamah."
"4894","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id, from Ibn Umar, and from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Malik al-Asadi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Maghrib and Isha' at Jam': he prayed Maghrib three and Isha' two with one iqamah."
"4895","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite talbiyah: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing belong to You, and sovereignty; there is no partner for You."
"4896","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, and Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4897","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of al-Hudaybiyah: O Allah, forgive those who shave. A man said: And those who shorten? He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. He said: And those who shorten? Until he said it three or four times, then he said: And those who shorten."
"4898","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth on the day of sacrifice, then returned and prayed Zuhr at Mina."
"4899","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that a man called out: O Messenger of Allah, what garments must the muhrim avoid? He said: He must not wear trousers, nor the shirt, nor the hooded cloak, nor the turban, nor any garment touched by saffron or wars. Let each of you enter ihram in a waist-wrapper, a cloak, and sandals; if he finds no sandals, let him wear leather socks and cut them so they are below the ankles."
"4900","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days."
"4901","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a share he owns in a slave, the value of the remainder is assessed against his wealth."
"4902","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not right for a Muslim man over whom three nights pass except that his will is with him."
"4903","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar told us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that Umar gave a horse of his in the path of Allah, then he saw it being sold and wanted to buy it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not take back your charity."
"4904","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan told us, from his father and al-A'mash and Mansur, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Ibn Umar, who said: Umar used to swear by my father, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him and said: Whoever swears by something other than Allah Almighty has committed shirk; and the other said: and it is shirk."
"4905","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan told us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah: the trustworthy told me, or one I do not suspect, from Ibn Umar, that he proposed to a relative of his for his daughter; he said: the inclination of the woman's mother was toward Ibn Umar, and the inclination of her father was toward an orphan of his; he said: so the father married her to that orphan of his, and she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Consult women regarding their daughters."
"4906","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Ata told me, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no umra and no ruqba; whoever is given something as a life grant or as a death-conditional grant, it is his in his life and after his death."
"4907","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place the stone of his ring on the inner side of the palm."
"4908","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Abi Rawwad told us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the mosque and saw spit in the qiblah; when he finished his prayer he said: When one of you prays in the mosque he is conversing privately with his Lord, and Allah Blessed and Exalted turns to him with His Face, so let none of you spit toward the qiblah nor to his right; then he called for a stick and scraped it, then he called for khaluq and stained it."
"4909","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than twenty-five times, or more than twenty times; Abd al-Razzaq said, and I doubt; reciting in the two rak'ahs of Fajr: Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One."
"4910","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, a shaykh from Najran told us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What is permissible of witnesses in fosterage? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man or a woman."
"4911","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from Mu'tamir, from Muhammad ibn Uthaym, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, meaning with this hadith."
"4912","Abu Abd al-Rahman said, and Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, who said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uthaym, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what is permissible of witnesses in fosterage; he said: A man and a woman."
"4913","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr both said: Ibn Jurayj told us, Ibn Tawus told me, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked him and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid making nabidh in the earthen jar and the gourd? He said: Yes."
"4914","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the earthen jar and the pitch-coated vessel and the gourd; Abu al-Zubayr said: And I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earthen jar and the pitch-coated vessel and the hollowed stump, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not find anything in which nabidh could be made for him, nabidh was made for him in a stone basin."
"4915","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar told us, from Thabit al-Bunani, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about the nabidh of the earthen jar, and he said: Forbidden; I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it? So Ibn Umar said: They claim that."
"4916","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar told us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine in this world then dies while drinking it, not having repented from it, Allah will forbid it for him in the Hereafter."
"4917","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he returns, it becomes due upon Allah Almighty to give him to drink from the river of al-Khabal; it was said: What is the river of al-Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of Hellfire."
"4918","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"4919","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar told us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon twice, with a sitting between them."
"4920","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar told us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on the minbar saying: Whoever among you comes to Friday, let him perform ghusl."
"4921","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs after Friday in his house."
"4922","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Hunayn, Umar asked about a vow he had vowed in the Jahiliyyah, i'tikaf for a day, so he commanded him with it; and Umar went ahead of him; he said: And he sent with me a slave girl he had acquired on the day of Hunayn; he said: So I placed her in one of the Bedouin houses when I alighted, and behold the captives of Hunayn had gone out hurrying, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has freed us; he said: So Umar said to Abdullah: Go and release her; he said: So I went and released her."
"4923","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar told us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the Quran when its companion keeps to it and recites it by night and day is like a man who has camels: if he hobbles them he preserves them, and if he releases their hobbles they go away; so too is the companion of the Quran."
"4924","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except over two: a man to whom Allah has given the Quran and he stands with it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends from it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day."
"4925","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten, in the last nine remaining."
"4926","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah, from Ibn Umar; Abd al-Razzaq said: once he would say Ibn Muhammad and once he would say Ibn Rabi'ah; who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying while on the steps of the Ka'bah: Praise be to Allah who fulfilled His promise and aided His servant and defeated the Confederates alone; verily every inherited honor from the Jahiliyyah is under my two feet today, except custodianship of the House and providing water to the pilgrims; verily what is between intentional and mistaken killing, and killing with the whip and the stone, is one hundred camels, forty of them pregnant with their young in their bellies."
"4927","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Omen is in three: the horse, the woman, and the house."
"4928","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Sadaqah al-Makki, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed i'tikaf and addressed the people and said: When one of you stands in prayer he is conversing privately with his Lord, so let each of you know what he converses with his Lord, and let none of you raise voices over others in recitation in prayer."
"4929","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May one of us sleep while junub? He said: Yes, and let him perform wudu as for prayer; Nafi' said: Ibn Umar, when he wanted to do anything of that, would perform wudu as for prayer, except his feet."
"4930","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it, that Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4931","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that one of you should aim for the setting of the sun and pray at that time."
"4932","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from coming, or he said: praying, in the mosque."
"4933","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, Umar ibn Habib narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man prevent his family from coming to the mosques; so a son of Abdullah ibn Umar said: Then we prevent them; Abdullah said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you say this? He said: So Abdullah did not speak to him until he died."
"4934","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bahir al-Qass told us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-San'ani told him that he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at the Day of Resurrection as if seeing with the eye, let him recite: When the sun is folded up, and When the sky splits asunder, and When the sky bursts open; and I think he said: and Surah Hud."
"4935","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Salih ibn Kaysan told me, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram when his mount stood upright with him."
"4936","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj told us, who said: Nafi' told me that Ibn Umar used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you eat from his sacrifice beyond three days."
"4937","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj told us, who said: Nafi' said to me: Abdullah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Five animals are killed, with no blame on whoever kills them in killing them: the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the vicious dog, and the mouse."
"4938","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj told us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from the hadith of Salim ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last seven of the month of Ramadan."
"4939","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr both said: Ibn Jurayj told us, who said: Ibn Shihab said: Salim ibn Abdullah narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Umar used to walk in front of the funeral, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman used to walk in front of it."
"4940","Hajjaj narrated to us, who said: I read to Ibn Jurayj: Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, similar to it."
"4941","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bahir narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who was from the people of Sanaa and was more knowledgeable of the lawful and the unlawful than Wahb, meaning Ibn Munabbih, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to look at the Day of Resurrection, let him recite: When the sun is folded up."
"4942","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, who heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the minbar: Whoever among you comes to Friday, let him perform ghusl."
"4943","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fruit being sold until its soundness appears."
"4944","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, who heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acquires a dog except a livestock dog or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"4945","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: A man invoked li'an against his wife? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between the two brothers of Banu al-Ajlan and said: One of you is lying, so is there a repenter among you? Three times."
"4946","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, who said: Ubaydullah told me, Nafi' told us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dealt with the people of Khaybar for half of what comes out of crops or dates, and he used to give his wives each year one hundred and eighty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley."
"4947","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he put his foot in the stirrup and his she-camel stood upright with him, would enter ihram from beside the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."
"4948","Hammad narrated to us, who said: Ubaydullah told us, and Muhammad ibn Bishr said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Messiah; Ibn Bishr said in his hadith: and he mentioned the Dajjal among the people, and said: Allah Blessed and Exalted is not one-eyed; verily the Messiah, the Dajjal, is blind in the right eye, as if his eye is a floating grape."
"4949","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is invited to a wedding feast, let him answer."
"4950","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this hadith and this description."
"4951","My father said, and before it he narrated to us, he said: Hisham and Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two afternoon prayers for two rak'ahs then gave salam, then he mentioned the hadith: so let him answer."
"4952","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten the dawn with witr."
"4953","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attributed the son of the li'an woman to his mother."
"4954","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal told me, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten the dawn with witr."
"4955","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Madinah ten years offering sacrifice."
"4956","Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him."
"4957","Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz told us, from Isma'il ibn Jarir, from Qaza'ah, who said: Abdullah ibn Umar said, and he had sent me on an errand of his: Come so I may bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade me farewell when he sent me on an errand of his; he took my hand and said: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the endings of your deeds."
"4958","Abdah ibn Sulayman Abu Muhammad al-Kilabi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over the well of Badr and said: Have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? Then he said: They hear what I say; that was mentioned to Aishah, and she said: What does Ibn Umar mean? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: They now know that what I used to say to them is the truth."
"4959","Abdah narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The dead is punished by the weeping of his family over him; that was mentioned to Aishah, and she said: What does Ibn Umar mean? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only passed by a grave and said: Its occupant is being punished while his family weep over him; then she recited this verse: No bearer of burdens bears the burden of another."
"4960","Abdah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he returned from armies and expeditions, or Hajj and Umrah, when he overlooked a high ground would say takbir three times then say: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Able; returning, repenting, worshipping, prostrating, to our Lord praising; He kept His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone."
"4961","Abdah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being asked about water in open desert land frequented by animals and beasts; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When water amounts to two qullahs, it does not carry filth."
"4962","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, one who heard Ibn Suraqah mentioning told me, from Ibn Umar, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying before prayer nor after it while traveling."
"4963","Abdah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar used to begin with prayer before the sermon on Eid."
"4964","Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed one tawaf for his qiran, did not exit between them, and bought a sacrificial animal on the way from Qudayd."
"4965","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, and Makhlad ibn Yazid told us, Sa'id told us the meaning, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi', the freedman of Ibn Umar: Ibn Umar heard the sound of a shepherd's flute, so he placed his two fingers in his ears and turned his mount from the road, saying: O Nafi', do you hear? I would say: Yes; he continued until I said: No; he said: Then he put down his hands and returned the mount to the road, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hear the sound of a shepherd's flute and do the like of this."
"4966","Al-Walid, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab narrated to me, that Ibn Abbas used to perform wudu once each and attribute that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that Ibn Umar used to perform wudu three times each and attribute that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4967","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar al-Thaqafi, that he heard Ibn Shihab reporting from Salim, from his father, who said: I witnessed Eid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he prayed without adhan or iqamah, then I witnessed Eid with Abu Bakr and he prayed without adhan or iqamah; he said: Then I witnessed Eid with Umar and he prayed without adhan or iqamah, then I witnessed Eid with Uthman and he prayed without adhan or iqamah."
"4968","Al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Rashid al-Jazari reporting that he heard Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri reporting from Salim ibn Abdullah reporting from his father Abdullah ibn Umar similar to this hadith or like it."
"4969","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No charity is accepted from misappropriated spoils, nor prayer without purification."
"4970","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu al-Sha'tha', who said: We came to Ibn Umar on the middle day of the days of Tashriq; he said: Food was brought, the people came near while a son of his withdrew; he said: So he said to him: Come near and eat; he said: So he said: I am fasting; he said: So he said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are days of eating and remembrance."
"4971","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever prays at the beginning of the night, let him make the last of his prayer witr, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command that."
"4972","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Salim narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown in sleep that I was drawing with a worn bucket on a well; then Abu Bakr came and drew a bucket or two, drawing weakly, and Allah forgive him; then Umar ibn al-Khattab came and drew, and it turned into a large bucket; I never saw a great man among the people drawing his drawing, until the people drank their fill and rested at the trough."
"4973","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Umar ibn Nafi', from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qaza'; Ubaydullah said: And qaza' is patching in the head."
"4974","Uthman narrated to us, Umar ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qaza'."
"4975","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us: I heard Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan al-Jumahi: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: That one of you should have his belly filled with pus is better for him than being filled with poetry."
"4976","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad told us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the stone of the ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the inner side of his palm."
"4977","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us: I heard Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan: I heard Salim saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw at the Ka'bah, on its front side, a dark man with straight hair, placing his hand on two men, his head dripping or trickling; I said: Who is this? They said: Isa son of Maryam, or the Messiah son of Maryam; and I saw behind him a red man, blind in the right eye, curly-haired, the one I have seen most resembling him is Ibn Qatan; I said: Who is this? They said: The Messiah, the Dajjal."
"4978","Ishaq ibn Sulayman and Abdullah ibn al-Harith both said: Hanzalah narrated to us: I heard Salim saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a suit of istabraq; he said: O Messenger of Allah, if you bought this suit and wore it when delegations come to you; he said: Only one who has no share wears this; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought three suits, and he sent to Umar a suit, and to Ali a suit, and to Usamah ibn Zayd a suit; so Umar brought his suit to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent this to me though I heard you say about it what you said; he said: I only sent it to you to sell it or tear it for your family into head coverings; Ishaq said in his hadith: And Usamah came to him wearing the suit, and he said: I did not send it to you to wear it; I only sent it to you to sell it; I do not know whether he said to Usamah: tear it into head coverings or not; Abdullah ibn al-Harith said in his hadith that he heard Salim ibn Abdullah saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: Umar found, then he mentioned its meaning."
"4979","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hanzalah told me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: And Usamah came to him having worn it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him and said: Did you clothe me? He said: Tear it among your women into head coverings, or fulfill with it your need."
"4980","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us: I heard Hanzalah: I heard Salim saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointing toward the east, or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) points toward the east, saying: Fitnah is here, indeed fitnah is here, indeed fitnah is here, from where the two horns of Satan rise."
"4981","Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us: I heard Yahya ibn Abi Kathir reporting that Abu Salamah told him, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he heard him saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The month is twenty-nine."
"4982","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd, who said: I was with Ibn Umar and he would pray on his mount here and here; I said to him; so he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing."
"4983","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Abdullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran three circuits from the Stone to the Stone and walked four."
"4984","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he returned from Uhud, the women of the Ansar began weeping over those killed of their husbands; he said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But Hamzah has no mourners; he said: Then he slept and awoke while they were weeping; he said: So they today are weeping, lamenting Hamzah."
"4985","Attab narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah told us, Yunus told us, from al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends punishment upon a people, the punishment strikes whoever is among them, then they are raised according to their deeds; and Ali said in his hadith, who said: Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me that he heard Ibn Umar saying it."
"4986","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I never came to the Corner since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching it, in hardship or ease, except that I touched it."
"4987","Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, make witr with one."
"4988","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab told me, from the hadith of Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the people in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being beaten when they bought food in bulk lest they sell it until they brought it to their dwellings."
"4989","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, and Yazid said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b told us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command us to lighten, and he would lead us with al-Saffat; Yazid said: In the morning."
"4990","Abd al-Wahid, meaning al-Haddad, narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in graves, say: In the name of Allah and upon the creed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4991","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya told us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, that his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban told him that he heard Ibn Umar saying: I once appeared on the roof of our house and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting on two bricks facing Bayt al-Maqdis."
"4992","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham told us, from Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Maghrib prayer is the witr of the daytime, so make your night prayer odd."
"4993","Yazid narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Ta'ifi, from Abdullah ibn al-Miqdam, who said: I saw Ibn Umar walking between al-Safa and al-Marwah; I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why do you not run? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran and left it."
"4994","Yazid narrated to us, Husayn ibn Dhakwan told us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, Sulayman the freedman of Maymunah narrated to me: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not pray a prayer twice in one day."
"4995","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Khaliq ibn Salamah al-Shaybani told us: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: I was at the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the delegation of Abd al-Qays came with al-Ashajj; they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about drinks, and he forbade them the hantam, the gourd, and the hollowed stump."
"4996","Yazid narrated to us, Humayd told us, from Bakr, who said: I mentioned to Ibn Umar that Anas narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Umrah and Hajj; so he said: What does Anas mean! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram for Hajj, and we entered ihram with him; when he arrived he said: Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him make it Umrah; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a sacrificial animal with him, so he did not exit ihram."
"4997","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: Four I learned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Here I am O Allah here I am, here I am with no partner for You here I am, indeed praise and blessing are Yours and dominion, with no partner for You."
"4998","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fruit being sold until its soundness appears; he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is its soundness? He said: When its blight is gone and its good is pure."
"4999","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned for a man and his horse three shares: a share for him and two shares for his horse."
"5000","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know a tree whose blessing is like the Muslim man: the date palm."
"5001","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he would pray wherever his mount turned with him, and: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing that, and he would cite concerning it: And wherever you are, turn your faces."
"5002","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of my garment or part of my body and said: Abdullah, be as though you are a stranger or a passerby, and count yourself among the people of the graves."
"5003","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one in ihram shall not wear the burnus, nor the shirt, nor the turban, nor trousers, nor the two leather socks, unless compelled; he shall cut them off below the ankles, and he shall not wear a garment touched by wars or saffron unless it has been washed."
"5004","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the dabb, and he said: I do not eat it nor do I forbid it."
"5005","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Malik, meaning Ibn Mighwal, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"5006","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah al-Taifi, from Abdullah ibn Miqdam ibn Ward, he said: I saw Ibn Umar circumambulate between al-Safa and al-Marwah and he did not trot, so I said: Why do you do this? He said: Yes, each I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do; he trotted and he left off."
"5007","Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyah narrated to us, Abu Janab informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If you abandon jihad and take hold of the tails of cattle and trade in inah, Allah will surely bind a humiliation upon your necks that will not be removed from you until you repent to Allah and return to what you were upon."
"5008","Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Subayi, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the minbar saying: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"5009","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Malik informed us, I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I asked Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, are the two who invoke mutual curses separated? He said: Glory be to Allah, yes; indeed the first one to ask about that was so-and-so; he said: O Messenger of Allah, what if one of us saw his wife committing indecency, what should he do? If he stays silent he stays silent over a grave matter, and if he speaks it is the like of that; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed silent and did not answer him, then he rose for his need, then after that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What I asked you about, I have been afflicted with it; so Allah the Exalted revealed these verses in Surat al-Nur: And those who accuse their wives, until he completed the verses; then he called the man and recited them to him and reminded him of Allah the Exalted and told him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter, so he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I did not lie against her; then he called the woman and admonished her and reminded her and told her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter, so she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, he is indeed a liar; then he called the man and he bore witness four testimonies by Allah that he is among the truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he is among the liars; then he called for the woman and she bore witness four testimonies by Allah that he is among the liars, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he is among the truthful; then he separated between them."
"5010","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Muslim al-Khabbat, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the riders, or that a town-dweller sell for a desert-dweller, and that one of you propose over the proposal of his brother until he marries or leaves off, and no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, nor after Fajr until the sun rises or is high."
"5011","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: I had a wife whom I loved, and Umar disliked her, so he ordered me to divorce her and I refused, so he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah ibn Umar has a wife whom I dislike for him, and I ordered him to divorce her but he refused; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abdullah, divorce your wife, so I divorced her."
"5012","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed me, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah, he said: We were on a journey and Ibn Umar was with us, so I asked him and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not performing voluntary prayers while traveling, neither before the prayer nor after it; he said: And I asked Ibn Umar about the sale of fruits, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruits until the blight goes away; I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the going away of the blight, what is the blight? He said: The rising of the Pleiades."
"5013","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Jabalah, I heard Ibn Umar narrating, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the hantamah; I said to him: What is the hantamah? He said: The earthen jar."
"5014","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Muharib ibn Dithar, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5015","Muhammad ibn Jafar and al-Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba, the hantam, and the muzaffat; Shubah said: I heard it more than once; Hajjaj said: And he said: I doubt concerning the naqir; Hajjaj said in his hadith: Several times."
"5016","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abi al-Tayyah, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The witr is the last rakah of the night."
"5017","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, I heard Said ibn Amr ibn Said narrating that he heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: We are an unlettered nation; we neither write nor calculate; the month is like this and like this and like this, and he folded the thumb in the third, and the month is like this and like this and like this, meaning a full thirty."
"5018","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, and I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I passed with Ibn Umar on a road of the roads of Madinah, and there were youths who had set up a chicken shooting at it, with every miss going to them; so he became angry and said: Who did this? So they scattered; then Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever mutilates an animal."
"5019","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Zayd and Abu Bakr, the two sons of Muhammad, that they heard Nafi narrating from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You."
"5020","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Waqid ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard Nafi say: Ibn Umar saw a poor man and began bringing him near and placing food before him, and he began eating a great deal, so he said to me: Do not bring this one in to me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"5021","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do not prevent your women from the mosques at night; so Salim or one of his sons said: By Allah, we will not let them take it as a deceit; so he struck his chest and said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you say this."
"5022","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, I heard Sulayman al-Amash, and Hajjaj said: From al-Amash, narrating from Yahya ibn Waththab, from a shaykh among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, and I think he is Ibn Umar, Hajjaj said: Shubah said: Sulayman said, and he is Ibn Umar, narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The believer who mixes with people and is patient over their harm is greater in reward than the one who does not mix with them nor is patient over their harm; Hajjaj said: Better than the one who does not mix with them."
"5023","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of one; so I said to Ibn Umar: And if they are four? He said: Then there is no harm in it."
"5024","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, that he said: The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You."
"5025","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, that he asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and he said: Do you know Abdullah ibn Umar? For he divorced his wife while menstruating, so Umar went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Order him to take her back, then if divorce seems fit to him, let him divorce her at the beginning of her waiting period; Ibn Bakr said: Or at the beginning of her purity; so I said to Ibn Umar: Is that divorce of his counted as a divorce? He said: Yes; what if he was incapable and foolish?"
"5026","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I neither eat it nor command it nor forbid it."
"5027","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, and Abd al-Ala, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: Ghaylan ibn Salamah embraced Islam while he had ten wives under him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Take four of them."
"5028","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"5029","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are only like a hundred camels among which a mount can hardly be found."
"5030","Bahz and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, Bahz said: Uqbah ibn Hurayth narrated to us, I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jarr, which is the dubba, and the muzaffat, and he said: Make nabidh in the skins."
"5031","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Hurayth narrated to us, I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is seeking it, let him seek it in the ten; and if he is unable or weak, let him not be overcome concerning the remaining seven."
"5032","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Uqbah informed me, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the night is two by two, and if you fear the dawn, then make it odd with one rakah; he said: I said: What is two by two? He said: Two rakahs, two rakahs."
"5033","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I saw Tawus when he opened the prayer raising his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, then a man among his companions narrated to me that he narrates it from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5034","Abu al-Nadr narrated it to us with its meaning."
"5035","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When a man says to a man: O disbeliever, then one of them has borne it; if he is as he said, and otherwise it returns upon the other."
"5036","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar say: There was a man of Quraysh who was cheated in buying and selling, so he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Say: No deception."
"5037","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, the meaning; Hajjaj said: From Jabalah, and Ibn Jafar said: I heard Jabalah say: Ibn al-Zubayr used to provide us dates; he said: And the people had been afflicted with hardship that day, so we would eat, and Ibn Umar would pass by us while we were eating and say: Do not eat two together, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating two together; Hajjaj said: He forbade joining except that a man ask permission of his brother; and Shubah said: I do not think this phrase about asking permission is except from the words of Ibn Umar."
"5038","Bahz and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Jabalah, I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever drags a garment among his garments out of pride, then Allah the Exalted will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5039","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, Bahz said: He informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is like this, and he joined his fingers twice, and he bent the thumb in the third; Muhammad ibn Jafar said in his hadith: Meaning his saying: Twenty-nine."
"5040","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray wherever his mount turned with him; he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"5041","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Ibn Umar, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would pray the travel prayer, meaning two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman for six years of his rule, then he prayed four."
"5042","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Farwah al-Hamdani, I heard Awn al-Azdi say: Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Mamar was a governor over Fars, so he wrote to Ibn Umar asking him about the prayer, so Ibn Umar wrote: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he left his family would pray two rakahs until he returned to them."
"5043","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, the meaning, they said: Shubah narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Hajjaj said: From Banu Umayyah, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali, Hajjaj said: al-Umawi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, and he saw a man fidgeting in his prayer, so Ibn Umar said: Do not fidget in your prayer, and do as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do; Muhammad said: So Ibn Umar placed his right thigh upon the left, and his left hand upon his left knee, and placed his right hand upon the right, and gestured with his finger."
"5044","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Hayyan, meaning al-Bariqi, he said: It was said to Ibn Umar: Our imam lengthens the prayer, so Ibn Umar said: Two rakahs of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are lighter, or like one rakah of the prayer of this one."
"5045","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, meaning al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not prevent your women from the mosques."
"5046","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Ayyub ibn Musa narrating from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, nor shall a man make his brother rise from his seat then sit in it."
"5047","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, he said: I accompanied Ibn Umar from Madinah to Makkah, and he began praying upon his mount toward Makkah, so I said to Salim: Had his face been toward Madinah, how would he have prayed? He said: Ask him; so I asked him and he said: Yes, and here and here, and he said: Because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it."
"5048","Husayn narrated it to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, freedman of the family of Umar, and he mentioned its meaning."
"5049","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he heard Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two, and make it odd with one rakah at the end of the night."
"5050","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, I heard Muslim ibn Yannaq narrating from Ibn Umar, that he saw a man dragging his izar and said: From whom are you? So he gave his lineage to him, and he was a man of Banu Layth, so Ibn Umar recognized him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two ears of mine saying: Whoever drags his izar wanting thereby nothing but pride, then Allah the Exalted will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5051","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Firas, I heard Dhakwan narrating from Zadahn, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever beats a slave boy of his for a prescribed punishment he did not commit, or slaps him, then its expiation is to free him."
"5052","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, he said: I heard Mawarriq al-Ijli say: I heard a man asking Ibn Umar, or he asked Ibn Umar, and said: Do you pray Duha? He said: No; he said: Umar? He said: No; then he said: Abu Bakr? He said: No; he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I do not think so."
"5053","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Simak al-Hanafi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the House, and you will come to one who forbids you from it, and you will hear from him, meaning Ibn Abbas; Hajjaj said: You will hear from his saying; Ibn Jafar said: And Ibn Abbas was sitting near him."
"5054","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, I heard Salim ibn Abdullah narrating that he saw his father raising his hands when he said takbir, and when he wanted to bow, and when he raised his head from bowing, so I asked him about that, and he claimed that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"5055","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found these hadiths in my father's book in his handwriting, and it is up to the hadith of Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drags a garment among his garments out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5056","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, janabah befalls me in the night; so he said: Wash your private part, then perform ablution, then sleep."
"5057","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, then Allah the Exalted will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5058","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man asked him about the dabb; he said: I neither eat it nor prohibit it."
"5059","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Sham al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd Qarn; Ibn Umar said: And I was told that he appointed for the people of Yemen Yalamlam."
"5060","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruit, or palms, until its soundness appears."
"5061","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar about the sale of palms, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of palms until its soundness appears."
"5062","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray upon his mount wherever it turned, and he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"5063","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr used to provide us dates while the people that day were in hardship; he said: So Abdullah ibn Umar passed by us and forbade us from eating two together, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating two together except that a man ask permission of his brother."
"5064","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."
"5065","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid informed us, Shubah informed us, from Simak, meaning al-Hanafi, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs in the House."
"5066","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, Muhammad said: Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Simak al-Hanafi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the House, and you will come to one who forbids you from it."
"5067","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from a man of Najran, that he asked Ibn Umar and said: I only ask you about two things: about raisins and dates, and about advance payment for palms; so Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drunken man, and he said: I only drank raisins and dates; he said: So he lashed him the prescribed punishment and forbade the two to be combined; he said: And a man paid in advance for the palms of a man, then he said: His palms did not bear that year, so he wanted to take his dirhams back but he did not give him, so he brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: His palms did not bear; he said: No; he said: Then for what do you withhold his dirhams? He said: So he paid them to him; he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade advance payment for palms until its soundness appears."
"5068","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon the minbar, and a man asked him about the dabb, so he said: I neither eat it nor prohibit it."
"5069","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Khalid said: I asked Abdullah ibn Umar about Umrah before Hajj, so Ibn Umar said: There is no harm upon one who performs Umrah before performing Hajj; Ikrimah said: Abdullah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah before performing Hajj."
"5070","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Nafi informed me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: A man stood in the mosque of Madinah and said: O Messenger of Allah, from where do you command us to enter ihram? He said: The entering place of the people of Madinah is from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the entering place of the people of Sham is from al-Juhfah, and the entering place of the people of Najd is from Qarn; Nafi said to me: And Ibn Umar said to me: And they claim that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the entering place of the people of Yemen is from Yalamlam, and he used to say: I do not recall that."
"5071","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Nafi informed me, that Ibn Umar used to say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You; Nafi said: And Ibn Umar used to say, and I added: Here I am, here I am, and at Your service, and good is in Your hands; here I am, and desire and deeds are to You."
"5072","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Yazid informed us, Hanzalah informed us, I heard Tawus saying: I heard Ibn Umar, and a man asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the jarr and the dubba? He said: Yes."
"5073","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hanzalah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting one or a livestock dog, then two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"5074","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, he said: I asked Ibn Umar and said: Was the nabidh of the jar forbidden? He said: They have claimed that; so I said: Who claimed that? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: They claimed that; so I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you hear it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: They claimed that; he said: So Allah the Exalted turned him away from me that day; and one of them when asked: Did you hear it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Would become angry then attack his companion."
"5075","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever does not find two sandals, let him wear two leather socks, and let him slit them or cut them below the ankles."
"5076","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade wars and saffron; Shubah said: So I said: For the one in ihram? He said: Yes."
"5077","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When a man says to his brother: You are a disbeliever, or: O disbeliever, then one of them has borne it."
"5078","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, I heard Yahya ibn Waththab, I asked Ibn Umar about bathing on Friday; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us with it."
"5079","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the hypocrite is like the parable of the stray sheep between the two flocks; it goes to this one once and to this one once; it does not know whether to follow this one or this one."
"5080","Ismail ibn Ibrahim and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from his father, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about fasting the day of Arafah, so he said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Umar and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Uthman and he did not fast it, and I do not fast it, nor command it, nor forbid it; and Sufyan once said: From one who asked Ibn Umar."
"5081","Ismail ibn Ibrahim informed us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands when he entered into prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and he would not do that in prostration."
"5082","Ismail narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar when he entered the nearest part of the Haram would stop the talbiyah, then he would come to Dhu Tuwa and spend the night there and pray the dawn prayer there and bathe, and he would narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that."
"5083","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"5084","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who misses Asr, it is as though his family and his wealth were destroyed."
"5085","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man called to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you command us to pray at night? He said: One of you prays two by two, and when he fears the dawn, he prays one, and it makes odd for him what he has prayed."
"5086","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You."
"5087","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, from where do we enter ihram? He said: The people of Madinah enter from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn; he said: And they say: And the people of Yemen from Yalamlam."
"5088","Ismail narrated to us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to me, from Nafi, he said: When the people deposed Yazid ibn Muawiyah, Ibn Umar gathered his sons and his family, then he testified, then he said: As for what follows, we have pledged allegiance to this man upon the pledge of Allah and His Messenger, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The traitor will have a banner set up for him on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so; and among the greatest treachery, there being no associating with Allah the Exalted, is that a man pledge allegiance to a man upon the pledge of Allah and His Messenger then break his pledge; so none of you shall depose Yazid, nor shall one of you engage in this matter, lest there be a severance between me and him."
"5089","Ismail narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, a man of Banu Ghifar narrated to me in the gathering of Salim ibn Abdullah, so-and-so narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food of bread and meat, so he said: Hand me the forearm, so a forearm was handed and he ate it; Yahya said: I only know it like this; then he said: Hand me the forearm, so a forearm was handed and he ate it; then he said: Hand me the forearm, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, there are only two forearms; so he said: By your father, had you stayed silent, I would have continued to be handed a forearm from it as long as I called for it; then Salim said: As for this, no; I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted forbids you to swear by your fathers."
"5090","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I was with Ibn Umar and he was asked about the nabidh of the jar, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it, so it distressed me when I heard it, so I went to Ibn Abbas and said: Ibn Umar was asked about something; he said: So I began magnifying it, so he said: And what is it? I said: He was asked about the nabidh of the jar, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it; so he said: He spoke the truth; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it; I said: And what is the jar? He said: Everything made of clay."
"5091","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what of the animals do we kill when we enter ihram? So he said: Five, there is no blame upon one who kills them in killing them: The kite, the mouse, the crow, the scorpion, and the vicious dog."
"5092","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I reached the people while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished the sermon, so I said: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoin? They said: He forbade the muzaffat and the dubba."
"5093","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I only know it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever swears then makes an exception, then he has the choice; if he wishes to carry out his oath, and if he wishes to return without sin, or he said: Without harm."
"5094","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you swears, then he mentioned it."
"5095","Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab saw in a market a garment of brocade and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you bought this garment for the delegations; he said: Silk is only worn, or he said: This, by one who has no share; he said: I think he said: In the Hereafter; he said: Then after that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a garment of it, so he sent it to Umar, so he disliked it and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, you sent it to me while you said concerning it what I heard: Silk is only worn, or he said: This, by one who has no share; he said: I did not send it to you to wear it, but I sent it to you to obtain a price for it; Salim said: Because of this hadith Ibn Umar used to dislike the embroidered mark on the garment."
"5096","Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Umar: Do I recite behind the imam? He said: The recitation of the imam suffices you; I said: The two rakahs of Fajr, do I lengthen the recitation in them? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the night prayer two by two; he said: I said: I only asked you about the two rakahs of Fajr; he said: You are indeed bulky; do you not see me beginning the narration? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the night prayer two by two, and when he feared the dawn he made it odd with one rakah, then he would lay his head; if you wish say: He slept, and if you wish say: He did not sleep; then he would rise to them with the call to prayer in his ears, so what length could there be? Then I said: A man bequeaths wealth in the path of Allah, may it be spent from it for Hajj? He said: If you did, it would be from the path of Allah; he said: I said: A man misses a rakah with the imam, and the imam salutes, does he stand to make it up before the imam rises? He said: The imam when he saluted would rise; I said: A man takes on debt more than his wealth? He said: For every traitor there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection at his buttocks according to his treachery."
"5097","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Jahdam narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Badr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not exit ihram, and with Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and they did not exit."
"5098","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Jabir informed me, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he did that, like the hadith of Yahya ibn Said concerning raising the hands."
"5099","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini al-Ansari narrated to me, Said ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a donkey while facing Khaybar."
"5100","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the bedouins dominate you over the name of your prayer; they darken over the camels; it is the Isha prayer."
"5101","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash and Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give permission to women at night to go to the mosques. So his son said: We will not give them permission; they will take that as a pretext for wrongdoing. So he said: Do you hear me saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and you yourself say no?"
"5102","Abdulwahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Horses have good tied into their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"5103","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, meaning Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, narrated to us, he said: Abdulaziz, meaning Ibn Abi Rawwad, narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about the night prayer, so he said: The night prayer is two by two; give the salutation of peace in every two rakahs, and when you fear the dawn, then pray one rakah making witr for what came before it."
"5104","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abdulaziz narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The righteous dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"5105","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about the sale of fruits, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of fruits until the blight is gone. I said: And when is that? He said: Until al-Thurayya rises."
"5106","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not find two sandals, let him wear two leather socks, cutting them off until they are below the two ankles."
"5107","He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, meaning: five, there is no sin upon him, while he is in ihram, to kill them: the snake, the scorpion, the mouse, the vicious dog, and the kite."
"5108","And he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Aslam, may Allah grant it safety, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it, and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"5109","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and he pointed with his hand toward the east, and said: Lo, indeed tribulations are from here; indeed tribulations are from here; indeed tribulations are from here, from where the horn of Satan rises."
"5110","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Aishah and Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited by night."
"5111","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed as the time-place of entering ihram for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Sham al-Juhfah. He said: These three I memorized from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I was told that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And for the people of Yemen, Yalamlam. So it was said to him: And Iraq? He said: There was no Iraq that day."
"5112","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Marthad, meaning Ibn Amir al-Hunai, narrated to us, Abu Amr al-Nadabi narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed Allah marvels at prayer in congregation."
"5113","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by food whose owner had beautified it, so he put his hand into it, and behold, it was bad food, so he said: Sell this separately and this separately; so whoever deceives us is not of us."
"5114","Muhammad ibn Yazid, meaning al-Wasiti, narrated to us, Ibn Thawban informed us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Munib al-Jurashi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was sent with the sword until Allah is worshipped, He having no partner, and my provision was placed under the shadow of my spear, and humiliation and abasement were placed upon whoever opposes my command, and whoever imitates a people is of them."
"5115","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Munib al-Jurashi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was sent before the Hour with the sword until Allah alone is worshipped, He having no partner, and my provision was placed under the shadow of my spear, and humiliation and abasement were placed upon whoever opposes my command, and whoever imitates a people is of them."
"5116","Ismail narrated to us, Layth informed us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed two rakahs in the House."
"5117","Ismail narrated to us, Ibn Abi Najih informed us, from his father, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about fasting the Day of Arafah, so he said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Umar and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Uthman and he did not fast it, and I do not fast it, nor do I command it, nor do I forbid it."
"5118","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: It is not the right of a man who spends two nights while he has what he wants to bequeath therein, except that his will is written with him."
"5119","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I consider that he raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you dies, his seat is exposed to him morning and evening; if he is of the people of Paradise, then it is of Paradise, and if he is of the people of the Fire, then it is of the Fire; it is said: This is your seat until you are resurrected to it on the Day of Resurrection."
"5120","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar was summoned urgently over Safiyyah, so he traveled that night a journey of three nights; he traveled until evening came, so I said: The prayer. So he traveled on and did not turn aside. Then he traveled until it grew dark, so Salim, or a man, said to him: The prayer, and evening has come. So he said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when travel pressed him, used to combine these two prayers, and I want to combine them, so travel on. So they traveled until the twilight disappeared, then he alighted and combined them."
"5121","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating, so he said: Do you know Abdullah ibn Umar? I said: Yes. He said: For he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to take her back, then divorce her so that she faces her waiting period."
"5122","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, that he heard Ali al-Azdi narrating that he heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The prayer of the night and the day is two by two. And Shubah used to distinguish it."
"5123","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, from Musab ibn Sad, he said: Ibn Amir fell ill, and they began praising him while Ibn Umar was silent, so he said: Yet I am not the least sincere of them toward you, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils."
"5124","Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, he said: I wrote to Nafi asking him about supplication at the time of fighting, so he wrote to me: That was only at the beginning of Islam; the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raided Banu al-Mustaliq while they were unaware and their cattle were being watered at the water, so he killed their fighters and took their offspring captive, and he captured on that day Juwayriyyah bint al-Harith. Abdullah narrated that to me, and he was in that army."
"5125","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, I heard Qatadah narrating from Bakr ibn Abdullah and Bishr ibn al-Muhtafiz, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said regarding silk: Only one who has no share wears it."
"5126","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, and I heard Abu Mijlaz, I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Witr is one rakah at the end of the night."
"5127","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Mughirah ibn Salman, Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Salman, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he did not leave was two rakahs before Zuhr, and two rakahs after it, and two rakahs after Maghrib, and two rakahs after Isha, and two rakahs before Subh."
"5128","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, I heard Abu Ishaq, and Hajjaj said in his hadith: from Abu Ishaq, I heard Yahya ibn Waththab, that he asked Ibn Umar about washing on Friday, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us with it."
"5129","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Abu Ishaq, I heard a man of the people of Najran, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, I said: I ask you only about two things: about advance payment for date-palms, and about raisins and dates. So he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a man intoxicated who had drunk raisins and dates. He said: So he lashed him the prescribed punishment and forbade that they be mixed. He said: And a man made advance payment to a man for date-palms, but his palms bore no fruit. He said: So he came to him demanding him. He said: But he refused to give him. He said: So they both came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Did your palms bear fruit? He said: No. He said: Then for what do you consume his wealth? He said: So he commanded him and he returned it to him, and he forbade advance payment for date-palms until their soundness appears."
"5130","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every two sellers, there is no sale between them until they separate, except the sale of option."
"5131","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar narrating that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wars and saffron. Shubah said: I said to him, meaning the one in ihram? He said: Yes."
"5132","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five, there is no sin upon one in ihram for killing them: the vicious dog, the crow, the kite, the mouse, and the snake."
"5133","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The keys of the unseen are five, none knows them but Allah: none knows what is in tomorrow but Allah, and none knows the sending down of rain but Allah, and none knows what is in the wombs but Allah, and none knows the Hour but Allah, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die."
"5134","Abdurrahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that fruit be sold until its soundness appears."
"5135","Abdurrahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, I heard Abdurrahman, Ibn Mahdi said: he is Ibn Alqamah, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let the beards grow full and trim the mustaches short."
"5136","Abdurrahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut down the date-palms of Banu al-Nadir and burned."
"5137","Abdurrahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Ishaq, meaning al-Azraq, said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Said ibn Amr, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Indeed we are an unlettered nation; we neither write nor calculate; the month is thus and thus, until he mentioned twenty-nine. Ishaq said: And he clasped his hands three times and withheld his thumb on the third."
"5138","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Alqamah, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded that beards be left full and that mustaches be clipped."
"5139","And Abdullah ibn al-Walid said: Sufyan narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Alqamah narrated to us."
"5140","Abdurrahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about what we act therein: is it in a matter already decided or newly begun? He said: In what has already been decided, so act, O son of al-Khattab, for each is made easy: as for whoever is of the people of felicity, he acts for felicity, and as for whoever is of the people of wretchedness, he acts for wretchedness."
"5141","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, he said: I entered upon Aishah and said: Will you not narrate to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? She said: Yes; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, grew heavy, so he said: Have the people prayed? So we said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put water for me in the washbasin. So we did, and he washed, then he went to rise and fell unconscious, then he recovered and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put water for me in the washbasin. Then he went to rise and was overcome. She said: And the people were staying in the mosque waiting for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the Isha prayer. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to Abu Bakr that he should pray with the people, and Abu Bakr was a tender man, so he said: O Umar, pray with the people. So he said: You are more entitled to that. So Abu Bakr prayed with them those days. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, found some relief, so he came out between two men, one of them al-Abbas, for the Zuhr prayer, and when Abu Bakr saw him he went to step back, so he gestured to him not to step back, and he commanded them both and they seated him at his side. So Abu Bakr prayed standing while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed sitting. Then I entered upon Ibn Abbas and said: Shall I not present to you what Aishah narrated to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Bring it. So I narrated it to him, and he did not deny anything of it, except that he said: Did she name for you the man who was with al-Abbas? I said: No. He said: He is Ali, may Allah have mercy upon him."
"5142","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, I heard Yahya ibn Waththab narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever comes to Friday, let him wash."
"5143","Abdurrahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ata, from Kathir ibn Jumhan, he said: I saw Ibn Umar walking between al-Safa and al-Marwah, so I said: Are you walking? So he said: If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walking, and if I hasten, I have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastening."
"5144","Abdulmalik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: I had a wife whom I loved, and my father disliked her, so he commanded me to divorce her, but I refused. So he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, so he sent to me and said: O Abdullah, divorce your wife. So I divorced her."
"5145","Abdulmalik ibn Amr narrated to us, Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Indeed Allah Most High has placed truth upon the tongue and heart of Umar."
"5146","Abdulmalik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ali, meaning Ibn Mubarak, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Qilabah narrated to me, Salim ibn Abdullah narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: A fire will emerge before the Day of Resurrection from the sea of Hadramawt, or from Hadramawt, gathering the people. They said: So what do you command us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you is Sham."
"5147","Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Anas informed us that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Labbayk with an Umrah and a Hajj. He said: Woe to Anas; he went out and declared the Hajj, and we declared with him, and when he arrived, he commanded whoever did not have the sacrificial animal with him to make it an Umrah. He said: So I mentioned that to Anas, so he said: You count us only as children."
"5148","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Ibn Abi Dhib, they both said: Ibn Shihab informed us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: I saw the people in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, being beaten when they traded food in bulk if they sold it until they sheltered it to their dwellings."
"5149","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and Abdurrahman, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"5150","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever frees a share of his in a slave, all of him is freed; and if the one who freed his share has of wealth what reaches its price, then upon him is freeing all of it."
"5151","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Abdullah, that he called the adhan at Dajanan on a night for Isha, then said after that: Lo, pray in the dwellings. And he informed us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command a caller to prayer to say: Lo, pray in the dwellings, on the cold or rainy night in travel."
"5152","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw sputum in the qibla of the mosque, so he scraped it off, then said: When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit, for Allah Most High is before the face of one of you in prayer."
"5153","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in what is besides it, except the Sacred Mosque."
"5154","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: I caught the talbiyah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Labbayk, O Allah, Labbayk; Labbayk, You have no partner, Labbayk; indeed praise and blessing belong to You, and dominion; You have no partner."
"5155","Yahya narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, I heard Nafi, I heard Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in what is besides it, except the Sacred Mosque."
"5156","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade gourd and pitch-coated vessels."
"5157","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut off for a shield whose price was three dirhams."
"5158","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Every two sellers, each of them has the option against his companion until they separate, or there is an option."
"5159","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the night prayer. He said: One of you prays two by two, and when he fears the morning, he prays one rakah making witr for his prayer."
"5160","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Five of the beasts, there is no sin upon whoever kills them in killing them while he is in ihram: the scorpion, the mouse, the crow, the kite, and the vicious dog."
"5161","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever misses Asr, it is as if his family and wealth were taken away."
"5162","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whatever date-palms are sold with their roots, its fruit belongs to the one who pollinated it, except that the buyer stipulates."
"5163","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, when travel pressed him, he used to combine Maghrib and Isha after the twilight disappeared, and he used to say: Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when travel pressed him, used to combine them."
"5164","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and sought his ruling, so he said: Command Abdullah to take her back until she is pure from this menstruation of hers, then she menstruates another menstruation, and when she is pure, let him separate from her before he has intercourse with her, or let him keep her, for that is the waiting period which women were commanded to be divorced for."
"5165","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, that Abdullah ibn Abdullah and Salim ibn Abdullah spoke to Abdullah when al-Hajjaj came down to fight Ibn al-Zubayr, so they said: It will not harm you not to perform Hajj this year, for we fear there will be fighting among the people and that you will be barred from the House. He said: If I am barred from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did, and I was with him, when the disbelievers of Quraysh barred him from the House. I call you to witness that I have made an Umrah obligatory. So if my way is left free, I will fulfill my Umrah, and if I am barred from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did, and I was with him. Then he went out until he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah and declared an Umrah, then he recited: Certainly for you in the Messenger of Allah is a good example. Then he traveled until when he was at the back of al-Bayda, he said: Their matter is but one; if I am barred from the Umrah, I am barred from the Hajj. I call you to witness that I have made a Hajj obligatory with my Umrah. So he went on until he bought a sacrificial animal at Qudayd, then he performed for them both one circumambulation of the House and of al-Safa and al-Marwah, then he remained so until the Day of Sacrifice."
"5166","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, that a man called to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What clothes do we wear when we enter ihram? He said: Do not wear shirts, nor turbans, nor burnuses, nor trousers, nor leather socks, except one who does not find two sandals. And Yahya said once: Except that there is a man who has no two sandals, so let him cut them below the two ankles. And let him not wear a garment touched by wars or saffron."
"5167","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock: so the ruler over the people is a shepherd over them and he is responsible for them, and the man is a shepherd over the people of his house and he is responsible for them, and the woman is a shepherdess over the house of her husband and his child and she is responsible for them, and the servant of a man is a shepherd over the house of his master and he is responsible for it. Lo, each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock."
"5168","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Those who make these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"5169","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to Friday, let him wash."
"5170","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy, fearing the enemy will attain it."
"5171","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever takes a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats of his deed decrease every day."
"5172","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man called to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: From where do you command us to enter ihram? He said: The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn. Abdullah said: And they claim that he said: And the people of Yemen from Yalamlam."
"5173","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And Sulayman ibn Yasar informed me that Umm Salamah mentioned women, so he said: She lets down a span. She said: Then she will be exposed. He said: Then a cubit; let them not exceed it."
"5174","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, imposed the charity of breaking the fast upon the small and the large, the free and the slave: a sa of dates or barley."
"5175","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Umar ibn Nafi informed me, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza. I said: And what is qaza? He said: That the head of the boy be shaved and part of it left."
"5176","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the House, he and Bilal and Usamah ibn Zayd and Uthman ibn Talhah, and they shut the door and stayed awhile, then he came out. So when it was opened, I was the first to enter, so I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray? So he said: Between the two front pillars. And I forgot to ask him how many he prayed."
"5177","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, that Umar, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, gave a horse as charity, so Umar gave it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to carry a man upon it, then Umar was told that he had stopped it to sell it. He said: So he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, whether to buy it. He said: Do not buy it, and do not return to your charity."
"5178","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr, and with Umar, and with Uthman early in his rule, then he completed."
"5179","Yahya ibn Said and Ismail said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, Yahya said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I acquired land at Khaybar; I never acquired anything at all more precious to me than it. So he said: If you wish, confine its origin and give charity with it. He said: So he gave charity with it; its origin is not sold, nor gifted, nor inherited. He said: So he gave charity with it for the poor, the guest, the necks, in the path of Allah, and the wayfarer; there is no sin upon whoever administers it to eat in a fair manner or feed a friend without amassing wealth therein."
"5180","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us in a detachment; our shares reached twelve camels, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave us extra a camel each."
"5181","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, held a race between trained horses from al-Hafya to Thaniyyat al-Wada, and what was untrained of them from Thaniyyat al-Wada to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."
"5182","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, Yahya ibn Abdurrahman informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The month is twenty-nine. So they mentioned that to Aishah, so she said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abdurrahman; did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, boycott his wives for a month? Then he came down after twenty-nine, so it was said to him, so he said: Indeed the month may be twenty-nine."
"5183","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that a man of the Ansar used to admonish his brother about shyness, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave him, for shyness is of faith."
"5184","Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not trade fruits until their soundness appears."
"5185","Yahya narrated to us, from Isa ibn Hafs, my father narrated to me, that he said: I was with Ibn Umar in travel, so he prayed Zuhr and Asr two rakahs each, then he stood toward a carpet, and he saw people performing supererogatory prayers after it, so he said: What are these doing? I said: They are performing supererogatory prayers. He said: Had I been praying before it or after it, I would have completed it. I accompanied the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until he died, and he did not exceed two, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, until he died, and he did not exceed them, and Umar and Uthman likewise."
"5186","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, combined Maghrib and Isha at Jam with one call to commence, and did not perform supererogatory prayers between them nor after either of them."
"5187","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Tawus, he heard Ibn Umar asked about the nabidh of the jar; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the nabidh of the jar, so he said: Yes. And Tawus said: By Allah, indeed I heard it from him."
"5188","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, I heard Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The example of one who drags his lower garment or his garment, Yahya doubted, out of arrogance: Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5189","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, I heard Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him."
"5190","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, I heard Ibn Umar, he said: Umar asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Ritual impurity befalls me at night. So he commanded him to wash his private part and perform ablution."
"5191","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, and Ibn Jafar said: Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Zadham, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Tell me what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade of vessels, and explain it to us in our language, for we have a language other than yours. He said: He forbade al-hantam, and it is the jar, and he forbade al-muzaffat, and it is the pitched, and he forbade al-dubba, and it is the gourd, and he forbade al-naqir, and it is the palm trunk hollowed out and woven. He said: So in what do you command us to drink? He said: The waterskins. Muhammad said: And he commanded that we make nabidh in waterskins."
"5192","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Ibn Dinar narrated to me, I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: A banner will be set up for the treacherous on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"5193","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Ibn Dinar narrated to me, I heard Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that the one in ihram wear a garment touched by saffron or wars."
"5194","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Wabarah informed me, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: Is it proper for me to circumambulate the House while I am in ihram? He said: What prevents you from that? He said: So-and-so forbids us that until the people return from the standing, and I saw him as if the world inclined him, and you are more pleasing to us than him. Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Hajj, then circumambulated the House and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and the practice of Allah Most High and His Messenger is more worthy to be followed than the practice of the son of so-and-so, if you are truthful."
"5195","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"5196","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He forbade that livestock be milked without the permission of their owners."
"5197","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: It is not the right of a man who has something to bequeath therein that he spends two nights except that his will is written with him."
"5198","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, he said: Cold afflicted Ibn Umar while he was in ihram, so I threw a burnus over Ibn Umar, so he said: Keep it away from me; did you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the burnus for the one in ihram?"
"5199","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to the mosque of Quba riding and walking."
"5200","Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"5201","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said: I will not leave touching them both in hardship nor in ease after I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching them both, the Yemeni Corner and the Stone."
"5202","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out lian between a man and his wife from among the Ansar and separated between them."
"5203","Yahya narrated to us from Ubaydullah, Nafi informed me from Ibn Umar who said: The day of Ashura was a day which the people of Jahiliyyah used to fast, and when Ramadan was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it; he said: It is a day from the days of Allah the Exalted, whoever wishes fasts it and whoever wishes leaves it."
"5204","Rawh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas informed us, Nafi informed me from Abdullah ibn Umar, and he mentioned the like of it."
"5205","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Musab ibn Sad from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted does not accept charity from ghulul nor prayer without purification."
"5206","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Amr ibn Yahya from Said ibn Yasar from Ibn Umar who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a donkey while he was facing toward Khaybar, toward the east."
"5207","And I read it to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Amr ibn Yahya from Abu al-Hubab Said ibn Yasar from Ibn Umar, and he did not say: toward the east."
"5208","Waki narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Umar from Said ibn Yasar who said: Ibn Umar said to me: Do you not have in the Messenger of Allah an example? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr upon his camel."
"5209","And I read it to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab from Said ibn Yasar, and he mentioned the hadith."
"5210","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Yahya ibn Waththab from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."
"5211","Waki narrated to us, Hanzalah al-Jumahi narrated to us from Salim from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your women ask your permission to go to the mosques, then permit them."
"5212","Waki narrated to us, Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajali narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs from Ibn Umar: that he went out on the day of Eid and did not pray before it nor after it, and he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it."
"5213","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from Abu Hanzalah who said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer while traveling, and he said: Two rakahs, the sunnah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5214","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman in the early part of his rule prayed in Mina two rakahs."
"5215","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Mujahid from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in the two rakahs before Fajr and the two rakahs after Maghrib some twenty times or some ten times: Say O you disbelievers and Say He is Allah the One."
"5216","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Umar ibn Muhammad from Nafi: A man asked Ibn Umar about witr, is it obligatory? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr, and the Muslims."
"5217","Waki narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli from Ibn Umar who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about night prayer, and I was between the questioner and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Two by two, and when you fear dawn, then perform witr with one rakah. He said: Then he came at the turn of the year while I was in that same place between him and the questioner, and he asked him, and he said: Two by two, and when you fear dawn, then perform witr with one rakah."
"5218","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Quba, and Abd al-Rahman said: the mosque of Quba, riding and walking."
"5219","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to me from his father from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5220","Waki narrated to us from Ali ibn Salih from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the refuge of the Muslims."
"5221","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Jews meet you they say: al-sam upon you, so say: and upon you."
"5222","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Sad ibn Ubaydah who said: I was with Ibn Umar in a circle, and he heard a man in another circle saying: No, by my father, so Ibn Umar pelted him with pebbles and said: It used to be the oath of Umar, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him from it and said: It is shirk."
"5223","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Najrani from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drunk man, so he administered the hadd punishment to him, then said: What is your drink? He said: Raisins and dates. He said: Do not mix them both together; each one of them suffices without the other."
"5224","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Muharib ibn Dithar who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-dubba and al-hantam and al-muzaffat. Shubah said: And I think he said: and al-naqir."
"5225","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not enter upon these punished people, the companions of al-Hijr, except that you be weeping; and if you are not weeping, then do not enter upon them, lest there befall you what befell them."
"5226","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The keys of the unseen are five, none knows them except Allah: Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down rain, and He knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"5227","Waki narrated to us from Fudayl, and Yazid said: Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us from Atiyyah al-Awfi who said: I read to Ibn Umar: Who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness, and he said: Allah who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness, then he said: I read to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you read to me, and he corrected me as I corrected you."
"5228","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freed slave of the family of Talhah, from Salim ibn Abdullah from Ibn Umar: that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Command him to take her back, then let him divorce her while she is pure or pregnant."
"5229","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan informed us from Asim ibn Ubaydullah from Salim from Ibn Umar: that Umar asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Umrah, and he permitted him and said: O my brother, include us in your righteous supplication and do not forget us. Abd al-Razzaq said in his hadith: Umar said: I would not love to have in exchange for it all upon which the sun has risen."
"5230","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah by day."
"5231","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter through the upper pass and exit through the lower."
"5232","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Zayd ibn Aslam, he heard it from Ibn Umar who said: Two men came from the east and spoke, or one of them spoke, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed among eloquence is magic, or: indeed eloquence is magic."
"5233","Waki narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in their graves, then say: In the name of Allah and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5234","Waki narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The son of Adam is shown his seat from Paradise and Hell morning and evening in his grave."
"5235","Waki narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."
"5236","Waki narrated to us from Israil from Abu Ishaq from al-Najrani from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: that two men traded at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) date-palms before the fruit appeared, and it produced nothing, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For what do you consume his wealth? And he forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"5237","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When you buy gold with silver, or one of them with the other, let him not leave you while there is still any confusion between you and him."
"5238","Waki narrated to us from al-Umari from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that he ran from the Stone to the Stone three times and walked four times, and prayed at the Maqam two rakahs, then he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it."
"5239","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said: I have not left touching the two corners in hardship nor in ease since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching them both, the Stone and the Yemeni Corner."
"5240","Waki narrated to us, Said ibn al-Saib narrated to us from Dawud ibn Abi Asim who said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer in Mina. He said: Have you heard of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes, and I have believed in him. He said: He used to pray in Mina two rakahs."
"5241","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Hakam and Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar: that he prayed them both with one iqamah, and he said: Thus the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did with us in this place."
"5242","Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Farqad al-Sabakhi from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to oil himself with non-perfumed oil at ihram."
"5243","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, and from al-Zuhri from Salim from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The muhrim shall not wear a garment touched by wars nor saffron."
"5244","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the muhrim to wear a garment touched by wars or saffron."
"5245","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Jubayr: that a man asked Ibn Umar about a man who vowed to fast a day, and it coincided with the day of Adha Eid or the day of Fitr; Ibn Umar said: Allah commanded fulfillment of vows, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from fasting this day."
"5246","Waki narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym from Ibn Umar who said, Abd al-Rahman said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to join between two dates together until he asks permission of his companions."
"5247","Waki narrated to us from al-Amash from al-Minhal, and he is Ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar: that he passed by people who had set up a chicken shooting at it with arrows, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilating animals."
"5248","Waki narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us from Salim from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5249","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Yazid said: Sufyan informed us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold, so the people took their rings of gold, then he threw it away and said: I will never wear it again. Yazid said: So the people discarded their rings."
"5250","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, and Sufyan from Umar ibn Muhammad from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He used to place the stone of his ring toward the inside of his palm."
"5251","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us from Said al-Maqburi and Nafi: that Ibn Umar used to wear sibtiyyah sandals and perform wudu in them, and he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"5252","Waki narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his father from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in solitude, no rider would ever travel by night."
"5253","Waki narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us from Salim from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his deed every day."
"5254","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or livestock, two qirats are deducted from his deed every day. Abd al-Rahman said: Deducted from his deed."
"5255","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar, and al-Umari from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the dabb, and he said: I do not eat it nor do I forbid it."
"5256","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Sad ibn Ubaydah who said: I was with Ibn Umar in a circle; he said: He heard a man in another circle saying: No, by my father, so Ibn Umar pelted him with pebbles and said: It used to be the oath of Umar, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him from it and said: It is shirk."
"5257","Waki narrated to us from his father from Ata ibn al-Saib from Kathir ibn Jumhan from Ibn Umar who said: If I run, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running, and if I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking, and I am an old man."
"5258","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When you are three, two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of one."
"5259","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever man says to his brother: O disbeliever, then one of them has incurred it."
"5260","Waki narrated to us from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whichever man declares a man a disbeliever, then one of them is a disbeliever."
"5261","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman from Shubah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam, may Allah grant it peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it, and Usayyah, it disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"5262","Waki narrated to us from Said ibn Ubayd from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is wailed over, he is punished for what is wailed over him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5263","Waki narrated to us from al-Umari from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not accept the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"5264","Waki narrated to us from Hammad from Bishr ibn Harb: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Your raising your hands is an innovation; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go beyond this, meaning up to the chest."
"5265","Waki narrated to us from his father from Ata from Kathir ibn Jumhan who said: I saw Ibn Umar walking in the valley between al-Safa and al-Marwah and not running, so I said to him, and he said: If I run, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running, and if I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking, and I am an old man."
"5266","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Firas from Abu Salih from Zadham: that Ibn Umar freed a slave of his and said: I have no reward from it, and he picked up something from the ground weighing this or like this; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever slaps his boy or beats him, its expiation is freeing him."
"5267","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Firas, Abu Salih informed me from Zadham who said: I was with Ibn Umar, and he called a boy of his and freed him, then said: I have no reward in it worth this or weighing this; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever beats a slave of his for a prescribed punishment he did not incur, or wrongs him, or slaps him, Abd al-Rahman doubted, then its expiation is to free him."
"5268","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Bahz narrated to us, both said: Shubah narrated to us from Anas ibn Sirin who said, Bahz said in his hadith: Anas ibn Sirin informed me: I heard Ibn Umar saying: He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Command him to take her back, and when she becomes pure, then let him divorce her. Bahz said: Is it counted?"
"5269","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayman asking Ibn Umar, while Abu al-Zubayr was listening, and Ibn Umar said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: O Prophet, when you divorce women, then divorce them at the beginning of their waiting period."
"5270","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Salim from his father: that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and he mentioned that to Umar, so Umar went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him keep her until she menstruates other than this menstruation, then becomes pure; if it appears good to him to divorce her, let him divorce her as Allah the Mighty and Majestic commanded him, and if it appears good to him to keep her, let him keep her."
"5271","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am deceived in selling, so he said: When you sell, say: No deceit."
"5272","Rawh narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us: I heard Salim, and he was asked about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and he said: It is not permitted; Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take her back, and he took her back."
"5273","Rawh narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us: I heard Tawus who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and said: Do not sell fruit until its soundness appears."
"5274","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What tree does its leaves not fall and it is like the believer, or he said: the Muslim? He said: The people fell into the trees of the deserts. Ibn Umar said: And it occurred to me that it is the date-palm, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the date-palm. He said: I mentioned that to Umar, and he said: If you had said it, it would have been more beloved to me than such and such."
"5275","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Abdullah ibn Murrah from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vows and said: It does not repel anything from the decree, but it is only extracted thereby from the miser."
"5276","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abd al-Karim from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman at al-Balat."
"5277","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Alqamah from Razin al-Ahmari from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who divorced his wife three times, then a man married her and closed the door and let down the curtain and removed the veil, then divorced her before consummating with her, is she lawful for her first husband? He said: No, until he tastes her little honey."
"5278","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad from Sulayman ibn Razin from Ibn Umar who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon the minbar addressing the people about a man who separated from his wife by three divorces, and he mentioned its meaning."
"5279","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Salim from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands when he began prayer, and when he wanted to bow, and when he raised his head from bowing, and he did not do that in prostration."
"5280","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the dabb, and he said: I am not eating it nor forbidding it."
"5281","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar who said: I was with Ibn Umar, I and another man, and he called another man, then said: Wait both of you, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two to converse privately to the exclusion of one."
"5282","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Shubah from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: When we pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon hearing, he would dictate to us, or prompt us: as much as you are able."
"5283","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Laylat al-Qadr, and he said: Seek it in the last seven."
"5284","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said: We used to avoid much speech and expansiveness toward our wives in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fearing that Quran would be revealed concerning us, but when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, we spoke."
"5285","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"5286","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned in the spoils for the horse two shares and for the man one share."
"5287","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from al-Zuhri from Salim from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Maghrib and Isha in Muzdalifah together."
"5288","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment toward Najd, and they gained many camels as spoils, and their shares reached eleven camels or twelve camels, and they were given an extra camel each."
"5289","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. Malik said: Shighar is that one says: Marry me your daughter and I will marry you my daughter."
"5290","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from al-Hakam and Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Said ibn Jubayr: that he prayed Maghrib at Jam and Isha with an iqamah, then he narrated from Ibn Umar that he did the like of that, and Ibn Umar narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did the like of that."
"5291","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn Umar who said: Two men came from the east and addressed, and the people were amazed at their eloquence, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some eloquence is magic, or: indeed among eloquence is magic."
"5292","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears; he forbade the seller and the buyer."
"5293","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy, fearing that the enemy may get hold of it."
"5294","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not break fast until you see it; and if it is obscured for you, then estimate for it."
"5295","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he returned from Hajj or Umrah or a military expedition, would say takbir upon every elevated ground three times, then say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable; returning, repenting, prostrating, worshipping, to our Lord praising; Allah has fulfilled His promise and aided His servant and defeated the confederates alone."
"5296","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray before Zuhr two rakahs and after it two rakahs, and after Maghrib two rakahs in his house, and after Isha two rakahs, and after Friday two rakahs in his house."
"5297","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabanah; and muzabanah is buying fruit with dates by measure, and grapes with raisins by measure."
"5298","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar: He went out during the fitnah of Ibn al-Zubayr and said: If we are prevented from the House, we will do as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did."
"5299","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Command him to take her back, then keep her until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure, then if he wishes he may divorce her and if he wishes he may keep her; that is the waiting period which Allah commanded that women be divorced for."
"5300","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"5301","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Let none of you deliberately seek a time and pray before the rising of the sun nor at its setting I said to Malik From Abdullah He said Yes"
"5302","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him when it was a night of wind and cold on a journey would order the muadhdhin who would call the adhan then say Prayer in the lodgings"
"5303","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him obligated the charity of al-Fitr a sa of dates or a sa of barley for every male and female and free and slave among the Muslims"
"5304","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade meeting the goods until they are brought down to the markets and forbade najsh and said Let none of you sell over the sale of another"
"5305","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him when travel hastened him would join Maghrib and Isha"
"5306","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said Whoever sells date palms that have been pollinated then their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise"
"5307","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade the sale of habal al-habala"
"5308","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him concerning what the muhrim wears of clothes who said Do not wear shirts nor turbans nor burnuses nor trousers nor leather socks except one who does not find sandals then let him cut them below the ankles and do not wear of clothes what has been touched by wars or saffron"
"5309","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said Whoever buys food let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it"
"5310","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him that he cut off for a shield worth three dirhams"
"5311","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said When one of you comes to al-Jumua let him wash"
"5312","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that a man invoked lian against his wife and disavowed her child so the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him separated between them and attributed the child to his mother"
"5313","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik he said My father and Haddathani Hammad al-Khayyat Haddathana Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said The one who misses the Asr prayer it is as if his family and his wealth have been taken away"
"5314","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik ibn Anas from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab mentioned to the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him that janaba befalls him at night so the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said to him Perform wudu and wash your private part then sleep"
"5315","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said The likeness of the companion of the Quran is like the likeness of the owner of hobbled camels if he watches over them he holds them and if he releases them they go away"
"5316","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Bilal calls at night so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls"
"5317","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad Haddathana Israil from Thuwayr from Ibn Umar raising it to the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is he who looks at his gardens and his bliss and his servants and his couches from the distance of a thousand years and the most honored of them to Allah is he who looks at His Face morning and evening then he recited this verse Faces on that day radiant looking at their Lord"
"5318","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd from Ayyub from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them both raising the hadith concerning His Exalted saying The day mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds who said They will stand on the Day of Resurrection in sweat up to the halves of their ears"
"5319","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi from Ayyub from Nafi that Ibn Umar used to lease his land at the time of Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and part of the rule of Muawiya he said If I wished I would say at the time of the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him until when it was at the end of the rule of Muawiya there reached him a hadith from Rafi ibn Khadij so he went and I was with him and asked him about it and he said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade the leasing of farms so he stopped leasing it and when he was asked after that he would say Ibn Khadij claimed that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade the leasing of farms"
"5320","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade muzabana he said Nafi used to explain it The fruit bought by its estimate dates for a named measure if it increases it is for me and if it decreases it is against me"
"5321","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid from Ayyub from Nafi that Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating so Umar asked the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and he ordered him to take her back then leave her until she menstruates another menstruation then leave her until she becomes pure then divorce her before touching her for that is the waiting period for which Allah ordered women to be divorced and Ibn Umar when asked about a man divorcing his wife while menstruating would say Either you divorced her once or twice for the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him ordered him to take her back then leave her until she menstruates another menstruation then leave her until she becomes pure then divorce her if he does not wish to keep her or else you divorced her three times for you have disobeyed Allah the Exalted in what He ordered you concerning the divorce of your wife and she is separated from you and you are separated from her"
"5322","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar that he would never leave Hajj and Umra and that Abdullah ibn Abdullah came to him and said I do not feel safe that this year there will be fighting among the people so if you stayed back He said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him performed Hajj and the disbelievers of Quraysh blocked him from the House so if I am blocked from it I will do as the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him did Allah the Blessed and Exalted said You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example then he said I make you witnesses that I have obligated an Umra then he traveled until when he was at al-Bayda he said By Allah I do not see the way of them both except one I make you witnesses that I have obligated a Hajj with my Umra then he performed one tawaf"
"5323","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said A man said O Messenger of Allah from where do you order us to enter ihram He said The people of al-Madina enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfa and the people of al-Sham from al-Juhfa and the people of Najd from Qarn he said And they say And the people of Yemen from Yalamlam"
"5324","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said A man called out to the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and said What of animals do we kill when we are in ihram He said Five there is no sin on whoever kills them in killing them The kite and the crow and the mouse and the vicious dog and the scorpion"
"5325","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said A man said O Messenger of Allah what of clothes do we wear when we enter ihram He said Do not wear the shirt nor trousers nor the turban nor the leather socks except one who does not find sandals then let him wear them below the ankles nor the burnus nor anything of clothes touched by wars or saffron"
"5326","Haddathana Ubayda ibn Humayd Haddathani Thuwayr from Mujahid from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Take from this and leave this meaning his upper mustache he takes from it meaning the tuft on the lower lip"
"5327","Haddathana Asbat ibn Muhammad Haddathana Abd al-Malik from Muslim ibn Yannaq who said I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar in the gathering of Banu Abdullah and a youth from Quraysh passed trailing his izar so Abdullah ibn Umar called him and said From whom are you He said From Banu Bakr He said Would you love that Allah the Exalted look at you on the Day of Resurrection He said Yes He said Lift your izar for I heard Aba al-Qasim peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and he gestured with his finger to his ears say Whoever drags his izar intending nothing but pride Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection"
"5328","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir Haddathana Israil from Thuwayr from Mujahid from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him cursed the effeminate among men and the masculine among women"
"5329","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and in the copy which I read to Abd al-Rahman it was Nafi so he corrected it and said Abdullah ibn Dinar used to come to Quba riding and walking"
"5330","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa Akhbarana Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to come to Quba riding and walking"
"5331","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik he said My father and Haddathana Ishaq Akhbarani Malik from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam from Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muawi that he said Abdullah ibn Umar saw me playing with pebbles in prayer and when he finished he forbade me and said Do as the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to do I said And how did the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him do He said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him when he sat in prayer would place his right palm on his right thigh and close all his fingers and point with the finger next to the thumb and place his left palm on his left thigh"
"5332","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said The congregational prayer exceeds the solitary prayer by twenty seven degrees"
"5333","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman Haddathana Malik from al-Zuhri from a man of the family of Khalid ibn Asid who said I said to Ibn Umar We find the fear prayer in the Quran and the settled prayer and we do not find the travel prayer He said Allah the Exalted sent Muhammad peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and we knew nothing so we only do as we saw Muhammad peace and blessings of Allah be upon him do"
"5334","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik and Haddathana Ishaq Akhbarana Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that he said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to pray on his mount while traveling wherever it turned with him"
"5335","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik and Haddathana Ishaq who said Akhbarana Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him saw spit on the wall of the qibla and scraped it then turned to the people and said When one of you prays let him not spit before his face for Allah the Mighty and Majestic is before his face when he prays Ishaq said in his hadith Spit"
"5336","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade that the muhrim wear a garment dyed with saffron or wars and said Whoever does not find sandals let him wear leather socks and cut them below the ankles"
"5337","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik and Haddathana Rawh Haddathana Malik from Musa ibn Uqba from Salim from his father that he said This Bayda of yours about which you lie about the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him did not enter ihram except from beside the mosque meaning the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfa Abd al-Rahman said I heard it from Malik"
"5338","He said I read to Abd al-Rahman Malik who said Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq Haddathana Malik from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Ubayd ibn Jurayj that he said to Abdullah ibn Umar O Aba Abd al-Rahman I saw you do four things I did not see any of your companions do them He said What are they O Ibn Jurayj He said I saw you touch none of the corners except the Yamani ones and I saw you wear hairless sandals and I saw you dye with yellow and I saw you when in Makka people enter ihram when they see the crescent and you do not enter ihram until the day of al-Tarwiya Abdullah said As for the corners I did not see the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him touch except the Yamani ones and as for the hairless sandals I saw the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him wear the sandals in which there is no hair and perform wudu in them so I love to wear them and as for the yellow dye I saw the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him dye with it so I love to dye with it and as for the ihram I did not see the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him enter ihram until his she camel set out with him"
"5339","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi Haddathana Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi from Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him obligated Zakat al-Fitr of Ramadan a sa of dates or a sa of barley upon every free or slave male or female among the Muslims"
"5340","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq Akhbarana Abdullah Akhbarana Yunus from al-Zuhri Akhbarani Salim that Ibn Umar narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said While a man was dragging his izar out of pride he was swallowed by the earth and he is sinking in the earth until the Day of Resurrection"
"5341","Haddathana Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri Haddathana Abd al-Aziz meaning Ibn Abi Rawwad from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said A man came to the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and asked him about the night prayer He said The night prayer is two by two you give salam in every two rakas and when you fear dawn then pray one raka making witr for what came before it"
"5342","Haddathana Yamur ibn Bishr Akhbarana Abdullah Akhbarana Mamar from al-Zuhri Akhbarani Salim ibn Abdullah from his father that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him when he passed by al-Hijr said Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged except weeping lest what befell them befall you and he covered himself with his cloak while on the mount"
"5343","Haddathana Harun ibn Maruf Haddathana Ibn Wahb and he said once Haywa from Ibn al-Had from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said O company of women give charity and increase for I saw you are most of the people of the Fire due to much cursing and ingratitude to the husband I have not seen among those deficient in intellect and religion more overpowering to a resolute man than you She said O Messenger of Allah and what is the deficiency of intellect and religion He said As for the deficiency of intellect and religion the testimony of two women equals the testimony of one man so this is the deficiency of intellect and she stays nights without praying and breaks fast in Ramadan so this is the deficiency of religion"
"5344","Haddathana Attab Haddathana Abdullah Akhbarana Musa ibn Uqba from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said The upper hand is better than the lower hand the upper hand is the spending one and the lower hand is the begging one"
"5345","Haddathana Attab Haddathana Abdullah Akhbarana Usama ibn Zayd from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him ordered Zakat al-Fitr to be given before the people go out to prayer"
"5346","Haddathana Attab Haddathana Abdullah Akhbarana Musa ibn Uqba from Salim from Abdullah ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Whoever swears by other than Allah and he said about it a stern saying"
"5347","He said And Akhbarana Salim from Abdullah ibn Umar who said Most of what the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him would swear with this oath saying No by the Turner of hearts"
"5348","Haddathana Attab Akhbarana Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him held a race with horses and staked a wager"
"5349","Haddathana Attab Haddathana Abu Hamza meaning al-Sukkari from Ibn Abi Layla from Sadaqa al-Makki from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him observed itikaf in the last ten of Ramadan and a house of palm leaves was made for him in it he said One day he put out his head and said The worshipper converses with his Lord the Mighty and Majestic so let each of you look at what he converses with his Lord and let none of you raise his voice over another in recitation"
"5350","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Harrani Akhbarana al-Darawardi from Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Whoever joins his Hajj and his Umra then one tawaf suffices him for both"
"5351","Haddathana Attab Haddathana Abdullah meaning Ibn al-Mubarak Akhbarana Musa ibn Uqba from Salim ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Whoever drags his garment out of pride Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection Abu Bakr said One side of my garment loosens unless I attend to it The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said You are not among those who do that out of pride Musa said I said to Salim Did Abdullah mention whoever drags his izar He said I did not hear him mention except his garment"
"5352","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq Akhbarana Abdullah Akhbarana Musa ibn Uqba and he mentioned the like of it with its isnad"
"5353","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salama from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Talha from Salim from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said The Dajjal will descend in this salt flat at Marr Qanat and most of those who go out to him will be women until a man returns to his relative and to his mother and his daughter and his sister and his paternal aunt and ties her with bonds fearing she will go out to him then Allah will give the Muslims power over him and they will kill him and kill his party until the Jew hides under the tree or the stone and the stone or the tree says to the Muslim This is a Jew under me so kill him"
"5354","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik Akhbarana Zuhayr Haddathana Abu Ishaq from Mujahid from Ibn Umar who said I was sitting with the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and I heard him seek forgiveness a hundred times then say O Allah forgive me and have mercy on me and turn to me You are the Oft Returning the Merciful or You are Oft Returning Forgiving"
"5355","Haddathana Ali ibn Hafs Akhbarana Warqa who said And Ata said from Muharib ibn Dithar from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said to us Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise its banks of gold and water flows over pearls and its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey"
"5356","Haddathana Ali ibn Hafs Akhbarana Warqa from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade qaza in the head"
"5357","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud Haddathana Ibn Lahia from Khalid ibn Abi Imran from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to say The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim he does not wrong him nor abandon him and say By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad no two who love each other then become separated except by a sin one of them commits and he used to say For a Muslim upon his brother are six acts of kindness he invokes mercy on him when he sneezes and visits him when sick and advises him when absent and attends him and greets him when he meets him and answers him when he invites him and follows him when he dies and he forbade the forsaking of a Muslim of his brother for more than three"
"5358","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud Haddathana Abdullah ibn Umar from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque"
"5359","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid Haddathana al-Hudhayl ibn Bilal from Ibn Ubayd from his father that he sat one day in Makka with Abdullah ibn Umar with him and my father said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said The likeness of the hypocrite on the Day of Resurrection is like a sheep between two resting places of sheep if she comes to these they butt her and if she comes to these they butt her Ibn Umar said to him You have lied and the people praised my father with good or kindness Ibn Umar said I do not think your companion except as you say but I witnessed the Prophet of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him when he said Like a sheep between two flocks of sheep He said It is the same He said Thus I heard it"
"5360","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Aban ibn Yazid Haddathana Qatada Haddathani Abdullah ibn Babay al-Makki who said I prayed beside Abdullah ibn Umar and when he finished the prayer he struck with his hand on my thigh and said Shall I not teach you the greeting of prayer as the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to teach us Then he recited to me these words meaning the saying of Abu Musa al-Ashari in the tashahhud"
"5361","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Hammad meaning Ibn Salama who said Akhbarana Thabit from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said to a man Did you do such and such He said No by Him besides Whom there is no god I did not do He said Jibril peace be upon him said to him He did but he has been forgiven by saying there is no god but Allah Hammad said He did not hear this from Ibn Umar between them is a man meaning Thabit"
"5362","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Wuhayb Haddathana Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said When a man swears and says If Allah wills then he has the choice if he wishes let him proceed and if he wishes let him leave"
"5363","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Hammad ibn Salama and Abd al-Warith from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him the like of it"
"5364","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Hammam Haddathana Qatada Haddathani Bakr ibn Abdullah and Bishr ibn Aidh al-Hudhali both from Abdullah ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said Only one who has no share wears silk"
"5365","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Abu Awana Haddathana Sulayman al-Amash from Mujahid from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said Whoever seeks refuge in Allah then grant him refuge and whoever asks you by Allah then give him and whoever invites you then answer him and whoever does kindness to you then reward him and if you do not find what to reward him then supplicate for him until you know you have rewarded him"
"5366","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Abu Awana from Abu Bishr from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said The Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him had a ring of gold and would place its stone inside his palm he said One day he threw it away and the people threw their rings then he took a ring of silver and would seal with it and not wear it"
"5367","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said Answer the invitation when you are invited"
"5368","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Wuhayb Haddathana Musa ibn Uqba Haddathani Salim that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say The oath of the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him by which he would swear was No by the Turner of hearts"
"5369","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Wuhayb Haddathana Musa ibn Uqba Akhbarani Salim that he heard Abdullah narrate from the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him that he met Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl at the lower part of Baldah and that was before revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him offered him a travel meal in which was meat but he refused to eat from it then he said I do not eat what you slaughter upon your altars and I eat only what the name of Allah has been mentioned over Abdullah ibn Umar narrated this from the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"
"5370","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Hammam Haddathana Qatada from Abi al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar Hammam said In my book The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said When you place your dead in the grave then say In the name of Allah and upon the sunna of the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"
"5371","Haddathana Affan Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Harithi Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani from his father from Abdullah ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said When you meet the pilgrim then greet him and shake his hand and order him to seek forgiveness for you before he enters his house for he is forgiven"
"5372","Haddathana Yaqub Haddathana Abi from al-Walid ibn Kathir from Qatan ibn Wahb ibn Uwaymir ibn al-Ajda from one who narrated to him from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar that he heard him say Haddathani Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Three Allah has forbidden Paradise to them The persistent wine drinker and the disobedient to parents and the dayyuth who approves filth in his family"
"5373","Haddathana Yaqub I heard Abi narrate from Yazid meaning Ibn al-Had from Umar ibn Abdullah that he narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Umar met people coming out from Marwan and said From where have these come They said We came out from the Amir Marwan He said Every truth you saw did you speak it and help it and every evil you saw did you deny it and turn it back upon him They said No by Allah he says what is denied and we say You are right may Allah set you right and when we leave him we say May Allah fight him how unjust and wicked he is Abdullah said In the time of the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him we used to count this as hypocrisy for whoever was like this"
"5374","Haddathana Yaqub Haddathana Abi from Ibn Ishaq Haddathani Nafi the freedman of Abdullah ibn Umar from Abdullah ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him gave Umar ibn al-Khattab a slave girl from the captives of Hawazin and he gave her to me and I sent her to my maternal uncles of Banu Jumah to prepare her for me until I circumambulate the House then come to them and I intended to have her when I returned to her he said I went out of the mosque when I finished and the people were rushing I said What is the matter with you They said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him has returned to us our sons and our women he said That companion of yours is among Banu Jumah so go and take her and they went and took her"
"5375","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad Haddathana Shayban from Mansur from Sad ibn Ubayda who said I sat I and Muhammad al-Kindi with Abdullah ibn Umar then I got up from him and sat with Said ibn al-Musayyab he said My companion came with his face yellow and his color changed and said Stand to me I said Was I not sitting with you just now Said said Stand to your companion he said I stood to him and he said Did you not hear what Ibn Umar said I said And what did he say He said A man came to him and said O Aba Abd al-Rahman is there sin on me to swear by the Kaba He said Why do you swear by the Kaba when you swear by the Kaba then swear by the Lord of the Kaba for Umar when he swore would say No by my father and he swore by it one day with the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Do not swear by your father nor by other than Allah for whoever swears by other than Allah has associated"
"5376","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad who said Haddathana Shayban from Yahya from Abi Qilaba from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said A fire will come out of Hadramawt or from the sea of Hadramawt before the Day of Resurrection gathering the people he said We said O Messenger of Allah what do you order us He said Upon you is al-Sham"
"5377","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa Haddathana Shayban from Yahya from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman meaning Ibn Thawban the freedman of Banu Zuhra that he heard Ibn Umar say The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Allah does not look at one who drags his izar out of pride"
"5378","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd from Bishr ibn Harb I heard Ibn Umar say I heard the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him at the chamber of Aisha say A banner will be set up for every treacherous one on the Day of Resurrection and there is no treachery greater than the treachery of a leader of the people"
"5379","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa Haddathana Hammad ibn Salama from Ata ibn al-Saib from Abi Yahya from Ibn Abbas that two men disputed to the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him asked the claimant for proof and he had no proof so he asked the defendant to swear and he swore by Allah besides Whom there is no god The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said You did it but you are forgiven by your sincerity in saying there is no god but Allah"
"5380","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Hammad ibn Salama from Thabit al-Bunani from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him the like of it except that he said Jibril peace and blessings of Allah be upon him told me you did it but Allah forgave you"
"5381","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Zuhayr from Bayan from Wabara from Said ibn Jubayr who said Abdullah ibn Umar came out to us and we were hoping he would narrate to us a hadith or a good hadith and a man among us called al-Hakam hastened to him and said O Aba Abd al-Rahman what do you say about fighting in fitna He said May your mother be bereaved of you do you know what fitna is Muhammad peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to fight the polytheists and entering among them or in their religion was fitna and it is not like your fighting over kingship"
"5382","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Zuhayr from Abi Ishaq from al-Bahiyy from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said to Aisha Hand me the mat from the mosque She said I have become ritually impure He said Is your menstruation in your hand"
"5383","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Zuhayr from Abi Ishaq from Mujahid from Ibn Umar who said He was asked How many times did the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him perform Umra He said Twice and Aisha said Ibn Umar knew that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him performed three besides the Umra which he joined with the Farewell Hajj"
"5384","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Zuhayr Haddathana Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Abdullah ibn Umar who said I was in a detachment of the detachments of the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and the people veered away and I was among those who veered and we said How do we do we have fled from battle and incurred anger then we said If we entered al-Madina and stayed overnight then we said If we presented ourselves to the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him if there is repentance for him otherwise we go away So we came to him before the dawn prayer and he came out and said Who are the people he said We said We are the fleers He said No rather you are the returners to fight I am your support and I am the support of the Muslims he said We came to him until we kissed his hand"
"5385","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa who said Haddathana Zuhayr Haddathana Umara ibn Ghaziyya from Yahya ibn Rashid who said We went out as pilgrims ten of the people of al-Sham until we came to Makka and he mentioned the hadith he said We came to him and he came out to us meaning Ibn Umar and said I heard the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him say Whose intercession blocks a hadd from the hudud of Allah the Mighty and Majestic has opposed Allah in His command and whoever dies with a debt upon him it is not by dinar nor dirham but by good deeds and evil deeds and whoever disputes in falsehood knowingly remains in the anger of Allah until he desists and whoever says about a believer what is not in him Allah will house him in Radghat al-Khabal until he exits from what he said"
"5386","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah meaning Ibn Dinar from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said Whoever withdraws a hand from obedience has no proof on the Day of Resurrection and whoever dies separating from the community has died a death of ignorance"
"5387","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn Umar from the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him who said People are like a hundred camels you hardly find among them a riding camel"
"5388","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Hammad ibn Salama from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him recited this verse The day mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds He said They will stand until sweat reaches their ears"
"5389","Haddathana Sakan ibn Nafi al-Bahili Abu al-Hasan Haddathana Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar from al-Zuhri from Salim ibn Abdullah from his father who said I was an unmarried young man sleeping in the mosque at the time of the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and dogs used to come and go in the mosque and they would not sprinkle anything of that"
"5390","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Ibn Lahia Haddathana Abu Tumah Ibn Lahia said I do not know what his name is who said I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him went out to al-Mirbad and I went out with him and I was on his right and Abu Bakr came and I stepped back for him and he was on his right and I was on his left then Umar came and I moved aside for him and he was on his left and the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him came to al-Mirbad and there were skins on al-Mirbad with wine in them Ibn Umar said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him called me for the knife and I did not know the knife except that day and he ordered the skins and they were cut open then he said Cursed is wine and its drinker and its pourer and its seller and its buyer and its carrier and the one carried to and its presser and the one pressed for and the eater of its price"
"5391","Haddathana Waki Haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar meaning Ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Tumah their freedman and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Ghafiqi that they heard Ibn Umar say The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Cursed is wine in ten aspects and he mentioned the hadith"
"5392","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Ibn Lahia Haddathana Abu Tumah that he said I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said O Aba Abd al-Rahman I am strong for fasting while traveling Ibn Umar said I heard the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him say Whoever does not accept the concession of Allah upon him is of sin like the mountains of Arafa"
"5393","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Ibn Lahia Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr I asked Jabir about keeping a dog He said Ibn Umar told me that he heard the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him say Whoever keeps it two qirats are deducted from his reward every day"
"5394","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Ibn Lahia Haddathana Jafar ibn Rabia from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi al-Hadrami who said I saw Ibn Umar in the prayer place on al-Fitr with a son of his beside him and he said to his son Do you know how the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to do on this day He said I do not know Ibn Umar said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him used to pray before the sermon"
"5395","Haddathana Surayj ibn al-Numan Haddathana Hushaym Akhbarana Yunus ibn Ubayd from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said The delay of the rich is injustice and when you are referred to a solvent one then follow him and no two sales in one"
"5396","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Ibn Lahia Haddathana Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar who said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him said Do not let fire spend the night in your houses for it is an enemy"
"5397","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Ibn Lahia Haddathana Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar from Nafi from Ibn Umar who said I saw the spoils divided into five parts then lots cast over them and what belonged to the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him is his he chooses"
"5398","Haddathana Hasan Haddathana Ibn Lahia Haddathana Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar from Zayd ibn Aslam who said I heard a man ask Abdullah ibn Umar about the sale of outbidding Ibn Umar said The Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him forbade that one of you sell over the sale of his brother except spoils and inheritances"
"5399","Haddathana Abu Said the freedman of Banu Hashim Haddathana Layth Haddathana Asim from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq who said I asked Ibn Umar about the night prayer Ibn Umar said A man asked the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him about the night prayer and I was between them and he said The night prayer is two by two and when you fear dawn then hasten dawn with one raka and two rakas before the dawn prayer"
"5400","Haddathana Abu Salama al-Khuzai Akhbarana Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah peace and blessings of Allah be upon him invoked lian between a man and his wife and attributed the child to his mother and he had disavowed her child"
"5401","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ramal from the Stone to the Stone."
"5402","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn al-Andarawardi, the freedman of Banu Layth, informed us, from Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi Hasan al-Ansari then al-Muharibi, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, who said: I said to Ibn Umar, Inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, how was it. He said: Then he mentioned the takbir each time he laid his head down and each time he raised it, and he mentioned: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, to his right; Peace be upon you, to his left."
"5403","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Ibn Bilal, meaning Sulayman, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to Quba riding and walking."
"5404","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, Ibn Bilal informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping; if you are not weeping then do not enter upon them, lest there befall you the like of what befell them."
"5405","Abu Salamah informed us, Sulayman ibn Bilal informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: A man who is deceived in buying was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to him: To whomever you transact, say: No deception. And he used to say when he transacted: No deception, and there was a lisp in his tongue."
"5406","Abu Salamah informed us, Sulayman informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray on his mount while traveling wherever it turned with him, and he mentioned that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do that while traveling."
"5407","Abu Salamah informed us, Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wear a ring of gold, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and cast it away and said: I will never wear it again. He said: So the people cast away their rings."
"5408","Abu Salamah informed us, Layth informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque while he was praying before the people, so he scraped it off, then said when he finished the prayer: When one of you is in prayer, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is before his face, so let none spit before his face during prayer."
"5409","Abu Salamah informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, oiled himself with oil that was not perfumed while he was in ihram."
"5410","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Abi al-Sahba narrated to us, Salim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Fajr then gave the salam, then faced the sunrise and said: Verily tribulation is here; verily tribulation is here, where the horn of Satan rises."
"5411","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about fasting the Day of Arafah, so he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not fast it, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar, nor Uthman. Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from a man, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not fast it, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar, nor Uthman, meaning the Day of Arafah."
"5412","Affan narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to me, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, apportioned in the additional spoils two shares for the horse and one share for the man."
"5413","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, that Ibn Umar used to pray on his mount while traveling wherever it turned with him. He said: And Ibn Umar mentioned that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do that while traveling."
"5414","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abi Talhah, informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited this verse one day upon the minbar: And they did not esteem Allah His true esteem, and the earth entirely is His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens are folded in His right hand; glory be to Him, exalted above what they associate. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was saying thus with his hand and moving it, bringing it forward and taking it back, glorifying the Lord Himself: I am the Compeller, I am the Proud, I am the King, I am the Mighty, I am the Generous. So the minbar shook with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until we said it would fall with him."
"5415","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about vessels. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade those vessels."
"5416","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Habib, meaning al-Muallim, informed us, from Ata, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that he asked Ibn Umar: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform Umrah in Rajab. He said: Yes. That was reported to Aishah, so she said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never performed an Umrah except while he was with him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never performed Umrah in Rajab at all."
"5417","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that he said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ten rakahs: two rakahs before Zuhr, two rakahs after it, two rakahs after Maghrib, two rakahs after Isha, and two rakahs before Subh."
"5418","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The two sellers have the choice as long as they have not parted, or one of them says to his companion: Choose."
"5419","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Musab ibn Sad, who said: Abdullah ibn Umar entered upon Abdullah ibn Amir to visit him in illness, so he said: Why do you not supplicate for me. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzlement, and you were over Basra, meaning as governor."
"5420","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Najih said, he informed me, he said: I heard my father narrate from a man, from Ibn Umar, that he asked him about fasting the Day of Arafah. He said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did not fast it, and with Abu Bakr and he did not fast it, and with Umar and he did not fast it, and with Uthman and he did not fast it; and I do not fast it, nor do I command you nor forbid you; if you wish then fast it, and if you wish then do not fast it."
"5421","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muawi, that a man prayed beside Ibn Umar and kept fiddling with the pebbles, so he said: Do not fiddle with the pebbles, for it is from Satan; but do as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do. He said: Thus, and Wuhayb showed us, Affan described it: He placed his left hand and spread his fingers upon his left knee, and placed his right hand upon his right knee, as if he made a circle, and pointed with the forefinger."
"5422","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, both said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no umra and no ruqba; whoever is given something as umra or ruqba, it is his for his life and his death. Ibn Bakr said in his hadith: Ata said: Ruqba is for the survivor. Abd al-Razzaq said: From me and from you."
"5423","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid the nabidh of the earthen jar. He said: They have claimed that."
"5424","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar said, he informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bilal calls at night, or: Ibn Umm Maktum calls at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"5425","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two men should not converse privately to the exclusion of one."
"5426","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."
"5427","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the muhrim to wear a garment dyed with wars or saffron. And he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has no sandals, let him wear the two khuffs and cut them below the ankles."
"5428","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointing toward the east and saying: Indeed tribulations are here; indeed tribulations are here, where the horn of Satan rises."
"5429","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the earthen jar, the gourd, and the pitched vessel, and commanded that nabidh be made in waterskins."
"5430","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Seek it in the last seven."
"5431","Bahz ibn Asad Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear two khuffs and cut them from the ankles."
"5432","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, I heard al-Mughirah ibn Salman narrate from Ibn Umar, who said: Ten rakahs the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to persist upon: two rakahs before Zuhr, two rakahs after Zuhr, two rakahs after Maghrib, two rakahs after Isha, and two rakahs before Fajr."
"5433","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let him take her back until she becomes pure, then let him divorce her if he wishes."
"5434","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he informed me, if Allah wills, Anas ibn Sirin, I heard Ibn Umar say: Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let him take her back until she becomes pure, then let him divorce her. He said: I said: Was it counted. He said: Famah."
"5435","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Jabalah narrated to us, who said: We were in Madinah in the dispatch of the people of Iraq, and a year of hardship struck us, so Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr used to provide us with dates, and Abdullah ibn Umar would pass by us and say: Do not join two dates together, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qiran, unless one of you asks permission of his brother."
"5436","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Affan said: From Safwan ibn Muhriz, who said: I was holding the hand of Ibn Umar when a man met him and said: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, speak about the private counsel on the Day of Resurrection. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brings the believer near and places upon him His cover and veils him from the people, and makes him acknowledge his sins, and says to him: Do you know such-and-such sin; do you know such-and-such sin; do you know such-and-such sin, until when He has made him acknowledge his sins and he sees in himself that he has perished, He says: I concealed them for you in the world, and I forgive them for you today. Then he is given the book of his good deeds. As for the disbelievers and the hypocrites, the witnesses will say: These are those who lied against their Lord; verily the curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers."
"5437","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him do so, for I intercede for whoever dies in it."
"5438","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Waqid, I heard Nafi, that a man came to Ibn Umar and kept offering him food, and he ate a great deal, so he said to Nafi: Do not bring this man to me, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"5439","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He who drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5440","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the dabb lizard. He said: I neither eat it nor forbid it."
"5441","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, while he was at al-Hijr: Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping; if you are not weeping then do not enter upon them, lest there befall you the like of what befell them."
"5442","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that janabah befalls him at night, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to wash his private part and perform ablution, then sleep."
"5443","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is seeking it, let him seek it in the last ten; if he is unable or weak, let him not be overcome regarding the remaining seven."
"5444","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ramal in the first three circuits around the House."
"5445","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"5446","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: There are no days greater with Allah, nor more beloved to Him than deeds done in them, than these ten days; so increase in them tahlil, takbir, and tahmid."
"5447","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him."
"5448","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray two rakahs after Jumuah."
"5449","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, that Muawiyah came to Makkah and entered the Kabah, then sent to Ibn Umar: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray. He said: He prayed between the two pillars facing the door. Then Ibn al-Zubayr came and shook the door violently, so it was opened for him, and he said to Muawiyah: You knew that I knew like what he knows, but you envied me."
"5450","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you come to Jumuah, perform ghusl."
"5451","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying on a donkey, male or female, while he was facing Khaybar."
"5452","Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi Abu Abdullah narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Numan ibn Qurad, from a man, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I was given the choice between intercession or half of my ummah entering Paradise, so I chose intercession, because it is more general and more sufficient. Do you think it is for the purified. No, but it is for the stained, those who err. Ziyad said: It is indeed a grammatical error, but thus narrated to us the one who narrated to us."
"5453","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, Abu Salamah informed me, that he heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The month is twenty-nine."
"5454","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah and Nafi, the freedman of Ibn Umar, that Ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The night prayer is two rakahs at a time; when you fear dawn, make witr with one."
"5455","Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever abandons Asr until it escapes him, it is as if his family and wealth have been taken from him. And Shayban said, meaning: He was overcome regarding his family and wealth."
"5456","Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah, Exalted, be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever comes to Jumuah, let him perform ghusl."
"5457","Hasan narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, a man narrated to me, that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For every traitor there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"5458","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw in one of his campaigns a slain woman, so he disapproved of that and forbade killing women and children."
"5459","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"5460","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, I heard Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar say: I ordered Muslim ibn Yasar, the freedman of Nafi ibn Abd al-Harith, to ask Ibn Umar, while I was sitting between them: What did you hear from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about one who drags his izar out of pride. He said: I heard him say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5461","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Hamzah, meaning al-Sukkari, narrated to us, from Ibrahim, meaning al-Saigh, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to separate between witr and shaf with a taslimah, and let us hear it."
"5462","Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever swears, let him swear only by Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Quraysh used to swear by their fathers, so he said: Do not swear by your fathers."
"5463","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, informed us, from Nafi, he informed him, from Ibn Umar, that a woman used to graze sheep for the family of Kab ibn Malik at Sala, and she feared one of them would die, so she slaughtered it with a stone, and that was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he commanded them to eat it."
"5464","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, I heard a man from the Ansar of Banu Salimah narrate to Abdullah ibn Umar in the mosque, that a slave girl of Kab ibn Malik used to graze sheep for him at Sala, and one sheep was exposed to danger, so she feared for it and took a sharp edge of stone and slaughtered it with it, so they asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, and he commanded them to eat it."
"5465","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid traveling with the mushaf to the land of the enemy."
"5466","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah forbid the sale of habal al-habalah, and that is that the people of Jahiliyyah used to sell that sale, so he forbade them that."
"5467","Yazid narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever abandons Asr deliberately until the sun sets, it is as if his family and wealth have been taken from him."
"5468","Yazid narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Do not prevent your women from the mosques, and their houses are better for them. He said: A son of Abdullah ibn Umar said: Indeed, by Allah, we will prevent them. So Ibn Umar said: You hear me narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and you say what you say."
"5469","Abu Dawud Umar ibn Sad narrated to us, Badr ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Marwan, from Abu Aishah, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us one morning after sunrise and said: I saw shortly before Fajr as if I was given the keys and the scales; as for the keys, these are the keys, and as for the scales, they are those with which you weigh. I was placed in a scale pan and my ummah was placed in a scale pan, so I outweighed them. Then Abu Bakr was brought and was weighed against them, so he outweighed. Then Umar was brought and was weighed, so he outweighed. Then Uthman was brought and was weighed against them, then it was raised."
"5470","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, from Ibn Umar, who said: A man from the Bedouins called to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while I was between him and the Bedouin, and said: O Messenger of Allah, how is the night prayer. He said: Two by two; when you fear dawn, then one, and two rakahs before the morning prayer."
"5471","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Do not prevent women from going out to the mosques, and their houses are better for them."
"5472","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, informed us, from Umar ibn Nafi, and Yazid once said: Umar ibn Nafi informed him, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What do we wear when we enter ihram. He said: Do not wear shirts, nor trousers, nor turbans, nor burnouses, nor khuffs, unless a man has no sandals, then let him wear the two khuffs and make them below the ankles; and do not wear anything of clothing touched by saffron or wars."
"5473","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not trade in fruits until their soundness appears."
"5474","My father said, and he informed us, meaning Yazid, he said: Yahya informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he used to say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever frees a share of his in a person or a slave is charged with freeing the rest; if he has no wealth with which to free him, what he freed is valid."
"5475","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Nafi, that he heard Ibn Umar narrate about that with which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say the talbiyah, saying: Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You, labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You. And Nafi mentioned that Ibn Umar used to add these words on his own: Labbayk, and longing is to You, and deeds; labbayk, labbayk."
"5476","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five, there is no sin upon whoever kills of them: the crow, the mouse, the kite, the vicious dog, and the scorpion."
"5477","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I entered the mosque and saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the people around him, so I hastened to hear his speech, but the people dispersed before I reached, and he once said: Before I got to them. So I asked a man among them: What did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say. He said: He forbade muzaffat and dubba."
"5478","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Nafi, that he informed him, he said: We came with Ibn Umar from Makkah, traveling with him, and with him were Hafs ibn Asim ibn Umar and Musahiq ibn Amr ibn Khidash. The sun set for us, so one of them said: The prayer, but he did not speak to him. Then the other said to him: The prayer, but he did not speak to him. Nafi said: So I said to him: The prayer. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when travel hastened him, join between these two prayers, so I want to join between them. He said: So we traveled miles, then he alighted and prayed. Yahya said: Nafi narrated this hadith to me another time and said: We traveled until near a quarter of the night, then he alighted and prayed."
"5479","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, Salim narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Harithah al-Kalbi, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say: We used to call him only Zayd ibn Muhammad, until the Quran came down: Call them by their fathers; it is more just with Allah."
"5480","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray two rakahs after Jumuah."
"5481","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, I heard Salim ibn Abdullah narrate from his father, that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, have you seen what we do in it: Is it a new or originated matter, or a matter already decided. He said: A matter already decided; so act, O son of al-Khattab, for each is made easy. Whoever is among the people of happiness will act for happiness, and whoever is among the people of misery will act for misery."
"5482","Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed and said: When one of you goes to Jumuah, let him perform ghusl."
"5483","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Uqbah ibn Hurayth, I heard Ibn Umar narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The night prayer is two by two; when you see that dawn overtakes you, make witr with one. He said: It was said to Ibn Umar: What is two by two. He said: You give salam in every two rakahs."
"5484","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The month is twenty-nine, and Shubah joined his hands three times and bent the thumb in the third. Uqbah said: And I think he said: And the month is thirty, and he joined his palms three times."
"5485","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek it in the last ten, meaning Laylat al-Qadr; if one of you is weak or unable, let him not be overcome regarding the remaining seven."
"5486","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Thabit: I asked Ibn Umar about the nabidh of the earthen jar: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid it. He said: They have claimed that. I said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it. He said: They have claimed that. I said: You heard it from him. He said: They have claimed that. So Allah turned it away from me, and when it was said to someone: You heard it, he became angry and nearly quarreled."
"5487","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, meaning al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any man who sells date palms that have been pollinated, its fruit belongs to its first owner, unless the buyer stipulates."
"5488","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: When one of you goes to Jumuah, let him perform ghusl."
"5489","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, that he heard Ibn Umar say: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, so Umar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, so he said: Order him to take her back, then when she becomes pure let him divorce her. I said to Ibn Umar: Was that divorce counted. He said: Famah."
"5490","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, who said: I asked Ibn Umar: What do I recite in the two rakahs before Subh. So Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray at night two by two and make witr with one rakah at the end of the night. Anas said: I said: I am only asking you what I recite in the two rakahs before Subh. So he said: Bah, bah, you are indeed bulky; I am only narrating, or he said: I am only relating to you the hadith: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray at night two rakahs at a time, then make witr with one rakah at the end of the night, then stand as if the adhan or the iqamah were in his ears."
"5491","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Abd Rabbihi ibn Said narrate from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any man who sells date palms that have been pollinated, its fruit belongs to the first owner; and any man who sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to his first owner, unless the buyer stipulates. Shubah said: So I narrated to him the hadith of Ayyub from Nafi, that he narrated about date palms from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and about the slave from Umar. Abd Rabbihi said: I know them both only from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said another time, and narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, without doubt."
"5492","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Sadaqah ibn Yasar, I heard Ibn Umar narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he set the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd at Qarn, for the people of Iraq at Dhat Irq, and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam."
"5493","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: It is not lawful for a man to give a gift then return in it, except a father in what he gives his child. And the likeness of one who gives a gift then returns in it is like a dog that ate until when it was full it vomited, then returned in it."
"5494","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Khaliq, I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab narrate from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dubba, hantam, muzaffat, and naqir. Said said: Muzaffat was mentioned from other than Ibn Umar."
"5495","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Abu Ishaq narrate that he heard Abdullah ibn Malik al-Hamdani say: I prayed with Ibn Umar at Jam, so he made the iqamah and prayed Maghrib three rakahs, then prayed Isha two rakahs with one iqamah. He said: Khalid ibn Malik asked him about that, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do like this in this place."
"5496","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of wala and its gifting."
"5497","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar say: Umar asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Janabah befalls me at night, what do I do. He said: Wash your private part, then perform ablution, then sleep."
"5498","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until Bilal or Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"5499","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit or date palms until their soundness appears. It was said to Ibn Umar: What is its soundness. He said: Its blight goes away."
"5500","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, I heard Ibn Umar narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."
"5501","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: I was with Ibn Umar, I and another man, then a man came, so Ibn Umar said: Step back, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When they are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of one."
"5502","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that he instructed a man, when he took his bed, to say: O Allah, You created my soul and You take it, to You belong its death and its life; if You give it life then protect it, and if You cause it to die then forgive it; O Allah, I ask You for well-being. A man said to him: Did you hear this from Umar? He said: From one better than Umar, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5503","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear the dawn, then prostrate a prostration, and two rakahs before the dawn."
"5504","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah: I heard Yunus ibn Jubayr: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating. He said: So Umar went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, and he said: Let him take her back, then when she becomes pure, if he wishes let him divorce her. He said: So I said to Ibn Umar: Is it counted against him? He said: What would prevent it? Yes. What do you think, if he were incapable and acted foolishly?"
"5505","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Hakam: I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for crops or sheep or hunting, then a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"5506","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I witnessed Said ibn Jubayr at Jam, and he established the prayer and prayed Maghrib three rakahs and gave salaam, and prayed Isha two rakahs, and Said narrated that Abd Allah ibn Umar prayed them in this place and did the same, and Ibn Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did the same in this place."
"5507","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: O Allah, have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: O Allah, have mercy on those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: And those who shorten."
"5508","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The talbiyah of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing belong to You, and sovereignty; there is no partner for You."
"5509","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr, he said: I mentioned to Abd Allah ibn Umar that Anas had narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for umrah and hajj together. So Ibn Umar said: May Allah have mercy on Anas. And was Anas present? Did we go out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except as pilgrims? Then when we arrived, he ordered us to make it an umrah, except one who had a sacrificial animal with him. He said: So I narrated that to Anas, and he became angry and said: Do not count us except as children."
"5510","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of the fetus in the womb of a she-camel."
"5511","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim man who has something to bequeath has the right to spend two nights except that his will is written with him."
"5512","Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Said: Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar informed them that a slave girl used to graze sheep for the family of Kab ibn Malik al-Ansari, and she feared that a sheep from the flock would die, so she took a stone and slaughtered it with it, and that was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered them to eat it."
"5513","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No Muslim man who spends two nights, while he has something to bequeath, has the right except that his will is written with him."
"5514","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should eat with his left hand, nor drink with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."
"5515","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who is deceived in selling. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you transact with someone, say: No deception."
"5516","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Yahya and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when travel pressed him, would combine Maghrib and Isha, and in part of the narration of the two of them: he delayed them both together until a quarter of the night."
"5517","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Ayyub ibn Musa and Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut off a hand for a shield worth three dirhams."
"5518","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, assigned two shares for the horse and one share for the man."
"5519","He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us in an expedition toward Tihamah, and we obtained booty, and our shares reached twelve camels, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave us an additional camel each."
"5520","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut down the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir and burned them."
"5521","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Awfi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not trade fruits until their soundness appears. He said: And what is the appearance of their soundness? He said: Its blight goes away and its good becomes pure."
"5522","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to the mosque of Quba riding and walking."
"5523","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us: I heard Tawus: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us and said: Do not sell fruits until their soundness appears."
"5524","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayman asking Ibn Umar, while Abu al-Zubayr was listening, and he said: What do you think about a man who divorced his wife while menstruating? He said: Ibn Umar divorced his wife in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, Abd Allah divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let him take her back to me, and he did not consider it anything, and he said: Then return her; when she becomes pure, then let him divorce or keep her. Ibn Umar said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them facing their waiting period. Ibn Jurayj said: And I heard Mujahid reciting it likewise."
"5525","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: So that was mentioned to Umar, and Umar went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let him keep her until she menstruates other than this menstruation, then becomes pure; then if it appears to him to divorce her, let him divorce her as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded him, and if it appears to him to keep her, let him keep her."
"5526","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar used to say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should eat from his sacrifice beyond three days. He said: And Abd Allah, when the sun set on the third day, would not eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal."
"5527","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab informed me of that, from Salim, concerning the sacrificial animals and the sacrifices."
"5528","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Concerning one in ihram, when he does not find sandals, let him wear khuffs, cutting them below the ankles."
"5529","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, he said: I saw Ibn Umar praying wherever his mount faced with him, and saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do it."
"5530","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: A Bedouin called to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: What do you think about this lizard? He said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it."
"5531","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for hearing and obedience, he would prompt us with: As much as you are able."
"5532","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Syria al-Juhfah. And Abd Allah said: And they claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And for the people of Yemen, Yalamlam."
"5533","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr used to provide us dates as provision. He said: And hardship had afflicted the people in those days, so we would eat, and Ibn Umar would pass by us while we were eating, and he would say: Do not eat two together, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade pairing, except that a man asks permission of his brother. Shubah said: I do not see the permission except as a word from the speech of Ibn Umar."
"5534","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym: I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever is seeking it, let him seek it in the last ten nights."
"5535","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, he said: I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever drags a garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5536","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabalah: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The month is like this, and he folded his fingers twice, and broke the thumb on the third, meaning his saying: Twenty-nine."
"5537","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr: I heard Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq narrating from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about witr. He said: So I walked, I and that man, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rakah. Shubah said: He did not say: From the end of the night."
"5538","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, that he witnessed Said ibn Jubayr leading at Jam. He said: And I think he also called the adhan. So he prayed Maghrib three rakahs, then gave salaam, then prayed Isha two rakahs, then said: Ibn Umar did with us in this place the same as this, and Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did with us in this place the same as this."
"5539","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar had vowed a day to observe itikaf in the pre-Islamic period, so he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, and he ordered him to observe itikaf."
"5540","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us: al-Zuhri informed us, from Salim, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sells pollinated palm trees, their fruits belong to the seller, and whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the seller, except that the buyer stipulates otherwise."
"5541","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One in ihram may kill five: the kite, the crow, the rat, the scorpion, and the vicious dog."
"5542","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The place of entering ihram for the people of Madinah is from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the place of entering ihram for the people of Syria is from al-Juhfah, and the place of entering ihram for the people of Najd is Qarn. So the people said: The place of entering ihram for the people of Yemen is from Yalamlam."
"5543","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut off a hand for a shield worth three dirhams."
"5544","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Atash narrated to us: al-Numan ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Ayyub ibn Salman, a man from the people of Sanaa, he said: We were in Makkah, and we sat with Ata al-Khurasani beside the wall of the mosque, and we did not ask him and he did not narrate to us. He said: Then we sat with Ibn Umar as in this sitting of yours, and we did not ask him and he did not narrate to us. He said: So he said: What is with you that you do not speak nor remember Allah? Say: Allah is Most Great, and praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah and with His praise, once ten times, and ten times a hundred times. Whoever adds, Allah adds for him, and whoever remains silent, he is forgiven. Shall I not inform you of five things I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? They said: Yes. He said: Whoever intercedes to block a hadd from the hudud of Allah opposes Allah in His command, and whoever aids in a dispute without right remains under the anger of Allah until he abandons it, and whoever slanders a believing man or believing woman, Allah confines him in Radghat al-Khabal, the discharge of the people of Hell, and whoever dies owing a debt, it is taken for its owner from his good deeds, there being no dinar nor dirham there, and the two rakahs of Fajr, guard them, for they are among the virtues."
"5545","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Atash narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab went out intending the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he came upon Utarid, a man from Banu Tamim, displaying a silk suit for sale. So Umar went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw Utarid selling his suit; buy it so you wear it when delegations come to you. He said: Only one who has no share wears silk."
"5546","Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us: I heard Abu Jafar saying: Abd Allah ibn Umar, when he heard something from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or witnessed a scene with him, would not fall short of it nor go beyond it. He said: While he was sitting, with Ubayd ibn Umayr narrating to the people of Makkah, Ubayd ibn Umayr said: The parable of the hypocrite is like a sheep between two flocks; if it approaches these sheep they butt it, and if it approaches these they butt it. So Abd Allah ibn Umar said: Not like this. So Ubayd ibn Umayr became angry, and in the gathering was Abd Allah ibn Safwan, and he said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how did he say, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: He said: The parable of the hypocrite is like a sheep between two resting places; if it approaches this resting place they butt it, and if it approaches this resting place they butt it. So he said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, they are one. He said: Thus I heard."
"5547","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed inside the House, and there will come one who forbids you from it, and you will hear from him. He said: Meaning Ibn Abbas. He said: And Ibn Abbas was sitting near him."
"5548","Abd al-Samad and Abu Said both said: Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza. Abd al-Samad said: And it is a patch on the head."
"5549","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harun al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Maghrib prayer is the witr of the daytime prayer, so make the night prayer odd, and the night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rakah at the end of the night."
"5550","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza in the head."
"5551","Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, he said: I entered with Ibn Umar upon Abd Allah ibn Muti, and he said: Welcome to Abu Abd al-Rahman; place a cushion for him. He said: I only came to you to narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever removes a hand from obedience to Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof for him, and whoever dies while separated from the community dies a death of ignorance."
"5552","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Qays al-Maribi informed us, Thumamah ibn Sharahil narrated to us, he said: I went out to Ibn Umar, and we said: What is the prayer of the traveler? He said: Two rakahs, two rakahs, except the Maghrib prayer, three. I said: What if we are at Dhu al-Majaz? He said: And what is Dhu al-Majaz? I said: A place where we gather and sell and remain twenty nights or fifteen nights. He said: O man, I was in Azerbaijan, I do not know, he said, four months or two months, and I saw them praying them two rakahs, two rakahs, and I saw the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, before my eyes praying them two rakahs, two rakahs. Then he cited this verse: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example, until he finished the verse."
"5553","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us: I heard Salim saying, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I saw him at the Kabah near the Maqam, a dark-skinned man with straight hair, placing his hand on two men, his head dripping or dropping water. So I asked: Who is this? It was said: Isa son of Maryam, or al-Masih son of Maryam, I do not know which of the two he said. Then I saw behind him a red man with curly hair, blind in the right eye, the one I have seen most resembling him being Ibn Qatan. So I asked: Who is this? It was said: al-Masih, the Dajjal."
"5554","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us: I heard Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I was brought, while sleeping, a cup of milk, and I drank from it until the milk came out from my nails, then I gave my remainder to Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you interpret it? He said: Knowledge."
"5555","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell camels at al-Baqi, selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars. So I went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was about to enter his room, and I took hold of his garment and asked him. He said: When you take one of the two for the other, no sale should remain between you and him when you part."
"5556","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrated in the first rakah of the noon prayer, and his companions thought that he had recited the chapter of the Prostration. He said: And I did not hear it from Abu Mijlaz."
"5557","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Said informed us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying on a donkey with his face toward the east, voluntarily."
"5558","Yazid narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi embraced Islam with ten wives under him in the pre-Islamic period, and they embraced Islam with him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to choose four of them."
"5559","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell camels at al-Baqi, selling for dinars and taking silver in their place, and selling for silver and taking dinars in their place. So I went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and found him coming out of the house of Hafsah, and I asked him about that. He said: There is no harm in it at the current value."
"5560","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, that Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas narrated that they heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying upon the wood of the pulpit: People must stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or Allah will seal their hearts, and they will surely be written among the heedless."
"5561","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I am deceived in selling. He said: Say: No deception."
"5562","Yazid narrated to us, Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: You saw us when the owner of the dinar and dirham had no more right than his Muslim brother. Then you saw us lately, and the dinar and dirham are dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If you follow the tails of cattle, and trade with inah, and abandon jihad in the path of Allah, Allah will impose humiliation on your necks, then it will not be removed from you until you return to what you were upon and repent to Allah. And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will be a migration after a migration to the migration place of your father Ibrahim. No one will remain on the earths except the worst of its people, and their lands will expel them, and the spirit of al-Rahman, Mighty and Majestic, will deem them foul, and the Fire will gather them with the apes and pigs, resting where they rest and spending the night where they spend the night, and what falls from them is for it. And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will emerge from my nation a people who do evil deeds, reciting the Quran, it not passing their throats. Yazid said: I know only that he said: One of you would belittle his own deed compared to their deed. They kill the people of Islam. When they emerge, kill them. Then when they emerge, kill them. Then when they emerge, kill them. Glad tidings for one who kills them, and glad tidings for one whom they kill. Whenever a horn emerges from them, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, cuts it off. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, repeated that twenty times or more, while I was listening."
"5563","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he returned from Uhud, heard the women of the Ansar weeping for their husbands, and said: But Hamzah has no women weeping for him. That reached the women of the Ansar, so they came weeping for Hamzah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke in the night and heard them while they were weeping, and said: Woe to them, they have continued weeping since the night. Order them to return and not to weep for one who perishes after today."
"5564","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab: Abu al-Fadl, or Ibn al-Fadl, narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Allah, forgive me and turn to me, indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Forgiving, until the counter counted with his hand a hundred times."
"5565","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, he said: al-Shabi said to me: Have you seen the hadith of al-Hasan from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? I sat with Ibn Umar for nearly two years, or a year and a half, and I did not hear him narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except this. He said: Some people from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among them Sad, went to eat some meat, and a woman from among the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called to them: It is lizard meat. So they held back, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat, for it is lawful, there is no harm in it. Tawbah is the one who doubted about it. But it is not from my food."
"5566","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail: I heard Hakim al-Hadhdha: I heard Ibn Umar, asked about prayer while traveling, saying: Two rakahs, the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5567","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Aqil ibn Talhah: I heard Abu al-Khasib saying: I was sitting, then Ibn Umar came, and a man stood from his seat for him, but he did not sit in it and sat in another place. The man said: It would not have harmed you to sit. He said: I would not sit in your seat nor the seat of another after something I witnessed from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man stood for him from his seat, and he went to sit in it, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade him."
"5568","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub: I heard Ibn Abi Nuaym: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, while a man asked him about something. Shubah said: And I think he asked him about one in ihram killing flies. So Abd Allah said: The people of Iraq ask about flies, while they killed the son of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: They are my two sweet basils in this world."
"5569","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us: I heard Abu Jafar, meaning the muezzin, narrating from Muslim Abu al-Muthanna, narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was twice, and Hajjaj said: Meaning twice, twice, and the iqamah once, except that he says: The prayer has begun, the prayer has begun. And when we heard the iqamah, we performed ablution, then went out to prayer. Shubah said: I do not remember other than this."
"5570","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us: I heard Abu Jafar, the muezzin of al-Urban in the mosque of Banu Hilal, from Muslim Abu al-Muthanna, the muezzin of the congregational mosque, and he mentioned this hadith."
"5571","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad: I heard Salim ibn Razin narrating from Salim ibn Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning a man who has a wife, then divorces her, then another man marries her and divorces her before consummating with her, so she returns to her first husband. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Until she tastes the little honey."
"5572","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade earthen jars, gourds, and pitch-coated vessels, and said: Make nabidh in waterskins."
"5573","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived in Makkah, he circumambulated the House seven times, then prayed two rakahs at the Maqam, then went out to al-Safa from the gate from which one goes out, and performed sai between al-Safa and al-Marwah. He said: And Ayyub informed me, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that he said: It is a sunnah."
"5574","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar would almost curse al-Bayda, and he would say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram from the mosque."
"5575","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard his father narrating from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: If there is anything of bad omen that is true, it is in the woman, the horse, and the house."
"5576","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard his father narrating from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Fever is from the blast of Hell, so extinguish it with water, or cool it with water."
"5577","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard his father Muhammad narrating from Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir, or he said: I feared he would make him an heir."
"5578","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Waqid ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard his father narrating from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said during the Farewell Hajj: Woe to you, or he said: Woe unto you, do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"5579","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard his father Muhammad narrating from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I was given the keys of everything except five: Indeed with Allah is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die; indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"5580","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, he said: I saw Ibn Umar pass by a man who had made his mount kneel intending to slaughter it, and he said: Standing, tied; the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5581","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Asim, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: If people knew what I know about solitude, no rider would travel at night alone."
"5582","Musa ibn Tariq Abu Qurrah al-Zubaydi, from the people of Zabid, from the people of al-Husayb in Yemen, narrated to us; my father said: And he was their storyteller; from Musa, meaning Ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, burned the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir and cut them."
"5583","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to place the stone of his ring toward the inside of his palm."
"5584","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd Allah, the freedman of Ghufrah, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every nation has Magians, and the Magians of my nation are those who say there is no divine decree. If they fall sick, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend them."
"5585","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you is praying, let him not leave anyone passing in front of him; if he refuses, let him fight him, for the companion is with him."
"5586","Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Ubayd Allah, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab died, and they wanted to take him out at night due to the crowding, so Ibn Umar said: If you delay him until morning, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The sun rises with the horn of Satan."
"5587","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I went out with Ibn Umar from his house, and we passed by youths from Quraysh who had set up a bird to shoot at, and they had assigned to the owner of the bird every miss from their arrows. He said: When they saw Ibn Umar, they dispersed. So Ibn Umar said: Who did this? May Allah curse whoever did this. Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed whoever takes a living thing as a target."
"5588","Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to train horses for racing."
"5589","Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Aishah: Hand me the prayer mat from the mosque. She said: She is menstruating. He said: It is not in your hand."
"5590","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir: I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not pray while traveling except two rakahs, except that he would perform tahajjud at night. Jabir said: So I said to Salim: Did they both perform witr? He said: Yes."
"5591","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar, he said: We were in an expedition and fled, and we wanted to board the sea. Then we went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are the deserters. He said: No, rather you are the returners to battle."
"5592","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade vows and said: It brings no good; it is only extracted from the miser."
"5593","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Said ibn Ubaydah, he said: I was with Ibn Umar, then I stood and left a man from Kindah with him. So I went to Said ibn al-Musayyab. He said: Then the Kindi came frightened and said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: Shall I swear by the Kabah? He said: No, but swear by the Lord of the Kabah, for Umar used to swear by his father, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not swear by your father, for whoever swears by other than Allah has associated partners."
"5594","He said: I read to Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah said, and Nafi said: Abd Allah, when he returned from hajj or umrah, would make his camel kneel at al-Batha which is at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and Abd Allah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to spend the last part of the night there until he prayed the dawn prayer."
"5595","Musa said: And Salim informed me that Abd Allah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came in his night resting place, and it was said to him: You are in a blessed batha."
"5596","He said: And he said: Nafi narrated to us that Abd Allah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed at the small mosque which is below the mosque overlooking al-Rawha."
"5597","He said: And Nafi said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to descend under the lote tree of al-Ruwaythah, on the right of the road, in a flat plain, when descending from the hillock, two miles before the post of al-Ruwaythah, its top broken while it stands upon a trunk."
"5598","And Nafi said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed beyond al-Arj, while going, at the top of five miles from al-Arj, in a mosque toward a hillock, at that mosque two or three graves, upon the graves a pile of stones, on the right of the road, at the acacia trees of the road. Between those acacia trees, Abd Allah would depart from al-Arj after the sun declined at midday, and pray Zuhr in that mosque."
"5599","And Nafi said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended under a lote tree, and other than Abu Qurrah said: Lote trees, on the left of the road, in a watercourse before Harsha, that watercourse adjoining Harsha, and another said: Adjoining the outskirts of Harsha, between it and the road nearly an arrow shot."
"5600","And Nafi said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to descend at Dhu Tuwa, spending the night there until he prayed the dawn prayer when he came to Makkah. And the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was upon a rugged hillock, not in the mosque later built there, but below that upon a rough rugged hillock."
"5601","He said, and he informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, faced the two passes of the long mountain which is toward the Kabah, and he placed the mosque that was built on his right, and the mosque is at the edge of the hillock, and the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was lower than it upon the black hillock, leaving about ten cubits of the hillock or thereabouts, then he would pray facing the two passes of the long mountain which is between him and the Kabah."
"5602","Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Jafar, I heard Abu al-Muthanna narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was twice twice, and the iqamah once, except that when the muadhdhin said qad qamat as-salah he said qad qamat as-salah twice."
"5603","Abdurrahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the two rakahs after Maghrib in his house."
"5604","Abdurrahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Waqid ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others."
"5605","Abdurrahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Nahshal ibn Mujammi, from Qazaah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Luqman the Wise used to say: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, when entrusted with something preserves it. And he said once: Nahshal, from Qazaah or from Abu Ghalib."
"5606","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Sufyan informed us, Nahshal ibn Mujammi ad-Dabbi informed me, and he was well-regarded, from Qazaah, from Ibn Umar, he said: That the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Luqman the Wise used to say: Indeed Allah, when entrusted with something preserves it."
"5607","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Asim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed among Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer."
"5608","Bahz and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah informed us, Bahz said in his hadith from Hammad, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited this verse while upon the minbar: and the heavens rolled up in His right hand, glory be to Him and exalted above what they associate. He said: Allah says: I am the Compeller, I am the Proud, I am the King, I am the Most High, glorifying Himself. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept repeating it until the minbar shook with him, until we thought it would fall with him."
"5609","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the two rakahs before the Fajr prayer as if the adhan were in his ears."
"5610","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Uthman ibn Yazdawayh, from Yafur ibn Rudhi, I heard Ubayd ibn Umayr narrating, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says: The example of the hypocrite is like the example of the sheep lying down between flocks. So Ibn Umar said: Woe to you, do not lie about the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Rather the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The example of the hypocrite is like the example of the stray sheep between two flocks."
"5611","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Nafi informed me, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was occupied one night and delayed it until we slept in the mosque, then we woke, then we slept, then we woke, then we slept, then we woke, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us, then said: There is no one among the people of the earth tonight waiting for the prayer other than you."
"5612","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had al-Laythi, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed the most righteous righteousness is a man maintaining ties with the beloved ones of his father after he has passed away."
"5613","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave permission to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib; he sought permission from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to spend the nights of Mina at Makkah because of his water provision, so he gave him permission."
"5614","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Nafi, that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shaved his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"5615","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a boy whose part of his hair had been shaved and part left, so he forbade that and said: Shave it all or leave it all."
"5616","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from the brother of az-Zuhri, Abdullah ibn Muslim, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Begging will continue with one of you until he meets Allah with not a piece of flesh on his face."
"5617","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from az-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abdullah and Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman informed me, that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Isha one night at the end of his life, then when he gave salam he stood and said: Have you seen this night of yours? At the head of one hundred years from it, there will remain no one who is upon the surface of the earth. Ibn Umar said: So the people misunderstood the statement of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what they discuss of these hadiths about one hundred years, but the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only said: There will not remain today anyone who is upon the surface of the earth, meaning that generation would pass away."
"5618","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no envy except over two: a man whom Allah has given wealth and he spends from it during hours of the night and hours of the day, and a man whom Allah has given the Quran and he stands with it during hours of the night and hours of the day."
"5619","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will find people like a hundred camels among which a man cannot find a riding camel."
"5620","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw upon Umar a white garment and said: Is your garment new or washed? He said: I do not know what he replied to him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wear new, and live praiseworthy, and die a martyr, I think he said: and may Allah grant you comfort of the eye in this world and the Hereafter."
"5621","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, and ath-Thawri, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed wiping the Yamani corner and the Black corner removes sins thoroughly."
"5622","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to touch the Yamani corner and did not touch the other two."
"5623","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shaved in his Hajj."
"5624","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman used to camp at al-Abtah."
"5625","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you make his brother stand then sit in his seat. Salim said: So a man would stand for Ibn Umar from his seat, but he would not sit in his seat."
"5626","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, from Jafar ibn Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When a Muslim man reaches forty years, Allah secures him from kinds of afflictions: madness, leprosy, and severe leprosy. And when he reaches fifty, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, eases his reckoning for him. And when he reaches sixty, Allah grants him repentance beloved to Him. And when he reaches seventy, Allah loves him and the people of heaven love him. And when he reaches eighty, Allah accepts his good deeds from him and erases his evil deeds from him. And when he reaches ninety, Allah forgives him his past and future sins, and he is named the captive of Allah on earth, and he intercedes for his family."
"5627","Hashim narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Amiri narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"5628","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I buy gold with silver or silver with gold? He said: When you buy one of them with the other, your companion must not leave you while there is confusion between you and him."
"5629","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, concerning the dream of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about Abu Bakr and Umar, he said: I saw the people gathered, then Abu Bakr stood and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and Allah forgives him. Then Ibn al-Khattab stood, and it turned into a large bucket, and I never saw a strong man among people working as he worked, until the people watered the camels to satisfaction."
"5630","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he appointed Usamah, it reached him that the people were criticizing Usamah and disparaging his command, so he stood as Salim narrated to me and said: You criticize Usamah and disparage his command, and you did that regarding his father before, and he was indeed worthy of command, and he was among the most beloved of all people to me, and this son of his after him is among the most beloved of people to me, so treat him well, for he is among your best."
"5631","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim ibn Abdullah informed me, that he heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he met Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl at the lower part of Baldah, and that was before revelation had descended upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, offered him a travel meal containing meat, but he refused to eat from it and said: I do not eat from what you slaughter upon your stone altars, nor do I eat from that upon which the name of Allah has not been mentioned."
"5632","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he came to him while he was in al-Muarras at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and it was said to him: You are in a blessed valley."
"5633","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I counted the white hair of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about twenty hairs."
"5634","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Firas, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in residence and in travel. So he prayed Dhuhr in residence four, and after it two, and he prayed Asr four with nothing after it, and he prayed Maghrib three and after it two, and he prayed Isha four. And he prayed in travel Dhuhr two and after it two, and Asr two with nothing after it, and Maghrib three and after it two, and Isha two and after it two."
"5635","Abu Abdurrahman Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Abu Hani narrated to us, from Abbas al-Hajari, from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a servant who behaves badly and wrongs, shall I strike him? He said: Pardon him seventy times every day."
"5636","Abu Abdurrahman narrated to us, Ibn Umar, meaning Abd al-Jabbar al-Ayli, narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Sumayyah narrated to us, I heard Ibn Umar saying: Umm Sulaym, who is the mother of Anas ibn Malik, asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, does a woman see in a dream what a man sees? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: If a woman sees that and discharges, let her wash."
"5637","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Mutarrif, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu as-Siddiq an-Naji, from Ibn Umar, that the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked him about the hem, so he said: Make it a span. They said: A span does not cover nakedness. So he said: Make it a cubit. So when one of them wanted to make a garment, she would let down a cubit and make it a hem."
"5638","Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Hamzah, from Salim, that a poet said in the presence of Ibn Umar: And Bilal, Abdullah is the best Bilal. So Ibn Umar said to him: You lie, that is Bilal, the Bilal of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5639","Abu Abdurrahman Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Abu Sakhr narrated to me, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar had a friend from the people of Sham who corresponded with him, then once Abdullah ibn Umar wrote to him: It has reached me that you have spoken about something concerning qadar, so beware of writing to me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will be among my ummah peoples who deny qadar."
"5640","Abu Abdurrahman narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Kab ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from Bilal ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not prevent women their shares of the mosques when they seek your permission. So Bilal said: By Allah, we will prevent them. So Abdullah said: I say the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and you say we will prevent them."
"5641","Abu Abdurrahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Fire is an enemy, so beware of it. He said: So Abdullah used to follow the fires of his family and extinguish them before sleeping."
"5642","Abu Abdurrahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Ata narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen, twice. Then a man said: And our east, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: From there the horn of Satan rises, and it holds nine-tenths of evil."
"5643","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Hurr ibn as-Sayyah, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast three days of every month: Thursday from the beginning of the month, and the Monday that follows it, and the Monday that follows it."
"5644","Hajjaj and Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Usm, Abu Alwan al-Hanafi, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed among Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer."
"5645","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not enter upon the punished people except weeping, lest what befell them befall you."
"5646","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that Salim ibn Abdullah informed him that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim, he does not wrong him nor surrender him. Whoever is engaged in the need of his brother, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will be engaged in his need. And whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will relieve him thereby of a distress from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. And whoever covers a Muslim, Allah will cover him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5647","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning His saying like a good tree, he said: It is that whose leaves do not fall, and I thought it is the palm tree."
"5648","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every intoxicant is forbidden; what intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden."
"5649","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Thuwayr narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed effeminate men and masculine women."
"5650","Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade solitude: that a man spend the night alone or travel alone."
"5651","Abu an-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Hurayth, I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever among you seeks it, let him seek it in the last ten, and if one of you is weak or overcome, let him not be overcome regarding the remaining seven."
"5652","Abu Nuh Qurad narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade meeting goods before they are brought down to the markets."
"5653","Abu Nuh informed us, Layth informed us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that a Bedouin passed by him while they were on the Hajj road, so Ibn Umar said to him: Are you not so-and-so son of so-and-so? He said: Yes. He said: So he went to a donkey upon which he used to rest when his mount wearied him, and a turban with which he used to bind his head, and gave them to the Bedouin. When he left, one of us said to him: You went to your donkey upon which you used to rest and your turban with which you used to bind your head and gave them to this Bedouin, while this one would have been content with a dirham. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed the most righteous righteousness is a man maintaining ties with the beloved ones of his father after he has passed away."
"5654","Qurad Abu Nuh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no jalab nor janab nor shighar in Islam."
"5655","Qurad informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reserved an-Naqi for his horses."
"5656","Qurad informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raced between horses and gave the winner."
"5657","Qurad informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to sit between the two sermons."
"5658","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, that Abdullah informed him that a woman was found killed in one of the campaigns of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disapproved of killing women and children."
"5659","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, from Abdullah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while facing the east, saying: Verily fitnah is here, verily fitnah is here, from where the horn of Satan rises."
"5660","And Ahmad said: Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bahiyy, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray upon al-khumrah."
"5661","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever mutilates a living soul then does not repent, Allah will mutilate him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5662","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, fear wrongdoing, for it is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"5663","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray the two Eids, al-Adha and al-Fitr, then deliver a sermon after the prayer."
"5664","Hashim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, and he is al-Asha, from Muhajir ash-Shami, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wears a garment of fame in this world, Allah will clothe him in a garment of humiliation on the Day of Resurrection."
"5665","Hashim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Asim, I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed among Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer."
"5666","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came on the day of Uhud and heard women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal weeping over their dead, so he said: But Hamzah has no weepers for him. So the women of the Ansar came weeping over Hamzah in his presence. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke while they were weeping and said: Woe to them, are you here weeping until now? Command them to return and not to weep over a dead one after today."
"5667","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Abu Munib al-Jurashi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was sent before the Hour with the sword, until Allah alone with no partner is worshipped. And my provision was placed under the shade of my spear. And humiliation and disgrace were placed upon whoever opposes my command. And whoever imitates a people is among them."
"5668","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: A funeral passed by us, so Ibn Umar said: If you would stand with it. He said: So he took my hand and gripped it with a strong grip. When we drew near the graves, he heard a wailing from behind him while gripping my hand, so he turned me and faced it and said evil to it, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a funeral be followed while a wailer is with it."
"5669","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood upon as-Safa and al-Marwah, and Umar used to command us to stand upon them from where he sees them."
"5670","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no sadaqah in less than five camels, nor five uqiyahs, nor five awsuq."
"5671","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil, meaning Abdullah ibn Aqil, narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Yazid ath-Thumali, Abu al-Ajlan al-Muharibi narrated to me, I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed the disbeliever will drag his tongue on the Day of Resurrection behind him the distance of two farsakhs, trampled by people."
"5672","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, from Barakah ibn Yala at-Taymi, Abu Suwayd al-Abdi narrated to me, he said: We came to Ibn Umar and sat at his door to be given permission, but permission was slow for us. He said: So I stood toward a hole in the door and began peeping through it, and he noticed me. When he gave us permission, we sat, and he said: Which of you peeped just now into my house? He said: I said: I did. He said: By what did you deem it lawful to peep into my house? He said: I said: Permission was slow for us, so I looked and did not mean it deliberately. He said: Then they asked him about things, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and establishing prayer, and giving zakah, and Hajj of the House, and fasting Ramadan. I said: O Abu Abdurrahman, what do you say about jihad? He said: Whoever strives, he only strives for himself."
"5673","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil, and he is Abdullah ibn Aqil, narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Salim narrated to us, from his father, he said: I would sometimes recall the saying of the poet while looking at the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon the minbar seeking rain, and he would not descend until every gutter flowed. And I recall the saying of the poet: And white, through whose face the clouds are asked for rain, guardian of orphans, protector of widows. And it is the saying of Abu Talib."
"5674","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil said, my father, and he is Abdullah ibn Aqil, sound in hadith, trustworthy, narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Allah, curse so-and-so. O Allah, curse al-Harith ibn Hisham. O Allah, curse Suhayl ibn Amr. O Allah, curse Safwan ibn Umayyah. He said: So this verse descended: Not for you is the decision, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers. He said: So they were all turned to."
"5675","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, from Ibn Abi Num, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar while I was sitting, and asked him about the blood of a mosquito. So he said to him: From where are you? He said: From the people of Iraq. He said: Look at this, he asks about the blood of a mosquito while they killed the son of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: They are my two sweet basils from this world."
"5676","Affan narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience will have no proof on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever dies separating from the community dies a death of ignorance."
"5677","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This matter will remain in Quraysh as long as two of the people remain."
"5678","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Abi as-Sahba narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called among the people: Prayer in congregation. That reached Abdullah, so he went to his family swiftly, cast off garments that were upon him, wore garments in which he used to come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then went to the prayer place while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had descended from his minbar, and the people stood facing him. So he said: What has the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, newly said today? They said: He forbade nabidh. He said: Which nabidh? He said: He forbade ad-dubba and an-naqir. He said: So I said to Nafi: And the jar? He said: What is the jar? He said: I said: al-hantamah. He said: What is al-hantamah? I said: al-qullah. He said: No. I said: And al-muzaffat? He said: What is al-muzaffat? I said: The skin coated with pitch, and ar-raqud coated with pitch. He said: No, he only forbade that day ad-dubba and an-naqir."
"5679","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Uqbah, meaning Ibn Abi as-Sahba, narrated to us, Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, that Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to him that he was one day with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a group of his companions, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to them and said: O these, do you not know that I am the Messenger of Allah to you? They said: Yes, we bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not know that Allah revealed in His Book: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah? They said: Yes, we bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed Allah, and that from obedience to Allah is obedience to you. He said: So from obedience to Allah is to obey me, and from obedience to me is to obey your leaders. Obey your leaders. If they pray sitting, then pray sitting."
"5680","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Begging is scratches on the face of its owner on the Day of Resurrection. So whoever is afflicted, let him preserve his face. And the lightest begging is asking a relative for a need. And the best begging is begging while independent. And begin with those you support."
"5681","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: A man will remain in the expanse of his religion as long as he does not shed unlawful blood."
"5682","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, he said: Ibn Umar entered upon Yahya ibn Said while a boy of his sons had tied a chicken and was shooting it. So he walked to the chicken and freed it, then came with it and the boy and said to Yahya: Restrain this boy of yours from tying this bird for killing, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding that an animal or other be tied for killing. And if you want to slaughter it, then slaughter it."
"5683","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Layth narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abdurrahman, from Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, that he said to Abdullah ibn Umar: We find the prayer of residence and the prayer of fear in the Quran, but we do not find the prayer of travel in the Quran. So Ibn Umar said to him: Son of my brother, indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent to us Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while we knew nothing, so we only do as we saw Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, doing."
"5684","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hakam informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: A man was praising Ibn Umar. He said: So Ibn Umar began saying thus, throwing dust in his face. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When you see the eulogists, throw dust in their faces."
"5685","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: On the ring of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was Muhammad Rasul Allah."
"5686","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet had two muadhdhins."
"5687","Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, I heard Ibn Umar saying: Two eloquent men from the East came in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They stood and spoke, then sat. And Thabit ibn Qays, the orator of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and spoke, then sat. The people marveled at their speech. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and said: O people, say your saying, for splitting of speech is from Satan. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed some eloquence is magic."
"5688","Abd as-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that when he left Jumuah he left to his house and prostrated two prostrations, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do that."
"5689","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from Junayd, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying of Hell: It has seven gates, a gate of them for whoever draws his sword against my ummah, or he said: the ummah of Muhammad."
"5690","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Khalid, meaning at-Tahhan, narrated to us, Bayan narrated to us, from Wabarah, from Ibn Jubayr, meaning Said, from Ibn Umar, he said: Ibn Umar came out to us while we hoped he would narrate to us a pleasing hadith, then a man rushed to him and said: O Abu Abdurrahman, what do you say about fighting in fitnah, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: And fight them until there is no fitnah? He said: Woe to you, do you know what fitnah is? Rather the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fight the polytheists, and entering their religion was fitnah, and it is not your fighting over kingship."
"5691","Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: I watched the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for a month, and he would recite in the two rakahs before Fajr: Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun and Qul huwa Allahu ahad."
"5692","Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Fudayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delayed Isha prayer until the people slept, and the night worshippers prayed tahajjud, and the wakeful awoke. Then he came out, the prayer was established, and said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would delay it to this time."
"5693","Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Aqil, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, clothed him in a striped silk hullah and clothed Usamah in two qibtiyyahs, then said: What touches the earth is in the Fire."
"5694","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, Iyad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Num, or Nuaym, al-Araji, Abu al-Walid doubted, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar about mutah, the mutah of women, while I was with him, so he said: By Allah, we were not adulterers nor fornicators in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said: By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Before the Day of Resurrection there will be the False Messiah and thirty liars or more."
"5695","Jafar ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, Iyad informed us, from Abdurrahman al-Araji, from Ibn Umar, without doubting in it, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"5696","Abu Amir narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, honor Islam with the more beloved of these two men to You: with Abu Jahl or with Umar ibn al-Khattab. So the more beloved of them to Allah was Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"5697","Abu Amir narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has placed truth upon the heart of Umar and his tongue. He said: And Ibn Umar said: No matter ever befell the people about which they said something and Umar ibn al-Khattab said something, or he said: Umar, except the Quran descended in accordance with what Umar said."
"5698","Abd as-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Matar narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, he said: I traveled with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with Umar, and they would not add beyond two rakahs. And we were astray, so Allah guided us through him, so him we follow."
"5699","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: I watched the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, twenty-four times or twenty-five times, reciting in the two rakahs before Fajr and after Maghrib: Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun and Qul huwa Allahu ahad."
"5700","Rawh narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Salim, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar used to give fatwa by what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed of the concession of tamattu, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, established it in practice. So people would say to Ibn Umar: How do you oppose your father while he forbade that? So Abdullah would say to them: Woe to you, do you not fear Allah? If Umar forbade that, seeking therein good, seeking thereby completeness of Umrah, then why do you forbid that while Allah has permitted it and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, practiced it? Is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more worthy that you follow his Sunnah or the Sunnah of Umar? Indeed Umar did not say to you that Umrah in the months of Hajj is forbidden, but he said that the most complete Umrah is that you single it out from the months of Hajj."
"5701","Rawh narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father who said: I said to Ibn Umar: I see you crowding upon these two corners. He said: If I do so, then I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Touching them both removes sins. He said: And I heard him say: Whoever circumambulates this House seven times, counting it, a good deed is written for him for every step, an evil deed is expiated from him, a degree is raised for him, and it is equal to freeing a slave."
"5702","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr meaning Ibn Ayyash informed us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibrahim ibn Quays, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you who command you with what they do not do, so whoever believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not from me and I am not from him, and he will never come to me at the Basin."
"5703","Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by Allah, give him, and whoever invites you, answer him, and whoever gives you a gift, reward him, and if you do not find what to reward him with, supplicate for him."
"5704","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hanzalah informed us, I heard Salim ibn Abdullah say: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For the inside of a man to be filled with pus is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry."
"5705","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, I heard Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, that Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves except while weeping, lest there befall you the like of what befell them."
"5706","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring of gold, he used to turn its stone toward the inside of his palm, then one day he threw it away, so his Companions threw away their rings, then he took a ring of silver, and he used to seal with it and not wear it."
"5707","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah said: Usama is the most beloved of people to me, excluding Fatima, and no one else."
"5708","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sumayrah who said: I was walking with Abdullah ibn Umar when we came upon a head set up on a piece of wood. He said: Wretched is the killer of this one. I said: Do you say this, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He pulled his hand from my hand and said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If a man from my nation walks to a man to kill him, let him say like this: the killed one is in Paradise and the killer is in Hellfire."
"5709","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Sakhr narrated to us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar gathered his sons when the people of Medina rose with Ibn al-Zubayr and deposed Yazid ibn Muawiyah, and said: We have pledged allegiance to this man by the pledge of Allah and His Messenger, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The treacherous one will have a banner set up for him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so, and among the greatest treachery, except for associating partners with Allah Almighty, is for a man to pledge allegiance to a man upon the pledge of Allah and His Messenger and then break his pledge. So let none of you depose Yazid, and let none of you go to extremes in this matter, lest it be a complete severance between me and you."
"5710","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, that Abu al-Malih said to Abu Qilabah: I and your father entered upon Ibn Umar, and he narrated to us that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he threw to him a cushion of leather stuffed with fiber, and I did not sit upon it; it remained between me and him."
"5711","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar, freed slave of Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah said: Among the greatest lies is for one to show his two eyes in a dream what they did not see."
"5712","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble: Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon them)."
"5713","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a suit from the suits of sira, which Fayruz had gifted to him. I wore the lower garment and its length and width overwhelmed me, so I dragged it, and I wore the upper garment and wrapped myself with it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of my shoulder and said: O Abdullah, raise the lower garment, for whatever of the lower garment touches the ground down to below the ankles is in the Fire. Abdullah ibn Muhammad said: I never saw any man more tucked up than Abdullah ibn Umar."
"5714","Muhanna ibn Abd al-Hamid Abu Shibl narrated to us, from Hammad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed him with a suit and he let it trail, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning it a stern saying, and mentioned the Fire."
"5715","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ikrimah, from Abu al-Mughirah ibn Hunayn, Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, he said: I saw for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a place of relieving himself facing the qiblah."
"5716","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wail al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed wine, and cursed its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, and the eater of its price."
"5717","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that he used to dye his clothes and oil himself with saffron. It was said to him: Why do you dye your clothes and oil yourself with saffron? He said: Because I saw it as the most beloved of dyes to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would oil himself with it and dye his clothes with it."
"5718","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that he narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Umar came to Ibn Muti during the nights of al-Harrah, and he said: Put a cushion for Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: I did not come to sit; I only came to inform you of two statements I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever withdraws a hand from obedience will have no proof on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever dies separating from the community dies a death of ignorance."
"5719","Ismail ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abbad meaning Ibn Abbad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: We entered ihram with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Hajj alone."
"5720","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibrahim ibn Salih, whose name by which he is known is Nuaym ibn al-Nahham, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had named him Salih, he informed him that Abdullah ibn Umar said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: Propose to me the daughter of Salih. He said: He has orphans, and he would not prefer us over them. So Abdullah went to his uncle Zayd ibn al-Khattab to propose, so Zayd went to Salih and said: Abdullah ibn Umar has sent me to you to propose your daughter. He said: I have orphans, and I would not soil my own flesh and raise your flesh; I call you to witness that I have married her to so-and-so. And the inclination of her mother was toward Abdullah ibn Umar, so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, Abdullah ibn Umar proposed my daughter, but her father married her to an orphan in his care without consulting her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Salih and said: You married your daughter without consulting her? He said: Yes. He said: Consult the women concerning themselves, and she is a virgin. Salih said: I only did this because of what Ibn Umar would give her as dowry, for he has in my wealth the like of what he gave her."
"5721","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Uthman al-Walid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah, that he said: Among the most dutiful righteousness is for a man to maintain ties with the family of his father's affection."
"5722","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, Awn ibn Abdullah informed us, that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a man said: Allah is most great, great, and praise be to Allah, much, and glory be to Allah, morning and evening. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who said the words? The man said: I did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, I was looking at them ascending until the gates of heaven were opened for them. Ibn Umar said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, I have not abandoned them since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Awn said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Ibn Umar."
"5723","Surayj narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two dead animals and two bloods have been made lawful for us. As for the two dead animals, they are the fish and the locust, and as for the two bloods, they are the liver and the spleen."
"5724","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the rows, for you only line up like the lining up of the angels. Align the shoulders, close the gaps, be gentle in the hands of your brothers, do not leave openings for Satan. Whoever joins a row, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, joins him, and whoever cuts a row, Allah cuts him."
"5725","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth and Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give permission to women at night to go to the mosques, unscented; Layth is the one who mentioned unscented."
"5726","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver two sermons on Friday, sitting between them once."
"5727","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a Qubti garment, and clothed Usama with a sira suit. He said: He looked and saw me trailing it, so he came and took hold of my shoulder and said: O Ibn Umar, everything of the clothes that touches the ground is in the Fire. He said: So I saw Ibn Umar wearing his waist-wrapper to mid-calf."
"5728","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad meaning Ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while delivering a sermon: The upper hand is better than the lower hand; the upper hand is the giving one, and the lower hand is the hand of the beggar."
"5729","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, who said: The one who does not pay the zakah of his wealth, Allah Almighty will make his wealth appear to him on the Day of Resurrection as a bald serpent with two black spots above its eyes, then it will cling to him, coiling around him, saying: I am your treasure, I am your treasure."
"5730","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, raising the hadith to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden, and whoever drinks wine in this world and dies while persisting in it without repenting will not drink it in the Hereafter."
"5731","My father said, and in another place he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"5732","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid al-Himsi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Zufar, from Hashim, from Ibn Umar who said: Whoever buys a garment for ten dirhams, in which is a forbidden dirham, Allah will not accept prayer from him as long as it is upon him. He said: Then he put his two fingers into his ears, then said: May they both be deaf if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not heard by me saying it."
"5733","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bahi, Sharik said: I think, from Abdullah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah used to pray upon a mat."
"5734","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Huraym informed us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: A short spear used to be carried with the Messenger of Allah on the two Eids in his travels, and it would be planted before him, and he would pray toward it."
"5735","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever performs ablution once, that is the required function of ablution which is indispensable, and whoever performs ablution twice, for him are two shares, and whoever performs ablution three times, that is my ablution and the ablution of the prophets before me."
"5736","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Salih ibn Qudamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib al-Jumahi Abu Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever is swearing, let him not swear except by Allah. Quraysh used to swear by their fathers. He said: So do not swear by your fathers."
"5737","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the first circumambulation, he trotted three times and walked four times, and he would hasten in the belly of al-Masil when he circumambulated between al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"5738","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A fire will emerge from the direction of Hadramawt, gathering the people. He said: We said: What do you command us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you is al-Sham."
"5739","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from al-Mughirah ibn Salman who said: Ibn Umar said: I memorized from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten prayers: two rakahs before the dawn prayer, two rakahs before the noon prayer, two rakahs after the noon prayer, two rakahs after the sunset prayer, and two rakahs after the night prayer."
"5740","Arim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever takes anything of land unjustly will be sunk with it to seven earths."
"5741","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ikrimah, from Rafi ibn Hunayn, that Ibn Umar informed him that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) go to a place of relieving himself facing the qiblah."
"5742","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: I watched the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-four or twenty-five times reciting in the two rakahs before dawn and the two rakahs after sunset: Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One."
"5743","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by Allah, give him, and whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge, and whoever does you a kindness, reward him, and if you do not find what to reward him with, supplicate for him until you know that you have rewarded him, and whoever seeks your protection, grant him protection."
"5744","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the refuge of every Muslim."
"5745","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you prays, let him not spit toward the qiblah, for before him is al-Rahman, nor to his right, but to his left or beneath his left foot."
"5746","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Yunus Hatim ibn Muslim, I heard a man from Quraysh say: I saw a woman come to Ibn Umar at Mina wearing a breastplate of silk, and she said: What do you say about silk? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"5747","Husayn narrated to us, Ayyub meaning Ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieving himself upon two bricks, facing the qiblah."
"5748","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abdullah, he narrated to him, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give Umar a gift, and Umar would say to him: Give it, O Messenger of Allah, to one more needy than me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to him: Take it, acquire wealth with it or give it in charity. Whatever comes to you of this wealth while you are neither aspiring nor asking, take it, and what is otherwise, do not follow it with your soul. Salim said: For that reason Ibn Umar would not ask anyone for anything, nor refuse anything."
"5749","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza, from Abdullah ibn al-Sadi, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, the like of that."
"5750","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Umar, I said: What do you say about fasting while traveling? He said: Will you take it if I narrate to you? I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he left this city, shortened the prayer and did not fast until he returned to it."
"5751","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid meaning Ibn Ata narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, al-Hasan ibn Suhayl ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the mitharah, the qassiyyah, the gold ring, and the mufdam. Yazid said: Al-mitharah is skins of beasts, al-qassiyyah is ribbed garments of silk brought from Egypt, and al-mufdam is what is saturated with safflower."
"5752","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Khalid meaning al-Tahhan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar who said: We met the enemy, and the Muslims veered aside in retreat, and I was among those who veered aside, then we entered Medina. He said: We presented ourselves to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came out for prayer, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we are the fleeing ones. He said: No, rather you are the returning ones; I am a refuge for you."
"5753","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Zayd meaning Ibn Jubayr, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed in a battle he fought by a killed woman, and he forbade killing women and children."
"5754","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sumayrah, that Ibn Umar saw a head and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevents one of you, when there comes to him one who wants to kill him, from being like the son of Adam: the killer in the Fire and the killed in Paradise."
"5755","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bahir al-Sanani al-Qass narrated to us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid informed him that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at the Day of Resurrection as if it is seen with the eye, let him recite: When the sun is folded up, and When the heaven is cleft asunder, and I think he said: and Surah Hud."
"5756","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, and Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed noon, afternoon, sunset, and night at al-Batha, then slept there a sleep, then entered Mecca, and Ibn Umar used to do it."
"5757","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Matar narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father who said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with Umar, and I did not see them add over two rakahs. We were astray, and Allah guided us through him, so by him we take example."
"5758","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, I heard al-Mughirah ibn Salman narrating in the house of Muhammad ibn Sirin that Ibn Umar said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten rakahs besides the obligatory: two rakahs before noon, two rakahs after noon, two rakahs after sunset, two rakahs after night, and two rakahs before dawn."
"5759","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli, from Ibn Umar, that a man from the desert people asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the night prayer, and he said with his two fingers: Two by two, and witr is one rakah at the end of the night."
"5760","Affan narrated to us, Sulaym ibn Akhdar narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi who said: Abdullah ibn Umar used to trot from the Stone to the Stone, and would inform us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that. Ubaydullah said: They mentioned to Nafi that he used to walk between the two corners. He said: He would not walk except when he wanted to touch."
"5761","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, I heard Nafi claim that Ibn Umar narrated to him that Aishah bargained for Barirah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to prayer, and when he returned she said: They refused to sell to me except on condition of the wala. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wala is only for the one who frees."
"5762","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered prayer, raised his hands level with his shoulders, and when he bowed, and when he raised from bowing."
"5763","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abu Matar narrated to me, from Salim, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard thunder and thunderbolts, he said: O Allah, do not kill us by Your anger, nor destroy us by Your punishment, and grant us health before that."
"5764","Affan said: Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jar and the gourd."
"5765","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, that he heard Ibn Umar say at the beginning of his matter: It does not repel. He said: Then I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave license to them."
"5766","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you is invited to the invitation, let him answer, or he said: let him come to it. He said: And Ibn Umar would answer whether fasting or not fasting."
"5767","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The makers of these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"5768","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"5769","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5770","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, Ayyub informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qaza. Hammad said: Its explanation is that part of the boy's head is shaved and a lock is left of it."
"5771","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon hearing and obeying, he would dictate to us: In what you are able."
"5772","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: A man from Egypt came performing Hajj to the House. He said: He saw a group sitting and said: Who are these people? They said: Quraysh. He said: Who is the elder among them? They said: Abdullah ibn Umar. He said: O Ibn Umar, I ask you about something, or I adjure you, or I adjured you by the sanctity of this House: Do you know that Uthman fled on the day of Uhud? He said: Yes. He said: Do you know that he was absent from Badr and did not witness it? He said: Yes. He said: And do you know that he was absent from the pledge of al-Ridwan? He said: Yes. He said: So the Egyptian exclaimed Allah is most great. Ibn Umar said: Come, I will explain to you what you asked me about. As for his flight on the day of Uhud, I bear witness that Allah has pardoned him and forgiven him. As for his absence from Badr, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was under him, and she was ill, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: For you is the reward of a man who witnessed Badr, and his share. As for his absence from the pledge of al-Ridwan, if there had been anyone in the belly of Mecca more honored than Uthman, he would have sent him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Uthman, and the pledge of al-Ridwan was after Uthman had gone, so he struck with his hand upon his hand and said: This is for Uthman. He said: And Ibn Umar said: Go with this now along with you."
"5773","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May I buy gold with silver, or silver with gold? He said: If you take one of them for the other, your companion must not leave you while between you and him there is confusion."
"5774","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Quba riding and walking."
"5775","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog of livestock or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his deed every day. And he used to command that dogs be killed."
"5776","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5777","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday, let him wash."
"5778","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"5779","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of one of you by twenty-seven degrees."
"5780","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses the afternoon prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"5781","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imposed the zakah of breaking the fast as a sa of dates or a sa of barley upon every slave or free, young or old."
"5782","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, may one of us sleep while he is junub? He said: Yes, when he performs ablution."
"5783","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good in their forelocks forever until the Day of Resurrection."
"5784","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave gives sincere advice to his master and performs worship of his Lord well, he will have reward twice."
"5785","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man must not make a man stand from his seat and then sit in it, but make room and widen."
"5786","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the flesh of domestic donkeys."
"5787","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi and Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5788","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys palm trees that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the one who pollinated them, unless the one who bought them stipulates."
"5789","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people one day, and I came after he had finished, so I asked the people: What did he say? They said: He forbade making nabidh in the pitched vessel and the gourd."
"5790","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the hypocrite is like the stray sheep between the two flocks, going to this one at times and to this one at times; it does not know which of them to follow."
"5791","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pressed by travel, he would combine sunset and night prayers."
"5792","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: I divorced my wife at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was menstruating, and Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Command him to take her back until she becomes pure, then menstruates again, then when she becomes pure, let him divorce her if he wishes before he touches her, or keep her, for that is the waiting period which Allah commanded that women be divorced for."
"5793","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon the pulpit about the night prayer. He said: Two by two, and when one of you fears the morning, let him pray one, and it will make odd what he prayed."
"5794","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make the last of your prayer at night witr."
"5795","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced continual fasting in Ramadan, so the people practiced it, and he forbade them. It was said to him: You practice continual fasting. He said: I am not like you; I am fed and given drink."
"5796","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar gave a horse in the path of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to a man. Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Shall I buy the horse which I gave? He said: Do not buy it, and do not take back your charity."
"5797","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar saw a sira suit being sold at the door of the mosque and said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you bought it and wore it on Friday and for delegations when they come to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears this. Then there came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some suits of it, and he gave Umar a suit of them. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you clothed me with it after you said concerning it what you said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not clothe you with it to wear it; I only clothed you with it to sell it or to clothe another. He said: So Umar clothed with it a brother of his, an idolater from his mother, in Mecca."
"5798","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who lies about me, a house in the Fire will be built for him."
"5799","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that men and women used to perform ablution at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from one vessel all together."
"5800","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar called for prayer on a night of cold and wind, then said at the end of his call: Pray in your dwellings, pray in your dwellings, pray in the dwellings, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command the caller to prayer, when it was a cold night, or one of rain, or one of wind, while traveling: Pray in the dwellings."
"5801","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Amr informed me, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I went out with Ibn Umar on one of the roads of Madinah, and he saw young men who had set up a chicken, shooting at it, with every miss going to them, so he said: Who did this, and he became angry, and when they saw Ibn Umar they dispersed, then Ibn Umar said, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Allah has cursed whoever mutilates an animal."
"5802","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Jabalah informed me, he said: We were in Madinah among the detachment for Iraq, and Ibn al-Zubayr used to provide us with dates, and Ibn Umar used to pass by us and say: Do not eat two dates together, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade pairing dates, except that a man among you seeks permission from his brother."
"5803","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Jabalah informed me: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drags a garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5804","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah will set up a banner for the treacherous person on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: Indeed, this is the treachery of so-and-so."
"5805","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, on the authority of Yaqub al-Sadusi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the people on the day of the Conquest and said: Indeed, the blood money for quasi-intentional killing with the whip or the stick is aggravated: one hundred camels, among them forty pregnant camels carrying their young in their bellies. Indeed, every blood, wealth, and distinction from the pre-Islamic period is under my two feet, except for the providing of water to the pilgrims and the custodianship of the House, for I have confirmed them for their people."
"5806","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When supper is placed and the prayer is established, begin with supper. He said: And Ibn Umar once had his supper while hearing the recitation of the imam."
"5807","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to go early to the mosque on Friday, pray rakahs prolonging the standing in them, and when the imam finished, he returned to his house and prayed two rakahs, and said: This is what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do."
"5808","Affan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Iyad, meaning Ibn Laqit, narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Nuaym al-Araji, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar while I was with him about mutah, the mutah of women, and he became angry and said: By Allah, in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, we were not fornicators nor adulterers. Then he said: By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Before the false Messiah there will be thirty liars or more. My father said, and Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi said: Before the Day of Resurrection."
"5809","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Waqid ibn Abdullah, thus Affan said, but he is in fact Waqid ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of his father, that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"5810","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Waqid ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard his father narrating on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: Woe to you, or he said: Woe unto you, do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"5811","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Qudamah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Husayn al-Tamimi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Alqamah, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, on the authority of Yasar, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: Ibn Umar saw me while I was praying after dawn had risen and said: O Yasar, how many have you prayed? I said: I do not know. He said: You do not know. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us while we were praying this prayer and said: Let your present inform your absent that there is no prayer after the morning prayer except two prostrations."
"5812","Abu Muawiyah al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate against four, then Allah the Exalted revealed: You have nothing to do with the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers. He said: And Allah guided them to Islam."
"5813","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, and he mentioned similar to it."
"5814","Abu Muawiyah al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped at al-Aqiq and forbade coming to women at night on the night he arrives, but two young men disobeyed him, and both of them saw what they disliked."
"5815","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim informed me, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was visited while he was at al-Muarras in Dhu al-Hulayfah in the belly of the valley, and it was said: You are in a blessed plain."
"5816","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, one side of my waist wrapper keeps hanging loose unless I attend to it. He said: You are not among those who do it out of arrogance."
"5817","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the dream of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning Abu Bakr and Umar, he said: I saw the people gathered, then Abu Bakr stood and drew one or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and Allah forgives him, then Ibn al-Khattab stood, and it turned into a large bucket, and I never saw a strong outstanding man among the people working as he worked, until the people watered the camels to satisfaction."
"5818","Affan narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for I shall intercede for whoever dies in it."
"5819","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yala ibn Hakim narrated to me: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the drink made in earthen jars. He said: Then I met Ibn Abbas and said: Do you not wonder at Abu Abd al-Rahman, who claims that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the drink made in jars? Ibn Abbas said: He spoke the truth. I said: And what is the jar? He said: What is made of clay."
"5820","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that Ibn Umar narrated to him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden. I said to him: Our companions narrated to us on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, without raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. My father said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me that Ibn Umar narrated to him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said it."
"5821","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: I heard Nafi, Ibn Umar narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever frees his share in a slave, if he has wealth reaching his value, he shall be assessed the just value, otherwise he has freed what he has freed."
"5822","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim narrated to me, that Abdullah used to pray at night and perform witr while riding on his camel, not caring in which direction it faced. He said: And I saw Salim himself doing that, and Nafi informed me, on the authority of Abdullah, that he attributed that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5823","Affan narrated to us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, concerning: The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds: One of them will sink in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."
"5824","Affan narrated to us, Sakhr, meaning Ibn Juwayriyah, narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man says to his companion: O disbeliever, it applies to one of them; if the one to whom it was said is a disbeliever, then he is a disbeliever, otherwise what he said returns to him."
"5825","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Said informed us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Safwan ibn Muhriz, he said: While Ibn Umar was circumambulating the House, a man met him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how did you hear the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, speak about the private counsel? He said: The believer will draw near to his Lord on the Day of Resurrection as if he were a young calf, and He will place His cover over him, meaning He will screen him, then say: Do you recognize? He will say: My Lord, I recognize. Then He will say: Do you recognize? He will say: My Lord, I recognize. Then He will say: I concealed it for you in the world, and today I forgive it for you, and he will be given his record of good deeds. As for the disbelievers and hypocrites, they will be called out before all witnesses: These are those who lied against their Lord; indeed, the curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers. Said said, and Qatadah said: No one will be disgraced that day such that his disgrace remains hidden from any of the creation."
"5826","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Hisham informed us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, the freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he saw Abdullah ibn Umar praying voluntary prayer on his mount, facing other than the qiblah, and said: What is this, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do it."
"5827","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: While the people were praying in the mosque of Quba, a man came and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has had Quran revealed to him, and he has been commanded to face the Kabah. He said: So they turned around."
"5828","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."
"5829","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu al-Shatha, he said: It was said to Ibn Umar: We enter upon our rulers and say something, and when we leave we say otherwise. He said: We used to consider this as hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5830","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, on the authority of Salim, and Nafi, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he returned from a military expedition, Hajj, or Umrah, would begin by saying takbir three times, then say: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is capable of all things, returning, repentant, worshipping, prostrating, praising our Lord, Allah has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone."
"5831","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, on the authority of Salim, and Nafi, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do so, and he mentioned similar to it."
"5832","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Ata, meaning Ibn al-Saib, on the authority of Muharib, meaning Ibn Dithar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"5833","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Bakkar, meaning Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jundah, that he asked Tawus about drink, and he informed him, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade earthen jars and gourds."
"5834","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the edge of the sun rises, delay the prayer until it appears fully, and when the edge of the sun disappears, delay the prayer until it has set."
"5835","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Let none of you intend prayer at the rising of the sun nor at its setting, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."
"5836","Waki narrated to us, Said ibn Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Subayh al-Hanafi, he said: I prayed beside Ibn Umar and placed my hand on my waist, so he struck my hand, and when he had prayed he said: This is resting the arms on the sides in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to forbid it."
"5837","Waki narrated to us, Thabit ibn Umarah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and there is no prayer after dawn until the sun rises."
"5838","Waki narrated to us, on the authority of al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When travel pressed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he would combine Maghrib and Isha."
"5839","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I had no place to sleep nor shelter in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except in the mosque."
"5840","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a spear used to be planted for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the two Eids, and he would pray toward it."
"5841","Waki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydullah, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed toward a camel."
"5842","Waki narrated to us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, on the authority of Atiyah al-Awfi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: One prostration of these people is longer than three prostrations of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5843","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to raise his hands level with his shoulders."
"5844","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, meaning he was brought unripe-date drink in the mosque of al-Fadikh and drank it, and for that reason it was so named."
"5845","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter."
"5846","Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, she said: Ibn Umar saw a boy with tufts on his head and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade boys to shave qaza."
"5847","Waki narrated to us, al-Umari narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you eats or drinks, let him not eat with his left nor drink with his left, for Satan eats and drinks with his left."
"5848","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim narrated to me, on the authority of his father, that he used to hear him narrating on the authority of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he appointed Usamah ibn Zayd, and it reached him that the people criticized Usamah and impugned his command, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among the people and said, as Salim narrated to me: Indeed, you criticize Usamah and impugn his command, although you did that with his father before, and he was indeed worthy of command, and he was indeed the most beloved of all people to me, and this son of his after him is indeed the most beloved of people to me, so treat him well, for he is among your best. Salim said: I never heard Abdullah narrate this hadith except that he said: Except Fatimah."
"5849","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim narrated to me, concerning the dream of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the epidemic of Madinah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I saw a black woman with disheveled hair who went out of Madinah until she stood at Mahyaah, so I interpreted that its epidemic was transferred to Mahyaah, and it is al-Juhfah."
"5850","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: He forbade the sale of wala and its gift. He said: I said: Did you hear it from Ibn Umar? He said: Yes, and his son Hamzah asked him about it."
"5851","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a ring of gold, so the people took their rings of gold, then one day he stood and said: I used to wear this ring, then he cast it away, so the people cast away their rings."
"5852","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"5853","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, Qarn for the people of Najd, al-Juhfah for the people of Syria, and they claimed that he appointed Yalamlam for the people of Yemen."
"5854","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man of Quraysh said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I buy and sell and get deceived. He said: When that happens, say: No cheating."
"5855","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Mundhir informed me, he said: We were in a garden belonging to us or to Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, shooting, and the prayer came, so Ubaydullah stood toward the water channel of the garden containing a camel skin and began performing ablution in it, so I said: Do you perform ablution in it while this skin is in it? He said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When water is two qullahs or three, it does not become impure."
"5856","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Yamar: I said to Ibn Umar: We have men with us who claim that the matter is in their own hands; if they wish they act, and if they wish they do not act. He said: Inform them that I am free of them and that they are free of me. Then he said: Jibril, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Muhammad, what is Islam? He said: You worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House. He said: If I do that, am I a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: You spoke the truth. He said: What is ihsan? He said: You fear Allah the Exalted as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: If I do that, am I a doer of good? He said: Yes. He said: You spoke the truth. He said: What is faith? He said: You believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the resurrection after death, Paradise, Hell, and the decree, all of it. He said: If I do that, am I a believer? He said: Yes. He said: You spoke the truth."
"5857","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Suwayd, on the authority of Yahya ibn Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with similar to it. He said: And Jibril, peace be upon him, used to come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the form of Dihyah."
"5858","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us: He heard Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Aslam, may Allah grant it peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it."
"5859","Affan narrated to us, Sakhr, meaning Ibn Juwayriyah, narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: While I was at a well drawing from it, Abu Bakr and Umar came, so Abu Bakr took the bucket and drew one or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and Allah forgives him, then Umar ibn al-Khattab took it from Abu Bakr, and it turned into a large bucket in his hand, and I never saw an outstanding strong man among the people working as he worked, until the people watered the camels to satisfaction."
"5860","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar informed me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to Quba riding and walking."
"5861","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar informed me: I heard Ibn Umar say, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he has taken possession of it."
"5862","Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafii, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to us, Malik informed us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you sell upon the sale of another, and he forbade najsh, and he forbade the sale of the fetus of a fetus, and he forbade muzabanah, and muzabanah is selling fruit for dates by measure, and selling grapes for raisins by measure."
"5863","Musab narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade najsh, similar to it."
"5864","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, on the authority of Uqayl, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded that blades be sharpened, that they be concealed from animals, and that when one of you slaughters, he should do it well."
"5865","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Use the siwak, for it purifies the mouth and pleases the Lord."
"5866","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah loves that His concessions be acted upon as He dislikes that His disobedience be committed."
"5867","Qutaybah narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sakhr Humayd ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There will be in this nation a transformation; indeed, that will be among those who deny the decree and the heretics."
"5868","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, on the authority of Uqayl, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamzah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: While I was asleep, I was brought a cup of milk, so I drank from it, then I gave my remainder to Umar ibn al-Khattab. They said: How did you interpret it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Knowledge."
"5869","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, and Wahb had met Ibn Umar; it is not in the book of Ibn Malik: that Ibn Umar saw a shepherd of sheep in an unsuitable place, and Ibn Umar had seen a better place than it, so Ibn Umar said: Woe to you, O shepherd, move them, for I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Every shepherd is responsible for his flock."
"5870","Musab narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade najsh."
"5871","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Husayn, meaning Ibn Numayr, Abu Mihsan narrated to us, on the authority of al-Fadl ibn Atiyah, Salim narrated to me, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out on the day of Eid and began by praying without adhan or iqamah, then he preached. He said: And Ata narrated to me, on the authority of Jabir, similar to that."
"5872","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Abu Mihsan ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of al-Fadl ibn Atiyah, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"5873","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, on the authority of Harb ibn Qays, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah loves that His concessions be acted upon as He dislikes that His disobedience be committed."
"5874","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghiyath, narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydullah, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We used to drink while standing and eat while walking in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"5875","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydullah, on the authority of Nafi, he said: I saw Ibn Umar touch the Stone, then kiss his hand, and say: I have not left it since I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do it."
"5876","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, Abu Usamah narrated to us, on the authority of Usamah, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He used to slaughter his sacrifice at the prayer place on the day of sacrifice, and he mentioned that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do it."
"5877","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it from Abdullah, Mutamir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Uthaym, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: What is permissible in nursing with respect to witnesses? He said: A man or a woman. And I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah."
"5878","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamzah informed us, Salim informed me, Ibn Umar informed me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Did you write this letter? He said: Yes. By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, faith has not changed in my heart, but there was no man of Quraysh except that he had kin and household who would protect his family for him, and I wrote a letter hoping that Allah would thereby protect my family. Umar said: Permit me regarding him. He said: Would you have killed him? He said: Yes, if you permit me. He said: How do you know; perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish."
"5879","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman said, and I heard it myself from Harun ibn Maruf, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to go out to the two Eids by one road and return by another road."
"5880","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar narrating, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Odd and loves the odd. Nafi said: And Ibn Umar would not do anything except in odd numbers."
"5881","Abdullah narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, he said: I saw Ghaylan, meaning al-Qadari, crucified at the gate of Damascus."
"5882","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People are like a hundred camels; you can hardly find among them a mount fit for riding, or when will you find among them a mount. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We know nothing better than a hundred like it except the believing man."
"5883","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life, but they are a sign among the signs of Allah, blessed and exalted, so when you see them, pray."
"5884","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah, meaning Ibn Ismah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Prayer was fifty, washing from major impurity seven times, and washing from urine seven times, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept asking until prayer was made five, washing from major impurity once, and washing from urine once."
"5885","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifah, narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sell a dinar for two dinars, nor a dirham for two dirhams, nor a sa for two sas, for I fear rima for you, and rima is riba. A man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a man selling a horse for horses, and a fine camel for camels? He said: No harm, if it is hand to hand."
"5886","Husayn narrated to us, Khalaf narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar: There was a palm trunk in the mosque against which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to lean his back when it was Friday or when an affair occurred about which he wanted to address the people, so they said: Shall we not make for you, O Messenger of Allah, something to the measure of your standing? He said: It is no burden on you to do so. So they made for him a pulpit with three steps. He said: Then he sat upon it. He said: Then the trunk moaned as cattle low, out of grief for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he embraced it and wiped it until it calmed."
"5887","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Ibn Dinar informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he took a ring of gold and wore it, so the people took rings of gold, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and said: I used to wear this ring, and I shall never wear it again, so he cast it away, and the people cast away their rings."
"5888","Sulayman informed us, Ismail informed us, Ibn Dinar informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition and appointed Usamah ibn Zayd over them, so some people impugned his command, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and said: If you impugn his command, you have impugned the command of his father before, and by Allah, he was indeed worthy of command, and he was indeed among the most beloved people to me, and this one is indeed among the most beloved people to me after him."
"5889","Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, Ismail informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah informed me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata ibn Alqamah, that he was sitting with Ibn Umar in the market, with Salamah ibn al-Azraq beside him, when a funeral passed followed by weeping, so Abdullah ibn Umar said: If the family of this dead man left weeping, it would be better for their dead. Salamah ibn al-Azraq said: Do you say that, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: Yes, I say it. He said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, when a dead person of Marwans family died and the women gathered weeping over him, Marwan said: Stand, O Abd al-Malik, and forbid them from weeping. Abu Hurayrah said: Leave them, for a dead person of the family of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, and the women gathered weeping over him, so Umar ibn al-Khattab stood forbidding them and driving them away, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave them, O Ibn al-Khattab, for the eye is tearful, the heart is stricken, and the covenant is recent. Ibn Umar said: Did you hear this from Abu Hurayrah? He said: Yes. He said: Relating it on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes. He said: Then Allah and His Messenger know best."
"5890","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed him, that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah sends punishment upon a people, the punishment strikes whoever is among them, then they will be raised according to their deeds."
"5891","Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Sabbah al-Ayli, he said: I heard Yazid ibn Abi Sumayyah say: I heard Ibn Umar say: Whatever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about the waist wrapper applies to the shirt."
"5892","Surayj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha at al-Muhassab, then slept a short sleep, then entered and circumambulated the House."
"5893","Ishaq, meaning Ibn al-Tabba, narrated to us, Malik informed me, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Sad, on the authority of Amr ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tawus al-Yamani, he said: I met people among the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Everything is by decree. He said: And I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Everything is by decree, even incapacity and shrewdness."
"5894","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed me, on the authority of Said ibn Abi Said, on the authority of Ubayd ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Abdullah ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I saw you do four things I have not seen any of your companions do. He said: What are they, O Ibn Jurayj? He said: I saw you touch only the two Yemeni corners, I saw you wear hairless sandals, I saw you dye with yellow, and I saw that when in Makkah, people enter ihram when they see the crescent, but you do not enter ihram until the day of Tarwiyah. Abdullah said: As for the corners, I did not see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, touch except the two Yemeni ones. As for sandals, I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wear sandals without hair and perform ablution in them, and I love to wear them. As for yellow dye, I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dye with it, and I love to dye with it. As for entering ihram, I did not see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enter ihram until his mount set out with him."
"5895","Ishaq ibn Isa and Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us in a detachment, and when we met the enemy we fled in the first assault, then we arrived at Madinah by night among a group, hid, then said: If we went out to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and apologized to him. So we went out, and when we met him we said: We are the deserters, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Rather, you are those who return to fight, and I am your support. Aswad ibn Amir said: And I am the support of every Muslim."
"5896","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The best of righteousness is a mans maintaining ties with his fathers loved ones after he has passed away."
"5897","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever dies without obedience to Allah dies with no proof for him, and whoever dies having withdrawn his hand from allegiance, his death is a death of misguidance."
"5898","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid ibn Abi Imran, on the authority of Nafi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays the morning prayer has the protection of Allah, so do not betray Allahs protection, for whoever betrays His protection, Allah will pursue him until He throws him upon his face."
"5899","Musa, meaning Ibn Dawud, narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd ibn Hani, on the authority of Abbas ibn Julayd al-Hajari, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, how often should the slave be pardoned? He remained silent, then he repeated, and he remained silent, then he repeated, and he said: He should be pardoned seventy times each day."
"5900","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever buys food by measure or weight, let him not sell it until he has taken possession of it."
"5901","Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: All of you are shepherds and all of you are responsible for his flock. The ruler is a shepherd over his subjects and he is responsible for them. The man is a shepherd over the people of his house and he is responsible for them. The slave is a shepherd over the wealth of his master and he is responsible for it. And the woman is a shepherd over the house of her husband and she is responsible for it."
"5902","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The parable of this nation, or he said my nation, and the parable of the Jews and the Christians is like the parable of a man who said: Who will work for me from the morning until midday for one qirat? The Jews said: We will. And they did. Then he said: Who will work for me from midday until Asr for one qirat? The Christians said: We will. And they worked. And you Muslims work from the Asr prayer until the night for two qirats. So the Jews and the Christians became angry and said: We did more work and received less reward. He said: Have I wronged you anything of your reward? They said: No. He said: That is My bounty, I give it to whom I will."
"5903","He said: I heard this hadith from Yahya ibn Said and I did not write it down: from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The Jews worked such and the Christians such, similar to the hadith of Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar about the story of the Jews."
"5904","My father said: And Muammal also narrated it to us from Sufyan, similar to the hadith of Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar as well."
"5905","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he pointed with his hand toward the east: Tribulation is here, tribulation is here, where the horn of Satan rises."
"5906","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When the pilgrim in ihram cannot find sandals, let him wear the leather socks, cutting them below the ankles."
"5907","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Salim, who said: When al-Bayda was mentioned in the presence of Ibn Umar, he would revile it and say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram only from Dhu al-Hulayfa."
"5908","Muammal narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad, meaning Ibn Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If people knew what is in being alone, no one would travel at night alone."
"5909","My father said: And Muammal narrated it another time and he did not say from Ibn Umar."
"5910","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: Muammal had heard from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, meaning some hadiths, and he had also heard from Ibn Jurayj."
"5911","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your appointed time compared to the appointed time of those who were before you is like what is between the Asr prayer and the setting of the sun."
"5912","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about: The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years, in sweat up to the halves of their ears."
"5913","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, he said: Muharib ibn Dithar said to me: What did you hear Said ibn Jubayr mention from Ibn Abbas about al-Kawthar? I said: I heard him saying: Ibn Abbas said: It is the abundant good. Muharib said: Glory be to Allah, how little falls to Ibn Abbas of a saying. I heard Ibn Umar saying: When: Indeed We have granted you al-Kawthar, was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is a river in Paradise, its banks of gold, flowing over pebbles of pearl and ruby, its drink sweeter than honey, whiter than milk, cooler than snow, and more fragrant than the scent of musk. He said: Ibn Abbas spoke the truth, this by Allah is the abundant good."
"5914","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says to his brother: O disbeliever, one of them has returned with it."
"5915","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: A banner will be raised for every treacherous person on the Day of Resurrection."
"5916","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the nabidh of the earthen jar. He said: I came to Abdullah ibn Abbas and informed him, and he said: Ibn Umar spoke the truth. He said: I said: What is the jar? He said: Everything made of clay."
"5917","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade continuous fasting without break. They said: Do you not yourself practice wisal? He said: I am fed and given drink."
"5918","Ishaq narrated to us, I heard Malik narrating from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"5919","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a detachment toward Najd, among them was Abdullah ibn Umar. Their shares were twelve camels each, and they were given an extra camel each."
"5920","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever frees a share in a slave, and he has wealth reaching the price of the slave, then he is assessed its just value, and he gives his partners their shares, and the slave is freed upon him. Otherwise, what he freed is freed."
"5921","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the solitary person by twenty-seven degrees."
"5922","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped at al-Batha which is at Dhu al-Hulayfa and prayed there, and that Ibn Umar used to do that."
"5923","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The parable of the companion of the Quran is like the parable of the owner of hobbled camels. If he tends them he holds them, and if he releases them they go away."
"5924","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: We used to buy food in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would send to us one who ordered us to move it from the place where we bought it to another place before we sold it."
"5925","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the killing of dogs and said: Whoever keeps a dog except a livestock dog or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his deeds every day."
"5926","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you dies, his seat is shown to him morning and evening. If he is of the people of Paradise, then of the people of Paradise, and if he is of the people of Hell, then of the people of Hell. It is said: This is your seat until Allah raises you to it on the Day of Resurrection."
"5927","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, and Ishaq said: Malik informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the Kaba, and with him were Uthman ibn Talha, Usama ibn Zayd, and Bilal. He closed it. When he came out, I asked Bilal: What did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do? He said: He left two pillars on his right, one pillar on his left, and three pillars behind him. Then he prayed, and between him and the qibla were three cubits. Ishaq said: The House on that day was upon six pillars, and he did not mention the one between him and the qibla."
"5928","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: They used to perform ablution together. I said to Malik: Men and women? He said: Yes. I said: In the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes."
"5929","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Aisha wanted to buy a slave girl to free her. Her family said: We will sell to you on condition that her wala is for us. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Let that not prevent you, for wala belongs to the one who frees."
"5930","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No person who has something about which to make a bequest has the right to spend two nights except that his will is written with him."
"5931","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his companions: Do not enter upon these punished people except that you are weeping. If you are not weeping, do not enter upon them, lest what befell them befall you."
"5932","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek the Night of Decree in the last seven nights of Ramadan."
"5933","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever man says to his brother: O disbeliever, one of them has returned with it."
"5934","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: While the people were in Quba in the dawn prayer, a comer came to them and said: A Quran has been sent down to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, tonight, and he has been ordered to face the Kaba, so face it. Their faces were toward Sham, so they turned toward the Kaba."
"5935","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Qatan ibn Wahb, or Wahb ibn Qatan al-Laythi, Ishaq doubted, from Yuhannas, freed slave of al-Zubayr, who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a freed slave woman of his came to him and mentioned hardship of condition and that she wanted to leave Madina. He said to her: Stay, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: None of you endures its hardship and severity except that I will be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"5936","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I asked Malik about a man performing witr while riding. He said: Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab informed me, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed witr while riding."
"5937","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the night prayer. He said: Two by two. If you fear the dawn, then one."
"5938","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the Jews greet you, they say: Death be upon you. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So say: And upon you."
"5939","Surayj narrated to us, Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to me, that he went out among a group of his companions as pilgrims until they reached Makka. They entered the mosque, touched the Stone, then circumambulated the House seven times, then prayed two rakas behind the Maqam. Then there was a bulky man in a waist-wrapper and cloak raising his voice to us at the cistern. We went to him, and I asked about him, and they said: Ibn Abbas. When we came to him, he said: Who are you? We said: People of the east, and there were people of al-Yamama. He said: Pilgrims or umra performers? I said: Rather pilgrims. He said: You have broken your hajj. I said: I have performed hajj many times and I used to do so. He said: We went on our way until Ibn Umar came. I said: O Ibn Umar, we arrived, and I told him our story and informed him of what he said: You have broken your hajj. He said: I remind you by Allah, did you go out as pilgrims? We said: Yes. He said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar performed hajj, all of them did like what you did."
"5940","Surayj narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, from Ibn Abi Num, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him asking about the blood of the mosquito. Ibn Umar said to him: From where are you? He said: I am of the people of Iraq. He said: Look at this one, he asks me about the blood of the mosquito while they killed the son of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: They are my two sweet basils in this world."
"5941","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ikrima, from Rafi ibn Hunayn Abu al-Mughira, from Ibn Umar, that he informed him that he saw a place of relief for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, facing the qibla."
"5942","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The charity of breaking the fast is upon every Muslim, young or old, free or slave, male or female: a sa of dates or a sa of barley."
"5943","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to trot three circuits from the Stone to the Stone and walk four, and he informed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do it."
"5944","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to stone the Jamra on the Day of Sacrifice riding, and the rest of it walking, and he informed them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do that."
"5945","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar would not touch anything of the House except the two Yemeni corners. He would touch them and inform that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do it."
"5946","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as pilgrims, and we did not leave ihram from anything until we left ihram on the Day of Sacrifice."
"5947","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to give my property at Thamgh as charity. He said: Keep its principal and make its fruit a public benefit."
"5948","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I never fasted Arafa, nor did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fast it, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar."
"5949","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, who said: I sat with Ibn Umar, and with him was a man speaking to him. I joined them, so he struck my chest with his hand and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When two converse privately, do not sit with them until you seek their permission."
"5950","Surayj narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to dye his beard yellow, wear Sibti sandals, touch the two corners, recite talbiya when his mount rose with him, and he informed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do it."
"5951","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to Umar a suit of silk or sira or something like this. He saw it upon him and said: I did not send it to you to wear it. It is only the clothing of one who has no share. I only sent it to you so that you may benefit from it."
"5952","Aswad narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to Umar a suit, and he mentioned it."
"5953","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sinan ibn Harun narrated to us, from Kulayb ibn Wail, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned a tribulation, then a man passed by and he said: This veiled one will be killed in it that day unjustly. He said: I looked, and it was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him."
"5954","Aswad narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Qatada, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he was asked about the nabidh of the earthen jar. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it. He said: I came to Ibn Abbas and said to him: I asked Abu Abd al-Rahman about the nabidh of the jar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it. He said: Abu Abd al-Rahman spoke the truth. He said: I said: What is the jar? He said: Everything made of clay."
"5955","Aswad narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, I heard Salama ibn Kuhayl mentioning from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I know a tree benefited from like the believer. It is the one whose leaves are not shed. Ibn Umar said: I wanted to say: It is the date palm, but I was in awe of Umar. Then I heard him afterward saying: It is the date palm."
"5956","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting: Aswad and Husayn narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muawiya ibn Ishaq, from Abu Salih, from a man of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I think Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever mutilates one possessing a soul then does not repent, Allah will mutilate him on the Day of Resurrection. Husayn said: Whoever mutilates one possessing a soul."
"5957","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, three times, and he recited the prostration chapter in the obligatory prayer."
"5958","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utba narrated to us, Ikrima ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Umar about a woman whom a man wanted to marry while he was leaving Makka intending umra or hajj. He said: Do not marry her while you are in ihram. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it."
"5959","Husayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a woman killed on the day of the conquest of Makka and said: She would not have been fighting. Then he forbade killing women and children."
"5960","Husayn and Ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, the meaning, they said: Shuba narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi and Ibrahim ibn Maysara, that they heard Tawus saying: By Allah, a man came to Ibn Umar and said: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid the nabidh of the jar? He said: Yes. And Ibrahim added for them al-Dubba. Ibn Abi Bukayr said: Ibrahim ibn Maysara said in his hadith: and al-Dubba."
"5961","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Nafi and Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying upon this minbar: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him wash."
"5962","Husayn narrated to us, from Jarir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the dabb lizard. He said: I do not eat it nor do I forbid it."
"5963","Husayn narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim and Hamza, sons of Abdullah ibn Umar, that Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to them that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Ill omen is in the horse, the woman, and the house."
"5964","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Zamaa narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believer is not stung from the same hole twice."
"5965","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to touch the Yemeni corner and the Black one in every tawaf, and he would not touch the other two corners which face the Hijr."
"5966","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, I heard Salama ibn Kuhayl narrating from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the sun was over Quayqian after Asr. He said: Your lifespans compared to the lifespans of those who passed are only like what remains of the day compared to what has passed of it."
"5967","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Umar asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Janaba befalls me at night. He ordered him to wash his private part, perform ablution, and sleep."
"5968","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For every treacherous person there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection known by it."
"5969","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Aslam, may Allah grant them peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them, and Usayya, those who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"5970","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: A man said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: I am deceived in buying. He said: When you bargain, say: No deception. The man used to say it."
"5971","Al-Fadl narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a ring of gold, so the people took rings of gold. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I took a ring of gold and I have cast it away. He said: I will never wear it again. So the people cast away their rings."
"5972","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man with his hand fallen in prayer and said: Do not sit like this. This is only the sitting of those who are punished."
"5973","Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamza al-Umari narrated to us, Salim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of you is able to be like the owner of the faraq of rice, let him be like him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the owner of the faraq of rice? He said: Three went out, the sky clouded over them, so they entered a cave. A rock came from the top of the mountain until it sealed the door upon them. They tried it but could not move it. One of them said to another: You have fallen into a grave matter, so let each man supplicate by the best he did, that Allah the Exalted may save us from this. One of them said: O Allah, You know that I had two aged old parents, and I used to milk their milk and bring it to them while they had slept. I would spend the night standing with their milk in my hand, disliking to begin with anyone before them or to wake them from their sleep, while my children cried around me. If You know that I did it only from fear of You, relieve us. He said: The rock moved. The second said: O Allah, You know that I had a cousin, nothing You created dearer to me than her. I sought her for herself, and she said: No, by Allah, for less than a hundred dinars. I gathered them and paid them to her, until when I sat from her as a man sits, she said: Fear Allah and do not break the seal except by its right. So I rose from her. If You know that I did it only from fear of You, relieve us. He said: The rock shifted until the sky appeared. The third said: O Allah, You know that I hired a laborer for a faraq of rice. In the evening I offered him his due, but he refused to take it, left me and went away. I was scrupulous about it, invested it for him and tended it until I bought from it cows and their herdsman. He met me after a while and said: Fear Allah, give me my wage and do not wrong me. I said: Go to those cows and their herdsman and take them. He said: Fear Allah and do not mock me. I said: I am not mocking you. He went and drove them away. If You know that I did it only seeking Your pleasure, fearing You, relieve us. The rock rolled away, and they went out walking."
"5974","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Nafi narrated to us, that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: While three men were walking, rain seized them, so they sheltered in a cave in a mountain. While they were in it, a rock fell from the mountain and closed upon them. He mentioned the hadith with similar meaning."
"5975","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, I heard Nafi saying: Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent out for the killing of dogs. I was among those sent. We killed the dogs until we found a woman who had come from the desert, and we killed a dog of hers."
"5976","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqba narrated to me, from Salim, that he narrated to him about the dream of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the epidemic of Madina, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I saw a black woman with disheveled head leaving Madina until she settled at Mahy aa, which is al-Juhfa. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, interpreted that the epidemic of Madina was transferred to al-Juhfa."
"5977","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in what he narrates from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, who said: Whatever servant of My servants goes out striving in My path seeking My pleasure, I guarantee that I return him with what he obtains of reward and booty, and if I take his soul, that I forgive him, have mercy on him, and admit him to Paradise."
"5978","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from al-Mughira ibn Salman, who said: Ibn Umar said: I memorized from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ten prayers: two rakas before the dawn prayer, two rakas before the noon prayer, two rakas after the noon prayer, two rakas after the sunset prayer, and two rakas after the night prayer."
"5979","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Mihran, freed slave of Quraysh, narrated to us: I heard my grandfather narrating from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not sleep except with the siwak with him. When he woke, he began with the siwak."
"5980","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Mihran narrated to us, that he heard his grandfather narrating from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah have mercy on a man who prayed four before Asr."
"5981","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Said ibn Amr, who said: I came to Ibn Umar while he had narrated the hadith. I said: What did he narrate? They said: He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive them, and Aslam, may Allah grant them peace."
"5982","Abd al-Samad narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid al-Bunani, who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I buy these walls in which are grapes, and we cannot sell them all as grapes until we press them. He said: So you ask me about the price of wine. I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raised his head to the sky, then bowed and scratched in the earth and said: Woe to the Children of Israel. Umar said: O Prophet of Allah, your saying about the Children of Israel has frightened us. He said: There is no harm upon you from that. When fats were forbidden to them, they melted them, sold them, and ate their price. Likewise the price of wine is forbidden upon you."
"5983","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Husayn, meaning al-Muallim, narrated to us, from Ibn Burayda, Ibn Umar narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say when he took his bed: Praise be to Allah who sufficed me, sheltered me, fed me, gave me drink, who bestowed upon me and favored, who gave me and granted abundantly. Praise be to Allah in every state. O Allah, Lord of everything, King of everything, God of everything, and to You belongs everything, I seek refuge in You from the Fire."
"5984","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sakhr, meaning Ibn Juwayriya, narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped with the people in the year of Tabuk. He stopped them at al-Hijr at the houses of Thamud. The people drew water from the wells from which Thamud used to drink, kneaded from it, and set the pots with meat. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered them, so they poured out the pots and fed the dough to the camels. Then he moved with them until he stopped them at the well from which the she-camel used to drink. He forbade them to enter upon the people who were punished, saying: I fear what befell them will befall you, so do not enter upon them."
"5985","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that there was with him a man of the people of Kufa who began narrating to him about al-Mukhtar. Ibn Umar said: If it is as you say, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Before the Hour there are thirty liars."
"5986","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a man: You did such and such. He said: No, by the One there is no god but He, O Messenger of Allah, I did not do it. He said: Yes, you did it, but you have been forgiven for sincerity."
"5987","Azhar ibn Sad Abu Bakr al-Samman narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham. O Allah, bless for us our Yemen. They said: And our Najd. He said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham. O Allah, bless for us our Yemen. They said: And our Najd. He said: There are earthquakes and trials. From it, or he said: by it, rises the horn of Satan."
"5988","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Hanzala mentioning from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Of the fitra are shaving the pubes, trimming the nails, and cutting the mustache. Ishaq once said: And cutting the mustaches."
"5989","Abu Jafar al-Madaini narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadala informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, who narrated to him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza."
"5990","Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting: Husayn narrated to me, he said: Al-Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, that Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to him, that Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, narrated to him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza."
"5991","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hanzala narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he disliked a mark in an image and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade striking the face."
"5992","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: From wheat comes wine, from dates comes wine, from barley comes wine, from raisins comes wine, and from honey comes wine."
"5993","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the people of Paradise are in Paradise and the people of Hell are in Hell, death is brought until it is made to stand between Paradise and Hell. Then it is slaughtered. Then a caller calls: O people of Paradise, eternity without death. O people of Hell, eternity without death. The people of Paradise increase in joy to their joy, and the people of Hell increase in sorrow to their sorrow."
"5994","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A vow neither brings anything forward nor delays it. By a vow is only extracted from the miser."
"5995","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yunus ibn al-Qasim al-Hanafi, a Yamami, informed us, I heard Ikrima ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever magnifies himself in his soul or walks arrogantly in his gait will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"5996","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to him, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life, but they are a sign of the signs of Allah. When you see them, pray."
"5997","Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd informed me, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate against men of the polytheists, naming them by their names, until Allah sent down: You have nothing of the affair, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers. So he left that."
"5998","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywa said: Abu Uthman informed me, that Abdullah ibn Dinar informed him, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Of the worst lies are one who claims to other than his father, one who shows his eyes in sleep what they did not see, and one who changes the landmarks of the land."
"5999","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, my father Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Qays ibn Makhrama, who said: I came from the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Awf at Quba upon a mule of mine, having prayed in it. I met Abdullah ibn Umar walking. When I saw him, I descended from my mule, then I said: Ride, O uncle. He said: O son of my brother, if I wanted to ride beasts I would ride, but I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walking to this mosque until he came and prayed in it. I love to walk to it as I saw him walking. He refused to ride and went on his way."
"6000","Muhammad ibn Abdullah Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Nafi, who said: When Abdullah ibn Umar sat in prayer, he placed his hands on his knees, pointed with his finger, and followed it with his gaze. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is harder upon Satan than iron, meaning the index finger."
"6001","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Qatan ibn Wahb ibn Uwaymir, from Yuhannas, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one endures its hardship and severity except I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6002","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Husayn, meaning al-Muallim, narrated to us, he said: Yahya said to me, Abu Qilabah narrated to me, Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: A fire will emerge before the Day of Resurrection from the sea of Hadramawt, gathering the people. They said: What do you command us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you is al-Sham."
"6003","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, from Abd Allah, that he said: A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us to wear of clothes in ihram? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not wear shirts, nor trousers, nor turbans, nor burnuses, nor khuffs, unless one has no sandals, then let him wear the two khuffs below the ankles, and do not wear anything of clothes touched by wars or saffron, and the woman in ihram shall not wear niqab nor wear gloves."
"6004","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, that Abd Allah would make his camel kneel at al-Batha which is at Dhu al-Hulayfah, at which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would make his camel kneel and pray there."
"6005","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head, and a group of his Companions shaved, and some of them shortened, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave, once or twice, then he said: And those who shorten."
"6006","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When two men trade, each one of them has the choice as long as they have not separated and were together, and one of them gives the other the choice; if one of them gives the other the choice and they trade upon that, the sale becomes binding, and if they separate after they traded and neither one of them abandoned the sale, the sale has become binding."
"6007","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring of gold made, and he would place its stone on the inside of his palm when he wore it, so the people made rings, then he sat on the minbar and took it off and said: I used to wear this ring and place its stone inside, and he threw it away, then he said: By Allah, I will never wear it again, so the people discarded their rings."
"6008","Hashim narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, from Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The night prayer is two by two, so if you fear the dawn, then pray witr with one, and make the last of your prayer witr."
"6009","Hashim narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The righteous dream is a part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"6010","Hashim narrated to us, Jisr narrated to us, Sulayt narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you sense fever, extinguish it with cold water."
"6011","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: O Ibn Umar, I am asking you about something you narrate to me. He said: Yes. And he mentioned Uthman, so Ibn Umar said: As for his absence from Badr, his wife was the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she was ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have the reward of a man who witnessed Badr and his share. And as for his absence from Bayat al-Ridwan, if there had been one in the belly of Makkah more honored than Uthman, he would have sent him, so he sent Uthman, and Bayat al-Ridwan was after Uthman had gone to Makkah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said with his right hand: This is the hand of Uthman, and he struck it with his other hand upon it and said: This is for Uthman. So Ibn Umar said to him: Go with this now with you."
"6012","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir and Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade naqir, muzaffat, and dubba."
"6013","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Jumhan, he said: I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, or another besides me said to him: Why do I see you walking while the people are running? So he said: If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking, and if I run, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running, and I am an old man."
"6014","Hashim narrated to us, Asim, meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, narrated to us, from his father, he said: Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the people knew what I know about being alone, no rider would ever travel by night alone."
"6015","Hashim narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing the prayer, giving zakah, hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"6016","Hashim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, he said: I departed with Ibn Umar on the day of departure, and a Yemeni caravan passed by us, their saddles of leather and the bridles of their camels of leather straps, so Abd Allah ibn Umar said: Whoever loves to look at the caravan most resembling the one that came for Hajj this year to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions when they came in the Farewell Hajj, let him look at this caravan."
"6017","Hashim ibn al-Qasim and Ishaq ibn Isa both said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, and Hashim said: Layth narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Salim, from his father, that he said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping of the House except the two Yemeni corners."
"6018","Waki narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I went out with Ibn Umar to meet the pilgrims, greeting them before they became soiled."
"6019","Ishaq narrated to me, Layth narrated to us, and Hashim said: Layth narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House, with Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal, and Uthman ibn Talhah al-Hajabi, and they closed it upon them; when they opened, I was the first to enter, and I met Bilal and asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in it? He said: Yes, between the two Yemeni pillars. Hashim said: He prayed between the two pillars."
"6020","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Layth narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, and Yunus said: Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said while upon the minbar: Whoever of you comes to Friday, let him perform ghusl."
"6021","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his voice with talbiyah, his hair matted, saying: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wal-ni'mata laka wal-mulk, la sharika lak, not adding to these words."
"6022","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah informed us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise go to Paradise and the people of Fire go to Fire, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and Fire, then it will be slaughtered, then a caller will call: O people of Paradise, no death; O people of Fire, no death; so the people of Paradise increase in joy upon their joy, and the people of Fire increase in grief upon their grief."
"6023","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise go to Paradise, and he mentioned the like of it."
"6024","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If three are together, two shall not converse privately excluding the third, and none of you shall make his brother stand from his seat then sit in it."
"6025","Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, my father informed me, from al-Zuhri, and he mentioned a hadith, and he said: Salim said: Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing upon the minbar saying: Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the tailless, for they seek eyesight and cause miscarriage."
"6026","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Each of you is a shepherd and responsible for his flock: the imam is a shepherd and responsible for his flock, and the man among his family is a shepherd and responsible for his flock, and the woman is a shepherdess in the house of her husband and responsible for her flock, and the servant in the wealth of his master is a shepherd and responsible for his flock. He said: I heard these from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I think the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the man in the wealth of his father is a shepherd and responsible for his flock; so each of you is a shepherd and each of you is responsible for his flock."
"6027","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I heard Umar saying: Whoever braids his hair, let him shave, and do not resemble talbid; and Ibn Umar would say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with matted hair."
"6028","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Hathmah narrated to us, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha prayer at the end of his life, and when he stood he said: Have you seen this night of yours? For at the head of one hundred years from it, none of those today upon the back of the earth will remain. Abd Allah said: The people were confused about this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding what they narrate of these hadiths about one hundred years; he only said, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): None of those today upon the back of the earth will remain, meaning by that that that generation will pass away."
"6029","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while standing upon the minbar saying: Indeed your remaining among what has passed before you of nations is as between Asr prayer to sunset: the people of the Torah were given the Torah and acted by it until when midday came they were incapable, so they were given a qirat a qirat; and the people of the Gospel were given the Gospel and acted by it until Asr prayer, then were incapable, so they were given a qirat a qirat; then you were given the Quran and acted by it until the sun set, so you were given two qirats two qirats; so the people of the Torah and the Gospel said: Our Lord, these are less in deed and greater in reward. So He said: Have I wronged you of your reward anything? They said: No. He said: It is My bounty, I give it to whom I will."
"6030","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People are like a hundred camels, you can hardly find among them a riding camel."
"6031","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying while upon the minbar: Indeed fitnah is here, pointing to the east, from where the horn of Satan rises."
"6032","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Jews will fight you and you will be given power over them, until the stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew behind me, so kill him."
"6033","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping I saw myself circumambulating the Kaba, and there was a dark man with straight hair between two men, water dripping from his head, so I said: Who is this? They said: The son of Maryam. Then I turned and there was a red bulky man with curly hair, blind in the right eye, as if his eye were a floating grape, so I said: Who is this? They said: The Dajjal. The closest of people to him in resemblance is Ibn Qatan, a man from Banu al-Mustaliq."
"6034","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, he said: Nafi said: Abd Allah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None of you shall sell upon the sale of another, nor shall one of you propose upon the proposal of another."
"6035","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed me, he said: Nafi said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous dream. Nafi said: I thought Abd Allah ibn Umar said: Is a part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"6036","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, Nafi informed us, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man propose upon the proposal of his brother until the one who proposed first leaves it or permits him."
"6037","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar informed him, that a woman was found killed in one of the battles of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapproved of killing women and children."
"6038","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any slave owned between two partners, and one of them frees his share, then its just value is assessed upon the wealth of the one who freed, so he is freed if that reaches his wealth."
"6039","Hashim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As narrated to us, from his father Said ibn Amr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The upper hand is better than the lower hand. Ibn Umar said: So I did not ask Umar nor anyone else of the people."
"6040","Hashim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Aslam, may Allah grant them peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them."
"6041","Hashim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are an unlettered nation, we neither calculate nor write; the month is thus and thus and thus, and he clasped his thumb on the third."
"6042","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, the nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman would walk in front of the funeral."
"6043","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, from al-Zuhri, and Yaqub said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The keys of the unseen are five: Indeed with Allah is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die; indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"6044","Sulayman narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, and Yaqub said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People are like a hundred camels, you can hardly find among them a riding camel. And Yaqub said: Like a hundred camels, in them there is no riding camel."
"6045","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-Jumahi, narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in your houses, do not take them as graves."
"6046","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter."
"6047","Abu Nuh narrated to us, Ubayd Allah informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran from the Black Stone to the Black Stone."
"6048","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever withdraws a hand from obedience has no proof on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever dies separating from the community has died a death of ignorance."
"6049","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are like a hundred camels, you can hardly find among them a riding camel."
"6050","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal does not know what the night is, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"6051","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until you hear the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum. He said: And Ibn Umm Maktum was a blind man who does not see, he would not call until the people say: Call, you have entered morning."
"6052","Hashim and Hujayn both said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the believer is like a tree that does not shed its leaves. He said: The people fell into the trees of the desert, and it fell into my heart that it is the palm tree, but I was shy to speak, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the palm tree. He said: So I mentioned that to Umar, and he said: O my son, what prevented you from speaking? By Allah, had you said that, it would be more beloved to me than such and such."
"6053","Hujayn and Musa ibn Dawud both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the treacherous there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection, it will be said: Indeed this is the treachery of so-and-so."
"6054","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) burned the palms of Banu al-Nadir and cut them, and it is al-Buwayrah, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: Whatever you cut of date-palms or left standing upon their roots, it is by permission of Allah and to disgrace the disobedient."
"6055","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, that Abd Allah ibn Umar informed him, that a woman was found killed in one of the battles of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapproved of killing women and children."
"6056","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, that when he prayed Friday he would leave and pray two prostrations in his house, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"6057","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would forbid, when there are three persons, that two converse privately excluding the third."
"6058","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he would say: Do not trade fruits until their soundness appears; he forbade the seller and the buyer; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabanah: that one sells the fruit of his garden, if it is dates, for dates by measure, and if it is grapes, that he sells it for raisins by measure, and if it is crops, that he sells it for a known measure; he forbade all of that."
"6059","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed when one of you dies, his seat is presented to him morning and evening: if he is of the people of Paradise, then from the people of Paradise, and if he is of the people of Fire, then from the people of Fire, until Allah, the Exalted, resurrects him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6060","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None of you shall sell upon the sale of another, nor propose upon the proposal of another."
"6061","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, that Abd Allah divorced his wife while she was menstruating, one divorce, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, Abd Allah divorced his wife one divorce while she was menstruating, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take her back and keep her until she becomes pure, then she menstruates with him another menstruation, then he waits until she becomes pure from her menstruation; if he wishes to divorce her, let him divorce her when she is pure before he touches her; that is the waiting period which Allah, the Exalted, commanded that women be divorced for. And Abd Allah, when asked about that, would say to one of them: As for you, you divorced your wife once or twice, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me with it; but if you divorced her three times, she has become forbidden to you until she marries another husband besides you, and you disobeyed Allah, the Exalted, in what He commanded you of divorcing your wife."
"6062","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you shall make a man stand from his seat then sit in it."
"6063","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Umar: How is the prayer of the traveler, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? So he said: As for you, you follow the sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I will inform you; and as for you, you do not follow the sunnah of your Prophet, I will not inform you. He said: We said: The best of ways is the way of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O Abu Abd al-Rahman. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he left this Madinah, would not add to two rakas until he returned to it."
"6064","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Bishr informed us, I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, bless for us our Madinah, and bless for us our Sham, and bless for us our Yemen, and bless for us our sa and bless for us our mudd."
"6065","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who misses Asr prayer, it is as if his family and wealth were taken from him."
"6066","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the parable of your lifespans among the lifespans of the nations before you is as between Asr prayer to sunset."
"6067","Yunus and Surayj both said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out for umrah, and the disbelievers of Quraysh came between him and the House, so he sacrificed his offering and shaved his head at al-Hudaybiyah, and he made peace with them that they would perform umrah the next year and not carry weapons against them, and Surayj said: And not carry weapons except swords, and not stay there except as long as they wished; so he performed umrah the next year and entered it as he had made peace with them; when he had stayed three days, they ordered him to leave, so he left."
"6068","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) matted his head and brought an offering; when he came to Makkah, he commanded his wives to exit ihram. They said: What about you, why do you not exit? He said: I have garlanded my offering and matted my head, so I will not exit until I exit from my hajj and shave my head."
"6069","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha at al-Batha, then slept a short sleep, then entered and circumambulated the House."
"6070","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ayyub and Ubayd Allah, from Nafi, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in the right eye, and his other eye is as if a floating grape."
"6071","Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon his mount; and Nafi, that Ibn Umar would pray upon his mount."
"6072","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, Ibn Umar heard a man saying: By the Kaba, so he said: Do not swear by other than Allah, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever swears by other than Allah has disbelieved and associated."
"6073","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, he said: I was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Umar, and I came to Said ibn al-Musayyab, leaving with him a man from Kindah, then the Kindi came frightened, so I said: What is behind you? He said: A man came to Abd Allah ibn Umar just now and said: I swear by the Kaba. So he said: Swear by the Lord of the Kaba, for Umar used to swear by his father, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not swear by your father, for whoever swears by other than Allah has associated."
"6074","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Ubayd Allah, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, Ibn Umar heard a man saying: Tonight is the middle, so he said: What makes you know it is the middle, rather fifteen; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The month is thus and thus and thus, and Abu Khalid joined in the third, fifty."
"6075","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: On the day mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds, he said: One of them will stand in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."
"6076","Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered Makkah, would say: O Allah, do not make our deaths in it until You take us out of it."
"6077","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih ibn Muhammad al-Ansari narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abd Allah, freedman of Ghufrah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every nation there are Magians, and the Magians of my nation are those who deny qadar; if they die, do not attend them, and if they are ill, do not visit them."
"6078","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab acquired land from the Jews of Banu Harithah called Thamgh, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have acquired valuable property I wish to give as charity. He said: So he made it a charity not to be sold, nor given, nor inherited, overseen by those of judgment among the family of Umar; whatever is surplus of its fruit is placed in the path of Allah, the Exalted, and for the wayfarer, and for necks, and the poor, and kin, and the weak; and there is no sin upon whoever oversees it to eat in a fitting manner or feed a friend, without accumulating wealth from it. Hammad said: Amr ibn Dinar claimed that Abd Allah ibn Umar would gift to Abd Allah ibn Safwan from it. He said: So Hafsah gave charity of land of hers upon that, and Ibn Umar gave charity of land of his upon that, and Hafsah oversaw it."
"6079","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before you is a Hawd, between its two sides as between Jarba and Adhruh."
"6080","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only turned aside to the mountain pass for his need."
"6081","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran three circuits, and Surayj said: Three rounds, and walked four, in Hajj and Umrah."
"6082","Yunus and Surayj ibn al-Numan both said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I only know we set out as pilgrims raising voice with Hajj, and neither the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor Umar exited ihram until they circumambulated the House. He said: Surayj said: On the day of sacrifice, and between al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"6083","Yunus and Surayj both said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined Maghrib and Isha when he halted on the night of Arafah."
"6084","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The makers of images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"6085","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two shall not converse privately excluding their third, nor shall a man make a man stand from his seat then sit in it."
"6086","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Hammad said: I only know it as raised, his saying: On the day mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds, he said: The people will stand on the Day of Resurrection before the Lord of the worlds, Blessed and Exalted, in sweat up to the middle of their ears."
"6087","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you swears and says: If Allah wills, he has the choice, if he wishes he does, and if he wishes he does not."
"6088","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Abd Allah, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man shall not sell upon the sale of his brother, nor propose except by his permission, or he said: Except he permits him."
"6089","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) oiled with oil not perfumed while in ihram."
"6090","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the two rakas before Fajr prayer as if the adhan were in his ears."
"6091","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, bless for us our Madinah, and our sa, and our mudd, and our Yemen, and our Sham, then he faced the rising of the sun and said: From here rises the horn of Satan, from here earthquakes and tribulations."
"6092","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Aslam, may Allah grant them peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them, and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger; O Allah, curse Ril, Dhakwan, and Banu Lihyan."
"6093","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For every treacherous there is a banner known by the measure of his treachery, and the greatest treachery is the treachery of a leader of the common folk."
"6094","Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman. He said: My father said: I heard from Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid in the year seventy-nine, in the first year I sought hadith, one sitting, then I returned to him for the other sitting and he had died, and it is the year in which Malik ibn Anas died."
"6095","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim and Hamzah, the two sons of Abd Allah ibn Umar, from their father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is in the house, the woman, and the horse."
"6096","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Zayd narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, that he would dye his clothes and oil with saffron, so it was said to him: Why do you dye this with saffron? He said: Because I saw it the most beloved of dyes to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he oils and dyes his clothes with it."
"6097","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed Isha one night until we slept, then we woke, then we slept, then we woke, and he only kept us back for a delegation that came to him, then he came out and said: No one awaits the prayer besides you."
"6098","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man invoked lian upon his wife in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and disowned her child, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them and attached the child to the woman."
"6099","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw myself in a dream at the Kaba, and I saw a dark man, as handsome as you see of men, with locks combed, his locks dripping water, placing his hand upon the shoulders of two men, circumambulating the House, with combed hair, so I said: Who is this? They said: The Messiah, son of Maryam. Then I saw a curly coarse-haired man, blind in the right eye, as if his eye were a floating grape, like the most resembling of those I have seen among people to Ibn Qatan, placing his hands upon the shoulders of two men, circumambulating the House, so I said: Who is this? They said: This is the Messiah, the Dajjal."
"6100","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not the right of a Muslim man who has wealth to bequeath in, to spend three nights except his will is with him written. Abd Allah said: I have not spent a night since I heard it except my will is with me written."
"6101","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said Za'idah narrated to us from al-A'mash, Mujahid narrated to us, he said Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give permission to women to go to the mosque at night. He said: Then a son of Abdullah ibn Umar said: By Allah, we will not give them permission, they will take that as a cover for their needs. He said: Then Abdullah rebuked him. He said: Uff to you, I say the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it and you say I will not do it."
"6102","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Did you do such and such. He said: No, by Allah besides whom there is no god, I did not do it. He said: Then Jibril (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: He did do it, but Allah the Exalted forgave him by his saying there is no god but Allah. Hammad said: He did not hear this from Ibn Umar, between them is a man, meaning Thabit."
"6103","Affan narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man swears an oath and says if Allah wills, then he has the choice, if he wishes let him carry it through and if he wishes let him leave it."
"6104","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah and Abdul-Warith narrated to us from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same as it."
"6105","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abdullah and Bishr ibn A'idh al-Hudhali both narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Only one who has no share wears silk."
"6106","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us from Mujahid from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever seeks refuge with Allah, then grant him refuge, and whoever asks you, then give him, and whoever invites you, then accept his invitation, and whoever does good to you, then reward him, and if you do not find what to reward him with, then supplicate for him until you know that you have rewarded him."
"6107","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring of gold, and he used to place its stone on the inside of his hand, then one day he threw it away, so the people threw away their rings, then he took a ring of silver, and he used to seal with it and did not wear it."
"6108","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zaid narrated to us from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Come to the invitation when you are invited."
"6109","Affan narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Salim narrated to me that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by which he used to swear was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"6110","Affan narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, Salim informed me that he heard Abdullah narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he met Zaid ibn Amr ibn Nufail at the lower part of Baldah, and that was before revelation had come down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) presented to him a dining mat containing meat, but he refused to eat from it and said: I do not eat from what you slaughter upon your stone altars, and I do not eat except that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned. And Abdullah narrated this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6111","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar, Hammam said in my book: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in the graves, say: In the name of Allah and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6112","Affan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Harithi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani narrated to me from his father from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you meet the pilgrim, greet him and shake his hand and order him to seek forgiveness for you before he enters his house, for he is forgiven."
"6113","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from al-Walid ibn Kathir from Qatan ibn Wahb ibn Uwaimir ibn al-Ajda from one who narrated to him from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar that he heard him say: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, Allah Blessed and Exalted has forbidden Paradise to them: the addict of wine, the disobedient to parents, and the dayyuth who approves filth in his family."
"6114","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us from Yunus ibn Ubaid, al-Hasan informed us from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant swallows a gulp better with Allah Mighty and Majestic than a gulp of anger he swallows seeking the face of Allah the Exalted."
"6115","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head in the Farewell Hajj."
"6116","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us from Umar ibn Muhammad from Salim from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant swallows a gulp better with Allah Mighty and Majestic than a gulp of anger he swallows seeking the face of Allah the Exalted."
"6117","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us from Umar ibn Muhammad from Salim from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you eat with his left hand nor drink with it, for Satan eats with it and drinks with it. He said: And Nafi added: Nor let him take with it nor give with it."
"6118","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to place the stone of his ring on the side facing the palm of his hand."
"6119","Muhammad ibn Ubaid narrated to us, Abd al-Malik meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us from Anas ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar, he said: I asked him about his wife whom he divorced at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I divorced her while she was menstruating, so I mentioned that to Umar, and Umar mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Order him to take her back, when she becomes pure let him divorce her in her purity according to the Sunnah. He said: So I did. Anas said: So I asked him: Did you count the one you divorced while she was menstruating. He said: What is with me that I should not count it, if I was incapable and foolish."
"6120","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us from Amr meaning Ibn Yahya from Sa'id ibn Yasar from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a donkey while he was facing toward Khaibar."
"6121","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us from Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zaid from his father from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This authority will remain in Quraish as long as two people remain among mankind."
"6122","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Abdullah informed us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The most beloved names to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman."
"6123","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, I heard Salim ibn Abdullah say: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6124","Ubaid ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, Sulayman meaning Ibn Bilal narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade traveling with the Quran to the land of the enemy, fearing that the enemy would get hold of it."
"6125","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting without break. So it was said to him: You fast continuously, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not like you in condition, I am fed and given drink."
"6126","Ubaidah ibn Humaid narrated to us from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir from Mujahid, he said: I and Urwah ibn al-Zubair entered the mosque, and there we were with Abdullah ibn Umar, so we sat with him. He said: And there were men praying Duha, so we said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is this prayer. He said: An innovation. So we said to him: How many Umrahs did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform. He said: Four, one of them in Rajab. He said: So we were too shy to refute him. He said: Then we heard the tooth-stick use of the Mother of the Believers A'ishah, so Urwah ibn al-Zubair said to her: O Mother of the Believers, do you not hear what Abu Abd al-Rahman says, he says the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four Umrahs, one of them in Rajab. So she said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman, indeed he did not perform an Umrah except that he was present at it, and he did not perform anything in Rajab."
"6127","Ubaidah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila narrated to us from a man called Sadu from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed i'tikaf in the last ten days. He said: So a house of palm leaves was built for him. He said: Then one night he put his head out of it and said: O people, when one praying prays, he privately converses with his Lord Blessed and Exalted, so let him know with what he converses with Him, and let none of you raise his voice over another."
"6128","Ubaidah ibn Humaid narrated to us, Ubaidullah ibn Umar narrated to me from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray placing the camel between him and the qiblah. And Ubaidullah said: I asked Nafi, so I said: When the camels had gone, what would Ibn Umar do. He said: He used to place the back of the saddle between him and the qiblah."
"6129","Ubaidah ibn Humaid narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Qais narrated to me from Sa'id ibn Amr al-Qurashi that Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: We are an unlettered nation, we do not calculate nor write, and the month is like this and like this and like this, then he decreased one in the third time."
"6130","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Mina in the morning when he had prayed Fajr on the morning of the day of Arafah until he came to Arafah, then he alighted at Namirah, and it is the dwelling of the imam at which he used to alight at Arafah, until when it was at the Zuhr prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out at midday, so he combined Zuhr and Asr, then he addressed the people, then he set out and stood at the standing place of Arafah."
"6131","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar that he used to like, if he was able, to pray Zuhr at Mina on the day of Tarwiyah, and that is because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr at Mina."
"6132","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed when he came back from his Hajj returning in that Batha. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Madinah and made his camel kneel at the door of his mosque, then he entered it and bowed in it two rak'ahs, then he left to his house. Nafi said: So Abdullah ibn Umar used to do likewise."
"6133","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed your remaining compared to what has passed before you of the nations is as between the Asr prayer to sunset. The people of the Torah were given the Torah, so they worked until when midday came, then they became incapable, so they were given a qirat a qirat. Then the people of the Gospel were given the Gospel, so they worked until the Asr prayer, then they became incapable, so they were given a qirat a qirat. Then we were given the Quran, so we worked until sunset, so we were given two qirats two qirats. Then the people of the two Books said: O our Lord, why did You give these two qirats two qirats and gave us a qirat a qirat, while we were more in deeds than them. Allah the Exalted said: Did I wrong you anything of your wages. They said: No. He said: Then it is My bounty, I give it to whom I will."
"6134","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar, he said: There was a man from the Ansar who was always cheated in sales, and there was a lisp in his tongue, so he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what he met of cheating. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When you buy and sell, say: No cheating. Ibn Umar says: So by Allah, as if I hear him buying and selling and saying: No cheating, stammering with his tongue."
"6135","Yaqub and Sa'd both narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: And Nafi the freed slave of Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid that a man propose over the proposal of his brother or sell over his sale."
"6136","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Umar ibn Husain ibn Abdullah the freed slave of the family of Hatib narrated to me from Nafi the freed slave of Abdullah ibn Umar from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: Uthman ibn Maz'un died and left a daughter of his from Khuwaylah bint Hakim ibn Umayyah ibn Harithah ibn al-Awqas. He said: And he bequeathed to his brother Qudamah ibn Maz'un. Abdullah said: And they are both my maternal uncles. He said: So I went to Qudamah ibn Maz'un proposing the daughter of Uthman ibn Maz'un, so he married her to me, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah entered meaning to her mother, so he made her desire wealth, so she inclined to him, and the girl inclined to the desire of her mother, so they both refused until their matter was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Qudamah ibn Maz'un said: O Messenger of Allah, the daughter of my brother, he bequeathed her to me, so I married her to the son of her maternal aunt Abdullah ibn Umar, and I did not fall short with her in righteousness nor in suitability, but she is a woman, and she only inclined to the desire of her mother. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is an orphan and she is not married except with her permission. He said: So by Allah she was taken away from me after I had possessed her, so they married her to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah."
"6137","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Nafi narrated to us that Abdullah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said upon the minbar: Ghifar, may Allah forgive it, and Aslam, may Allah grant it safety, and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"6138","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Nafi narrated to us that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will enter Paradise. My father said and Sa'd narrated it to us, he said: Allah will admit the people of Paradise into Paradise and the people of Hell into Hell, then a caller will stand between them and say: O people of Paradise, no death, and O people of Hell, no death, each abiding in what he is in."
"6139","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Nafi narrated to us that Abdullah informed him that the mosque was at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) built of bricks, and its roof was palm branches, and its pillars were palm wood, so Abu Bakr did not add anything to it, and Umar added to it and built it upon its building in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with bricks and palm branches, and restored its pillars as wood, then Uthman changed it, so he added to it a great addition and built its wall with engraved stones and plaster, and made its pillars of engraved stone and its roof of teak."
"6140","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab narrated to me from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim, Salim ibn Abdullah informed me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The miqat of the people of Madinah is Dhu al-Hulaifah, and the miqat of the people of Sham is Mahya'ah, and it is al-Juhfah, and the miqat of the people of Najd is Qarn. Salim said: I heard Abdullah say: I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6141","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab informed me from his uncle, Salim ibn Abdullah informed us that Abdullah ibn Umar said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, so Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry, then he said: Let him take her back until she menstruates a coming menstruation other than her menstruation in which he divorced her, then if it appears to him to divorce her, let him divorce her pure from her menstruation before he touches her, for that is the divorce for the waiting period as Allah the Exalted commanded. And Abdullah had divorced her one divorce, so it was counted of her divorce, and Abdullah took her back as he was ordered."
"6142","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping I was brought a cup of milk, so I drank from it until I see moisture coming out from my limbs, then I gave my remainder to Umar ibn al-Khattab. So those around him said: Then what did you interpret that as, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Knowledge."
"6143","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate: While I was sleeping I saw myself brought a cup, then he mentioned it."
"6144","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Nafi narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and mentioned the False Messiah al-Dajjal, so he said: Allah the Exalted is not one-eyed, indeed the False Messiah al-Dajjal is blind in the right eye, as if his eye is a floating grape."
"6145","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Nafi narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon the people of the well at Badr then called them, so he said: O people of the well, did you find what your Lord promised you true. Some of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, do you call dead people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are not more hearing of what I said than them."
"6146","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab narrated to me from his uncle, he said: Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering ihram while his hair was matted, saying: Here I am O Allah, here I am, here I am, no partner have You, here I am, indeed praise and blessing are Yours and dominion, no partner have You. He said: And I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab entering ihram with the ihram of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and adding in it: Here I am and happiness to You, and good is in Your hands, and desire is to You and deeds."
"6147","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab narrated to me from his uncle, Salim ibn Abdullah informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews will fight you, so you will be given power over them, until the stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew behind me, so kill him."
"6148","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab narrated to us from his uncle, Salim ibn Abdullah informed me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha for us, and it is the one the people call Atamah, then he left, so he turned to us and said: Have you seen this night of yours, for at the head of a hundred years from it, none of those who are today upon the back of the earth will remain."
"6149","Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Jabalah ibn Suhaim from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats with his companion, let him not join dates together until he asks his permission, meaning dates."
"6150","Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Jabalah from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6151","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Abd al-Malik informed us from Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I was with Ibn Umar at Arafat, so when it was time to set out in the afternoon, I set out with him until he came to the imam, so he prayed with him the first and Asr, then he stood with him, and I and companions of mine, until the imam poured forth, so we poured forth with him until we ended at the narrow pass below the two Mazim, so he made his camel kneel and we made ours kneel, and we thought he wanted to pray, so his boy who was holding his mount said: He does not intend prayer, but he remembered that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he ended at this place relieved his need, so he likes to relieve his need."
"6152","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Abd al-Malik informed us from Muslim ibn Yannaq, he said: I was with Abdullah ibn Umar in the assembly of Banu Abdullah at Makkah, so a youth trailing his lower garment passed us, so he said: Come, O youth. So he came to him. So he said: Who are you. He said: I am one of Banu Bakr ibn Sa'd. He said: Do you like that Allah look at you on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Yes. He said: Then raise your lower garment then, for I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say with these two ears of mine, and he pointed with his two fingers to his two ears, saying: Whoever drags his lower garment not intending by it except pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6153","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sat to testify placed his left hand upon his left knee and placed his right hand upon his right knee and tied fifty-three and supplicated."
"6154","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Mujahid from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There are no days greater with Allah nor more beloved to Him the deeds in them than these ten days, so increase in them tahlil and takbir and tahmid."
"6155","Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, Shu'aib ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, and Abu al-Yaman said: Shu'aib ibn Abi Hamzah informed us from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abdullah narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to glorify Allah while upon the back of his mount, not caring wherever his face was, and nodding with his head nodding, and Ibn Umar used to do that."
"6156","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah informed me from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of part of my body and said: Worship Allah as if you see Him, and be in the world as if you are a stranger or a passerby."
"6157","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one of us sleep while he is junub. He said: Yes, and let him perform ablution."
"6158","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn al-Muttalib al-Makhzumi narrated to us that Abdullah ibn Umar used to perform ablution three times three times and attribute that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6159","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer with one of the two groups one rak'ah and two prostrations, and the other group facing the enemy, then the group that was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, and the other group came forward, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them one rak'ah and two prostrations, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam, then each man of the two groups stood and bowed for himself one rak'ah and two prostrations."
"6160","Ali ibn Ayyash and Isam ibn Khalid both narrated to us, they said: Ibn Thauban narrated to us from his father from Makhul from Jubair ibn Nufair from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah accepts the repentance of the servant as long as he does not gargle with death."
"6161","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us from Shuraih ibn Ubaid al-Hadrami that he heard al-Zubair ibn al-Walid narrating from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he raided or traveled and night overtook him said: O earth, my Lord and your Lord is Allah, I seek refuge with Allah from your evil and the evil of what is in you and the evil of what is created in you and the evil of what crawls upon you, I seek refuge with Allah from the evil of every lion and black thing and snake and scorpion, and from the evil of the dweller of the town, and from the evil of a father and what he begot."
"6162","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Umar ibn Amr Abu Uthman al-Ahmusi narrated to us, al-Mukhariq ibn Abi al-Mukhariq narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Umar that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Hawd is as between Adan and Amman, colder than snow and sweeter than honey and better smelling than musk, its cups like the stars of the sky, whoever drinks from it a drink will never thirst after it ever, the first people to come to it are the poor of the Muhajirin. A speaker said: And who are they, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Disheveled heads, pale faces, dirty clothes, doors are not opened for them, nor do they marry pampered women, those who give all that is upon them and do not take that which is for them."
"6163","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Salih ibn Kaysan from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands level with his shoulders when he said takbir and opened the prayer and when he bowed and when he prostrated."
"6164","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Salih ibn Kaysan from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same as that."
"6165","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Abu Bakr meaning Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us from Damrah ibn Habib, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to bring him a mudyah, and it is the blade, so I brought it to him, so he sent with it and it was sharpened, then he gave it to me and said: Come to me with it in the morning. So I did. So he went out with his Companions to the markets of Madinah, and in them were skins of wine that had been brought from Sham, so he took the mudyah from me and cut what was of those skins in his presence, then he gave it to me, and he ordered his Companions who were with him to go with me and to help me, and he ordered me to come to all the markets, so I find no skin of wine in them except that I cut it. So I did, so I did not leave in its markets a skin except that I cut it."
"6166","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, Zaid ibn Aslam narrated to us that he said: Abdullah ibn Umar came to Ibn Muti, so he said: Throw a cushion for Abu Abd al-Rahman. So he said: I did not come to sit with you, but I came to inform you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I heard him say: Whoever pulls a hand from obedience or parts from the community dies a death of ignorance."
"6167","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, Salih ibn Kaysan informed me that Isma'il ibn Muhammad informed him that Nafi informed him from Abdullah ibn Umar from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Only one envied is envied, or as Allah willed him to say, for two qualities: a man to whom Allah the Exalted gave the Quran, so he stands with it the hours of night and day, and a man to whom Allah gave wealth, so he spends it."
"6168","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Utbah al-Himsi or al-Yahsubi narrated to me from Umair ibn Hani al-Ansi: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting, so he mentioned trials, so he mentioned them much until he mentioned the trial of al-Ahlas. So a speaker said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is the trial of al-Ahlas. He said: It is a trial of flight and war, then the trial of sarra, its entrance or its smoke is from under the feet of a man of my household, he claims that he is from me and he is not from me, my allies are only the God-fearing, then the people agree upon a man like a hip upon a rib, then the trial of al-Duhayma, it will not leave anyone of this nation except that it slaps him a slap, then when it is said it has ended it continues, a man becomes in it a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, until the people become two camps, a camp of faith with no hypocrisy in it, and a camp of hypocrisy with no faith in it, when that is so, then await the Dajjal from today or tomorrow."
"6169","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala meaning Ibn Zabr narrated to us, Salim ibn Abdullah narrated to me from his father Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: How is the night prayer. So he said: Two by two, then when you fear dawn, then pray witr with one."
"6170","Zaid ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, I heard Salim ibn Abdullah say: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two, then when you fear dawn, then pray witr with a rak'ah making odd your prayer. He said: And Abdullah used to pray witr with one."
"6171","Zaid ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, I heard Salim ibn Abdullah say: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order killing dogs."
"6172","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe i'tikaf in the last ten of Ramadan."
"6173","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Kathir meaning Ibn Zaid narrated to me from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Umar that he was standing at Arafat, so he looked at the sun when it hung down like a shield for setting, so he wept and his weeping intensified, so a man with him said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, you have stood with me times, why do you do this. So he said: I remembered the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while standing at this place of mine, so he said: O people, nothing remains of your world compared to what has passed of it except as remains of this day of yours compared to what has passed of it."
"6174","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik meaning Ibn Anas narrated to us from Qatan ibn Wahb from Yuhannas that a freed woman of Ibn Umar came to him and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: And what is your matter. She said: I wanted to go out to the countryside. So he said to her: Sit, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None endures its hardship and severity except that I will be for him a witness or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."
"6175","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab narrated to us from his uncle, Salim ibn Abdullah narrated to me that Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he stood to prayer raised his hands until when they were level with his shoulders he said takbir, then when he wanted to bow he raised them until they were level with his shoulders, he said takbir and while they were likewise he bowed, then when he wanted to raise his backbone he raised them until they were level with his shoulders, he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, then he prostrated and did not raise his hands in prostration, and he raised them in every rak'ah and takbir he said before bowing until his prayer ended."
"6176","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab narrated to us from his uncle, Humaid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the night prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two, then when you fear dawn, then pray witr with one."
"6177","Yaqub narrated to us, the son of the brother of Ibn Shihab narrated to us from his uncle, Salim ibn Abdullah informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses Asr, it is as if his family and wealth have been taken away."
"6178","Yahya ibn Abi Bukair narrated to us, Zuhair ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Musa ibn Jubair from Nafi the freed slave of Abdullah ibn Umar from Abdullah ibn Umar that he heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah the Exalted sent Adam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) down to the earth, the angels said: O Lord, will You place in it one who corrupts in it and sheds blood, while we glorify with Your praise and sanctify You. He said: I know what you do not know. They said: Our Lord, we are more obedient to You than the sons of Adam. Allah the Exalted said to the angels: Bring two angels from the angels until they are sent down with them to the earth, so We see how they act. They said: Our Lord, Harut and Marut. So they were sent down to the earth, and al-Zuharah was represented to them as a woman of the most beautiful of mankind, so she came to them, so they asked her for herself, so she said: No, by Allah, until you speak with this word of polytheism. So they said: By Allah, we will never associate with Allah ever. So she went away from them, then she returned carrying a boy, so they asked her for herself, so she said: No, by Allah, until you kill this boy. So they said: By Allah, we will never kill him ever. So she went, then she returned carrying a cup of wine, so they asked her for herself. She said: No, by Allah, until you drink this wine. So they drank, so they became drunk, so they fell upon her and killed the boy. So when they awoke, the woman said: By Allah, you left nothing of what you refused me except that you did it when you became drunk. So they were given choice between the punishment of the world and the Hereafter, so they chose the punishment of the world."
"6179","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and every intoxicant is wine."
"6180","Yaqub narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad meaning Ibn Zaid ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad from Abdullah ibn Yasar the freed slave of Ibn Umar, he said: I bear witness, Salim said, Abdullah may Allah be pleased with him said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will not enter Paradise, and Allah will not look at them on the Day of Resurrection: the disobedient to his parents, and the masculine woman imitating men, and the dayyuth. And three, Allah will not look at them on the Day of Resurrection: the disobedient to his parents, and the addict of wine, and the one who reminds of what he gave."
"6181","Yaqub narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before you is a Hawd as between Jarba and Adhruh, in it are pitchers like the stars of the sky, whoever comes to it and drinks from it will never thirst after it ever."
"6182","Yaqub narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad from Salim from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the weeping of the living."
"6183","Yaqub narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Zaid or Salim from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is only something of the blast of Hell, so cool it with water."
"6184","Yaqub narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad from al-Qasim ibn Ubaidullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar: I heard Salim say: Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you eat with his left hand nor drink with it, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with it."
"6185","Yaqub narrated to me, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Zaid meaning Abu Umar ibn Muhammad, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar said: We used to speak of the Farewell Hajj and we did not know that it was farewell from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so when it was in the Farewell Hajj, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed, so he mentioned the False Messiah al-Dajjal, so he spoke at length in mentioning him, then he said: Allah did not send a prophet except that he warned his nation of him, Nuh warned his nation of him and the prophets after him. Indeed what is hidden to you of his matter, then let it not be hidden to you that your Lord is not one-eyed. Indeed what is hidden to you of his matter, then let it not be hidden to you that your Lord is not one-eyed."
"6186","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Jews will fight you, so you will be given power over them, until the stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew behind me, so kill him."
"6187","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me the freed slave of Abdullah ibn Umar from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you dozes in his sitting on Friday, let him move from it to another."
"6188","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, al-Zuhri narrated to me from Salim ibn Abdullah from his father that he narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the people to eat the meat of their sacrifices above three days."
"6189","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to me from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Sulayman ibn Yasar, both narrated to him from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: And I was with them in the sitting, but I was small, so I did not memorize the hadith. They said: A man asked him about witr, so he mentioned the hadith, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the last of the night prayer be made witr."
"6190","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar that he when he was asked about witr said: As for me, if I prayed witr before I sleep, then I wanted to pray at night, I made odd with one what had passed of my witr, then I prayed two by two, then when I finished my prayer I prayed witr with one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the last of the night prayer be made witr."
"6191","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Nafi narrated to me from Ibn Umar, he narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send upon them when they bought foods from the caravans one who prevents them from trading them until they bring them to their dwellings."
"6192","al-Fadl ibn Dukain narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Yemen Yalamlam."
"6193","al-Fadl ibn Dukain narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every two sellers, there is no sale between them until they part, except the sale of choice."
"6194","al-Fadl ibn Dukain narrated to us, Malik meaning Ibn Mighwal narrated to us from Abu Hanzalah, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about the travel prayer. So he said: Two rak'ahs. He said: I said: Then where is the word of Allah Blessed and Exalted: If you fear, while we are safe. He said: The Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: Thus is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6195","Abu Ahmad al-Zubairi Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Shu'bah al-Tahhan the neighbor of al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu al-Rabi, he said: I was with Ibn Umar at a funeral, so he heard the voice of a man shouting, so he sent to him and silenced him. So I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why did you silence him. He said: The dead is harmed by it until he is entered into his grave. So I said to him: I pray Fajr with you, then I turn and do not see the face of my sitter, then sometimes it becomes light. He said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray, and I liked to pray it as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray it."
"6196","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us from al-Zuhri that Salim ibn Abdullah and Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar both narrated to him from their father that he narrated to them that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Bad omen is in the horse and the house and the woman."
"6197","Ubaidullah ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us from Humaid ibn Yazid Abu al-Khattab from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever drinks wine, then flog him, then if he drinks it, then flog him, then if he drinks it, then flog him. Then he said in the fourth or the fifth: Then kill him."
"6198","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam, may Allah grant it safety, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it, and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"6199","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Yahya ibn Isma'il ibn Jarir from Qaza'ah, he said: Ibn Umar sent me on a need, so he said: Come that I farewell you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) farewelled me and sent me on a need of his. So he said: I entrust to Allah your religion and your trust and the endings of your deeds."
"6200","Muhammad ibn Kunasa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sa'id narrated to us from his father, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar came to Abdullah ibn al-Zubair, so he said: O Ibn al-Zubair, beware of deviation in the sanctuary of Allah Blessed and Exalted, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man of Quraish will deviate in it, if his sins were weighed with the sins of the two heavy beings they would outweigh. He said: So see that you are not him."
"6201","Haddathana Abu al-Jawwab, haddathana Ammar ibn Ruzayq from al-Amash from Mujahid from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah forgives the muadhdhin as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing that hears his voice bears witness for him."
"6202","Haddathana Muawiyah, haddathana Zaidah from al-Amash from a man from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah forgives the muadhdhin to the furthest extent of his adhan, and every moist and dry thing that hears his voice seeks forgiveness for him."
"6203","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, anbaana Ismail that is Ibn Jafar, akhbarani Musa ibn Uqbah from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar from his father that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Then Abu Bakr said: One side of my izar slips down unless I attend to it. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are not of those who do it out of pride."
"6204","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abd Allah, akhbarana Musa ibn Uqbah from Salim ibn Abd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Then he mentioned its meaning."
"6205","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, akhbarana Ismail, akhbarani Musa ibn Uqbah from Salim ibn Abd Allah from his father that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was visited while he was in his resting place at Dhu al-Hulayfah in the belly of the valley, and it was said to him: You are in a blessed flat land. Musa said: Salim made us halt at the halting place where Abd Allah used to halt, seeking the resting place of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which is lower than the mosque that is in the belly of the valley, midway between it and the road."
"6206","Haddathana Muawiyah ibn Amr, haddathana Zaidah from Ata from Muharib ibn Dithar from Abd Allah ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: O people, fear wrongdoing, for it is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"6207","Haddathana Surayj ibn al-Numan, haddathana Abu Shihab from al-Hajjaj from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hunaydah from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah sends punishment upon a people, the punishment befalls whoever is among them, then Allah will raise them according to their deeds. Thus it is in the book."
"6208","Haddathana Harun ibn Maruf, akhbarana Abd Allah ibn Wahb, akhbarani Abu Sakhr from Nafi, he said: While we were sitting with Abd Allah ibn Umar, a man came and said: So-and-so greets you with peace, for a man of the people of Syria. Then Abd Allah said: It has reached me that he has innovated an innovation, and if that is so then do not convey my greeting of peace to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There will be in my ummah transformation and pelting, and it is among the zindiqs and the Qadariyyah."
"6209","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who does not pay the zakat of his wealth, there will appear to him on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent with two spots. He said: It will cling to him, or encircle him. He said: It will say to him: I am your treasure, I am your treasure."
"6210","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"6211","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while he was in al-Hijr: Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping, lest there befall you the like of what befell them."
"6212","Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Umar ibn Nafi from his father from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza, and qaza is that the head of the boy is shaved and part of his hair is left."
"6213","Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, haddathana Shubah from Tawbah, he said: Al-Shabi said: I accompanied Ibn Umar for a year and a half, and I did not hear him narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except one hadith. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a dabb was brought, and the people began eating, then a woman of his wives called out: It is a dabb. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat, for it is lawful, or: Eat, there is no harm. He said: But he refrained. He said: Then he said: It is not unlawful, but it is not of my food."
"6214","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, haddathana Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, obligated the zakat of fitr of Ramadan, a sa of dates or a sa of barley, upon every free or slave, male or female, of the Muslims."
"6215","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, akhbarana Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The righteous dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood. Whoever sees good, let him praise Allah for it and mention it, and whoever sees other than that, let him seek refuge in Allah from the evil of his dream and not mention it, for it will not harm him."
"6216","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from Musa ibn Uqbah from Salim ibn Abd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Umar: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I saw in a dream a black woman with disheveled hair, unkempt, taken out of Madinah and settled in Mahyaah. Then I interpreted it in the dream as the epidemic of Madinah which Allah the Exalted transfers to Mahyaah."
"6217","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, akhbarana Mamar from a man from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not drink by direct mouthful, but let one of you drink in his two palms."
"6218","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abd Allah, akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ajlan from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful, and every intoxicant is khamr."
"6219","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, he said: Akhbarana Abd Allah, he said: Akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ajlan from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the like of it."
"6220","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abd Allah, and Attab, haddathana Abd Allah, akhbarana Abu al-Sabbah al-Ayli: I heard Yazid ibn Abi Sumayyah say: I heard Ibn Umar say: Whatever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about the izar, it applies to the shirt."
"6221","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from Musa ibn Uqbah from Salim ibn Abd Allah that Abd Allah ibn Umar used to pray in travel his night prayer and perform witr riding upon his camel, not caring where his camel faced, and he mentioned that from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Musa said: And I saw Salim do that."
"6222","Haddathana Nuh ibn Maymun, akhbarana Abd Allah that is Ibn Umar al-Umari from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar used to stone Jamrat al-Aqabah upon his mount on the Day of Sacrifice, and he would not come to the rest of them after that except walking, going and returning, and he claimed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would come to them only walking, going and returning."
"6223","Haddathana Nuh ibn Maymun, akhbarana Abd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, alighted at al-Muhassab."
"6224","Haddathana Nuh ibn Maymun, akhbarana Abd Allah from Musa from Salim from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform witr upon his mount."
"6225","Haddathana Nuh, akhbarana Abd Allah from Saeed al-Maqburi, he said: I saw Ibn Umar in private conversation with a man, then a man entered between them, so he struck his chest and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When two are in private conversation, the third should not enter between them except with their permission. Haddathana Yaqub, haddathana my father from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Haddathani Saeed ibn Abi Saeed al-Maqburi from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, freedman of Banu Taym, then he mentioned the hadith."
"6226","Haddathana Yamur ibn Bishr, haddathana Abd Allah that is Ibn Mubarak, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd said: Haddathani Nafi that Ibn Umar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was cleaning his teeth with a siwak, then he gave it to the eldest of the people, and said: Jibril, peace be upon him, commanded me to give precedence to the elder."
"6227","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Nafi that Abd Allah ibn Umar went out to Makkah performing Umrah during the fitnah, and said: If I am blocked from the House, we shall do as we did with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he entered ihram for Umrah, because the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram for Umrah in the year of Hudaybiyyah."
"6228","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, he said, and haddathana Ishaq, haddathana Malik from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five of the animals, whoever kills them while in ihram, there is no sin upon him: the scorpion, the mouse, the vicious dog, the crow, and the kite."
"6229","Haddathanahu Ishaq, akhbarani Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five of the animals. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"6230","My father said: And I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Nafi also."
"6231","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Nafi from Abd Allah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the Kabah, he and Usamah ibn Zayd and Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah al-Hajabi, and closed it upon himself, and remained in it. Abd Allah said: I asked Bilal when he came out what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did. He said: He placed a pillar on his left and two pillars on his right and three pillars behind him, and the House that day was upon six pillars. Then he prayed, and between him and the wall was three cubits."
"6232","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, halted at al-Batha which is at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and prayed there."
"6233","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah al-Dili from Muhammad ibn Imran al-Ansari from his father that he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar turned aside to me while I was alighting under a samurah tree on the road to Makkah, and said: What made you alight under this samurah tree. I said: I wanted its shade. He said: Was there other than that. I said: No, nothing made me alight except that. Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you are between the two Akhshabs of Mina, and he gestured with his hand toward the east, then there is a valley there called al-Surar, in it is a samurah tree under which seventy prophets were gladdened."
"6234","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, he said, and haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa, akhbarana Malik from Nafi from Abd Allah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And those who shorten."
"6235","Haddathana Ismail, akhbarana Yunus ibn Ubayd from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar while he was walking in Mina, and said: I vowed to fast every Tuesday or Wednesday, and this day coincided with the Day of Sacrifice, so what do you think. He said: Allah the Exalted commanded fulfillment of the vow, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade, or he said: We were forbidden, to fast the Day of Sacrifice. He said: The man thought he had not heard, so he said: I vowed to fast every Tuesday or Wednesday, and this day coincided with the Day of Sacrifice. Then he said: Allah commanded fulfillment of the vow, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us, or he said: We were forbidden, to fast the Day of Sacrifice. He said: He did not add to that until he leaned against the mountain."
"6236","Haddathana Ismail, akhbarana Yunus from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, he said: I saw Ibn Umar come upon a man who had made his sacrificial camel kneel to slaughter it in Mina, and said: Make it stand, bound, the sunnah of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"6237","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, haddathana Zuhayr from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People are but like a hundred camels, you can hardly find among them a riding camel."
"6238","Haddathana Bahz, haddathana Hammad, akhbarana Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Kurayz from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in the House between the two pillars."
"6239","Haddathana Bahz and Abu Kamil, they said: Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, haddathana Simak ibn Harb from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell camels in al-Baqi, taking silver for dinars and dinars for silver. So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in the house of Hafsah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, wait, I ask you: I used to sell camels in al-Baqi, taking this for this and this for this. Then he said: No harm to take them at the rate of the day, so long as you do not separate with something still between you."
"6240","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Yusuf from Sharik from Abd Allah ibn Sharik al-Amiri, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar and Abd Allah ibn Abbas and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr asked about Umrah before Hajj in tamattu, and they said: Yes, the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. You come first, circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then exit ihram, even if that is a day before the Day of Arafah. Then you enter ihram for Hajj, so you have combined an Umrah and a Hajj, or Allah has combined for you an Umrah and a Hajj."
"6241","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Yusuf, haddathana Sufyan from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Asim from Salim from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No servant makes an image except it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Give life to what you created."
"6242","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Yusuf from Sharik from Abu Ishaq from Mujahid from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Umrah twice before he performed Hajj. That reached Aishah, and she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed four Umrahs; Abd Allah ibn Umar knew of them, among them an Umrah with his Hajjah."
"6243","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Shubah from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar say: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon hearing and obeying, he would teach us to say in it: As far as you are able."
"6244","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathani Shubah from Abd Allah ibn Dinar: I heard Ibn Umar narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever does not find two sandals, let him wear two khuffs, and let him split them or cut them below the ankles."
"6245","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Sharik from Uthman ibn Abi Zarah from Muhajir al-Shami from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wears a garment of fame, Allah the Blessed and Exalted will clothe him with a garment of humiliation on the Day of Resurrection. Sharik said: I saw Muhajir and sat with him."
"6246","Haddathana Hajjaj from Ibn Jurayj, and Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Ibn Jurayj, akhbarani Abu al-Zubayr that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them facing their waiting period."
"6247","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Layth, he said: Haddathani Uqayl from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abd Allah that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed tamattu in the Farewell Hajj with Umrah to Hajj, and sacrificed, driving the sacrificial animals with him from Dhu al-Hulayfah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began by entering ihram for Umrah, then entered ihram for Hajj. The people performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with Umrah to Hajj. Some of the people drove sacrificial animals, and some did not. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived in Makkah, he said to the people: Whoever of you has driven a sacrificial animal, he is not released from anything he became forbidden from until he completes his Hajj. Whoever of you has not driven an animal, let him circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, and shorten, and exit ihram. Then let him enter ihram for Hajj and sacrifice. Whoever does not find a sacrificial animal, let him fast three days in Hajj and seven when he returns to his family. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he arrived in Makkah, circumambulated, touching the Corner first, then hastened three circuits of the seven and walked four circuits. Then he bowed, when he finished his circumambulation of the House, at al-Maqam two rakahs. Then he greeted, left, came to al-Safa, and performed circuits between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he was not released from anything he became forbidden from until he completed his Hajj, sacrificed his animal on the Day of Sacrifice, went forth, circumambulated the House, then was released from everything he became forbidden from. Those of the people who drove and brought sacrificial animals did the like of what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did."
"6248","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Layth, haddathani Uqayl from Ibn Shihab from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr that Aishah informed him from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about his tamattu with Umrah to Hajj and the tamattu of the people with him, with the like of what Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me from Abd Allah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"6249","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Layth, haddathana Uqayl from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood addressing and said: Verily tribulation is here, from where the horn of Satan rises, meaning the east."
"6250","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Layth from Uqayl from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to give extra booty to some of those he sent of the expeditions for themselves exclusively, apart from the division of the general army, and the fifth in that is due to Allah the Exalted."
"6251","Haddathana Hajjaj and Abu al-Nadr, they said: Haddathana Layth, haddathani Nafi from Abd Allah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, burned the palms of Banu al-Nadir and cut them, and it is al-Buwayrah. Then Allah the Exalted sent down: Whatever you cut of linah or left them, to the end of the verse."
"6252","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Layth, haddathani Uqayl from Ibn Shihab that he said: Akhbarani Salim ibn Abd Allah that he heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Do not prevent, meaning your women, the mosques when they ask your permission to them. Bilal ibn Abd Allah said: By Allah, we shall surely prevent them. Then Abd Allah turned to him when he said that and reviled him."
"6253","Haddathana Hajjaj, haddathana Layth, haddathani Uqayl ibn Khalid from Ibn Shihab that Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar informed him that Abd Allah ibn Umar used to walk in front of the funeral, and that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to walk in front of it, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them."
"6254","Haddathana Hajjaj, he said: I read to Ibn Jurayj, haddathani Ziyad ibn Sad that Ibn Shihab said: Haddathani Salim from Abd Allah ibn Umar that he used to walk in front of the funeral, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, used to walk ahead of it."
"6255","Haddathana Mubashshir ibn Ismail, haddathana al-Awzai from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Isha prayer in Mina two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, two rakahs, and with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, two rakahs, and with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, two rakahs at the beginning of his caliphate. Then Uthman completed it afterwards, may Allah be pleased with them all."
"6256","Haddathana Harun, haddathana Ibn Wahb, akhbarani Yunus from Ibn Shihab, akhbarani Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in Mina two rakahs. Then he mentioned it."
"6257","Haddathana Jarir from Sadaqah ibn Yasar: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fixed times: For the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Syria al-Juhfah, he said: And for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam. It was said to him: And Iraq. He said: There was no Iraq that day."
"6258","Haddathana Jarir from Mansur from Habib from Tawus, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, claims that witr is not obligatory. He said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the night prayer, and said: The night prayer is two by two, then when you fear the dawn, perform witr with one."
"6259","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarana Abu Bishr from Saeed ibn Jubayr, he said: I went out with Ibn Umar from his house, and we passed youths of Quraysh who had set up a bird and were shooting at it, making for the owner of the bird every arrow of theirs that missed. When they saw Ibn Umar they dispersed. Then Ibn Umar said: Who did this. May Allah curse whoever did this. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah curse whoever takes a living creature as a target."
"6260","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarana Mansur and Ibn Awn from Ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar, he said: The voluntary prayer of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was two rakahs before Zuhr and two rakahs after it, and two rakahs after Maghrib and two rakahs after Isha. He said: And Hafsah informed me that he used to pray two rakahs after the dawn rises."
"6261","Haddathana Mutamir from Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to place his mount across and pray toward it."
"6262","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi, haddathana Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Image-makers will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"6263","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi, haddathana Ayyub from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn Umar, he said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with an izar rattling upon me. He said: Who is this. I said: Abd Allah ibn Umar. He said: If you are Abd Allah, raise your izar. So I raised my izar to mid-calves. His izar remained so until he died."
"6264","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Yusuf, haddathana al-Amash from Abu Salih from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion."
"6265","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, haddathana Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque, scraped it with his hand, then turned to the people and was angry with them, then said: Allah the Exalted is facing one of you in his prayer, so none of you should spit toward his face in his prayer."
"6266","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi, haddathana Ayyub from Nafi that Ibn Umar went out performing Hajj, entered ihram, and laid his head down in severe cold. So I threw a burnus over him, and he woke and said: What did you throw over me. I said: A burnus. He said: You throw it over me while I told you that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us wearing it."
"6267","Haddathana Mutamir from Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever comes to Friday, let him perform ghusl."
"6268","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: If I am blocked from the House, we did as we did with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the disbelievers of Quraysh blocked him from the House, so he shaved and returned. I call you to witness that I have made an Umrah obligatory. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"6269","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah. He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. Then he said on the fourth: And those who shorten."
"6270","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When they are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of one."
"6271","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a ring of silver. It was in his hand, then it was in the hand of Abu Bakr after him, then it was in the hand of Umar, then it was in the hand of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them. Its inscription: Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."
"6272","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Hajjaj from Ata and Ibn Abi Mulaykah and from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he entered Makkah, touched the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner, and did not touch other than them of the corners."
"6273","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the slave is sincere to his master and performs the worship of his Lord well, he has reward twice."
"6274","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drinks khamr in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter unless he repents."
"6275","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to buy food from the riders in bulk, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to sell it until we move it from its place."
"6276","Haddathana Ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd, they said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should propose over the proposal of his brother, nor sell over the sale of his brother, except with his permission."
"6277","Haddathana Ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd, they said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"6278","Haddathana Ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hearing and obeying upon the Muslim man in what he loves or hates, unless he is commanded with disobedience. If he is commanded with disobedience, there is no hearing nor obeying."
"6279","Haddathana Ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd, they said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever frees a share of his in a slave, upon him is freeing all of him, if he has wealth reaching his price. It is assessed upon him with a just value. If he has no wealth, freed of him what is freed."
"6280","Haddathana Ibn Numayr and Hammad ibn Usamah, they said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever accuses his brother of disbelief, one of them has incurred it."
"6281","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a banner is raised for every treacherous one on the Day of Resurrection, and it is said: This is the treachery of so-and-so son of so-and-so."
"6282","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade meeting goods until they enter the markets."
"6283","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi, thus my father said: Women and men used to perform ablution in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from one vessel, and all dipped into it together."
"6284","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah, and Hammad that is Abu Usamah, he said: Akhbarani Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that when he went out he went out by the way of al-Shajarah, and entered by the way of al-Muarras. Ibn Numayr said: When he entered Makkah he entered from the upper pass and exits from the lower pass."
"6285","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray, that is, recite the sajdah outside the prayer, then prostrate, and we prostrated with him, until perhaps one of us would not find a place to prostrate in."
"6286","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, he said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he went out on the Day of Eid, would order a spear to be placed before him, then pray toward it, with the people behind him. He used to do that in travel. Hence the rulers took it."
"6287","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying his supererogatory prayer wherever his camel faced."
"6288","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, caught Umar ibn al-Khattab while he was in a riding party, swearing by his father. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Verily Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Let one who swears swear by Allah or be silent."
"6289","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A woman should not travel three except with a mahram."
"6290","Yahya ibn Saeed said: I found nothing objectionable in Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except one hadith: The hadith of Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: No woman should travel a journey of three except with a mahram. My father said: And Abd al-Razzaq narrated it to us from al-Umari from Nafi from Ibn Umar, and did not raise it."
"6291","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade on the Day of Khaybar the flesh of domestic donkeys."
"6292","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, akhbarana Ubayd Allah from Nafi, he said: Akhbarani Ibn Umar that the people of Jahiliyyah used to fast the Day of Ashura, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fasted it, and the Muslims, before Ramadan was obligated. When Ramadan was obligated, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ashura is a day of the days of Allah the Exalted. Whoever wishes fasts it, and whoever wishes leaves it."
"6293","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah, akhbarani Nafi from Ibn Umar, he informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut for a shield worth three dirhams."
"6294","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade qaza."
"6295","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, akhbarana al-Amash from Mujahid, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr asked Ibn Umar in which month the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed Umrah. He said: In Rajab. Then Aishah heard us, so Ibn al-Zubayr asked her and informed her of the saying of Ibn Umar. Then she said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never performed an Umrah except he witnessed it, and he never performed an Umrah at all except in Dhu al-Hijjah."
"6296","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana al-Amash from Mujahid, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Permit women in the mosques at night. Then a son of Abd Allah ibn Umar said: By Allah, we shall surely prevent them, they take it as deceit for their needs. Then he said: May Allah do to you and do. I say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and you say: We shall not let them."
"6297","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, allotted for the horse two shares and for the man one share."
"6298","Haddathana Ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd, they said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The parable of the hypocrite is like the stray sheep between the two flocks, going to this once and to this once, not knowing which to follow."
"6299","Haddathana Ibn Numayr, haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed wisal in Ramadan, and the people saw him and he forbade them. It was said to him: You perform wisal. Then he said: I am not like you, I am fed and given drink."
"6300","Haddathana Ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd, they said: Haddathana Ubayd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Make the last of your prayer at night witr."
"6301","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, I heard Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrating to Tawus, he said: A man said to Abdullah ibn Umar: Will you not go out to fight? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Islam is built upon five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the fasting of Ramadan, and the pilgrimage to the House."
"6302","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointing with his hand toward Iraq: Indeed tribulation is here, indeed tribulation is here, three times, from where the horn of Satan rises."
"6303","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, I heard Salim saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When your women ask your permission to go to the mosques, then permit them."
"6304","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hanzalah informed us, he said: Salim narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When your women ask your permission to go to the mosques, then permit them."
"6305","Yala narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays over a funeral, for him is a qirat. They said: O Messenger of Allah, like this qirat of ours? He said: No, rather like Uhud or greater than Uhud."
"6306","Yala and Muhammad, the two sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, they said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, Muhammad said in his hadith, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a pebble in his hand with which he was scraping mucus he had seen in the qiblah, and he was saying: When one of you prays, let him not spit in front of him, for when the servant prays he stands conversing privately with his Lord, the Exalted. Muhammad said: In front of him."
"6307","Yala and Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of gharar, and he said: The people of the Jahiliyyah used to trade in that sale, a man would buy with an old she-camel the unborn offspring of an unborn camel, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it. Muhammad ibn Ubayd said in his hadith: the unborn offspring of an unborn camel, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that."
"6308","Yala narrated to us, Fudayl, meaning Ibn Ghazwan, narrated to us, from Abu Dahqanah, from Ibn Umar, he said: There were people with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he called Bilal for dates that were with him, and he brought dates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disapproved of, and he said: What are these dates? He said: The dates that were with us, we exchanged two sa for a sa, so he said: Give us back our dates."
"6309","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed the one who lies against me, a house will be built for him in the Fire."
"6310","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi and Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade eating the flesh of domestic donkeys."
"6311","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ali ibn Abdullah al-Bariqi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted his riding animal, he said Allahu Akbar three times, then he said: Glory be to the One Who has subjected this for us though we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we will return. Then he would say: O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine for righteousness and piety and of deeds what You are pleased with. O Allah, make the journey easy for us and fold up the distance for us. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family. O Allah, accompany us in our travel and succeed us over our families. And when he returned to his family he would say: Returning, repenting, if Allah wills, worshipping, praising our Lord."
"6312","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, he said: Salim narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Umar said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, never said of Isa, peace be upon him, that he was red at all, but he said: While I was sleeping I saw myself circumambulating the Kabah, and there was a man of dark wheat complexion, lank hair, being supported between two men, his head dripping or pouring water, so I said: Who is this? They said: This is the son of Maryam. He said: So I turned to look, and there was a red bulky man, curly headed, blind in the right eye as if his eye were a floating grape. I said: Who is this? They said: This is the Dajjal. The one I have seen most resembling him is Ibn Qatan. Ibn Shihab said: A man of Khuzah from al-Mustaliq who died in the Jahiliyyah."
"6313","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decreed that wala belongs to the one who frees."
"6314","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is the Isha prayer, so let not the Bedouins overcome you over the names of your prayers, for they delay it on account of the camels."
"6315","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to send us to the outskirts of Madinah and command us not to leave a dog except that we killed it, until we would kill the dog belonging to a woman of the desert people."
"6316","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Najrani, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man bought palm trees from a man, and they produced nothing that year, so they gathered and disputed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By what do you deem his dirhams lawful? Return his dirhams to him, and do not pay in advance for palm trees until their soundness appears. So I asked Masruq: What is its soundness? He said: It reddens or yellows."
"6317","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ismail ibn Umayyah informed me that Nafi, the freed slave of Abdullah, narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to them that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cut off the hand of a man who stole a shield from the suffah of the women, its price three dirhams."
"6318","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash and Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Permit women at night to the mosque. So his son said to him: By Allah, we will not permit them, they will take that as a means of deceit. So he said: May Allah do to you and may Allah do to you, you hear me saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and you say: You yourself will not. Layth said: But let them go out unattired."
"6319","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would have a small spear brought out with him on the day of al-Fitr and al-Adha in order to plant it and pray toward it."
"6320","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been bereft of his family and his wealth."
"6321","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"6322","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Farqad al-Sabakhi informed us, from Sad ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, oiled himself with oil that was not scented while he was in ihram."
"6323","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Salim, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see the crescent then fast, and when you see it then break fast, and if it is obscured for you then estimate for it."
"6324","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, and Yaqub said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Yaqub said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been bereft of his family and his wealth."
"6325","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from al-Jahm ibn al-Jarud, from Salim, from his father, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab gave as a gift a Bukhtiyyah camel for which he was offered three hundred dinars, so he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have gifted a Bukhtiyyah camel of mine for which I was offered three hundred dinars, so shall I sacrifice it or buy sacrificial camels with its price? He said: No, but sacrifice it itself."
"6326","Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Salim ibn Abdullah while he was reclining on a cushion in which were images of birds and beasts, so I said: Is this not disliked? He said: No, only what is set up erect is disliked. My father Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever makes an image will be punished. And Hafs said once: He will be charged to breathe into it while he is not one to breathe."
"6327","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Nafi saying: Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon the minbar saying: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him wash."
"6328","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Muharib ibn Dithar, he said: I saw Ibn Umar raising his hands whenever he bowed and whenever he raised his head from bowing. He said: So I said to him: What is this? He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood in the two rakahs, would say takbir and raise his hands."
"6329","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he heard Ibn Umar being asked about a man who divorced his wife while menstruating, so he said: Do you know Abdullah ibn Umar? He said: Yes. He said: For he divorced his wife while menstruating, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of the news, so he ordered him to take her back. He said: And I did not hear him add to that. Rawh said: Order him to take her back."
"6330","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: During the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a man saw a dream he would narrate it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I wished to see a dream and narrate it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: And I was a young unmarried youth, and I used to sleep in the mosque in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I saw in sleep as if two angels took me and went with me to the Fire, and it was folded like the folding of a well, and it had two horns, and in it were people I knew, so I began saying: I seek refuge with Allah from the Fire, I seek refuge with Allah from the Fire. Then another angel met them and said to me: You will not be frightened. So I narrated it to Hafsah, and Hafsah narrated it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: An excellent man is Abdullah, if only he would pray at night. Salim said: So Abdullah would not sleep of the night except little."
"6331","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took a ring of gold, and made its bezel inward. He said: While he was delivering a sermon one day he said: I had made a ring and I used to wear it with its bezel inward, and by Allah I will never wear it again. So he threw it away, and the people threw away their rings."
"6332","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, and Abd al-Ala, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"6333","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, raising the hadith, he said: When one of you eats, then he mentioned the hadith."
"6334","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, I heard Malik ibn Anas and Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrating from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"6335","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered in Madinah the killing of dogs, so he was informed of a woman who had a dog in a district of Madinah, so he sent to it and it was killed."
"6336","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing house snakes."
"6337","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you invites his brother, let him answer him, whether it be a wedding or the like."
"6338","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you are three, let not two converse privately to the exclusion of the third except with his permission, for that grieves him."
"6339","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw Utarid selling a suit of brocade, so he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw Utarid selling a suit of brocade, so if you bought it and wore it for delegations and for Eid and for Friday. So he said: Silk is worn only by one who has no share, I think he said: In the Hereafter. He said: Then suits of striped silk were gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he gave Ali ibn Abi Talib a suit, and gave Usamah ibn Zayd a suit, and sent to Umar ibn al-Khattab a suit, and said to Ali: Divide it among the women as headcovers. And Umar came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard you say about it what you said, then you sent me a suit. So he said: I did not send it to you to wear it, but to sell it. As for Usamah, he wore it and went out in it, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began looking at him, and when Usamah saw him fixing his gaze upon him, he said: O Messenger of Allah, you clothed me in it. He said: Divide it among the women as headcovers, or as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"6340","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever drags his izar out of pride, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Zayd said: And Ibn Umar used to narrate that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw him with a rustling izar upon him, meaning new, and said: Who is this? So I said: I am Abdullah. So he said: If you are Abdullah, then raise your izar. He said: So I raised it. He said: More. He said: So I raised it until it reached mid-shin. He said: Then he turned to Abu Bakr and said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. So Abu Bakr said: My izar loosens at times. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are not of them."
"6341","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man of the Ansar while he was admonishing his brother about shyness, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Leave him, for shyness is part of faith."
"6342","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, and Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever takes a dog except a dog of livestock or hunting, two qirats will be deducted from his reward every day."
"6343","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to narrate, he said: While I was sleeping I saw myself brought a cup of milk, so I drank from it until I could see satiation coming out of my nails, then I gave my remainder to Umar ibn al-Khattab. So they said: How did you interpret that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Knowledge."
"6344","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, then he mentioned it."
"6345","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to raise his hands when saying takbir until they were parallel to his shoulders or near to that, and when he bowed he would raise them, and when he raised his head from bowing he would raise them, and he would not do that in prostration."
"6346","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raised his head from bowing, saying: Our Lord, and to You belongs praise."
"6347","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to sit in prayer while leaning on his hands."
"6348","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat in prayer, he placed his hands upon his knees and raised his right finger which is next to the thumb, and supplicated with it, and his left hand was upon his knee spread over it."
"6349","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying in the Fajr prayer when he raised his head from bowing, he said: Our Lord, and to You belongs praise, in the last rakah, then he said: O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so, supplicating against people of the hypocrites, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed: Not for you of the affair is anything, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"6350","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, Salim narrated to me, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raised his head from bowing in the last rakah of Fajr, saying: O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so, after saying: Allah hears the one who praises Him, our Lord, and to You belongs praise, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed: Not for you of the affair is anything, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"6351","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the fear prayer with one of the two groups one rakah, while the other group faced the enemy, then they left and stood in the place of their companions facing the enemy, and those others came and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them one rakah, then he gave salam, then these made up one rakah and those one rakah."
"6352","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two rakahs at Mina, and with Abu Bakr two rakahs, and with Umar two rakahs, and with Uthman early in his caliphate, then he prayed it four."
"6353","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umayyah ibn Abdullah, that he said to Ibn Umar: We find the fear prayer and the resident prayer in the Quran, and we do not find the traveler prayer. So Ibn Umar said: Allah sent His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while we were the most ignorant of people, so we do as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did."
"6354","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastened in travel, he would combine Maghrib and Isha."
"6355","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The night prayer is two by two, so when you fear dawn, then make it odd with one."
"6356","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, informing from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or from Umar, Nafi was certain of the speaker, I am now certain it was one of them, and I think it was only from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Let none of you wrap himself in prayer as the Jews wrap. Let whoever has two garments wear a lower wrap and an upper wrap, and whoever does not have two garments, let him wear a lower wrap then pray."
"6357","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr, with the same meaning, narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar used to say: The Muslims when they came to Madinah would gather and await the prayer, and no one would call to it, so they discussed that one day, and some of them said: Take a bell like the bell of the Christians, and some of them said: Rather a horn like the horn of the Jews, so Umar said: Will you not send a man to call to prayer? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Bilal, stand and call to prayer."
"6358","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar used to say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed the one who misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been bereft of his family and his wealth. I said to Nafi: Until the sun sets? He said: Yes."
"6359","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar would sometimes send him while he was fasting, and his dinner would be served to him after the Maghrib prayer had been called, then the iqamah would be made while he hears it, yet he would not leave his dinner nor hasten until he finished his dinner, then he would go out and pray. He said: And he used to say: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not hasten away from your dinners when they are served to you."
"6360","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by Ibn Sayyad among a group of his companions, among them Umar ibn al-Khattab, while he was playing with boys near the fortress of Bani Maghalah, and he was a boy, and he did not notice until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck his back with his hand, then said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? So Ibn Sayyad looked at him and said: I testify that you are the Messenger of the unlettered. Then Ibn Sayyad said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What comes to you? Ibn Sayyad said: There comes to me one truthful and one lying. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The matter has been confused for you. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have hidden for you something hidden, and he had hidden for him: The day the heaven brings clear smoke. So Ibn Sayyad said: It is smoke. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be gone, you will not exceed your measure. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me concerning him and I will strike his neck. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If it is he, you will not be given power over him, and if it is not he, there is no good for you in killing him."
"6361","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out toward Ibn Sayyad, then he mentioned it."
"6362","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with a group of his companions, among them Umar ibn al-Khattab, until he found Ibn Sayyad, a boy near puberty, playing with boys near the fortress of Bani Muawiyah, then he mentioned its meaning."
"6363","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, or from more than one, he said: Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with Ubayy ibn Kab going to the palm trees in which was Ibn Sayyad, until when they entered the palms, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began sheltering behind the palm trunks, seeking to hear something from Ibn Sayyad before he saw him, while Ibn Sayyad was lying on his bed in a blanket of his in which was a murmur. He said: So his mother saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sheltering behind the palm trunks, and she said: O Saf, and it is his name, this is Muhammad. So he jumped up. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If she had left him, he would have shown."
"6364","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abdullah informed me, I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: After that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with Ubayy ibn Kab heading for the palms, then he mentioned the hadith."
"6365","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among the people and praised Allah, the Exalted, as He deserves, then he mentioned the Dajjal and said: I warn you of him, and there is no prophet but that he warned his people of him. Nuh, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, warned his people of him, but I shall say to you about him a word no prophet said to his people: You know that he is one-eyed, and that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is not one-eyed."
"6366","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Jews will fight you and you will be given power over them, until the stone will say: O Muslim, this is a Jew behind me, so kill him."
"6367","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Jews of Bani al-Nadir and Qurayzah fought the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, expelled Bani al-Nadir and left Qurayzah and favored them, until Qurayzah fought after that, so he killed their men and divided their women and children and wealth among the Muslims, except some of them who joined the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he granted them safety and they became Muslim, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, expelled all the Jews of Madinah, Bani Qaynuqa, and they are the people of Abdullah ibn Salam, and the Jews of Bani Harithah, and every Jew who was in Madinah."
"6368","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab expelled the Jews and Christians from the land of the Hijaz, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prevailed over Khaybar, he wanted to expel the Jews from it, and the land when he prevailed over it belonged to Allah, the Exalted, and to His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and to the Muslims, so he wanted to expel the Jews from it, so the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to leave them in it on condition that they undertake its work and for them half the fruit, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: We leave you in it on that as long as we wish. So they remained in it until Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled them to Tayma and Ariha."
"6369","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer, let him wash."
"6370","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while standing upon the minbar: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer, let him wash."
"6371","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, I heard Nafi saying: Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you make his brother stand from his seat then take his place in it. So I said to him, meaning Ibn Jurayj: On Friday? He said: On Friday and other than it."
"6372","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us that Ibn Umar used to say: Whoever prays at night, let him make the last of his prayer witr, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered that. So when dawn comes, all night prayer and witr have gone, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Make witr before dawn."
"6373","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Nafi informed me that Ibn Umar used to say: Whoever prays of the night, let him make the last of his prayer witr before dawn, thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order them."
"6374","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Ali al-Azdi informed him that Ibn Umar taught him that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, settled upon his camel going out to travel, he would say takbir three times, then say: Glory be to the One Who has subjected this for us though we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we will return. O Allah, we ask You in this journey of ours for righteousness and piety and of deeds what You are pleased with. O Allah, make this journey of ours easy for us and fold up its distance from us. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel and the gloom of return and the evil sight in family and wealth. And when he returned he would say them and add in them: Returning, repenting, worshipping, praising our Lord."
"6375","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Nafi informed me, he said: Ibn Umar combined the two prayers once, news came to him about Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd that she was ill, so he departed after praying Asr and left the baggage, then hastened the march, and went until the time of Maghrib came, so a man of his companions spoke to him and said: The prayer, but he did not respond to him, then another spoke to him and he did not respond to him, then another spoke to him, so he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when travel pressed him, delay this prayer until combining the two prayers."
"6376","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling fruit for dates, and selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"6377","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me about the fear prayer and how is the sunnah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah ibn Umar used to narrate that he prayed it with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said takbir, and a group of us lined up behind him, and a group faced the enemy, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bowed with them one rakah and two prostrations, prostrating like half the dawn prayer, then they left and faced the enemy, then the other group came and lined up with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did the like of that, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave salam, so every man of the two groups stood and prayed for himself one rakah and two prostrations."
"6378","Abu al-Yaman informed us, Shuayb informed us, he said: I asked al-Zuhri, he said: Salim informed me that Abdullah ibn Umar said: I fought with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in an expedition toward Najd, so we faced the enemy and lined up against them, then he mentioned the hadith."
"6379","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the people in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, being beaten if a man bought food in bulk from selling it until he moved it to his place."
"6380","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sells a slave, his wealth belongs to the seller except that the buyer stipulates, and whoever sells palm trees in which is fruit that has been pollinated, its fruit belongs to the seller except that the buyer stipulates."
"6381","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"6382","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to Bani, I think he said Jadhimah, so he called them to Islam, but they did not know how to say: We have become Muslim, so they began saying: We have left, we have left. And Khalid began taking them captive and killing, he said: And he handed to every man of us a captive, until one morning Khalid ordered that every man of us kill his captive. Ibn Umar said: So I said: By Allah, I will not kill my captive, nor will a man of my companions kill his captive. He said: So they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned to him what Khalid had done, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his hands and said: O Allah, I dissociate myself to You from what Khalid has done, twice."
"6383","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A woman of Makhzum used to borrow goods and deny them, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered her hand to be cut."
"6384","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that on the day of al-Hudaybiyah the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. So a man said: And those who shorten. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, forgive those who shave, until he said it three or four times, then he said: And those who shorten."
"6385","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he ordered their stoning, and when they were stoned I saw him shielding her with his hands to protect her from the stones."
"6386","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We were in a detachment, and our shares reached eleven camels for every man, then after that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave us extra a camel a camel."
"6387","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, and from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from praying in the mosque."
"6388","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: On the day of al-Fitr a small spear would be brought out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so it would be planted before him and he would pray toward it."
"6389","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Zakat al-Fitr to be paid before the people go out to the prayer place, and he said once: To the prayer."
"6390","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man stood in the mosque and called: From where do we enter ihram, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one entering ihram of the people of Madinah enters from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the one entering ihram of the people of Sham enters from al-Juhfah, and the one entering ihram of the people of Najd enters from Qarn. He said: And they claim, or they say, that he said: And the one entering ihram of the people of Yemen enters from Yalamlam."
"6391","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, I heard Ubaydullah ibn Umar and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrating from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar went out intending Hajj at the time al-Hajjaj came down against Ibn al-Zubayr, so it was said to him: The people will fight among themselves and we fear they will block you. So he said: You had in the Messenger of Allah a good example, then I shall do as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did. I call you to witness that I have made Umrah obligatory. Then he went out, until when he was at the back of al-Bayda he said: What is the matter of Umrah and Hajj but one. I call you to witness that I have made Hajj obligatory with my Umrah. And he gave as guidance sacrificial animals he had bought at Qudayd. So he went on until he came to Makkah, and circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, adding nothing to that, not slaughtering nor shaving nor shortening nor exiting anything he had entered ihram for, until the day of sacrifice came, so he slaughtered and shaved, then he saw that he had completed his tawaf for Hajj and Umrah with his first tawaf. Then he said: Thus the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did."
"6392","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about the enjoyment of Hajj, so he ordered it and said: Allah, the Exalted, made it lawful and His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered it. Al-Zuhri said: And Salim informed me that Ibn Umar said: Umrah in the months of Hajj is complete, acted upon by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and revealed in it is the Book of Allah, the Exalted."
"6393","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri informed us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I saw Ibn Umar walking between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then he said: If I walked, I have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walking, and if I hastened, I have seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastening."
"6394","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave for the horse two shares and for the man one share."
"6395","Rawh narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, Nafi informed me, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to touch these two Yemeni corners whenever he passed them, and he would not touch the other two."
"6396","Rawh and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar about touching the Stone, Hasan said: From al-Zubayr ibn Arabi, he said: I heard a man ask Ibn Umar about the Stone. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, touching it and kissing it. So a man said: What if I am crowded? So Ibn Umar said: Put what if in Yemen. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, touching it and kissing it."
"6397","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya informed me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi, that he asked Abdullah ibn Umar about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Allahu Akbar whenever he lowered and whenever he raised, then he would say: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, on his right, Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, on his left."
"6398","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard a man ask Abdullah ibn Umar: May a man approach his wife before circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah? He said: As for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he came and circumambulated the House, then bowed two rakahs, then went between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then he recited: You had in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"6399","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah together."
"6400","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Abu Ishaq, I heard Abdullah ibn Malik saying: I prayed with Ibn Umar at Jam, so he made the iqamah and prayed Maghrib three, then prayed Isha two with one iqamah. He said: So Khalid ibn Malik asked him, so he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did the like of this in this place."
"6401","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: It reached me from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform nahr on the day of Adha in Madinah, and when he did not perform nahr he would slaughter."
"6402","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, and Safwan said: Ibn Ajlan informed us, with the same meaning, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim that Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan wrote to Abd Allah ibn Umar: Report to me your need. So Abd Allah ibn Umar wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Begin with those you maintain, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and I deem the upper hand the giving one and the lower the begging one, and I neither ask you for anything nor refuse any provision that Allah drives to me from you."
"6403","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri from Salim ibn Abd Allah from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah Almighty has given this Book and he stands with it through the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom Allah Almighty has given wealth and he gives it in charity through the hours of the night and the hours of the day."
"6404","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri, he said: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he stoned the first jamrah which is next to the mosque, he stoned it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with every pebble, then he would stand in front of it facing the House, raising his hands, supplicating, and he would prolong the standing, then he would stone the second with seven pebbles, saying takbir with every pebble, then he would turn to the left toward the belly of the valley and stand facing the qiblah, raising his hands, supplicating, then he would go on until he came to the jamrah at al-Aqabah and stone it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with every pebble, then he would leave and not stand. Al-Zuhri said: I heard Salim narrating from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of this, and Ibn Umar used to do the like of this."
"6405","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri from Salim from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no omens, and ill omen is in three: in the woman and the house and the mount."
"6406","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, I heard Ibn Abi Num say: I witnessed Ibn Umar when a man from the people of Iraq asked him about a muhrim who killed a fly, and he said: O people of Iraq, you ask me about a muhrim who killed a fly while you killed the son of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are my two sweet basils in this world."
"6407","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah informed us, Aidh ibn Nusayb informed me, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the Kabah."
"6408","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit informed us, my father narrated to me from Makhul from Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty accepts the repentance of His servant so long as he has not reached the death rattle."
"6409","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, he heard Ibn Umar, he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ghifar, may Allah forgive her, and Aslam, may Allah grant her peace."
"6410","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us from his father, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: From whom are you, he said: From Aslam, he said: Shall I not give you glad tidings, O brother of Aslam, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ghifar, may Allah forgive her, and Aslam, may Allah grant her peace."
"6411","Arim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No man shall sell over the sale of his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother, except by his permission, and perhaps he said: he gives him permission."
"6412","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed us from Nafi from Abd Allah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold and put it on his right, with its bezel toward the inside of his palm, so the people took rings of gold. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar and threw it away and forbade wearing gold rings."
"6413","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced continual fasting, so the people practiced it, and he forbade them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, you practice continual fasting, and he said: I am not like you, I am fed and given drink."
"6414","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ayyub narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and makes an exception, then if he wishes he may go ahead and if he wishes he may retract without breaking his oath."
"6415","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us from Ibn Umar that Aishah bargained for Barirah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the prayer, and she said: They refused to sell her unless they stipulate the wala, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wala belongs to the one who frees."
"6416","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yala ibn Hakim narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr, I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of the earthen jar. He said: So I went to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: He spoke the truth. He said: I said: What is the jarr, he said: Everything made of clay."
"6417","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Sakhr narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a townsman selling for a Bedouin, and he used to say: Do not meet the caravans for trade, and let none sell over the sale of another, and let none of you propose, or anyone propose, over the proposal of his brother until the first suitor leaves or gives him permission, then he may propose."
"6418","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub informed us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Jiirranah, saying: I vowed in the Jahiliyyah to seclude myself in the Sacred Mosque. Abd al-Samad said: And with him was a boy from the captives of Hawazin, so he said to him: Go and seclude yourself, so he went and secluded himself, and while he was praying he heard the people saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has freed the captives of Hawazin, so he called the boy and freed him."
"6419","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed him with a fine suit and he wore it, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it and mentioned what is below the ankles and mentioned the Fire, until he mentioned a severe saying about letting the izar hang low."
"6420","Abd al-Samad and Abu Said narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qaza. Abd al-Samad said: And it is the qazah, a patch on the head."
"6421","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harun ibn Ibrahim al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Maghrib prayer is the witr of the daytime prayer, so make the night prayer odd, and the night prayer is two by two, and the witr is one rakah at the end of the night."
"6422","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qaza on the head."
"6423","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from his father, he said: I entered with Ibn Umar to Abd Allah ibn Muti, and he said: Welcome to Abu Abd al-Rahman, put a cushion for him, so Ibn Umar said: I only came to narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof for him, and whoever dies while separating from the community dies a jahili death."
"6424","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Qays al-Maribi informed us, Thumamah ibn Sharahil narrated to us, he said: I went out to Ibn Umar and said: What is the prayer of the traveler, he said: Two by two, except the Maghrib prayer, three. I said: What if we are at Dhu al-Majaz, he said: What is Dhu al-Majaz, I said: A place where we gather and sell and stay twenty nights or fifteen nights, so he said: O man, I was in Adharbayjan, I do not know, he said: four months or two months, and I saw them praying it two by two, and I saw the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my own eyes praying it two by two, then he cited to me this verse: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"6425","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan informed us, I heard Salim say from Abd Allah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw near the Kabah, by the Maqam, a brown man with lank hair, placing his hand on two men, his head dripping or trickling, so I asked: Who is this, and it was said: Isa son of Maryam, or al-Masih son of Maryam, I do not know which of the two he said. Then I saw behind him a red man with curly hair, blind in the right eye, the one I have seen most resembling him being Ibn Qatan, so I asked: Who is this, and it was said: Al-Masih al-Dajjal."
"6426","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, I heard Yunus from al-Zuhri from Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I was brought while sleeping a cup of milk, and I drank from it until the milk came out from my nails, then I gave my remainder to Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you interpret it, he said: Knowledge."
"6427","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Simak from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell camels at al-Baqi, selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars, so I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was about to enter his room, and I took hold of his garment and asked him, and he said: If you exchange one of them for the other, let none leave you while there is still an unsettled sale between you and him."
"6428","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: Al-Bayda where you tell lies about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."
"6429","Yahya ibn Adam and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruwasi narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Nafi informed me from Abd Allah ibn Umar that he used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Zakat al-Fitr to be paid before the people go out to the prayer."
"6430","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Mufaddal narrated to us from Mansur from Mujahid, he said: I entered the mosque with Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and Ibn Umar was leaning on the room of Aishah, with people praying Duha, so Urwah said to him: Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is this prayer, he said: An innovation. So Urwah said to him: Abu Abd al-Rahman, how many umrahs did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform, and he said: Four, one of them in Rajab. He said: And we heard Aishah cleaning her teeth in the room, so Urwah said to her: Abu Abd al-Rahman claims that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four umrahs, one of them in Rajab, and she said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never performed an umrah except while he was with him, and he never performed umrah in Rajab at all."
"6431","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqbah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer on one of his days, so one party stood with him and one party faced the enemy, and he prayed one rakah with those with him, then they went and the others came, and he prayed one rakah with them, then the two parties each made up one rakah."
"6432","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to the mosque of Quba riding and walking."
"6433","Asbat narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that he used to run three circuits from the Stone to the Stone and walk four at a leisurely pace. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"6434","Asbat narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi narrated to us from Abu Umamah al-Taymi, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: We hire out camels, so do we have any Hajj, he said: Do you not circumambulate the House and come to Arafah and stone the jamarat and shave your heads, he said: We said: Yes, so Ibn Umar said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about what you asked me, and he did not answer him until Jibril, peace be upon him, came down to him with this verse: There is no blame on you to seek bounty from your Lord, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: You are pilgrims."
"6435","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid, meaning al-Adani, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab from a man of Banu Taym Allah, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: We are people who hire out camels, and he mentioned the like of the meaning of the hadith of Asbat."
"6436","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Ata from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer in this mosque of mine is better than prayer in other mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"6437","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gharar sale, and that is that the Jahiliyyah used to trade in the offspring of the unborn camel, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that."
"6438","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us from Abd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reserved al-Naqi for horses. Hammad said: So I said to him: For his own horses, he said: No, for the horses of the Muslims."
"6439","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Atiyyah ibn Sad from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The night prayer is two by two, and if you fear the dawn then one, Allah Almighty is Witr and loves the witr."
"6440","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Isa ibn Hafs ibn Asim ibn Umar narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever endures its hardship and severity, I will be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"6441","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us from Hanzalah that he heard Tawus say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar when a man asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the earthen jar and the gourd, he said: Yes."
"6442","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan from Salim ibn Abd Allah from Abd Allah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah Almighty will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6443","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to me that he heard Salim ibn Abd Allah say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"6444","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to me, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Umar that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your women ask your permission to go to the mosque, permit them."
"6445","Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Jahdam narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Badr from Ibn Umar, he said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not exit ihram, and with Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them, and they did not exit ihram."
"6446","Abu Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Injustice is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"6447","Abu Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"6448","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who does not pay the zakat of his wealth, Allah Almighty will represent his wealth to him on the Day of Resurrection as a bald serpent with two spots, and it will cling to him or encircle him. He said: It will say: I am your treasure, I am your treasure."
"6449","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to me from Nafi from Ibn Umar that he was on a journey when a companion of his dismounted to pray witr, so Ibn Umar said: What is the matter with you that you do not ride, he said: I will pray witr, Ibn Umar said: Is there not for you in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a good example."
"6450","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa said to me, Nafi narrated to us that Ibn Umar used to say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spread peace and feed food and be brothers as Allah Almighty commanded you."
"6451","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the riders for trade, and he forbade najsh."
"6452","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wala belongs to the one who frees."
"6453","Hammad narrated to us from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees his share in a slave, it shall be valued against his wealth, and if he has no wealth, then of him is freed what is freed."
"6454","Hammad narrated to us from Malik from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment toward Najd, I was in it, and we took many camels as booty, and our shares were eleven or twelve camels, and we were given an extra camel each."
"6455","Hammad narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By twenty-seven, meaning the congregational prayer."
"6456","Hammad narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the beards and trim the mustaches."
"6457","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us from Nafi that Ibn Umar used to stone the jamarat after the day of sacrifice walking, and he claimed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"6458","Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us from Abd Allah, meaning al-Umari, from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted al-Zubayr the gallop of his horse in a land called Thurayr, so he ran the horse until it stopped, then he threw his whip and said: Give him up to where the whip reached."
"6459","Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he disliked qaza for boys."
"6460","Hammad narrated to us, Abd Allah informed us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The first charity in Islam was the charity of Umar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Keep its principal and make its fruit charitable."
"6461","Hammad narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the Quran, and when he passed a Quranic prostration he would prostrate and we would prostrate with him."
"6462","Hammad narrated to us from Abd Allah from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar used to spend the night at Dhu Tuwa, and when morning came he would wash and order those with him to wash, and he would enter from the upper side, and when he left he would leave from the lower side, and he claimed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"6463","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar used to run from the Stone to the Stone, and he claimed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"6464","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reserved al-Naqi for horses, so I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, meaning al-Umari, for his own horses, he said: For the horses of the Muslims."
"6465","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar from al-Shabi, he said: I sat with Ibn Umar for two years and never heard him narrate anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the hadith of the lizard."
"6466","Uqbah Abu Masud al-Mujaddir narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a race between horses and favored the mature horses in the distance."
"6467","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn Uthman, narrated to us from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he ordered the zakat, the Zakat al-Fitr, to be paid before the people go out to the prayer."
"6468","Umar ibn Sad, who is Abu Dawud al-Hafari, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among trees there is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is like the Muslim man. He said: So the people fell into the trees of the desert, and I was among the youngest of the people, and it occurred to me that it is the palm tree, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the palm tree. He said: So I mentioned that to my father, and he said: Had you said it, it would be dearer to me than such and such."
"6469","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us from Abd Allah from Nafi from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a sharecropping agreement with the people of Khaybar on half, and he used to give his wives from it one hundred wasqs, eighty of dates and twenty of barley. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I read to my father these hadiths to their end."
"6470","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father, Hammad, meaning al-Khayyat, narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman from Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab from his father, he said: I had a wife whom Umar disliked, so my father said to me: Divorce her, I said: No, so he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he called me and said: Abd Allah, divorce your wife. He said: So I divorced her."
"6471","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father, Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman from Salim from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order us to lighten, though he would lead us with al-Saffat."
"6472","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father this hadith, Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father, he said: When we bought food haphazardly in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we were prevented from selling it until we brought it to our dwellings."
"6473","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Muzdalifah the Maghrib and the Isha with one iqamah, combining them."
"6474","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father this hadith and I heard it as audition, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Laylat al-Qadr, he said: Whoever seeks it, let him seek it on the twenty-seventh night. Shubah said: And a trustworthy man mentioned to me from Sufyan that he used to say: He only said: Whoever seeks it, let him seek it in the remaining seven. Shubah said: So I do not know whether he said this or that, Shubah doubted, the trustworthy man is Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan."
"6475","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I read to my father, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Ikrimah ibn Khalid ibn al-As al-Makhzumi narrated to me, he said: I came to Madinah with a group of the people of Makkah, intending umrah from it, and I met Abd Allah ibn Umar and said: We are people of Makkah, we came to Madinah and never performed Hajj at all, may we perform umrah from it, he said: Yes, and what prevents you from that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed all his umrahs before his Hajj, so we performed umrah."
"6476","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I found this hadith in my fathers book in his handwriting, Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us from Ata, meaning Ibn al-Saib, from Ibn Jubayr: Indeed We gave you al-Kawthar, it is abundant good. And Ata said from Muharib ibn Dithar from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise, its banks of gold, and the water flows over pearls, and its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. End of the Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"6477","Hushaym narrated to us from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman and Mughirah al-Dabbi from Mujahid from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: My father married me to a woman of Quraysh, and when she came to me I would not turn to her because of my strength in worship, in fasting and prayer, so Amr ibn al-As came to his daughter-in-law until he entered upon her and said to her: How did you find your husband, she said: The best of men, or like the best of husbands, a man who never uncovered our side nor knew our bed, so he turned to me and blamed me and lashed me with his tongue, saying: I married you to a woman of Quraysh of lineage and you neglected her and did such and such, then he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained about me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me and I came to him, and he said to me: Do you fast the day, I said: Yes, he said: And do you stand the night, I said: Yes, he said: But I fast and break my fast and pray and sleep and touch women, so whoever turns away from my sunnah is not from me. He said: Recite the Quran in every month, I said: I find myself stronger than that, he said: Then recite it in every ten days, I said: I find myself stronger than that. One of them, either Husayn or Mughirah, said: Then recite it in every three. He said: Then he said: Fast three days in every month, I said: I am stronger than that. He said: He kept raising me until he said: Fast one day and break one day, for it is the best fasting and it is the fasting of my brother Dawud. Husayn said in his hadith: Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every worshipper has zeal and every zeal has a lull, either toward a sunnah or toward an innovation, so whoever whose lull is toward a sunnah is guided, and whoever whose lull is to other than that is ruined. Mujahid said: So Abd Allah ibn Amr, when he weakened and grew old, would fast the days in that way, joining some of them to others to strengthen himself thereby, then break his fast by the count of those days. He said: And he would recite in each of his portions in that way, sometimes increasing and sometimes decreasing, except that he would complete the number, either in seven or in three. He said: Then he would say after that: Had I accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it would be dearer to me than what was exchanged for it, but I parted from him on a matter I dislike to oppose for another."
"6478","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed me from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Amr ibn al-Walid from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire, and he forbade wine and gambling and the kubah and the ghubayra. He said: And every intoxicant is forbidden."
"6479","Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Abi Saghirah from Abu Balj from Amr ibn Maymun from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man on earth who says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no power nor strength except by Allah, but his sins are expiated from him, even if they were more than the foam of the sea."
"6480","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, al-Hadrami from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Abd Allah ibn Amr that a man of the Muslims asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a woman called Umm Mahzul who used to commit fornication and stipulated for him that she would spend on him. He said: So he asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he mentioned her matter to him. He said: So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to him: The adulteress none marries but an adulterer or a polytheist."
"6481","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to me from Yazid ibn Amr from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is silent is saved."
"6482","Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Alqamah ibn Marthad from al-Qasim, meaning Ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No person is afflicted with a trial in his body but Allah Almighty orders the angels who guard him, saying: Write for My servant every day and night what he used to do of good while he is in My bonds."
"6483","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood and we stood with him, and he prolonged the standing until we thought he would not bow, then he bowed and hardly raised his head, then he raised and hardly prostrated, then he prostrated and hardly raised his head, then he sat and hardly prostrated, then he prostrated and hardly raised his head, then he did in the second rakah as he did in the first, and he began blowing on the ground and weeping while prostrating in the second rakah, saying: My Lord, why do You punish them while I am among them, My Lord, why do You punish us while we seek Your forgiveness. Then he raised his head when the sun had cleared, and finished his prayer, and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah Almighty, so when one of them eclipses, hasten to the mosques. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Paradise was shown to me, so that had I wished I could have taken some of its branches, and the Fire was shown to me, so that I kept extinguishing it fearing it would overwhelm you, and I saw in it a tall black woman of Himyar being punished for a cat of hers, she tied it and neither fed it nor gave it drink nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth, whenever it came forward it clawed her and whenever it turned away it clawed her, and I saw in it the brother of Banu Dadah, and I saw the owner of the crooked staff reclining in the Fire on his staff, he used to steal from the pilgrims with his staff, and when they noticed him he would say: I am not stealing from you, it only caught on my staff."
"6484","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Isa ibn Talhah from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing on his mount at Mina, when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought shaving is before slaughter, so I shaved before I slaughtered, he said: Slaughter and no harm. Then another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought slaughter is before stoning, so I slaughtered before I stoned, and he said: Stone and no harm. He said: So he was never asked about anything that a man had advanced before another thing but he said: Do it and no harm."
"6485","Abd al-Ala narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The just in this world will be on pulpits of pearl on the Day of Resurrection before the Merciful for their justice in this world."
"6486","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai informed us, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to me, Abu Kabshah al-Saluli narrated to me that Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning he said: Convey from me though it be a verse, and narrate from the Children of Israel and there is no harm, and whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6487","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Shubah from Amr ibn Murrah from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith from Abu Kathir from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Injustice is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity nor vulgarity, and beware of miserliness, for miserliness destroyed those before you, it commanded them to sever ties and they severed, and commanded them to be stingy and they were stingy, and commanded them to immorality and they committed it. He said: So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best, he said: That the Muslims be safe from your tongue and your hand. So that one or another stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which migration is best, he said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes, and migration is two migrations, the migration of the settled and the Bedouin, so the migration of the Bedouin is to answer when called and obey when commanded, and the settled one has the greater trial and the better reward."
"6488","al-Walid narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to me, Abu Kabshah al-Saluli narrated to us that Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Forty good deeds, the highest of them lending a goat, no servant, or he said: no man, does one of them hoping for its reward or believing its promise but Allah will admit him to Paradise for it."
"6489","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Isa ibn Talhah from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I stoned, he said: Stone and no harm, and he said once: before I slaughtered, and he said: Slaughter and no harm. He said: I slaughtered before I stoned, he said: Stone and no harm."
"6490","Sufyan narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him, he said: I came to pledge to you on migration, and I left my parents weeping, he said: Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."
"6491","Sufyan narrated to us, I heard Amr, Amr ibn Aws informed me, he heard it from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved fasting to Allah is the fasting of Dawud, and the most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of Dawud, he used to sleep half of it and stand a third of it and sleep a sixth of it, and he used to fast one day and break one day."
"6492","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Amr ibn Aws from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The just with Allah on the Day of Resurrection will be on pulpits of light at the right of the Merciful Almighty, and both His hands are right, those who are just in their judgment and their families and what they govern."
"6493","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, and he was in charge of the baggage, and he said once: in charge of the heavy goods, of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man called Karkarah died, and he said: He is in the Fire, so they looked and found a cloak he had stolen, and he said once: or a garment he had stolen."
"6494","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Abu Qabus from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The merciful will be shown mercy by the Merciful, have mercy on the people of the earth and the people of heaven will have mercy on you, and the womb is a branch from the Merciful, whoever joins it He joins him, and whoever cuts it He severs him."
"6495","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from Wahb ibn Jabir from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Enough sin for a man to neglect those he feeds."
"6496","Sufyan narrated to us from Dawud, meaning Ibn Shabur, and Bashir Abu Ismail from Mujahid, Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept enjoining me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"6497","Sufyan narrated to us from Sulayman al-Ahwal from Mujahid from Abu Iyad from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vessels, they said: Not all people find a waterskin, so he permitted the earthen jar that is not pitched."
"6498","Jarir narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traits, whoever guards them will be admitted by them to Paradise, and they are easy, and few act upon them. They said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah, he said: That you praise Allah and magnify Him and glorify Him after every prescribed prayer ten times ten times, and when you come to your bed you glorify Allah and magnify Him and praise Him one hundred times, so those are fifty and two hundred fifty by the tongue, and two thousand five hundred in the balance, so which of you does two thousand five hundred sins in the day and night. They said: How is it that few act upon them, he said: Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and reminds him of the need of such and such, so he does not say them, and he comes to him at his sleep and puts him to sleep, so he does not say them. He said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counting them with his hand."
"6499","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, he said: I was traveling with Muawiyah on his return from Siffin, between him and Amr ibn al-As. He said: So Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: O father, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Ammar: Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah, the rebellious party will kill you. He said: So Amr said to Muawiyah: Do you not hear what this one says, so Muawiyah said: You always bring us trouble, did we kill him, those who brought him killed him."
"6500","Abu Nuaym narrated to us from Sufyan from al-Amash from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad the like of it or similar to it."
"6501","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Kaba, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever pledges allegiance to an imam and gives him the clasp of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as much as he can, and if another comes disputing him, strike the neck of the other."
"6502","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu al-Safar, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by us while we were repairing a thatch hut of ours, and he said: What is this. We said: A hut of ours has weakened and we are repairing it. He said: He said: Indeed the matter is more urgent than that."
"6503","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Kaba, he said: I came to Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As while he was sitting in the shade of the Kaba, and I heard him say: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, he stopped at a halting place, and some of us were pitching their tents, and some of us were with their pasturing animals, and some of us were competing in archery, when his caller called: Prayer in congregation. He said: So we gathered. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and addressed us and said: There was no prophet before me except that he guided his nation to what he knew was good for them and warned them of what he knew was evil for them, and this nation of yours has had its well-being placed in its beginning, and its end will be afflicted with severe tribulation and matters you will disapprove of. Trials will come, some of them lighter than others. A trial will come and the believer will say: This will destroy me, then it will pass, then a trial will come and the believer will say: This, then it will pass. Whoever among you wishes to be removed from the Fire and admitted to Paradise, let death overtake him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him treat people as he loves to be treated. And whoever pledges allegiance to an imam and gives him the clasp of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as much as he can, and if another comes disputing him, strike the neck of the other. He said: So I pushed my head through the people and said: I adjure you by Allah, did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he pointed with his hand to his ears and said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it. He said: So I said: This cousin of yours Muawiya orders us to consume our wealth among us falsely and to kill ourselves, and Allah the Exalted has said: O you who believe, do not consume your wealth among you falsely. He said: So he gathered his hands and placed them on his forehead, then lowered his head for a while, then raised his head and said: Obey him in obedience to Allah and disobey him in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"6504","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was not obscene nor deliberately obscene, and he used to say: Among the best of you are the best of you in character."
"6505","Ismail narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abi Lubaba narrated to me, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, Abu Abdullah the freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to us while we were circumambulating the House, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are no days in which deeds are more beloved to Allah than these days. It was said: Not even striving in the path of Allah. He said: Not even striving in the path of Allah, except one who goes out with himself and his wealth and then does not return until his lifeblood is shed. He said: So I met Habib ibn Abi Thabit and asked him about this hadith, and he narrated to me something like this hadith. He said: And Abdah said: They are the ten days."
"6506","Ismail narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Read the Quran in a month. Then he kept reducing with me and I kept reducing with him until it came down to seven."
"6507","Ismail narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Aslam al-Ijli, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Sur. He said: A horn that will be blown into."
"6508","Ismail narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, that Abdullah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how will that be. He said: When their covenants and trusts are corrupted and they become like this, and Yunus interlaced his fingers describing that. He said: I said: What should I do at that time, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and take what you know and leave what you disapprove of, and concern yourself with your own circle, and beware of their common folk."
"6509","Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Shuba, Amr ibn Murra narrated to me, I heard a man in the house of Abu Ubayda, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr narrating to Ibn Umar that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever shows off to people with his deed, Allah will expose him before the hearing of His creation and belittle him and humiliate him. He said: So the eyes of Abdullah shed tears."
"6510","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhnas, al-Walid ibn Abdullah informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I used to write down everything I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, intending to memorize it, but Quraysh forbade me and said: You write down everything you hear from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is a man who speaks in anger and contentment. So I refrained from writing, then I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Write, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, nothing has come out of me except truth."
"6511","Yahya narrated to me, from Hisham, he dictated it to us: My father narrated to me: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr from his mouth to my mouth saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give rulings without knowledge, so they go astray and mislead."
"6512","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Mansur narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Amr: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying while seated. I said to him: I was told that you say the prayer of one seated is half the prayer of one standing. He said: I am not like you."
"6513","Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw him wearing two saffron-dyed garments and said: These are the clothes of the disbelievers, do not wear them."
"6514","Yahya narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Burayda narrated to us, from Abu Sabra, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad used to ask about the Hawd, the Hawd of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he used to deny it after asking Abu Barza and al-Bara ibn Azib and Aidh ibn Amr and another man, and he used to deny it. So Abu Sabra said: I will narrate to you a hadith in which there is healing for this. Your father sent with me some wealth to Muawiya, and I met Abdullah ibn Amr, and he narrated to me from what he heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and dictated to me, and I wrote it with my hand, neither adding a letter nor omitting a letter. He narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah does not love obscenity, or He hates the obscene and the deliberately obscene. He said: And the Hour will not rise until obscenity and deliberate obscenity appear, and severing of kinship, and bad neighboring, and until the traitor is trusted and the trustworthy is betrayed. And he said: Indeed your appointed meeting is my Hawd, its width and length are one, and it is like what is between Ayla and Mecca, and it is a journey of a month, in it are pitchers like the stars, its drink is whiter than silver. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it ever. So Ubayd Allah said: I have never heard about the Hawd a hadith more established than this, so he believed it and took the sheet and kept it with him."
"6515","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Amir narrated to us, he said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Amr and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"6516","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Yahya ibn Hakim ibn Safwan, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I collected the Quran and recited it every night, and that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: I fear that a long time may pass over you and you will become weary. Read it every month. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth. He said: Read it every twenty. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth. He said: Read it every ten. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth. He said: Read it every seven. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and youth. But he refused."
"6517","Yahya narrated to us, from Shuba, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed during the eclipse of the sun two rakahs."
"6518","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw on one of his companions a ring of gold and turned away from him, so he threw it away and took a ring of iron, and he said: This is worse, this is the ornament of the people of the Fire. So he threw it away and took a ring of silver, and he was silent about it."
"6519","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Umayr Abu al-Yaqzan, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The dusty earth has not carried, nor has the green sky shaded, a man more truthful than Abu Dharr."
"6520","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Amr ibn al-As had gone to put on his clothes to catch up with me, and he said while we were with him: A cursed man will enter upon you. By Allah, I remained fearful, looking out for one entering and going out, until so-and-so entered, meaning al-Hakam."
"6521","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When you see my nation fearing the oppressor so as to say to him: You are an oppressor, then they have been forsaken. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be in my nation a collapse and a transformation and a pelting."
"6522","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Qilaba, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"6523","Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Amr, and Abdullah ibn Masud was mentioned, and he said: That is a man I will always love forever. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Take the Quran from four: from Ibn Umm Abd, and he began with him, and from Muadh, and from Salim the freedman of Abu Hudhayfa. Yala said: And I forgot the fourth."
"6524","Yala narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The womb is attached to the Throne, and the maintainer is not the mere requiter, but the maintainer is the one who joins it when his kinship is cut."
"6525","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Naim the freedman of Umm Salama, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I performed Hajj with him, until when we were on one of the roads of Mecca, I saw him look at a tree until when it became clear, he sat beneath it, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, beneath this tree when a man came from this mountain path and greeted the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then said: O Messenger of Allah, I have intended to strive with you, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and the Hereafter. He said: Is either of your parents alive. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, both of them. He said: Then go back and be dutiful to your parents. He said: So he turned back from where he had come."
"6526","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from his father, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr and Abdullah ibn Umar met, then Abdullah ibn Umar came forward while weeping, and the people said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: What this one narrated to me. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No person will enter Paradise in whose heart is the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance."
"6527","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan and Misar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas al-Makki, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He has not fasted who fasts perpetually."
"6528","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perform ablution fully."
"6529","Waki narrated to us, Misar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, Sufyan raised it as the saying of the Prophet and Misar stopped it as the saying of the companion, he said: Among the major sins is that a man reviles his parents. They said: And how would a man revile his parents. He said: He reviles the father of a man, so he reviles his father, and he reviles his mother, so he reviles his mother."
"6530","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Rayhan ibn Yazid al-Amiri, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man nor for one strong and able-bodied."
"6531","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan, from Abu Zura, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sun will rise from its west and the Beast will emerge to people in the forenoon, so whichever of them comes out before the other, the other is near after it, and I do not think it is except the rising of the sun from its west that is first."
"6532","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from his uncle al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the briber and the bribe-taker."
"6533","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ayyub: I heard al-Qasim ibn Rabia narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The victim of mistaken killing that resembles the intentional, killed by a whip or a stick, for him is one hundred, forty of them pregnant in their bellies."
"6534","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan and Misar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best fasting is the fasting of my brother Dawud, peace be upon him. He used to fast a day and break fast a day, and he did not flee when he met the enemy."
"6535","Waki narrated to us, Hammam narrated to me, from Qatada, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever reads the Quran in less than three has not understood it."
"6536","Waki narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me with saffron-dyed clothes on me and said: Cast them off, for they are the clothes of the disbelievers."
"6537","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jaban, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Neither the one who reminds of his favors, nor the wine addict, will enter Paradise."
"6538","Yazid narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, Aswad ibn Masud narrated to me, from Hanzala ibn Khuwaylid al-Anazi, he said: While I was with Muawiya, two men came to him disputing over the head of Ammar, each one saying: I killed him. So Abdullah ibn Amr said: Let one of you give it up to his companion with a good heart, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The rebellious party will kill him. Muawiya said: Then what are you doing with us. He said: My father complained about me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Obey your father as long as he is alive and do not disobey him. So I am with you but I am not fighting."
"6539","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Abbas the freedman of Banu al-Dil, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: Men who exert themselves strenuously in worship were mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: That is the eagerness of Islam and its zeal, and for every eagerness there is a zeal, and for every zeal there is a lull. So whoever whose lull is toward moderation and the Sunna, then he is on the right course, and whoever whose lull is toward sins, then he is doomed."
"6540","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki narrated to me, from Abu al-Abbas the freedman of Banu al-Dil, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: Men among his companions who exert themselves severely in worship were mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is the eagerness of Islam and its zeal, and for every eagerness there is a zeal, and for every zeal there is a lull. So whoever whose lull is toward the Book and the Sunna, then he is on the right course, and whoever whose lull is toward disobedience of Allah, then he is doomed."
"6541","Yazid narrated to us, Hariz informed us, Hibban al-Sharabi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said while on the minbar: Show mercy and you will be shown mercy, and forgive and Allah will forgive you. Woe to the funnels of speech. Woe to those who persist, who persist in what they did while they know."
"6542","Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Qasim, narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, Hibban ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the minbar saying it, and he mentioned its meaning."
"6543","Yazid narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Asim ibn Sufyan, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as far as Nafi knows that he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates the eloquent man who rolls his tongue as the cow rolls with its tongue."
"6544","Yazid narrated to us, Misar informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asking his permission for striving, and he said: Are your parents alive. He said: Yes. He said: Then in them strive."
"6545","Yazid and Affan narrated to us, Yazid said: informed us, and Affan said: narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Shuayb ibn Abdullah ibn Amr, from his father Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Fast a day and you will have ten. I said: Give me more. He said: Fast two days and you will have nine. I said: Give me more. He said: Fast three days and you will have eight."
"6546","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in how long should I read the Quran. He said: Read it every month. He said: I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Read it in twenty-five. I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Read it in twenty. He said: I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Read it in fifteen. He said: I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Read it in seven. He said: I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Whoever reads it in less than three does not understand it."
"6547","Yazid narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadala informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has forbidden for my nation wine and gambling and mizr and the kubah and the qinnin, and He has added for me the Witr prayer. Yazid said: The qinnin is the barabit."
"6548","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Ibn Sirin and Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr came and asked permission, and he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. Then Umar came and asked permission, and he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. Then Uthman came and asked permission, and he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: I said: Then where am I. He said: You are with your father."
"6549","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Shuayb ibn Abdullah ibn Amr, from his father, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eating while reclining, nor two men treading his heels. Affan said: His two heels."
"6550","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Suhayb the freedman of Ibn Amir, narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever slaughters a sparrow or kills it needlessly, Amr said: I think he said: except by its right, Allah will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection."
"6551","Hasan and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Affan said: He said: Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Suhayb al-Hadhdha, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever kills a sparrow, Allah will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is its right. He said: He slaughters it properly and does not seize it by its neck and break it."
"6552","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ayyub: I heard al-Qasim ibn Rabia narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The victim of mistaken killing that resembles the intentional, killed by a whip or a stick, for him is one hundred, forty of them pregnant in their bellies."
"6553","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, and Abd al-Samad said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For wine, if they drink it, flog them, then if they drink it, flog them, then if they drink it, flog them, then if they drink it, kill them at the fourth time."
"6554","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he commanded Fatima and Ali, when they took to their beds, to glorify Allah and praise Him and magnify Him, Ata does not know which of them is thirty-four, completing one hundred. He said: So Abdullah ibn Amr said: So I have not left them since. He said: So Ibn al-Kawwa said to him: Not even on the night of Siffin. Ali said: Not even on the night of Siffin."
"6555","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Salim: I heard Yaqub ibn Asim ibn Urwa ibn Masud: I heard a man say to Abdullah ibn Amr: You say that the Hour will rise in such and such time. He said: I had intended never to narrate anything to you. I only said: You will see after a little while a great matter, like the burning of the House. Shuba said: This or something like it. Then Abdullah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Dajjal will emerge among my nation and remain among them for forty, I do not know: forty days, or forty years, or forty nights, or forty months. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will send Isa son of Maryam, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as if he is Urwa ibn Masud al-Thaqafi, and he will appear and destroy him. Then people will remain after him seven years with no enmity between any two. Then Allah will send a cold wind from the direction of Sham, and no one in whose heart is an atoms weight of faith will remain except it will take him, even if one of them were in the depth of a mountain, it would enter upon him. He said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And the worst of people will remain, as light as birds and with the minds of beasts, knowing no good and rejecting no evil. He said: Then Satan will appear to them and say: Will you not respond. And he will command them to worship idols, and they will worship them, while their provisions are abundant and their life is good. Then the Sur will be blown, and no one will hear it except he will incline toward it, and the first to hear it will be a man plastering his cistern, and he will fall unconscious, then no one will remain except he will fall unconscious. Then Allah will send, or Allah will send down, rain like dew or shade, Numan is the doubter, and the bodies of people will grow from it. Then it will be blown into again, and they will be standing, looking. He said: Then it will be said: O people, come to your Lord, and detain them, for they will be questioned. He said: Then it will be said: Bring forth the contingent of the Fire. He said: So it will be said: How many. And it will be said: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine. For on that day children will be made grey-haired, and on that day the shin will be uncovered. Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Shuba narrated this hadith to me many times, and I checked it with him."
"6556","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Ustadh al-Hizzani, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever among my nation wears gold and dies while wearing it, Allah will forbid him the gold of Paradise, and whoever among my nation wears silk and dies while wearing it, Allah will forbid him the silk of Paradise."
"6557","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Sinan, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seek refuge from knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not heard, and a heart that does not humble itself, and a soul that is not satisfied."
"6558","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Umari narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden."
"6559","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So deeds were mentioned, and he said: There are no days in which deeds are better than these ten. They said: O Messenger of Allah, striving in the path of Allah. He said: So he deemed it great and said: Not even striving, except that a man goes out with himself and his wealth in the path of Allah, then his lifeblood is shed therein."
"6560","Abu al-Nadr and Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and deeds were mentioned, and he mentioned the like of it."
"6561","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl: An elder narrated to me, he said: I entered a mosque in Sham and prayed two rakahs, then sat down, and an elder came praying toward a pillar, and when he finished, people gathered around him, so I asked: Who is this. And they said: Abdullah ibn Amr. Then the messenger of Yazid ibn Muawiya came and said: This one wants to prevent me from narrating to you, and your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a soul that is not satisfied, and a heart that does not humble itself, and knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not heard. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from these four."
"6562","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shuayb ibn Abdullah ibn Amr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was never seen eating while reclining, nor two men treading his two heels."
"6563","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Abu Qabil al-Maafiri narrated to me, from Shufayy al-Asbahi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us with two books in his hand and said: Do you know what these two books are. He said: We said: No, except that you tell us, O Messenger of Allah. He said, of the one in his right hand: This is a book from the Lord of the worlds, Blessed and Exalted, with the names of the people of Paradise and the names of their fathers and their tribes, then it has been sealed at the last of them, never to be added to nor diminished. Then he said of the one in his left: This is the book of the people of the Fire, with their names and the names of their fathers and their tribes, then it has been sealed at the last of them, never to be added to nor diminished. So the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then for what should we act, if this is a matter already finished. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be right and draw near, for the companion of Paradise will be sealed for him with the deed of the people of Paradise, whatever deed he does, and the companion of the Fire will be sealed for him with the deed of the people of the Fire, whatever deed he does. Then he said with his hand and clenched it, then said: Your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has finished with the servants. Then he said with the right and cast with it and said: A party in Paradise, and he cast with the left and said: A party in the Blaze."
"6564","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has forbidden for my nation wine and gambling and mizr and the qinnin and the kubah, and He has added for me the Witr prayer."
"6565","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Sharik al-Maafiri informed us, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi al-Tanukhi say that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I do not care what I take, or I do not care what I ride, when I drink theriac, or he said: hang an amulet, or compose poetry from myself. Al-Maafiri is the doubter: I do not care what I ride, or I do not care what I take."
"6566","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywa and Ibn Lahia narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Sharik informed us, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The best of companions with Allah is the best of them to his companion, and the best of neighbors with Allah is the best of them to his neighbor."
"6567","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywa and Ibn Lahia narrated to us, they said: Shurahbil ibn Sharik narrated to us, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The whole world is enjoyment, and the best enjoyment of the world is the righteous woman."
"6568","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, Kab ibn Alqama informed us, that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr say that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When you hear a caller to prayer, say like what he says, then invoke blessings upon me, for whoever invokes a blessing upon me, Allah will bless him with it tenfold, then ask for me al-Wasila, for it is a station in Paradise befitting only one servant among the servants of Allah, and I hope that I am he. So whoever asks al-Wasila for me, intercession becomes due for him."
"6569","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, Abu Hani informed me, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The hearts of the children of Adam are all between two fingers of the Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic, as one heart, turning as He wills. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Turner of hearts, turn our hearts to Your obedience."
"6570","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me, Maruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me, from Abu Ushshana al-Maafiri, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Do you know the first of Allahs creation to enter Paradise. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The first of Allahs creation to enter Paradise are the poor and the emigrants, through whom the frontiers are guarded and through whom hardships are warded off, and one of them dies with his need in his chest, unable to fulfill it. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to whomever of His angels He wills: Go to them and greet them. So the angels say: We are the dwellers of Your heaven and the best of Your creation, would You command us to go to these and greet them. He said: They were servants worshipping Me, not associating anything with Me, and through them the frontiers were guarded and through them hardships were warded off, and one of them dies with his need in his chest, unable to fulfill it. He said: So the angels come to them at that, and enter upon them from every gate: Peace upon you for what you endured, and excellent is the final abode."
"6571","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Abu Ushshana narrated to us, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The first group to enter Paradise are the poor emigrants, through whom hardships are warded off, and when they are commanded, they hear and obey, and when one of them has a need from the ruler, it is not fulfilled for him until he dies with it in his chest. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will call Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and it will come with its adornment and beauty, and He will say: Where are My servants who fought in My path and were killed and harmed in My path and strove in My path. Enter Paradise. So they will enter it without reckoning nor punishment. And he mentioned the hadith."
"6572","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us from his book, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Sharik narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Successful is one who submits and is given sufficiency and Allah makes him content with what He has given him."
"6573","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Rabia ibn Sayf al-Maafiri narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, the bier of a disbeliever passes by us, should we stand for it. So he said: Yes, stand for it, for you do not stand for it, rather you stand in veneration of the One who seizes souls."
"6574","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Rabia ibn Sayf al-Maafiri narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: While we were walking with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he saw a woman we did not think he knew, and when we turned toward the road, he stopped until she reached him, and she was Fatima the daughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may Allah be pleased with her. So he said: What brought you out of your house, O Fatima. She said: I came to the people of this house and offered mercy for their dead and consoled them. So he said: Perhaps you reached with them al-Kuda. She said: Allah forbid that I should have reached it with them, and I have heard you mention concerning that what you mention. He said: If you had reached it with them, you would not see Paradise until the grandfather of your father sees it."
"6575","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to me, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Teach me to recite, O Messenger of Allah. He said to him: Read three from Dhat al-Ra. So the man said: My age is great and my heart is hard and my tongue is thick. He said: Then read from Dhat Ha-Mim. So he said the like of his first saying. So he said: Read three from the Musabbihat. So he said the like of his saying. So the man said: But teach me, O Messenger of Allah, a comprehensive surah. So he taught him: When the earth is shaken, until when he finished it, the man said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never add to it ever. Then the man turned away, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The little man has prospered, the little man has prospered. Then he said: Bring him to me. So he came to him, and he said to him: I have been commanded with the Day of Sacrifice, Allah has made it a feast for this nation. So the man said: What if I find only a kid goat of my son, should I sacrifice it. He said: No, but take from your hair and trim your nails and cut your moustache and shave your pubic hair, for that is the completion of your sacrifice with Allah."
"6576","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Kab ibn Alqama narrated to me, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he mentioned prayer one day and said: Whoever guards it, it will be for him a light and a proof and a salvation on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever does not guard it, there will be for him neither light nor proof nor salvation, and he will be on the Day of Resurrection with Qarun and Pharaoh and Haman and Ubayy ibn Khalaf."
"6577","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywa and Ibn Lahia narrated to us, they said: Abu Hani al-Khawlani narrated to us, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: No raiding party raids in the path of Allah and gains booty except they hasten two-thirds of their reward from the Hereafter, and a third remains for them. And if they gain no booty, their reward is completed for them."
"6578","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywa narrated to us, Abu Hani informed me, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The poor emigrants precede the rich on the Day of Resurrection by forty autumns. Abdullah said: If you wish, we will give you from what we have, and if you wish, we will mention your case to the ruler. They said: We will endure and ask for nothing."
"6579","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywa and Ibn Lahia narrated to us, they said: Abu Hani al-Khawlani informed us, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah decreed the decrees before He created the heavens and the earth by fifty thousand years."
"6580","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Musa, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us: I heard my father narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, when mentioning the people of the Fire: Every coarse, insolent, arrogant hoarder and withholder."
"6581","Hajjaj and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which deeds are best. He said: That you feed food and greet whom you know and whom you do not know."
"6582","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Rabia ibn Sayf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No Muslim dies on the day of Friday or the night of Friday except Allah shields him from the trial of the grave."
"6583","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Saqab ibn Zuhayr, from Zayd ibn Aslam, Hammad said: I think it is from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man from the desert people came wearing a cloak of sijan buttoned with silk, and said: Indeed this companion of yours has put down every horseman son of a horseman. He said: Meaning he wants to put down every horseman son of a horseman and raise every shepherd son of a shepherd. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took hold of the folds of his cloak and said: Do I not see upon you the clothing of one who has no sense. Then he said: The Prophet of Allah Nuh, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when death came to him, said to his son: I am telling you the bequest. I command you with two and forbid you from two. I command you with: There is no god but Allah, for if the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed in a scale, and: There is no god but Allah, were placed in a scale, it would outweigh them. And if the seven heavens and the seven earths were a closed ring, it would shatter them. And: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, for it is the prayer of everything, and through it creation is given provision. And I forbid you from association and arrogance. He said: I said, or it was said: O Messenger of Allah, this association we know, so what is arrogance. He said: That one of us has two fine sandals with two fine straps. He said: No. He said: That one of us has a suit he wears. He said: No. He said: Arrogance is that one of us has a mount he rides. He said: No. He said: Is it that one of us has companions who sit with him. He said: No. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, then what is arrogance. He said: Scorning the truth and despising people."
"6584","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Muawiya and Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abdullah, do not be like so-and-so, he used to pray at night and then abandoned praying at night."
"6585","Al-Zubayri, meaning Abu Ahmad, narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me, and he mentioned the like of it."
"6586","Abu Ahmad and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, this is in the hadith of Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, he said: A man stayed with Masruq and said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever meets Allah while not associating anything with Him will enter Paradise, and no sin with it will harm him, just as if he met Him while associating with Him, he will enter the Fire, and no good deed with it will benefit him. Abu Nuaym said in his hadith: A man, or an elder, from the people of Medina came and stayed with Masruq and said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever meets Allah not associating anything with Him, no sin with it will harm him, and whoever dies while associating with Him, no good deed with it will benefit him. Abdullah said: And the correct is what Abu Nuaym said."
"6587","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, and Abd al-Samad said: My father narrated to me, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Worship the Most Merciful, and spread peace, and feed food, you will enter the Gardens. Abd al-Samad said: You will enter Paradise."
"6588","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that he narrated to them from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: A guest stayed with a man from the Children of Israel, and in his house was a pregnant dog, and the dog said: By Allah, I will not bark at the guest of my household. He said: So her pups barked in her belly. He said: It was said: What is this. He said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to a man among them: This is the likeness of a nation that will be after you, whose fools will overpower its wise."
"6589","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Jews used to say to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Poison upon you, then they would say within themselves: Why does Allah not punish us for what we say. So this verse was revealed: When they come to you they greet you with what Allah did not greet you with, to the end of the verse."
"6590","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man came and said: O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad, and associate no one with us in Your mercy. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who said it. So the man said: I did. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have restricted it against many people."
"6591","Abu Asim, and he is al-Nabil, narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar informed us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Walid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in Hell. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden wine and gambling and the kubah and ghubayra, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"6592","Wahb, meaning Ibn Jarir, narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, he said: So-and-so wanted Junada ibn Abi Umayya to be claimed as his son, so Abdullah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever claims to other than his father will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its scent is found from a distance of seventy years, or a journey of seventy years. He said: And whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6593","Husayn, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, from Abu Sufyan, from Muslim ibn Jubayr, from Amr ibn al-Harish, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, saying: We are in a land with neither dinar nor dirham, and we trade camels and sheep on credit to a term, so what do you think of that. He said: You have alighted on an expert. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, equipped an army with charity camels until they ran out and people remained, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Buy for us riding camels from the charity camels when they come, until we repay them to them. So I bought a camel for two and three young she-camels, until I finished, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, paid that from the charity camels."
"6594","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Abu Qabil informed us, from Malik ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sought refuge from seven deaths: sudden death, and the bite of a snake, and the beast, and burning, and drowning, and falling upon something or something falling upon him, and being killed while fleeing battle."
"6595","Harun ibn Maruf and Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr narrated to me, that Bakr ibn Sawada narrated to him, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr narrated to him, that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to him, that a group from Banu Hashim entered upon Asma bint Umays, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered while she was his wife that day, and saw them and disliked that, and mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: I saw only good. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has exonerated her from that. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood on the minbar and said: No man after this day of mine shall enter upon a woman whose husband is absent except with one or two men."
"6596","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abdullah al-Maafiri narrated to me, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My father slaughtered his sacrifice before praying. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Tell your father to pray and then slaughter."
"6597","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abdullah narrated to us, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr brought out for us a paper and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach us, saying: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Lord of everything and God of everything, I bear witness that there is no god but You alone with no partner for You, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger, and the angels bear witness. I seek refuge in You from Satan and his association, and I seek refuge in You lest I commit a sin against myself or bring it upon a Muslim. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to teach it to Abdullah ibn Amr to say it when he wanted to sleep."
"6598","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Marry mothers of children, for I boast of them on the Day of Resurrection."
"6599","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abdullah narrated to us, that Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever goes to the congregational mosque, one step erases a sin and one step is written for him as a good deed, going and returning."
"6600","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abdullah narrated to me, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man comes visiting a sick person, he says: O Allah, heal Your servant, he will wound for You an enemy and walk for You to prayer."
"6601","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Amr that a man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, the mu'adhdhins excel us with their adhan. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Say as they say, and when you finish, ask and you will be given."
"6602","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me that Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Amr said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the best of deeds, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer. Then he said: What next? He said: Prayer. Then he said: What next? He said: Prayer, three times. He said: Then when it overcame him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jihad in the cause of Allah. The man said: But I have two parents. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I command you to treat your parents well. He said: By the One Who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, I will surely fight and I will surely leave them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You know best."
"6603","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me that Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the tormentors of the graves, so Umar said: Will our minds be restored to us, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, as you are today. So Umar said: Stone in the mouth."
"6604","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I recite the Quran but I do not find my heart grasping it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your heart has been filled with faith, and faith is given to the servant before the Quran."
"6605","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Murayh al-Khawlani, he said: I heard Abu Qays, the freedman of Amr ibn al-As, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr saying: Whoever sends one blessing upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah and His angels send seventy blessings upon him, so let a servant do little of that or much."
"6606","And I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day as if bidding farewell, and said: I am Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet - he said it three times - and there is no prophet after me. I have been given the openings of speech and its seals and its comprehensive utterances, and I know how many are the keepers of the Fire and the bearers of the Throne, and exemption was granted to me and to my ummah, so hear and obey as long as I am among you, and when I am taken away, then upon you is the Book of Allah: permit its lawful and forbid its unlawful."
"6607","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Abd Allah, and another time he said: Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah informed me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day as if bidding farewell, and he mentioned it."
"6608","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah from Abu Hubayrah al-Kala'i from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day and said: My Lord has forbidden for me wine, gambling, mizr, the kubah and the qinnin."
"6609","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us from Shurahbil ibn Sharik from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has succeeded who believed and was provided sufficiency and Allah made him content with it."
"6610","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Abu Hani al-Khawlani narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the son of Adam is upon two fingers of the fingers of the Almighty, Exalted is He; when He wills to turn it, He turns it. And he used to often say: O Turner of hearts."
"6611","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal said, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah: Sharik narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Sa'ib ibn Malik from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were the rich and women."
"6612","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to castrate myself. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The castration of my ummah is fasting and standing in prayer."
"6613","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari was in a gathering saying: Can none of you stand with a third of the Quran every night? They said: And can we do that? He said: Then Say: He is Allah, the One is a third of the Quran. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while he was hearing Abu Ayyub, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Ayyub has spoken the truth."
"6614","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that a man brought a son of his to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine recites the Mushaf by day and stays awake by night. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you dislike about your son remaining mindful and spending the night safe?"
"6615","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, he narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a chamber whose outside is seen from its inside and its inside from its outside. So Abu Musa al-Ash'ari said: For whom is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: For whoever softens speech and feeds food and stands at night for Allah while people are sleeping."
"6616","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me that Tawbah ibn Namir narrated to him that Abu Ufayr Arif ibn Sari' narrated to him that a man asked Ibn Amr ibn al-As and said: An orphan was in my care; I gave him a slave girl in charity, then he died and I am his heir. So Abd Allah ibn Amr said to him: I will inform you of what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Umar ibn al-Khattab carried on a horse in the cause of Allah, then he found its owner had stopped it offering it for sale, and he wanted to buy it, so he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he forbade him from it and said: When you give charity, carry it through."
"6617","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate saying: O Allah, forgive us our sins and our wrongdoing and our jest and our earnestness and our deliberate acts, and all of that is with us."
"6618","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these words: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the overwhelming of debt and the overwhelming of the enemy and the gloating of enemies."
"6619","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, would lie down on his right side."
"6620","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he lay down to sleep, would say: In Your name, my Lord, I have laid my side, so forgive me my sin."
"6621","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him safeguard his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."
"6622","Musa ibn Dawud and Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Hilal ibn Ali from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: I met Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As and said: Inform me of the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Torah. So he said: Yes, by Allah, he is described in the Torah with his description in the Quran: O Prophet, We have sent you as a witness and a bearer of glad tidings and a warner and a safeguard for the unlettered, and you are My servant and My Messenger; I have named you al-Mutawakkil; you are not harsh nor rude nor loud in the markets - Yunus said: nor clamorous in the markets - and you do not repel evil with evil, but you pardon and forgive; and He will not take him until He straightens through him the crooked creed, that they say: There is no god but Allah, and He opens thereby blind eyes and deaf ears and covered hearts. Ata said: I met Ka'b and asked him, and they did not differ in a letter except that Ka'b says in his dialect: blind eyes and deaf ears and covered hearts. Yunus said: ghulfa."
"6623","Hasan narrated to us, Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifah, narrated to us from Abu Janab from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution, a lingering ablution, so he raised his head and looked at me and said: Six among you, O ummah: the death of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - as if my heart was torn from its place. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One. He said: And wealth will overflow among you until a man is given ten thousand and still resents it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two. He said: And a trial that will enter the house of every man among you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three. He said: And death like the plague of sheep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four. And a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar; they will gather against you for nine months, like the carrying of a woman, then they will be more treacherous than you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five. He said: And the conquest of a city. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Six. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which city? He said: Constantinople."
"6624","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Haywah, meaning Ibn Shurayh, narrated to me from Ibn Shufayy al-Asbahi from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the warrior is his reward, and for the one who equips him is his reward and the reward of the warrior."
"6625","Ishaq narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to me from Ibn Shufayy al-Asbahi from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A return is like a raid."
"6626","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting and the Quran will intercede for the servant on the Day of Resurrection. Fasting will say: My Lord, I prevented him from food and desires by day, so let me intercede for him. And the Quran will say: I prevented him from sleep by night, so let me intercede for him. He said: So they will both be allowed to intercede."
"6627","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Husayn al-Mu'allim from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying, turning from his right and from his left; and I saw him praying barefoot and shod; and I saw him drinking standing and sitting. Muhammad, meaning Ghundar, said: Al-Husayn informed us of it from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather."
"6628","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales in one sale, and a sale with a loan, and profit on what is not guaranteed, and selling what is not with you."
"6629","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who takes back what he gifted is like the dog that vomits then eats from it; and when the giver takes back, let him be stopped with what he took back, then let what he gifted be returned to him."
"6630","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us from al-A'mash, Uthman narrated to us from Abu Harb al-Dili: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither the green sky has shaded nor the dusty earth has carried a man more truthful in speech than Abu Dharr."
"6631","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As that he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so it was called: Prayer in congregation. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed two bowings in one prostration, then stood and bowed two bowings in one prostration, then the sun cleared. He said: A'ishah said: I never prostrated a prostration nor bowed a bowing that was longer than it."
"6632","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Ata from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr that a man said one day as he entered prayer: Praise be to Allah filling the heaven; and he glorified and supplicated. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who said them? So the man said: I did. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw the angels receiving them, some of them meeting others with them."
"6633","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us from his book, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh narrated to us: I heard Shurahbil ibn Yazid al-Ma'afiri that he heard Muhammad ibn Hudayyah al-Sadafi saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters."
"6634","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters."
"6635","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr from Abd Allah ibn Amr that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What distances me from the anger of Allah, Exalted is He? He said: Do not become angry."
"6636","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The souls of the believers meet at a day's journey, though neither of them has ever seen his companion."
"6637","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh al-Ma'afiri narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Yazid narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Hudayyah from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters."
"6638","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment; they took spoils and returned quickly. So people talked of the nearness of their raid and the abundance of their spoils and the speed of their return. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to nearer in raid than it, and more in spoils, and swifter in return? Whoever performs ablution then goes to the mosque for the forenoon supererogatory prayer, he is nearer in raid and more in spoils and swifter in return."
"6639","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint me over something I can live by. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hamzah, is a soul you give life to more beloved to you, or a soul you kill? He said: Rather a soul I give life to. He said: Then keep to yourself."
"6640","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear for my ummah only milk, for Satan is between the foam and the pure milk."
"6641","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the deed of Paradise? He said: Truthfulness; when the servant is truthful he is dutiful, and when he is dutiful he believes, and when he believes he enters Paradise. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the deed of the Fire? He said: Lying; when the servant lies he is wicked, and when he is wicked he disbelieves, and when he disbelieves he enters, meaning the Fire."
"6642","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted is He, looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives His servants except for two: one harboring grudges and a killer of a soul."
"6643","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr saying: The Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was riding his mount, and it could not carry him, so he dismounted from it."
"6644","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Rabi'ah ibn Yazid narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami, he said: I entered upon Abd Allah ibn Amr while he was in a garden of his at al-Ta'if called al-Waht, and he was holding by the waist a youth of Quraysh suspected of drinking wine. So I said: It reached me from you a hadith that whoever drinks a draught of wine, Allah will not accept repentance from him for forty mornings, and that the wretched is he who is wretched in his mother's womb, and that whoever comes to Bayt al-Maqdis intending nothing but prayer in it comes out of his sins as the day his mother bore him. When the youth heard the mention of wine, he pulled his hand from his hand then left. Then Abd Allah ibn Amr said: I do not permit anyone to report from me what I did not say. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever drinks a draught of wine, prayer will not be accepted from him for forty mornings; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he returns, prayer will not be accepted from him for forty mornings; if he repents, Allah turns to him; if he returns, he said: I do not know whether on the third or the fourth - if he returns, it will be due upon Allah to give him to drink from the pus of the wounded on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, Exalted is He, created His creation in darkness, then cast upon them of His light on that day; so whoever was struck by His light that day was guided, and whoever missed it went astray; therefore I say: The pen has dried upon the knowledge of Allah, Exalted is He. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Sulayman ibn Dawud, peace be upon him, asked Allah for three things; He gave him two, and we hope the third is his. He asked Him for judgment coinciding with His judgment, so Allah gave it to him; and he asked Him for a kingdom that befits no one after him, so He gave it to him; and he asked Him that any man who leaves his house wanting nothing but prayer in this mosque comes out of his sins as the day his mother bore him; so we hope that Allah, Exalted is He, has given it to him."
"6645","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Qabil narrated to me, he said: We were with Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As and he was asked: Which of the two cities will be opened first, Constantinople or Rome? So Abd Allah called for a chest of his with rings. He said: He brought out from it a book. He said: Abd Allah said: While we were around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) writing, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which of the two cities will be opened first, Constantinople or Rome? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The city of Heraclius will be opened first, meaning Constantinople."
"6646","Surayj narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us from Mu'awiyah ibn Sa'id from Abu Qabil from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies on Friday or the night of Friday is protected from the trial of the grave."
"6647","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us from Abu Salim al-Jayshani from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful to marry a woman upon the divorce of her sister, nor is it lawful for a man to outbid his companion until he leaves it, nor is it lawful for three persons in a desert land except to appoint one of them over them, nor is it lawful for three persons in a desert land for two to converse privately to the exclusion of their companion."
"6648","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us from Ali ibn Rabah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The upright Muslim attains the rank of the fasting, night-praying one through the verses of Allah, by his good character and generous nature."
"6649","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Yazid from Ibn Hujayrah from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The upright Muslim - then he mentioned it."
"6650","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us from Jundub ibn Abd Allah that he heard Sufyan ibn Awf saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day while we were with him: Glad tidings to the strangers. It was said: Who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Righteous people among many evil people; those who disobey them are more than those who obey them. He said: And we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) another day when the sun rose, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come people of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection whose light is like the light of the sun. We said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The poor emigrants, those by whom hardships are warded off; one of them dies with his need in his chest; they will be gathered from the regions of the earth."
"6651","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Rashid ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri narrated to us that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrating from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the spoil of gatherings of remembrance? He said: The spoil of gatherings of remembrance is Paradise, Paradise."
"6652","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami from Ibn Hujayrah from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four, when they are in you, you do not care what you miss of the world: guarding a trust, truthful speech, good character, and chastity in purity."
"6653","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us from Suwayd ibn Qays from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guarding the frontier for a day is better than fasting a month and standing it in prayer."
"6654","Hasan and Ishaq ibn Isa and Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Amr al-Ma'afiri narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is silent is saved."
"6655","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hearts are vessels, and some are more capacious than others. When you ask Allah, Exalted is He, O people, ask Him while you are certain of the answer, for Allah does not answer a servant who calls Him from behind a heedless heart."
"6656","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man died in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over him and said: Would that he had died elsewhere than his birthplace. So a man among the people said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man dies elsewhere than his birthplace, there is measured for him from his birthplace to where his trace ends in Paradise."
"6657","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Huyayy ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, he narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Amr that a woman stole in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so those she stole from brought her and said: O Messenger of Allah, this woman stole from us. Her people said: We will ransom her, meaning her family. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cut her hand. So they said: We will ransom her for five hundred dinars. He said: Cut her hand. He said: So her right hand was cut. So the woman said: Is there repentance for me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes; you are today from your sin as the day your mother bore you. So Allah, Exalted is He, revealed in Surah al-Ma'idah: But whoever repents after his wrongdoing and reforms, to the end of the verse."
"6658","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in sheep pens and would not pray in camel and cattle pens."
"6659","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr, meaning Ibn al-Harith, narrated to me from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from Abd Allah ibn Amr from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever abandons prayer drunk once, it is as if he had the world and all that is in it and was stripped of it; and whoever abandons prayer drunk four times, it is due upon Allah, Exalted is He, to give him to drink from the pus of the wounded. It was said: And what is the pus of the wounded, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The pus of the people of Hell."
"6660","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Ja'far, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us from Matar al-Warraq from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals, and I saw him praying barefoot, and I saw him drinking standing and sitting, and I saw him turning to his right and turning to his left."
"6661","Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us from Ibn Harmalah from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None narrates to the people except a ruler or one commanded or one showing off."
"6662","Husayn ibn Muhammad and Hashim, meaning Ibn al-Qasim, narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Khuza'i narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Musa from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that a Muslim is not killed for a disbeliever."
"6663","Husayn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us from Sulayman from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that whoever is killed by mistake, his blood money is one hundred camels: thirty bint makhad, thirty bint labun, thirty hiqqah, and ten sons of labun, males."
"6664","Sufyan narrated to us from Ya'qub ibn Ata and others from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of two different religions do not inherit from one another."
"6665","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man marries a virgin, he stays with her three days."
"6666","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave contracted for one hundred ounces who pays them except ten ounces is still a slave."
"6667","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: Two women came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with bracelets of gold on their hands, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Do you love that Allah bracelet you on the Day of Resurrection with bracelets of fire? They said: No. He said: Then give the due of this that is on your hands."
"6668","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day while people were talking about the decree. He said: As if pomegranate seeds had burst in his face from anger. He said: So he said to them: What is with you, striking the Book of Allah, part of it against part? With this those before you perished. He said: I never congratulated myself for a sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I did not attend as I congratulated myself for that sitting that I did not attend."
"6669","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand at the second jamrah longer than he stood at the first jamrah, then he came to the jamrah of al-Aqabah, stoned it, and did not stand at it."
"6670","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the two circumcised parts meet and the glans disappears, ghusl has become obligatory."
"6671","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, my father narrated to me from his father, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amr mentioned, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A loan with a sale is not lawful, nor two conditions in a sale, nor profit on what is not guaranteed, nor the sale of what is not with you."
"6672","Isma'il narrated to us, Layth narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pluck grey hair, for it is the light of the Muslim; no Muslim grows grey hair in Islam except a good deed is written for him thereby and he is raised a degree thereby or a sin is removed from him thereby."
"6673","Isma'il narrated to us from Layth from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever withholds surplus water or surplus pasture, Allah withholds His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6674","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Ubayd Allah, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"6675","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not pluck grey hair, for no servant grows grey in Islam except Allah writes for him thereby a good deed and removes from him thereby a sin."
"6676","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying and selling in the mosque, and that poems be recited in it, and that lost property be announced in it, and circles on Friday before prayer."
"6677","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The arrogant will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection like ants in the form of men; all littleness overcomes them until they enter a prison in Hell called Bulas; the fire of fires overcomes them; they are given to drink the pus of the wounded, the pus of the people of the Fire."
"6678","Yahya narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me from his father from his grandfather, he said: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father wants to take all my wealth. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father; the sweetest you eat is from your earnings, and the wealth of your children is from your earnings, so eat it wholesomely."
"6679","Yahya narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us from his father from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying barefoot and shod, and fasting in travel and breaking fast, and drinking standing and sitting, and turning to his right and to his left."
"6680","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw on one of his companions a ring of gold, so he turned away from him; so he threw it away and took a ring of iron. He said: So he said: This is worse; this is the jewelry of the people of the Fire. So he threw it away and took a ring of silver, and he was silent about him."
"6681","Yahya narrated to us from Husayn from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: When Makkah was opened to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hold back weapons except Khuza'ah against Banu Bakr. So he permitted them until he prayed Asr, then he said: Hold back weapons. Then a man of Khuza'ah met a man of Banu Bakr the next day at al-Muzdalifah and killed him. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood preaching. He said: And I saw him leaning his back to the Ka'bah. He said: The most hostile of people to Allah is he who kills in the sanctuary, or kills other than his killer, or kills for the grudges of the Jahiliyyah. So a man stood to him and said: So-and-so is my son. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No claim in Islam; the matter of the Jahiliyyah has gone; the child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is al-athlab. They said: And what is al-athlab? He said: The stone. He said: And for fingers, ten ten; and for wounds exposing the bone, five five. He said: And he said: No prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and no prayer after Asr until the sun sets. He said: And a woman is not married upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt, and no gift by a woman is permitted except with her husband's permission."
"6682","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined the two prayers on the day he raided Banu al-Mustaliq."
"6683","Ya'la narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: I heard a man of Muzaynah asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, I came asking you about the lost camel. He said: With it are its shoes and its water skin; it eats trees and comes to water, so leave it until its seeker comes to it. He said: The lost sheep? He said: For you or for your brother or for the wolf; gather it until its seeker comes to it. He said: The grazing animal taken from its pastures? He said: In it is its price twice and an exemplary beating, and what is taken from its resting place, in it is cutting if what is taken thereof reaches the price of the shield. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and fruits and what is taken thereof in their calyxes? He said: Whoever takes with his mouth and does not take in a garment, nothing is upon him; and whoever carries away, upon him is its price twice and beating and punishment, and what is taken from its storehouses, in it is cutting if what is taken thereof reaches the price of the shield. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and lost property we find on the inhabited road? He said: Announce it for a year; if its seeker is found, give it to him, otherwise it is yours. He said: What is found in the ruined ancient site? He said: In it and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"6684","Ya'la narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: A bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about ablution, so he showed him three three. He said: This is ablution; whoever exceeds this has done badly, transgressed, and wronged."
"6685","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed three umrahs, all of that in Dhu al-Qa'dah, calling talbiyah until he touched the Stone."
"6686","Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed three umrahs, all of that in Dhu al-Qa'dah, calling talbiyah until he touched the Stone."
"6687","Ibn Idris narrated to us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the value of the shield in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ten dirhams."
"6688","Waki' narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he heard it from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir in Eid twelve takbirs, seven in the first and five in the last, and he did not pray before it nor after it. My father said: And I hold to this."
"6689","Waki' narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Dawud narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command your children to pray when they reach seven, and strike them for it when they reach ten, and separate between them in beds. My father said: And al-Tufawi Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman said in this hadith Sawwar Abu Hamzah, and erred in it."
"6690","Waki' narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his sermon while leaning his back to the Ka'bah: A Muslim is not killed for a disbeliever, nor one with a covenant while in his covenant."
"6691","Waki' narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a date in his house under his side and ate it."
"6692","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the year of the conquest, he stood among the people preaching and said: O people, whatever alliance there was in the Jahiliyyah, Islam has only increased it in strength; there is no alliance in Islam; the Muslims are one hand against others; their blood is equal; the lowest of them grants protection, and the farthest of them returns upon them; their detachments are returned upon those who sit; a believer is not killed for a disbeliever; the blood money of the disbeliever is half the blood money of the Muslim; there is no jallab nor janab, and their charities are not taken except in their lands."
"6693","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted is He, has added you a prayer, and it is witr."
"6694","Yazid narrated to us from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined the two prayers in travel."
"6695","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam informed us from Qatadah from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat and drink and give charity and dress without conceit nor excess. And Yazid once said: Without extravagance nor conceit."
"6696","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us words we say at sleep from fright: In the name of Allah, I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His anger and His punishment and the evil of His servants and from the whispers of the devils and that they attend me. He said: Abd Allah ibn Amr used to teach them to the grown among his children to say at his sleep, and whoever among them was small, unable to memorize, he wrote it for him and hung it on his neck."
"6697","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us from Ata from Jabir and from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir and from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and for the people of Syria at al-Juhfah, and for the people of Yemen and the people of Tihamah at Yalamlam, and for the people of al-Ta'if, which is Najd, at Qarn, and for the people of Iraq at Dhat Irq."
"6698","Yazid narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Rashid from Sulayman ibn Musa from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of a treacherous man nor a treacherous woman is permitted; and he rejected the testimony of the dependent servant follower of the household, and permitted it for others."
"6699","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid informed us from Sulayman ibn Musa from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed: Any child claimed after his father to whom he is attributed, his heirs claiming him - he decreed: If he is from a free woman he married or from a slave woman he owns, he is joined to the one who claimed him; and if he is from a free woman or a slave woman he fornicated with, he is not joined to the one who claimed him; and if his father to whom he is attributed is the one who claimed him, and he is a son of adultery, he belongs to the people of his mother, whoever they are, free or slave."
"6700","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us from Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have kin whom I join and they cut me, and I pardon and they wrong, and I do good and they do evil; shall I requite them? He said: No, then you would all be abandoned together; but take to excellence and join them, for there will remain with you a supporter from Allah, Exalted is He, as long as you are upon that."
"6701","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Yusuf, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three attend the Friday prayer: a man who attends it with supplication and prayer, so that is a man who supplicated his Lord; if He wills He gives him, and if He wills He withholds from him; and a man who attends it with silence and listening attentively, so that is its due right; and a man who attends it engaging in idle talk, so that is his share of it."
"6702","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I sat, I and my brother, a sitting I would not love to have red camels in exchange for it. I came forward, I and my brother, and there were elderly men from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting at one of his doors, so we disliked to separate between them, so we sat aside, when they mentioned a verse of the Quran and disputed about it until their voices rose, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out angry, his face reddened, throwing dust at them, saying: Slowly, O people. By this the nations before you were destroyed, by their differing over their prophets and striking parts of the Books against one another. Indeed the Quran did not descend to belie one part of it another; rather one part of it confirms another. So what you know of it, act upon it, and what you do not know of it, refer it to its knower."
"6703","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man does not believe until he believes in the Decree, its good and its evil. Abu Hazim said: May Allah curse a religion I am older than it, meaning denial of the Decree."
"6704","Hushaym narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that al-As ibn Wail vowed in the Jahiliyyah to slaughter one hundred camels, and that Hisham ibn al-As slaughtered his share, fifty camels, and that Amr asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, so he said: As for your father, had he affirmed Tawhid, then had you fasted and given charity on his behalf, that would have benefited him."
"6705","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Said, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None takes back his gift except the father from his child, and the one who goes back in his gift is like the one who goes back in his vomit."
"6706","Abdurrahman narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the minor Lutiyyah, meaning a man approaching his wife in her anus."
"6707","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine, my belly was a vessel for him, and my lap was a shelter for him, and my breast was a drink for him, and his father claims he will take him away from me. He said: You have more right to him so long as you do not marry."
"6708","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat and drink and give charity and wear, without vanity nor extravagance. Indeed Allah loves that His blessing be seen upon His servant."
"6709","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Shuayb said, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever woman marries upon a dower or gift or promise before the marriage tie, it belongs to her; and whatever is after the marriage tie, it belongs to whom it was given to; and what a man is most entitled to be honored for is his daughter or his sister."
"6710","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed me that Ibn Jurayj informed him, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that Zinba Abu Rawh found a slave boy of his with a slave girl of his, so he cut off his nose and castrated him, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Who did this to you. He said: Zinba. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: What carried you to do this. He said: Such and such was of his affair. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the slave: Go, for you are free. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then whose freedman am I. He said: A freedman of Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined the Muslims concerning him. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, he came to Abu Bakr and said: The bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, we shall provide maintenance for you and your dependents. So he provided it for him until Abu Bakr passed away. When Umar was made caliph, he came to him and said: The bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes. Where do you intend. He said: Egypt. So Umar wrote to the governor of Egypt to give him land to eat from."
"6711","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every finger ten camels, and for every tooth five camels, and fingers are equal, and teeth are equal. Muhammad said: And I heard Makhul saying it, and he did not attribute it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abdurrazzaq said: I have not seen anyone more scrupulous in hadith than Muhammad ibn Rashid."
"6712","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abdulkarim al-Jazari, that Amr ibn Shuayb informed him, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaned against a house and exhorted the people and reminded them. He said: None shall pray after Asr until night, nor after Subh until the sun rises; and a woman shall not travel except with a mahram for a distance of three days; and no woman shall be married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt."
"6713","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the aqiqah, so he said: Indeed Allah does not love disobedience, and it is as if he disliked the name. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we only ask you about one of us to whom a child is born. He said: Whoever of you loves to sacrifice for his child, let him do so: for the boy two equal sheep, and for the girl one sheep. He said: And he was asked about the fara, he said: The fara is a right, and that you leave it until it becomes a sturdy young camel, a son of makhad or a son of labun, then you carry upon it in the cause of Allah or give it to a widow, is better than that you slaughter it with its flesh sticking to its hair, and you overturn your vessel and cause your she-camel to grieve. And he said: And he was asked about the atirah, so he said: The atirah is a right. Some of the people said to Amr ibn Shuayb: What is the atirah. He said: They used to slaughter a sheep in Rajab, then cook and eat and feed."
"6714","Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad and Surayj narrated to us, both said: Ibn Abi az-Zinad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon two men tied together walking to the House, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this tying together. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we vowed to walk to the House tied together. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is not a vow. So he cut their tying. Surayj said in his hadith: A vow is only what the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is sought by."
"6715","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, al-Faraj narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall preach except a commander, or one commanded, or an ostentatious one. So I said to him: We used to hear, or an affectatious one. He said: Thus I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it."
"6716","Abu an-Nadr and Abdussamad narrated to us, both said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the blood-money of the people of the two Books is half the blood-money of the Muslims, and they are the Jews and the Christians."
"6717","Abu an-Nadr and Abdussamad narrated to us, both said: Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills deliberately is handed over to the guardians of the slain; if they wish they kill him, and if they wish they take the blood-money, and it is thirty hiqqah and thirty jadhaah and forty khalifah, and that is the blood-money of deliberate killing; and whatever they agree upon is theirs, and that is the aggravation of the blood-money."
"6718","Abu an-Nadr and Abdussamad narrated to us, both said: Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood-money of quasi-deliberate killing is aggravated like the blood-money of deliberate killing, but its perpetrator is not killed, and that is when Satan leaps between people. Abu an-Nadr said: So it becomes blind shooting in blindness, without tribulation nor bearing of weapons."
"6719","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed: Whoever is killed by mistake, his blood-money is one hundred camels."
"6720","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sleeping and found a date under his side, so he took it and ate it, then he began to toss about at the end of the night, and one of his wives was alarmed at that, so he said: I found a date under my side and ate it, and I feared it might be from the dates of charity."
"6721","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The seller and the buyer have the choice until they separate, except if it is a transaction with a stipulated choice; and it is not lawful for him to leave him fearing he will cancel the deal."
"6722","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, that Abdullah ibn Amr wrote to an agent of his over land of his: Do not withhold your surplus water, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever withholds surplus water to withhold thereby surplus pasture, Allah will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6723","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik informed me, the trustworthy one informed me, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the urbun sale."
"6724","Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us, nor one who lies in wait by the road."
"6725","Abdussamad ibn Abdulwarith narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Habib narrated to us, from Amr, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that Abu Thalabah al-Khushani came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have trained hunting dogs, so give me a ruling about their game. So he said: If you have trained dogs, eat of what they hold for you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, slaughtered and unslaughtered. He said: Slaughtered and unslaughtered. He said: Even if it eats of it. He said: Even if it eats of it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, give me a ruling about my bow. He said: Eat what your bow holds for you. He said: Slaughtered and unslaughtered. He said: Slaughtered and unslaughtered. He said: Even if it disappears from me. He said: Even if it disappears from you, so long as it has not putrefied, meaning changed, or you find in it the trace of other than your arrow. He said: O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about the vessels of the Magians when we are compelled to them. He said: When you are compelled to them, wash them with water and cook in them."
"6726","Abdussamad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Abbas al-Jazari narrated to us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever slave makes a contract of manumission for one hundred uqiyyah and pays it except ten awaq, he is still a slave; and whatever slave makes a contract for one hundred dinars and pays it except ten dinars, he is still a slave. Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: Thus Abdussamad said, Abbas al-Jazari. In the copy it was Abbas al-Juwayri, so my father corrected it as Abdussamad said, al-Jazari."
"6727","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest: No gift by a woman is permissible except with her husband's permission."
"6728","Abdussamad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it."
"6729","Abdussamad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, and the delegations of Hawazin came to him and said: O Muhammad, we are a root and a clan, so bestow favor upon us; may Allah bestow favor upon you, for there has befallen us of calamity what is not hidden from you. So he said: Choose between your women and your wealth and your children. They said: You gave us choice between our honor and our wealth; we choose our children. So he said: As for what belongs to me and to Banu Abdulmuttalib, it is yours. When I pray Zuhr, say: We seek the intercession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the believers, and of the believers with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning our women and our children. He said: So they did so. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for what belongs to me and to Banu Abdulmuttalib, it is yours. And the Muhajirun said: And what belongs to us belongs to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the Ansar said the like of that. And Uyaynah ibn Badr said: As for what belongs to me and to Banu Fazarah, no. And al-Aqra ibn Habis said: As for me and Banu Tamim, no. And Abbas ibn Mirdas said: As for me and Banu Sulaym, no. So the two tribes said: You lied; rather it belongs to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, return to them their women and their children. Whoever holds on to anything of the booty, he shall have upon us six shares from the first thing Allah bestows upon us. Then he mounted his camel, and the people clung to him saying: Distribute our booty among us, until they forced him to a samurah tree which snatched his cloak, so he said: O people, return my cloak to me. By Allah, had you as many cattle as the trees of Tihamah, I would distribute it among you, then you would not find me miserly nor cowardly nor lying. Then he drew near to his camel and took a hair from its hump and placed it between his index and middle fingers, then raised it and said: O people, I have of this booty not even this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. So return the needle and the thread, for misappropriation will be upon its people on the Day of Resurrection shame and fire and disgrace. So a man stood with a ball of hair and said: I took this to mend the saddle blanket of a camel of mine that had sores. He said: As for what belongs to me and to Banu Abdulmuttalib, it is yours. So the man said: O Messenger of Allah, since it has reached what I see, I have no need of it, and he cast it away."
"6730","Abdussamad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charities of the Muslims are taken at their waters."
"6731","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abdulkarim, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave my mother a garden for her lifetime, and she died leaving no heir but me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your charity became due, and your garden returned to you."
"6732","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Abi az-Zinad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow except in what the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is sought by, and no oath in severing kinship."
"6733","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Abi az-Zinad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not have mercy on our young and does not know the right of our elder."
"6734","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and senility and debt and sin, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire."
"6735","Yunus and Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, both said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Shall I not inform you of the most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in sitting on the Day of Resurrection. So the people fell silent, so he repeated it two or three times. The people said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best of you in character."
"6736","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and sees another better than it, abandoning it is its expiation."
"6737","Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makki narrated to us, al-Aslami, meaning Abdullah ibn Amir, narrated to me, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed for the boy two sheep, and for the girl one sheep."
"6738","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr narrated to us, Aban, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"6739","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Qaysar at-Tujibi, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a young man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may I kiss while I am fasting. He said: No. Then an old man came and said: May I kiss while I am fasting. He said: Yes. He said: So some of us looked at one another, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knew why some of you looked at one another. Indeed the old man controls himself."
"6740","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful, two hundred times in every day, none before him surpassed him, nor shall any after him reach him, except with better than his deed."
"6741","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from az-Zuhri, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard people disputing, so he said: Those before you were destroyed only by this; they struck parts of the Book of Allah against one another. The Book of Allah only descended confirming one part of it another, so do not belie one part of it with another. What you know of it, say it, and what you do not know, entrust it to its knower."
"6742","Abdussamad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us, nor one who lies in wait by the road; and whoever is killed otherwise than that is quasi-deliberate, and its blood-money is aggravated, and its perpetrator is not killed, and it is like the sacred month in sanctity and protection."
"6743","Abdussamad and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, Husayn said in his hadith, he said: Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed by mistake, his blood-money is one hundred camels: thirty daughters of makhad, and thirty daughters of labun, and thirty hiqqah, and ten sons of labun, males."
"6744","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Jubayr, that Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to him that a group of Banu Hashim entered upon Asma bint Umays, then Abu Bakr entered while she was his wife that day, and saw them and disliked that, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw only good. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has declared her innocent of that. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the pulpit and said: No man shall enter after this day of mine upon a woman whose husband is absent except with one or two men."
"6745","Ismail ibn Muhammad, meaning Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib, narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, Mujahid narrated to us, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a slain person from among the people of dhimmah shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its scent is found from a distance of forty years."
"6746","Al-Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi az-Zinad narrated to me, from Abdurrahman, meaning Ibn al-Harith, Amr ibn Shuayb informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard a man from Muzaynah asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you say, O Messenger of Allah, about stray camels. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have you to do with them; with them are their shoes and their water. He said: Then stray sheep. He said: For you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: Then whoever takes it from its pasture. He said: He is punished and fined the like of its price; and whoever releases it from its tether or brings it out of its shelter, and they are the shaded folds, upon him is amputation. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then fruit taken in its unripe covering. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no liability upon an eater passing by. Whoever takes a load in his garment is fined the like of its price and punished; and whoever takes anything of it after it has been taken to the drying place, or breaks a door over it, and what he takes reaches the price of the shield, upon him is amputation. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then treasure we find in ruins and in ancient mounds. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In it and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"6747","Abdulwahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have no wealth, but I have an orphan. So he said: Eat from the wealth of your orphan without extravagance, or he said: And do not ransom your wealth with his wealth; Husayn doubted."
"6748","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muslim, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, from Abdurrahman, meaning Ibn Harmalah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A lone rider is a devil, and two riders are two devils, and three are a company."
"6749","Al-Khuzai, meaning Abu Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and senility and sin and debt, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire."
"6750","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, that Nawf and Abdullah ibn Amr, meaning Ibn al-As, met together, so Nawf said: Had the heavens and the earth and what is in them been placed in one scale of the balance, and La ilaha illa Allah been placed in the other scale, it would outweigh them. Had the heavens and the earth and what is in them been a layer of iron, and a man said La ilaha illa Allah, it would pierce them until it reaches Allah, Mighty and Majestic. So Abdullah ibn Amr said: We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); those who stayed stayed, and those who returned returned. Then he came (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), almost uncovering his garments from his knees, and said: Rejoice, O company of Muslims. This is your Lord; He has opened a door of the doors of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, saying: These are My servants; they have completed an obligation and are awaiting another."
"6751","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn ash-Shikhkhir, that Nawf and Abdullah ibn Amr met together, so Nawf said, and he mentioned the hadith. So Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: And I narrate to you from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night; those who stayed stayed, and those who returned returned. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came before the people assembled for Isha prayer; he came with his breath hastened, raising his finger thus, and he contracted twenty-nine, and pointed with his forefinger to the heaven, saying: Rejoice, O company of Muslims. This is your Lord, Mighty and Majestic; He has opened a door of the doors of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, saying: My angels, look at My servants; they have performed an obligation and are awaiting another."
"6752","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Ayyub al-Azdi, and from Nawf, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, and he added in it: And he almost uncovered his garment from his knees, with his breath hastened."
"6753","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, that he heard Abu al-Khayr saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best. He said: Whom people are safe from his tongue and his hand."
"6754","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Ibn Murayh, freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr, that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: Whoever sends blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once, Allah and His angels send seventy blessings upon him."
"6755","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Uksum, he said: I heard Ibn Hujayrah asking al-Qasim ibn al-Barhi: How did you hear Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As reporting. He said: I heard him saying: Two litigants disputed before Amr ibn al-As, so he judged between them, and the one judged against was displeased, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the judge judges and strives and is correct, he has ten rewards; and when he strives and errs, he has one reward or two rewards."
"6756","Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman at-Tufawi and Abdullah ibn Bakr as-Sahmi narrated to us, the meaning is one, both said: Sawwar Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command your children to pray at seven years, and strike them for it at ten years, and separate between them in beds. And when one of you marries off his slave or his hired worker, let him not look at anything of his nakedness, for what is below his navel to his knees is of his nakedness."
"6757","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Habib al-Muallim informed me, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the most insolent of people against Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is one who kills in the sanctuary of Allah, or kills other than his killer, or kills for the blood-revenge of the Jahiliyyah."
"6758","Abu Kamil and Yunus narrated to us, both said: Nafi ibn Amr narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Asim ath-Thaqafi, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: Nafi said: And I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: My father said, and Yunus did not doubt, he said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates the eloquent among men who moves his tongue as the cow moves its tongue."
"6759","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays informed us, I heard Amr ibn Shuayb narrating, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the fara, so he said: The fara is a right. If you leave it until it becomes a sturdy young camel, a son of makhad or a son of labun, then you carry upon it in the cause of Allah or give it to a widow, it is better than that you slaughter it with its flesh sticking to its hair, and you overturn your vessel and make your she-camel grieve."
"6760","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abdurrahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me and said: Have I not been told that you stand the night, or are you the one who says: I shall surely stand the night and surely fast the day. He said: I think he said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I said that. He said: So stand and sleep, and fast and break fast, and fast three days of every month, and you shall have the like of fasting the age. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I can do more than that. He said: Then fast a day and break fast two days. I said: I can do better than that. He said: Then fast a day and break fast a day, and that is the most just fasting, and it is the fasting of Dawud. I said: I can do better than that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing better than that."
"6761","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abdurrahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: It reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I say: I shall surely fast the age and surely stand the night as long as I live. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you the one who says, or you said: I shall surely fast the age and surely stand the night as long as I live. He said: I said: Yes. He said: Then you cannot bear that. He said: So stand and sleep, and fast and break fast, and fast three days of every month, for the good deed is ten like it. Then he mentioned its meaning."
"6762","Abdussamad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of az-Zuhri."
"6763","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and lengthened the standing, then bowed and lengthened the bowing, then raised and lengthened. Shubah said: And I think he said: The like of that in prostration. And he began to weep in his prostration and blow, saying: My Lord, did You not promise me this while I seek Your forgiveness; My Lord, did You not promise me this while I am among them. When he prayed, he said: Paradise was shown to me, so that had I stretched my hand I would have taken of its clusters; and the Fire was shown to me, so I began to blow fearing its heat would overwhelm you. And I saw in it the thief of the two sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and I saw in it the brother of Banu Dada, the thief of the pilgrims; when he was suspected he said: This is the deed of the staff. And I saw in it a tall black Himyari woman tormented for a cat she tied; she neither fed it nor gave it drink, nor let it eat of the vermin of the earth, until it died. And the sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life, but they are two signs of the signs of Allah. So when one of them is eclipsed, or he said: When something of that is done to one of them, hasten to the remembrance of Allah. My father said: Ibn Fudayl said: Why do You torment them while I am among them; why do You torment us while we seek Your forgiveness. And Shubah agreed with Zaidah, and he said: Of the vermin of the earth. Muawiyah narrated it to us."
"6764","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that he married a woman of Quraysh, and he would not go to her; fasting and prayer kept him busy. So that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Fast three days of every month. He said: I can do more than that. He kept with him until he said to him: Fast a day and break fast a day. And he said to him: Recite the Quran in every month. He said: I can do more than that. He said: Recite it in every fifteen days. He said: I can do more than that. He said: Recite it in every seven, until he said: Recite in every three. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every deed has eagerness, and every eagerness has slackness. So whoever whose eagerness is to my Sunnah has succeeded, and whoever whose slackness is to other than that has perished."
"6765","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Habib, he said: I heard Abu al-Abbas saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr narrating that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his permission for jihad, so he said: Are your parents alive. He said: Yes. He said: Then in them strive."
"6766","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Habib, from Abu al-Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My father said, and Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Habib ibn Abi Thabit, I heard Abu al-Abbas the poet, and he was truthful, narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah ibn Amr, you fast the age; when you fast the age and stand the night, the eye sinks and the soul becomes weary. He does not fast who fasts forever. Fast three days of the month, the fasting of the whole age. He said: I said: I can do more. He said: Fast the fasting of Dawud, for he would fast a day and break fast a day, and would not flee when he met. And Rawh said: The soul becomes breathless."
"6767","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, I heard Abu Wail narrating, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Learn the Quran from four: from Abdullah ibn Masud, and Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, and Muadh ibn Jabal, and Ubayy ibn Kab. Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not obscene nor foul-mouthed. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the most beloved of you to me are the best of you in character."
"6768","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, and Ibn Numayr said: al-Amash informed us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Four, whoever has them in him is a hypocrite, or whoever has a trait of the four has in him a trait of hypocrisy until he leaves it: when he speaks he lies, and when he promises he breaks, and when he covenants he betrays, and when he disputes he acts wickedly."
"6769","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, both said: Said narrated to us, from Matar, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: No divorce is upon a man in what he does not own, nor emancipation in what he does not own, nor sale in what he does not own."
"6770","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he conquered Makkah, said: A woman shall not be married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt."
"6771","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Juwayriyah bint al-Harith while she was fasting on a Friday, so he said to her: Did you fast yesterday. She said: No. He said: Do you intend to fast tomorrow. She said: No. He said: Then break fast. Said said: And Matar agreed with me on it, from Said ibn al-Musayyab."
"6772","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he conquered Makkah, said in his sermon: For fingers ten each, and for head wounds exposing the bone five each."
"6773","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Nafi ibn Asim, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights. If he drinks it and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights. If he drinks it and becomes intoxicated, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights, the third and the fourth. If he drinks it, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah shall not accept his repentance, and it shall be due upon Allah to give him to drink from the spring of khabal. It was said: What is the spring of khabal. He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"6774","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Abu Thumamah ath-Thaqafi, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The womb shall be placed on the Day of Resurrection, having a hook like the hook of the spindle, speaking with an eloquent fluent tongue; it shall join whoever joined it, and cut whoever cut it. And Affan said: The spindle, and he said: With tongues it has."
"6775","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid, brother of Mutarrif, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): In how many shall I recite the Quran. Then he mentioned the hadith. Yahya said: He said: In seven. He does not understand who recites it in less than three. And he said: How shall I fast. He said: Fast three days of every month, one day of every ten days, and there shall be written for you the reward of nine days. He said: I am stronger than that. He said: Fast two days of every ten, and there shall be written for you the reward of eight days, until he reached five days."
"6776","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Ibn Muslim, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: And it was in my father's book, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, so he struck over al-Hasan and said: From Ibn Muslim, and it is Muhammad ibn Muslim Abu az-Zubayr; al-Azraq erred, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When you see my nation not saying to the wrongdoer among them: You are a wrongdoer, then they have been forsaken."
"6777","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Yahya, my father said: Hasan al-Ashyab said: Rashid Abu Yahya al-Maafiri, that he heard Abu Abdurrahman al-Hubuli, from Ibn Amr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the spoils of gatherings of remembrance. He said: The spoils of gatherings of remembrance is Paradise."
"6778","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, and Yazid said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abdurrahman, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber and the bribed. Yazid said: The curse of Allah upon the briber and the bribed."
"6779","Abdulmalik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber and the bribed."
"6780","Hushaym narrated to us, Amir al-Ahwal informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No vow is upon the son of Adam in what he does not own, nor emancipation upon the son of Adam in what he does not own, nor divorce for him in what he does not own, nor oath in what he does not own."
"6781","Abdulaziz ibn Abdussamad narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: No divorce is permissible, nor sale, nor emancipation, nor fulfillment of a vow, in what one does not own."
"6782","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the second jamrah longer than he stood at the first jamrah, then came to the jamrah of Aqabah and stoned it and did not stand at it."
"6783","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turning from his right and from his left in prayer, and drinking standing and sitting, and praying barefoot and shod, and fasting while traveling and breaking fast."
"6784","Abdurrahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see my nation fearing the wrongdoer to say to him: You are a wrongdoer, then they have been forsaken."
"6785","Abdurrazzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The joiner is not the requiter, but the joiner is one who, when his kinship is cut, joins it."
"6786","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the Quran from four: from Ibn Masud, and Ubayy ibn Kab, and Muadh ibn Jabal, and Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah. He said: So Abdullah said: That is a man I shall ever love since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) begin with him."
"6787","Waki narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders, so they are asked and give rulings without knowledge, so they stray and lead astray."
"6788","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah dictated to me, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from his mouth to my mouth, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then he mentioned the like of it."
"6789","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan and Misar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas al-Makki, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best fasting is the fasting of my brother Dawud; he would fast a day and break fast a day, and would not flee when he met. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He does not fast who fasts forever."
"6790","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the Quran from four: from Ibn Umm Abd, so he began with him, and from Muadh ibn Jabal, and Ubayy ibn Kab, and Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah."
"6791","Waki narrated to us, Qurrah narrated to me, and Rawh narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, and Qurrah ibn Khalid, the meaning, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, kill him. He said: And Waki said in his hadith, he said: Abdullah said: Bring me a man who drank wine a fourth time, and it is upon me to kill him."
"6792","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, and Yazid said: al-Masudi informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Mukattib, from Abu Kathir az-Zubaydi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of stinginess, for it destroyed those before you; it commanded them to wrong, so they wronged, and commanded them to sever, so they severed, and commanded them to commit indecency, so they committed indecency. And beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity nor foul speech. He said: So a man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which Muslims are best. He said: Whom the Muslims are safe from his tongue and his hand. He said: So he stood, he or another, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best. He said: Who hamstrings his horse and his blood is shed. My father said, and Yazid ibn Harun said in his hadith: Then this one or another called to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which emigration is best. He said: That you forsake what your Lord dislikes. And they are two emigrations: an emigration of the Bedouin and an emigration of the townsman. As for the emigration of the Bedouin, he obeys when commanded and answers when called. As for the emigration of the townsman, it is the severer of the two in trial and the greater of the two in reward."
"6793","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdurrahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Kabah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I was sitting with him in the shade of the Kabah while he narrated to people. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, so we alighted at a stop; among us was one pitching his tent, and among us was one among his livestock, and among us was one practicing archery, when the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Prayer in congregation. He said: So I came to him while he addressed people, saying: O people, there was no prophet before me but it was due upon him to guide his nation to what he knows is good for them, and to warn them of what he knows is evil for them. Verily the well-being of this nation is in its beginning, and its end shall be afflicted with calamity and trials, one softening another. A trial comes, so the believer says: This shall destroy me; then it passes. Then it comes, so he says: This, this. Then it comes, so he says: This, this. Then it passes. So whoever loves to be removed from the Fire and entered into Paradise, let his death overtake him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him come to people what he loves to be brought to him. And whoever pledges allegiance to a leader, giving him the clasp of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him if he can. And he said once: As much as he can. When I heard it, I put my head between two men and said: Your cousin Muawiyah commands us. So he placed his hands together upon his forehead, then lowered, then raised his head and said: Obey him in obedience to Allah, and disobey him in disobedience to Allah. I said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, my ears heard it and my heart retained it."
"6794","Ismail ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi as-Safar narrated to me, from ash-Shabi, from Abdurrahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Kabah as-Saidi, he said: I saw a group at the Kabah and sat with them, and there was a man narrating to them, and he was Abdullah ibn Amr. He said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, so we alighted at a stop, then he mentioned the hadith."
"6795","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, he said: We used to come to Abdullah ibn Amr and converse with him. One day we mentioned Abdullah ibn Masud, so he said: You mentioned a man I shall ever love since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Take the Quran from four: from Ibn Umm Abd, so he began with him, and Muadh ibn Jabal, and Ubayy ibn Kab, and Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah."
"6796","Waki narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to me, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Muslim shall not be killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant during his covenant."
"6797","Waki narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to me, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said in his sermon while leaning his back against the Kabah: Muslims, their blood is equal, and the lowest of them strives for their protection, and they are a hand against others."
"6798","Waki and Abdurrahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Rayhan ibn Yazid al-Amiri, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich one, nor for one of sound strength. And Abdurrahman said: Strong. And Abdurrahman ibn Mahdi said: Sad did not raise it, nor his son, meaning Ibrahim ibn Sad."
"6799","Abdurrahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Zir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: It shall be said to the companion of the Quran: Recite and ascend and recite slowly as you used to recite slowly in the world, for your station is at the last verse you recite."
"6800","Abdurrahman narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not feel; I slaughtered before I stoned. He said: Stone, and no harm. Another said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I slaughtered. He said: Slaughter, and no harm. So he was not asked that day about anything advanced nor delayed except he said: Do, and no harm."
"6801","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, he said: Abdullah ibn Rabah wrote to me narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and while we were sitting two men differed about a verse and their voices rose, so he said: The nations before you perished only because of their differing about the Book."
"6802","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Malik, meaning Ubayd ibn al-Akhnas, al-Walid ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I used to write everything I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting to memorize it, then Quraysh forbade me from that and said: You write while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speaks in anger and in pleasure, so I stopped until I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Write, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, nothing has come out of it except truth."
"6803","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yisaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."
"6804","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Aslam, from Abu Murayyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The two blowers in the second heaven, the head of one of them in the east and his feet in the west, or he said: the head of one of them in the west and his feet in the east, waiting for when they will be commanded to blow into the Sur, then they will blow."
"6805","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, from Aslam, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a Bedouin asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Sur, and he said: A horn that is blown into."
"6806","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: Amir informed me, he said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Amr while people were with him, so he stepped over to him and they stopped him, and he said: Leave him, so he came until he sat beside him and said: Inform me of something you memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"6807","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Kabah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to be moved away from the Fire and admitted to Paradise, let death come to him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him treat people as he loves to be treated."
"6808","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from a shaykh called Abu Musa, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: Sufyan said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."
"6809","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people performing ablution with their heels showing, so he said: Woe to the heels from the Fire; perfect the ablution."
"6810","Waki narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from a man, Yazid or Abu Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reads the Quran in less than three has not understood it."
"6811","Waki narrated to us, Misar and Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas al-Makki, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A man came asking permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for jihad, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are your parents alive, he said: Yes, he said: Then strive in them."
"6812","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, from Abu al-Abbas, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Amr about jihad, and he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the hadith."
"6813","Waki narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Mukattib, from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which emigration is best, he said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes, and they are two emigrations, the emigration of the resident and the emigration of the Bedouin; as for the emigration of the Bedouin, he obeys when commanded and answers when called, and as for the emigration of the resident, it is the more severe of the two in trial and the greater of the two in reward."
"6814","Waki narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, from Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the emigrant, he said: One who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"6815","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Kabah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever pledges allegiance to an imam and gives him the fruit of his heart and the clasp of his hand, let him obey him as much as he can."
"6816","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from his maternal uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his wealth sought unjustly and is killed defending it, he is a martyr."
"6817","Waki narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun said: Fitr informed us, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kinship is suspended from the Throne, and the maintainer is not the mere requiter, but the maintainer is one who joins his kin when his kin cuts him off; Yazid said: Al-Muwasil."
"6818","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, and Ibn Numayr said: al-Amash informed us, from Shaqiq, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not obscene nor deliberately obscene, and he used to say: Among the best of you are the best of you in character; Ibn Numayr said: The best of you are the best of you in character."
"6819","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is enough of a sin for a man to neglect those he sustains."
"6820","Waki narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a date under his side at night and ate it, then he did not sleep that night, so one of his wives said: O Messenger of Allah, you were sleepless last night, he said: I found a date under my side and ate it, and we had dates from charity dates with us, so I feared it was from them."
"6821","Waki narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me wearing saffron-dyed garments and said: Cast them off, for they are the garments of the disbelievers."
"6822","Waki narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the aqiqah, and he said: I do not like disobedience, and whoever has a child born to him and loves to sacrifice for him, let him do so: for a boy two equal sheep, and for a girl one sheep."
"6823","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Hasan, from his maternal uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his wealth sought unjustly and is killed defending it, he is a martyr."
"6824","Waki narrated to us, from Khalifah ibn Khayyat, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached while leaning his back against the Kabah, then he mentioned it."
"6825","Waki narrated to us, and Ishaq, meaning al-Azraq, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim is afflicted with a trial in his body except that Allah the Mighty and Majestic commands the guardian angels who guard him: Write for My servant like what he used to do while healthy, as long as he is confined in My bond; and Ishaq said: Write for My servant in every day and night."
"6826","Waki narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like it."
"6827","Waki narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believer is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant during his covenant."
"6828","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is enough of a sin for a man to neglect those he sustains."
"6829","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever has his wealth sought unjustly and fights and is killed, he is a martyr; and I think al-Araj narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah like it."
"6830","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber and the bribe-taker."
"6831","Rawh narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Kabshah al-Saluli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forty good deeds, the highest of them the lending of a goat; no servant does a good deed among them hoping for its reward and believing its promise except that Allah admits him to Paradise through it."
"6832","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Salim, meaning Ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, from Said ibn Mina, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has reached me that you; my father said: And Affan narrated it to us, he said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Said ibn Mina narrated to us, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: It has reached me that you fast the day and pray the night, so do not do it, for your body has a share upon you, and your eye has a share upon you, and your wife has a share upon you; fast three days of every month, for that is the fast of a lifetime; he said: I said: I have strength, he said: Fast the fast of Dawud, fast a day and break a day; and Ibn Amr used to say: Would that I had taken the concession; and Affan and Bahz said: I find strength in me."
"6833","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have come to pledge allegiance to you while leaving my parents weeping, he said: Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep, and he refused to accept his pledge."
"6834","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever claims to belong to other than his father will never smell the scent of Paradise, and its scent is found from a distance of seventy years."
"6835","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, I heard Sayf narrating from Rushayd al-Hajari, from his father, that a man said to Abdullah ibn Amr: Narrate to me what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and leave me what you found in your load on the day of Yarmuk; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"6836","Husayn narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard al-Hakam, I heard Sayf narrating from Rushayd al-Hajari, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: And leave us and what you found in your two loads."
"6837","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abu Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Beware of injustice, for injustice is darkness on the Day of Resurrection, and beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity nor deliberate obscenity, and beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you: it commanded them to sever kinship so they severed, and to be miserly so they were miserly, and to commit immorality so they committed it; he said: Then a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best: that the Muslims be safe from your tongue and your hand; that man or another man said: O Messenger of Allah, then which emigration is best, he said: That you abandon what Allah dislikes; and emigration is two emigrations, the emigration of the resident and the Bedouin; as for the Bedouin, he obeys when commanded and answers when called, and as for the resident, he is the greater of the two in trial and the greater of the two in reward."
"6838","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, he said: They mentioned Ibn Masud before Abdullah ibn Amr, and he said: That is a man I will always love after I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Take the Quran from four: from Ibn Masud, and Salim the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, and Ubayy ibn Kab, and Muadh ibn Jabal."
"6839","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, a man in the house of Abu Ubaydah narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr narrating to Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make the hearers of His creation hear of him, and will belittle him and humiliate him; he said: Then the eyes of Abdullah ibn Umar shed tears."
"6840","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd; Hajjaj said: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among the greatest of sins is that a man should curse his parents; they said: And how would a man curse his parents, he said: He curses the father of a man so he curses his father, and he curses his mother so he curses his mother."
"6841","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever reads the Quran in less than three has not understood it."
"6842","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, I heard Wahb ibn Jabir saying: A freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr said to him: I want to stay this month here in Bayt al-Maqdis, so he said to him: Have you left for your family what will sustain them this month, he said: No, he said: Return to your family and leave for them what will sustain them, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is enough of a sin for a man to neglect those he sustains."
"6843","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Abbas narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Read the Quran in a month, so I said: I can do more than that, and I kept asking him until he said: Read the Quran in five days, and fast three days of the month; I said: I can do more than that, he said: Then fast the most beloved fast to Allah the Mighty and Majestic, the fast of Dawud, peace be upon him: he used to fast a day and break a day."
"6844","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People of two different religions do not inherit from one another."
"6845","Ismail narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that some men were sitting at the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and some of them said: Did not Allah say such and such, and some of them said: Did not Allah say such and such, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard that and came out as if pomegranate seeds had burst on his face, and said: Is this what you were commanded, or is this what you were sent with, to strike the Book of Allah part against part; the nations before you strayed only in the like of this; you have nothing to do with this; look at what you were commanded and act upon it, and what you were forbidden, then stop."
"6846","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Humayd and Matar al-Warraq and Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to his Companions while they were disputing about the Decree, this one citing a verse and this one citing a verse, then he mentioned the hadith."
"6847","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said narrated to me, Said ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I swear by Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It will be made lawful, and a man of Quraysh will violate it through whom, if his sins were weighed against the sins of the two worlds, they would outweigh them."
"6848","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, feed food, and enter the Gardens."
"6849","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man said: O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad alone, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have withheld it from many people."
"6850","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Umaymah bint Ruqayqah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him in Islam, and he said: I pledge you that you associate nothing with Allah, and do not steal, and do not fornicate, and do not kill your child, and do not bring a slander you fabricate between your hands and feet, and do not wail, and do not display yourself as in the former ignorance."
"6851","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, he said: I came to Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As and said to him: Narrate to us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he cast a sheet before me and said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for me, so I looked in it and there was in it that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me what to say when I wake and when I evening, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abu Bakr, say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, there is no god but You, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, and from the evil of Satan and his association, and that I commit evil against myself or bring it upon a Muslim."
"6852","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We came down with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Thaniyyat Adhakhir, he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at me, and I was wearing a wrap dyed with safflower, so he said: What is this, so I knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked it, so I went to my family while they were heating their oven, so I wrapped it then cast it into it, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What did the wrap do, he said: I said: I knew what you disliked of it, so I went to my family while they were heating their oven and cast it into it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would you not have clothed some of your family with it; and he mentioned that when he came down with them from Thaniyyat Adhakhir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them toward a wall he took as a qiblah, then a lamb came passing in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he kept warding it off and drawing near to the wall until I saw the belly of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stuck to the wall, and it passed behind him."
"6853","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, I heard Abu Kabshah al-Saluli saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forty good deeds, the highest of them the lending of a goat; there is no good deed among them that a servant does hoping for its reward and believing its promise except that Allah admits him to Paradise through it."
"6854","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, Urwah ibn Ruwaym informed me, from Ibn al-Daylami who used to live in Bayt al-Maqdis, he said: Then I asked him: Did you hear, O Abdullah ibn Amr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the drinker of wine with anything, he said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one of my nation drinks wine and Allah accepts a prayer from him for forty mornings; he said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah created His creation then placed them in darkness, then He took of His light what He willed and cast it upon them, so the light struck whom He willed to strike and missed whom He willed, so whoever the light struck that day was guided, and whoever missed that day strayed, therefore I said: The pen has dried upon what will be."
"6855","And Ali ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Abdullah ibn Junadah al-Maafiri informed me that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him from Abdullah ibn Amr, he narrated to him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The world is the prison of the believer and his year of hardship, so when he leaves the world he leaves the prison and the hardship."
"6856","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Said ibn Yazid informed us, from Abu al-Samh, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a piece of lead like this, and he pointed to the like of a skull, were sent from heaven to earth, and it is a journey of five hundred years, it would reach the earth before night, and if it were sent from the head of the chain it would travel forty autumns, night and day, before reaching its root or its bottom."
"6857","Al-Hasan ibn Isa narrated it to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Said ibn Yazid Abu Shuja informed us, from Abu al-Samh, from Isa ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like it."
"6858","Affan and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I heard Abu al-Abbas, and he was a poet, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked his permission for jihad, and he said: Are your parents alive, he said: Yes, he said: Then strive in them; Bahz said: Ibn Abi Thabit informed me, from Abu al-Abbas, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Amr."
"6859","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Yala ibn Ata informed me, from his father, he said: I think it is from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: Shubah doubted: A man stood to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking his permission for jihad, and he said: Do you have parents, he said: Yes, he said: My mother, he said: Go and be dutiful to her; he said: Then he went off passing through the riders."
"6860","Bahz narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us, from Thabit, a man from Sham narrated to us, and he used to follow Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As and hear, he said: I was with him when he met Nawf, so Nawf said: It was mentioned to us that Allah the Exalted said to His angels: Call My servants to Me, they said: O Lord, how, while the seven heavens are below them and the Throne above that, He said: When they say there is no god but Allah they respond; Abdullah ibn Amr says to him: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Maghrib prayer or another, he said: Then some people sat, I among them, waiting for the next prayer, he said: Then he came to us hurrying in walk, as if I am looking at him lifting his waist-wrapper to be quicker in walking, then he ended to us and said: Shall I not give you glad tidings, this is your Lord, He commanded the middle gate of heaven, or he said: the gate of heaven, so it was opened, and He boasted of you to the angels, He said: Look at My servants, they have fulfilled a right of My right, then they are waiting to fulfill another right they will fulfill."
"6861","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Suhayb al-Hadhdha, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever slaughters a sparrow without its right, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection; it was said: And what is its right, he said: He slaughters it properly and does not seize it by its neck and cut it."
"6862","Affan narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Said ibn Mina narrated to us, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abdullah ibn Amr, it has reached me that you fast the day and pray the night, so do not, do not do it, for your body has a share upon you, and your wife has a share upon you, and your two eyes have a share upon you; break fast and fast three days of every month, for that is the fast of a lifetime; he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength, he said: Fast the fast of Dawud, fast a day and break a day; he said: And Abdullah used to say: Would that I had taken the concession."
"6863","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mughirah, I heard Mujahid narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Fast three days of the month; he said: I can do more than that, he said: It continued until he said: Fast a day and break a day, then he said to him: Read the Quran in every month; he said: I can do more than that, he said: It continued until he said: Read the Quran in every three."
"6864","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Four, whoever has them in him is a hypocrite, or whoever has a trait of the four has in him a trait of hypocrisy until he leaves it: when he speaks he lies, and when he promises he breaks, and when he makes a covenant he betrays, and when he disputes he is wicked."
"6865","Affan narrated to us, Khalid, meaning al-Wasiti al-Tahhan, narrated to us, Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from a shaykh of Nakha, he said: I entered the mosque of Iliya and prayed two rakahs toward a pillar, then a man came and prayed near me, so people leaned toward him, and he was Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, then a messenger of Yazid ibn Muawiyah came to him to answer, he said: This one forbids me to narrate to you as his father used to forbid me, and I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I seek refuge in You from a soul that is not satisfied, and from a heart that is not humble, and from a supplication that is not heard, and from knowledge that does not benefit; I seek refuge in You from these four."
"6866","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Ata, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts perpetually, he has not fasted."
"6867","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I have been told that you pray the night and fast the day; he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, yes, he said: Then fast and break, and pray and sleep, for your body has a right upon you, and your wife has a right upon you, and your visitor has a right upon you, and it suffices you to fast three days of every month; he said: Then I was strict so it was made strict upon me; he said: Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength, he said: Then fast three days of every Jumuah; he said: Then I was strict so it was made strict upon me; he said: Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength, he said: Fast the fast of Allahs Prophet Dawud and do not add to it; I said: O Messenger of Allah, and what was the fasting of Dawud, he said: He used to fast a day and break a day."
"6868","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them on the day the sun eclipsed, the day his son Ibrahim died, so he stood with the people, and it was said he will not bow, then he bowed, and it was said he will not rise, then he rose, and it was said he will not prostrate, and he prostrated, and it was said he will not rise, then he stood in the second and did the like of that, and the sun cleared."
"6869","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have come to pledge allegiance to you while leaving my parents weeping; he said: Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."
"6870","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim afflicted with a trial in his body except that Allah the Exalted commands the guardian angels who guard him, He said: Write for My servant in every day and night like what he used to do of good as long as he is confined in My bond."
"6871","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: When the allegiance of Yazid ibn Muawiyah came to us, I arrived in Sham and was told of a station where Nawf stands, so I came to him when a man came and people crowded upon him in a cloak, and he was Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, so when Nawf saw him he held back from speech, so Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be an emigration after an emigration, people will gather to the emigration place of Ibrahim, and none will remain on earth except the wicked of its people, their lands cast them out, the soul of Allah loathes them, the Fire gathers them with the monkeys and the pigs, it stays with them when they stay and rests with them when they rest, and it eats whoever lags behind; he said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People of my nation will come out from the east reciting the Quran, it does not pass their throats, every time a horn comes out of them it is cut, every time a horn comes out of them it is cut, until he counted more than ten times, every time a horn comes out of them it is cut, until the Dajjal comes out among their remnant."
"6872","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Matar, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad doubted about the Hawd, so Abu Sabrah, a man of the companions of Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad, said to him: Your father, when he set out as a delegate to Muawiyah, I set out with him, then I met Abdullah ibn Amr and he narrated to me from his mouth to my mouth a hadith he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he dictated it to me and I wrote it; he said: I adjure you to tire this mule until you bring me the book; he said: So I rode the mule and galloped it until it sweated, then I brought him the book, and there was in it: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah hates obscenity and deliberate obscenity, and by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the Hour will not come until the trustworthy is betrayed and the traitor is trusted, until obscenity and deliberate obscenity appear, and severing of kinship, and bad neighboring; and by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the likeness of the believer is like a piece of gold, its owner blew upon it and it did not change nor decrease; and by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the likeness of the believer is like the bee, it ate good and produced good, and it landed and did not break nor spoil; he said: And he said: Indeed I have a Hawd, between its two sides as between Aylah to Makkah, or he said: Sanaa to Madinah, and in it are pitchers like the stars, it is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, whoever drinks from it will never thirst after it; Abu Sabrah said: Then Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad took the book, so I was distressed over it, then Yahya ibn Yamar met me and I complained that to him, so he said: By Allah, I remember it better than me of a surah of the Quran, then he narrated it to me as it was in the book alike."
"6873","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating from Yahya ibn Hakim ibn Safwan that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: I gathered the Quran and read it in a night, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear the time will be long upon you and you will grow weary; read it in every month; I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth; he said: Read it in twenty; I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth; he said: Read it in ten; I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth; he said: Read it in every seven; I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth, then he refused."
"6874","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata claiming that Abu al-Abbas the poet informed him that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: It reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I fast continuously and pray the night; he said: Either he sent to me or I met him, then he said: Have I not been told that you fast and do not break, and pray the night, then do not do it, for your eye has a share, and your soul has a share, and your family has a share; so fast and break, and pray and sleep, and fast one day of every ten days, and for you is the reward of nine; he said: I find myself stronger than that, O Prophet of Allah; he said: Then fast the fast of Dawud; he said: And how did Dawud fast, O Prophet of Allah; he said: He used to fast a day and break a day, and he did not flee when he met; he said: Who can do this for me, O Prophet of Allah; Ata said: I do not know how he mentioned perpetual fasting, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has not fasted who fasts perpetually; Abd al-Razzaq and Rawh said: He has not fasted who fasts perpetually, twice."
"6875","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Umar ibn Hawshab, a righteous man, informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Ata, from a man of Hudhayl, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, and his house in the lawful area and his mosque in the sacred area; he said: While I was with him, he saw Umm Said, the daughter of Abu Jahl, wearing a bow and walking the walk of a man, so Abdullah said: Who is this, Hudhali said: Then I said: This is Umm Said bint Abi Jahl, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He is not of us who imitates men among women, nor who imitates women among men."
"6876","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I entered upon Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As and he asked me, thinking that I belong to Umm Kulthum the daughter of Uqbah, so I said: I belong only to the Kalbiyyah; he said: Then Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered my house and said: Have I not been told that you read the Quran in every day and night, then read it in every month; I said: I am stronger than that; he said: Then read it in half of every month; he said: I said: I am stronger than that; he said: Then read it in every seven, do not add to that; and it reached me that you fast the whole time; he said: I said: I fast it, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Then fast three days of every month; he said: I said: I am stronger than that; he said: Then fast two days of every Jumuah; he said: I said: I am stronger than that; he said: Then fast the fast of Dawud, fast a day and break a day, for it is the most just fasting with Allah, and he did not break when he promised and did not flee when he met."
"6877","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed me, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with fasting; he said: Fast a day and for you is the reward of nine; he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength, so add for me; he said: Fast two days and for you is the reward of eight days; he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength, so add for me; he said: Then fast three days and for you is the reward of seven days; he said: He kept reducing for me until he said: The best fasting is the fast of my brother Dawud, or Allahs Prophet Dawud, al-Jurayri doubted: Fast a day and break a day; so Abdullah said when he grew weak: Would that I had been content with what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me."
"6878","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed me, from Abu Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered his house and said: O Abdullah ibn Amr, have I not been told that you burden yourself with night prayer and day fasting; he said: I do it; then he said: It suffices you, and I do not say do, to fast three days of every month, a good deed is ten likes of it, so as if you have fasted the whole time; he said: Then I was strict so it was made strict upon me; he said: Then I said: I find strength beyond that; he said: It suffices you to fast three days of every Jumuah; he said: Then I was strict so it was made strict upon me, then I said: I find strength in me; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most just fasting with Allah is the fasting of Dawud, half a lifetime; then he said: Your soul has a right upon you and your family has a right upon you; he said: And Abdullah used to fast that fasting until age and weakness reached him, he used to say: That I had accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is dearer to me than my family and wealth."
"6879","Al-Walid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Walid narrated to us, I heard my father mentioning it from Abu al-Hajjaj, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, when they are in a man he is a pure hypocrite: if he speaks he lies, and if he promises he breaks, and if he is trusted he betrays; and whoever has a trait of them in him, there remains, meaning in him a trait of hypocrisy, until he leaves it."
"6880","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I entered upon Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As in his house, and he asked me, thinking that I am of Bani Umm Kulthum the daughter of Uqbah, so I said to him: I belong only to the Kalbiyyah the daughter of al-Asbagh, and I have come to ask you about what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to you or said to you; he said: I used to say in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I will read the Quran in every day and night, and I will fast the whole time, so that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from me, so he came to me and entered my house and said: Has it not reached me, O Abdullah, that you say: I will fast the whole time and I will read the Quran in every day and night; he said: I said: Yes, I said that, O Prophet of Allah; he said: Then do not do it; fast three days of every month; he said: Then I said: I am stronger than that; he said: Then fast Monday and Thursday; he said: Then I said: I am stronger than that, O Prophet of Allah; he said: Then fast a day and break a day, for it is the most just fasting with Allah, and it is the fasting of Dawud, peace be upon him, and he did not break when he promised and did not flee when he met; and read the Quran once in every month; he said: Then I said: I am stronger than that, O Prophet of Allah; he said: Then read it once in every half month; he said: I said: I am stronger than that, O Prophet of Allah; he said: Then read it in every seven, do not add to that; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left."
"6881","Ismail ibn Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, Abu Hayyan informed us, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, he said: Three men of the Muslims sat with Marwan in Madinah and heard him speaking about the Signs that the first of them is the coming of the Dajjal; he said: Then the men went to Abdullah ibn Amr and told him what they heard from Marwan about the Signs, so Abdullah said: Marwan said nothing; I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the like of that a hadith I have not forgotten after: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first of the Signs to come is the rising of the sun from its west and the coming of the Beast at forenoon, so whichever of them is before its companion, the other follows it; then Abdullah said, and he used to read the books: And I think the first of them to come is the rising of the sun from its west, and that is that every time it sets it comes under the Throne and prostrates and asks permission to return, so it is permitted to return, until when it appears to Allah to rise from its west, it does as it used to do, it comes under the Throne and prostrates, then asks permission to return, and nothing is answered to it, then it asks permission to return and nothing is answered to it, then it asks permission and nothing is answered to it, until when as much of the night as Allah wills to pass has passed, and it knows that if it were permitted to return it would not reach the east, it says: Lord, how far is the east, who will help me with the people, until when the horizon becomes like a collar it asks permission to return, so it is said to it: From your place then rise, so it rises upon the people from its west; then Abdullah recited this verse: On the day some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"6882","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to me, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Nubayt ibn Sharit, Ghundar said: Nubayt ibn Sumayt, Hajjaj said: Nubayt ibn Sharit, from Jaban, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The begrudging giver will not enter Paradise, nor one disobedient to his parents, nor an addict of wine."
"6883","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya al-Araj, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of a man sitting, and he said: Half his prayer standing; he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people performing ablution without completing the ablution, so he said: Perfect, meaning the ablution, woe to the heels from the Fire, or the backs of the feet."
"6884","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Shabi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The major sins are associating with Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and disobedience to parents, or killing a soul, Shubah is the doubter, and the immersing oath."
"6885","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Mashar al-Barra narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Taysalah narrated to me, Man ibn Thalabah al-Mazini narrated to me, and the tribe after, he said: al-Asha al-Mazini narrated to me, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and recited to him: O Malik of the people and judge of the Arabs, I met a she-camel among camels, I went out seeking food for her in Rajab, so she left me with dispute and flight, she broke the covenant and plastered with the tail, and they are the worst conquerors for him who conquers; he said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that used to say: And they are the worst conquerors for him who conquers."
"6886","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to me, Abu Salamah Ubayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Junayd ibn Amin ibn Dhirwah ibn Nadlah ibn Tarif ibn Buhsul al-Hirmazi narrated to me, my father Amin ibn Dhirwah narrated to me, from his father Dhirwah ibn Nadlah, from his father Nadlah ibn Tarif, that a man of them called al-Asha, and his name is Abdullah ibn al-Awar, had a wife called Muadhah, he went out in Rajab to bring food for his family from Hajar, then his wife fled after him, disobedient to him, and sought refuge with a man of them called Mutarrif ibn Buhsul ibn Kab ibn Qumaysha ibn Dulaf ibn Ahdam ibn Abdullah, so he placed her behind his back, so when he arrived and did not find her in his house, and was told that she was disobedient to him and sought refuge with Mutarrif ibn Buhsul, he went to him and said: O son of my uncle, is my wife Muadhah with you, then hand her to me; he said: She is not with me, and if she were with me I would not hand her to you; and Mutarrif was mightier than him, so he went out until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and sought refuge with him, and began saying: O master of the people and judge of the Arabs, to you I complain of a she-camel among camels, like a dusky wolf in the shade of the thicket, I went out seeking food for her in Rajab, so she left me with dispute and flight, she broke the covenant and plastered with the tail, and she cast me among tangled thickets, and they are the worst conquerors for him who conquers; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that said: And they are the worst conquerors for him who conquers; then he complained to him of his wife and what she did with him, and that she was with a man of them called Mutarrif ibn Buhsul, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him to Mutarrif: Look at the wife of this one, Muadhah, and hand her to him; then the book of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and was read to him, so he said to her: O Muadhah, this is the book of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about you, so I am handing you to him; she said: Take for me upon him the covenant and the pact and the protection of His Prophet that he will not punish me for what I did, so he took that for her upon him, and Mutarrif handed her to him, so he began saying: By your life, my love of Muadhah is not what the slanderer changes, nor the length of the covenant, nor the evil of what she brought when the misguided men removed her, when they confide to her after me."
"6887","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing on his mount at Mina, he said: Then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought that shaving is before slaughter, so I shaved before I slaughtered, so he said: Slaughter and no harm; he said: Then another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought that slaughter is before stoning, so I slaughtered before I stoned, he said: Then stone and no harm; he said: He was not asked about anything a man put before a thing except he said: Do and no harm; Abd al-Razzaq said: And another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought that shaving is before stoning, so I shaved before I stoned, he said: Stone and no harm."
"6888","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq, I heard al-Awzai, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Kabshah, Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Convey from me even a verse, and narrate from Bani Israil and no harm, and whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6889","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sad, he said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Amr and said: I ask you only about what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I do not ask you about the Torah, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"6890","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah ibn Ulathah al-Qadi Abu Sahl narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Rafi narrated to us, from al-Farzdaq ibn Hanan al-Qass, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith my ears heard and my heart retained, I have not forgotten it after: I went out, I and Ubaydullah ibn Haydah, on the road of Sham, then we passed by Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, then he mentioned the hadith, and he said: A harsh rude Bedouin man of your people came and said: O Messenger of Allah, where is emigration, to you wherever you are, or to a known land, or to special people, or when you die is it cut, he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent a while, then he said: Where is the asker about emigration, he said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah; he said: When you establish prayer and give zakah, you are an emigrant, even if you die in Hadramawt, he said: Meaning a land in Yamamah; he said: Then a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, have you seen the garments of the people of Paradise, are they woven by weaving or split from the fruit of Paradise; he said: As if the people were amazed at the question of the Bedouin, so he said: What do you amaze at, of an ignorant one asking a scholar; he said: Then he was silent a little, then he said: Where is the asker about the garments of Paradise, he said: I am; he said: No, rather they are split from the fruit of Paradise."
"6891","Ibn Idris narrated to us, I heard Ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man of Muzaynah asking him about the stray camel, and he said: With it are its shoes and its water, it eats the trees and comes to water, so leave it until its seeker comes; he said: And he asked him about the stray sheep, so he said: For you, or for your brother, or for the wolf, gather it to you until its seeker comes; and he asked him about the eaten crop found in its pastures, he said: Then he said: In it is its price twice and an exemplary beating; he said: What is taken from its enclosures, in it is cutting if what is taken of that reaches the price of a shield; then he asked him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, the found object we find on the traveled road; he said: Announce it a year, then if its owner comes, and otherwise it is yours; he said: O Messenger of Allah, what is found in the ancient ruin; he said: In it and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"6892","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jaban, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The disobedient will not enter Paradise, nor an addict of wine, nor a begrudging giver, nor a child of adultery."
"6893","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, I heard al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah saying: Amr ibn Shuayb informed me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the mother is more entitled to her child as long as she does not marry."
"6894","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying sitting, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was told that you said that the prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing, while you pray sitting; he said: Yes, but I am not like any of you."
"6895","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant is upon a good way of worship then becomes sick, it is said to the angel entrusted with him: Write for him like his deed when he was free, until I release him or take him to Me."
"6896","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not strip knowledge from people after He has given it to them, but He takes the scholars, every time a scholar goes He takes what is with him of knowledge, until there remains one who does not know, so people take ignorant leaders, then they are asked for fatwa and give fatwa without knowledge, so they stray and mislead."
"6897","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The just in the world are upon pulpits of pearl on the Day of Resurrection, before the Most Merciful, the Mighty and Majestic, for their justice in the world."
"6898","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Shuayb informed me, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at part of the upper valley, wanting to pray, he had stood and we stood, when a donkey came out to us from the ravine of Abu Dubb, the ravine of Abu Musa, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held back and did not say takbir, and he sent Yaqub ibn Zamah to it until he returned it."
"6899","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of a treacherous man or treacherous woman is not allowed, nor one with rancor against his brother, and the testimony of the dependent for the household is not allowed, and his testimony for others is allowed; and the dependent is one upon whom the household spends."
"6900","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting for less than ten dirhams."
"6901","Haddathana Nasr ibn Bab from al-Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that he said: Two women from the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two bracelets of gold, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would you two like Allah to encircle you with two bracelets of Fire? They said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then render the due of Allah upon you both in this."
"6902","Haddathana Nasr ibn Bab from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing with his father, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, this one has come to need my wealth. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You and your wealth belong to your father."
"6903","Haddathana Nasr ibn Bab from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer in which there is no recitation is deficient, then it is deficient, then it is deficient."
"6904","Haddathana Nasr ibn Bab from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote a document between the Muhajirun and the Ansar that they share their blood-money obligations and ransom their captives with kindness and reconciliation among the Muslims."
"6905","Haddathana Nasr ibn Bab from Ismail from Qays from Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali who said: We used to count gathering at the family of the deceased and preparing food after his burial as part of wailing."
"6906","Haddathana Nasr ibn Bab from Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers on the day he raided Banu al-Mustaliq."
"6907","Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Musa, Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: and I heard it myself from al-Hakam ibn Musa, haddathana Muslim ibn Khalid from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath then sees what is better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath."
"6908","Haddathana Ali ibn Abdullah, haddathana al-Walid ibn Muslim, haddathani al-Awzai, haddathani Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, haddathani Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, haddathani Urwah ibn al-Zubayr who said: I said to Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As: Inform me of the harshest thing the polytheists did to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying in the courtyard of the Kaaba, Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt came forward, seized the shoulder of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), twisted his garment around his neck, and strangled him with it severely. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came forward, seized his shoulder, pushed him away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah, when he has come to you with clear proofs from your Lord."
"6909","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah from Ata ibn al-Saib from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledging him upon emigration, and he was stern with him, and he said: I did not come to you until I made them both weep, meaning his parents. He said: Return and make them laugh as you made them weep."
"6910","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah from Ata ibn al-Saib from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Two traits or two habits no Muslim man observes except he enters Paradise; they are easy, and few act upon them: you glorify Allah ten times and praise Allah ten times and magnify Allah ten times at the end of every prayer, so that is one hundred and fifty by the tongue and one thousand five hundred in the balance; and you glorify thirty-three times and praise thirty-three times and magnify thirty-four times, Ata does not know which of them is thirty-four, when you take your bed, so that is one hundred by the tongue and one thousand in the balance. So which of you commits two thousand five hundred sins in a day. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how are they easy yet few act upon them. He said: Satan comes to one of you when he finishes his prayer and reminds him of the need of such-and-such, so he stands and does not say them; and when he lies down, Satan comes to him and lulls him before he says them. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counting them on his hand. Abdullah said: I heard Ubaydullah al-Qawariri: I heard Hammad ibn Zayd say: Ata ibn al-Saib came to us in Basra, and Ayyub said to us: Go to him and ask him about the hadith of tasbih, meaning this hadith."
"6911","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah from Abu Bishr from a man of the people of Makkah from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw people who performed ablution without completing the ablution, and he said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"6912","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah from Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden, and the Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"6913","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah from Sad ibn Ibrahim that he heard a man of Banu Makhzum narrating from his uncle that Muawiyah wanted to take land belonging to Abdullah ibn Amr called al-Waht, so he ordered his retainers, and they put on their gear and intended to fight. He said: So I came to him and said: What is this. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim is wronged with a wrong and then fights and is killed except he is killed as a martyr."
"6914","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Hilal ibn Talhah or Talhah ibn Hilal who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abdullah ibn Amr, fast three days of every month. He said: And he recited this verse: Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten likes of it. He said: I said: I can do more than that. He said: Fast the fast of Dawud; he used to fast a day and break a day."
"6915","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Shubah from Ziyad ibn Fayyad from Abu Iyad: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Fast a day, and you have the reward of what remains, until he counted four days or five, Shubah doubts. He said: Fast the best fast, the fast of Dawud, peace be upon him; he used to fast a day and break a day."
"6916","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, who said: We visited Abu Husayn when he was ill, and Asim was with us. Abu Husayn said to Asim: Do you recall a hadith al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah narrated to us. He said: Yes, one day he narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim servant falls ill, it is said to the scribe who writes his deeds: Write for him like his deeds when he was free, until I take him or release him. Abu Bakr said: Asim and Abu Husayn both narrated it to us."
"6917","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Ibn Abi al-Zinad from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Conquest say: Every alliance that was in the Jahiliyyah, Islam only increased it in strength, and there is no alliance in Islam."
"6918","Haddathana Asbat ibn Muhammad, haddathana Ibn Ajlan from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade advance payment with a sale, two sales in one sale, selling what is not with you, and profit on what was not guaranteed."
"6919","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Sawa Abu al-Khattab al-Sadusi who said: I asked al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah about Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has added for you a prayer, so observe it, and it is the Witr. And Amr ibn Shuayb held that the Witr should be repeated even after a month."
"6920","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shubah who said: Ibrahim ibn Maymun informed me who said: I heard a man of Banu al-Harith who said: I heard a man of us called Ayyub who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: Whoever repents a year before his death, it is accepted from him, and whoever repents a month before his death, it is accepted from him, until he said a day, until he said an hour, until he said a moment. The man said: What if he was a polytheist and became Muslim. He said: I only narrate to you as I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"6921","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq who said: Haddathana Ibn Jurayj, and Rawh said: Akhbarana Ibn Jurayj, akhbarani Amr ibn Dinar that Amr ibn Aws informed him from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved fasting to Allah is the fasting of Dawud; he used to fast half of the lifetime. And the most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of Dawud; he used to sleep half the night, then stand, then sleep its end, then stand a third of the night after its half."
"6922","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq who said: Akhbarana Ibn Jurayj, akhbarani Sulayman al-Ahwal that Thabit, the freedman of Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed him that when there occurred between Abdullah ibn Amr and Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan what occurred and they prepared for fighting, Khalid ibn al-Asi rode to Abdullah ibn Amr and admonished him. So Abdullah ibn Amr said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr. And Abd al-Razzaq said: Whoever is killed over his wealth is a martyr."
"6923","Haddathana Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, akhbarana Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever slave is contracted for one hundred ounces and pays all but ten ounces, then is unable, he is a slave."
"6924","Haddathana Abdah ibn Sulayman from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plucking white hair."
"6925","Haddathana Zayd ibn al-Hubab, akhbarani Musa ibn Ali: I heard my father say: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do you know who the Muslim is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. He said: Do you know who the believer is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: One whom the believers trust with their lives and wealth. And the emigrant is one who abandons evil and avoids it."
"6926","Haddathana al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, haddathana Sufyan from al-Amash from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith who said: I was traveling with Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As and Muawiyah, and Abdullah ibn Amr said to Amr: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The transgressing party will kill him, meaning Ammar. So Amr said to Muawiyah: Hear what this one says. So he narrated to him. He said: Did we kill him; those who brought him are the ones who killed him."
"6927","Haddathana Abu Muawiyah, meaning al-Darir, haddathana al-Amash from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad, and he mentioned the like of it."
"6928","Haddathana Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad, haddathana Husayn al-Muallim, and Yazid said: Akhbarana Husayn from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fast while traveling and break his fast, and I saw him drink standing and sitting, and I saw him pray barefoot and shod, and I saw him turn away to his right and to his left."
"6929","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana al-Awwam, haddathani Aswad ibn Masud from Hanzalah ibn Khuwaylid al-Anbari who said: While I was with Muawiyah, two men came to him disputing over the head of Ammar, each of them saying: I killed him. So Abdullah said: Let one of you comfort the other, for I heard, meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: Thus my father said it, meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The transgressing party will kill him. So Muawiyah said: Will you not relieve us of your madman, O Amr; what is the matter with you being with us. He said: My father complained of me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Obey your father while he is alive and do not disobey him, so I am with you but I do not fight."
"6930","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun and Muhammad ibn Yazid who said: Akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I write what I hear from you. He said: Yes. I said: In pleasure and anger. He said: Yes, for I ought not to say in that except the truth. Muhammad ibn Yazid said in his hadith: O Messenger of Allah, I hear things from you, shall I write them. He said: Yes."
"6931","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana Hisham, and Abd al-Samad said: Haddathana Hisham from Yahya from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith that Khalid ibn Madan narrated to him that Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Amr informed him, Abd al-Samad said: Ibn al-As, narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him wearing two saffron-dyed garments and said: These are the clothes of the disbelievers, so do not wear them."
"6932","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no divorce in what you do not own, no emancipation in what you do not own, no vow in what you do not own, and no vow in disobedience to Allah."
"6933","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Husayn al-Muallim from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: When Makkah was opened to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Withhold weapons except Khuzaah against Banu Bakr, so he permitted them until they prayed Asr, then he said: Withhold weapons. Then the next day a man of Khuzaah met a man of Banu Bakr at Muzdalifah and killed him. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood addressing and said: The most hostile of people to Allah is one who transgresses in the sanctuary, one who kills other than his killer, and one who kills for the grudges of the Jahiliyyah. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, my son so-and-so, I had intercourse with his mother in the Jahiliyyah. He said: There is no claim in Islam; the affair of the Jahiliyyah is gone. The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is al-athlab. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-athlab. He said: The stone. And for the fingers ten ten, and for wounds exposing bone five five. And there is no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and no prayer after Asr until the sun sets. And a woman is not married over her paternal aunt nor over her maternal aunt. And no gift by a woman is permitted except with her husband's permission. And fulfill the oaths of the Jahiliyyah, for Islam only increased them in strength, and do not make a new alliance in Islam."
"6934","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana al-Awwam, haddathani a freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the sun when it set and said: In the blazing Fire of Allah; were it not for what restrains it by the command of Allah, it would have destroyed what is on the earth."
"6935","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not recognize the right of our elder and show mercy to our younger."
"6936","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard a man of Muzaynah asking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Idris. He said: And he asked him about fruits and what is in its husks. He said: Whoever eats with his mouth and does not take in a pocket, nothing is upon him; and whoever is found carrying, in it is its price twice over plus an exemplary beating; and what is taken from its storehouse, in it is cutting if it reaches what the price of a shield is taken for. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what about lost property we find on the frequented road. He said: Announce it for a year; if its owner comes, otherwise it is yours. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what about what we find in the ruined ancient site. He said: In it and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"6937","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plucking white hair and said: It is the light of the believer. And he said: No man grows white hair in Islam except Allah raises him a degree by it, a sin is erased from him by it, and a good deed is written for him by it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not honor our elder and show mercy to our younger."
"6938","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned his daughter to Abu al-As with a new dowry and a new marriage. My father said in the hadith of Hajjaj: He returned Zaynab, his daughter. He said: This hadith is weak, or he said: feeble, and al-Hajjaj did not hear it from Amr ibn Shuayb; he only heard it from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, and al-Arzami, his hadith is worth nothing. And the authentic hadith that was narrated is that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left them both upon the first marriage."
"6939","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: Two women of the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing bracelets of gold, and he said: Would you two like Allah to encircle you with a bracelet of Fire. They said: No. He said: Then render the due of this."
"6940","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana al-Hajjaj, and Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The testimony of a treacherous one is not permitted, nor one flogged in Islam, nor one bearing malice against his brother."
"6941","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has added for you a prayer, and it is the Witr."
"6942","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives I join and they cut, I pardon and they wrong, I do good and they do evil; shall I requite them. He said: No, then you would all be abandoned; rather take bounty and join them, for there will not cease to be with you a supporter from Allah while you are upon that."
"6943","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana al-Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who returns in his gift is like the dog that returns in its vomit."
"6944","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Ibrahim ibn Amir from Said ibn al-Musayyab and from al-Zuhri from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came tearing his hair and crying woe. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is the matter with you. He said: He had intercourse with his wife in Ramadan. He said: Free a slave. He said: I cannot find one. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot. He said: Feed sixty poor. He said: I cannot find. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket in it fifteen sa of dates. He said: Take this and feed sixty poor on your behalf. He said: O Messenger of Allah, there is no household between its two lava plains poorer than us. He said: Eat it, you and your family."
"6945","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana al-Hajjaj from Ata and from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather with the like of it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he added a sacrificial camel. Amr said in his hadith: And he commanded him to fast a day in its place."
"6946","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Ali ibn Zayd from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir that Nawf and Abdullah ibn Amr met, and Nawf mentioned the hadith, and Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: And I narrate to you from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and those who stayed after stayed and those who returned returned. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came before the people dispersed for the Isha prayer, and he came breathless, raising his finger like this, and he contracted twenty-nine, and he pointed with his index finger to the sky, saying: Glad tidings, community of the Muslims, this is your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has opened a gate of the gates of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, saying: O My angels, look at these servants of Mine; they have performed an obligation and they await another."
"6947","Struck through: Haddathana Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq and Hawdhah ibn Khalifah who said: Haddathana Awf from Maymun ibn Ustadh, Hawdhah said: al-Hizzani, who said: Abdullah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my nation wears gold and dies wearing it will not wear the gold of Paradise, and Hawdhah said: Allah has forbidden him the gold of Paradise; and whoever of my nation wears silk and dies wearing it, Allah has forbidden him the silk of Paradise. Abdullah said: My father struck through this hadith, and I thought he struck through it because it is a mistake; it is only Maymun ibn Ustadh from Abdullah ibn Amr, and there is no al-Sadafi in it; and it is said this Maymun is al-Sadafi; for the hearing of Yazid ibn Harun from al-Jurayri was at the end of his life, and Allah knows best."
"6948","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, akhbarana al-Jurayri from Maymun ibn Ustadh from al-Sadafi from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever of my nation dies drinking wine, Allah has forbidden him drinking it in Paradise; and whoever of my nation dies adorning himself with gold, Allah has forbidden him wearing it in Paradise."
"6949","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Hajjaj from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever slave is contracted for one hundred ounces and pays all but ten ounces, he is a slave."
"6950","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, akhbarana Qatadah from Abu Thumamah al-Thaqafi from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The womb will be placed on the Day of Resurrection with a hook like the hook of the spindle, speaking with fluent sharp tongues; it joins whoever joined it and cuts whoever cut it."
"6951","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad from Thabit from Shuayb ibn Abdullah ibn Amr from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fast a day, and you have ten days. He said: Give me more, O Messenger of Allah, I have strength. He said: Fast two days, and you have nine days. He said: Give me more, for I find strength. He said: Fast three days, and you have eight days."
"6952","Haddathana Abu Dawud and Abd al-Samad, the meaning, who said: Haddathana Hisham from Qatadah from Shahr who said: Abdullah ibn Amr came upon Nawf al-Bikali while he was narrating, and he said: Narrate, for we have been forbidden narration. He said: I would not narrate while with me is a man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then of Quraysh. So Abdullah ibn Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a migration after a migration, so the best of the earth, Abd al-Samad said: to the best of the earth, to the place of Ibrahim's migration; and there will remain in the earth the worst of its people, the earth ejects them, the soul of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, finds them foul, and the Fire gathers them with the apes and pigs. Then he said: Narrate, for we have been forbidden narration. So he said: I would not narrate while with me is a man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then of Quraysh. So Abdullah ibn Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People emerge from the east reciting the Quran not passing their throats; whenever a horn is cut off another horn grows, until the Dajjal emerges among their remnants."
"6953","Haddathana Abu al-Jawab, haddathana Ammar ibn Ruzayq from al-Amash from Abu Said who said: I came to Abdullah ibn Amr and said: Narrate to me what you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and do not narrate to me from the Torah and the Gospel. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"6954","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Thawr ibn Yazid from Uthman al-Shami that he heard Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever washes and bathes, goes early and arrives early, draws near and approaches, listens and is silent, for every step he takes is the reward of standing a year and fasting it."
"6955","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, akhbarana Abu Israil from al-Hakam from Hilal al-Hajari who said: I said to Abdullah ibn Amr: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake; it is only al-Hakam from Sayf from Rushayd al-Hajari from his father."
"6956","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad from Qatadah from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"6957","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, haddathana Ibn Shihab from Isa ibn Talhah from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man came to him on the Day of Sacrifice while he was standing at the Jamarah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I stoned. He said: Stone, no harm. And another came to him and said: I slaughtered before I stoned. He said: Stone, no harm. And another came to him and said: I performed the Ifadah before I stoned. He said: Stone, no harm. He said: I never saw him asked that day about anything except he said: Do, no harm."
"6958","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Shubah, akhbarani Husayn: I heard Mujahid narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every deed is enthusiasm, and for every enthusiasm is a lull; so whoever's lull is toward my Sunnah has succeeded, and whoever's is toward other than that has perished."
"6959","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hatim ibn Abi Saghairah, haddathana Abu Balj from Amr ibn Maymun from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah, and no power nor strength except with Allah, his sins are expiated even if like the foam of the sea."
"6960","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Shubah from Amr ibn Dinar: I heard Suhayb, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir, from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever kills a sparrow for nothing except by its right, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection."
"6961","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, akhbarani Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The most frequent supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Arafah was: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; in His hand is good, and He is over everything Capable."
"6962","Haddathana Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, haddathana Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pluck white hair, for it is the light of the Muslim; whoever grows white hair in Islam, Allah writes for him a good deed by it, expiates a sin from him by it, and raises him a degree by it."
"6963","He said: Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathani my father, haddathana Habib, meaning al-Muallim, from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man entered Paradise for his leniency as a buyer and as a seller."
"6964","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah from al-Hasan from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until Allah takes His chosen from the people of the earth, and there remains in it riffraff who know no good nor deny evil."
"6965","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Hammam from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Abdullah ibn Amr, and he did not raise it, and he said: Until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, takes His chosen from the people."
"6966","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah from Abu Ayyub from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The time of Zuhr is when the sun declines and the shadow of a man is like his length while Asr has not come; and the time of Asr is while the sun has not yellowed; and the time of Maghrib prayer is while the twilight has not gone; and the time of Isha prayer is till the middle of the night; and the time of Fajr prayer is from the rising of dawn while the sun has not risen; and when the sun rises, refrain from prayer, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."
"6967","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about one who approaches his wife in her anus: It is the lesser sodomy."
"6968","Haddathana Abdullah, haddathana Hudbah, haddathana Hammam who said: Qatadah was asked about one who approaches his wife in her anus, so Qatadah said: Haddathana Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the lesser sodomy. Qatadah said: And Uqbah ibn Wassaj narrated to me from Abu al-Darda who said: None does that except a disbeliever."
"6969","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Khalifah ibn Khayyat al-Laythi from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever swears an oath then sees better than it, it is its expiation."
"6970","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Khalifah from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them while leaning his back against the Kaaba, and he said: There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and no prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rises; and the believers, their blood is equal, the lowest of them grants protection, and they are one hand against others; no believer is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant."
"6971","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Imran al-Qattan, haddathana Amir al-Ahwal from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that a man said: So-and-so is my son. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no claim in Islam."
"6972","Haddathana Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, haddathana Hisham from Yahya from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Khalid ibn Madan from Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him wearing two saffron-dyed garments and said: These are the clothes of the disbelievers, so do not wear them."
"6973","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Bakr, meaning al-Sahmi, haddathana Hatim from Abu Balj from Amr ibn Maymun that he informed him that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no man on the earth who says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and no power nor strength except with Allah, except his sins are expiated, even if like the foam of the sea."
"6974","He said: Haddathana Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, haddathana Qurrah from al-Hasan who said: By Allah, they claimed that Abdullah ibn Amr testified upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: If he drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; and when at the fourth, strike his neck. Abdullah ibn Amr used to say: Bring me a man flogged for wine four times, and you have upon me that I strike his neck."
"6975","Haddathana Surayj ibn al-Numan, haddathana Ibn Abi al-Zinad from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a Bedouin standing in the sun while he was addressing and said: What is the matter with you. He said: I vowed, O Messenger of Allah, never to leave the sun until you finish. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is not a vow; the vow is only what the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is sought with."
"6976","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Abu Awanah, haddathana Abu Bishr from Yusuf ibn Mahak from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed behind on a journey we traveled, and he caught us while Asr had pressed us and we were performing ablution, and we began wiping over our feet. So he called with his loudest voice: Woe to the heels from the Fire, twice or thrice."
"6977","Haddathana Surayj, haddathana Abdullah ibn al-Muammal from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As that he wore a ring of gold, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it as if he disliked it, so he threw it away. Then he wore a ring of iron, and he said: This is worse and worse, so he threw it away. Then he wore a ring of silver, and he was silent about it."
"6978","Haddathana Surayj, haddathana Abdullah ibn al-Muammal from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Corner will come on the Day of Resurrection greater than Abu Qubays, with a tongue and two lips."
"6979","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Sharik from Ziyad ibn Fayyad from Abu Iyad from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid of vessels the gourd, the tar-coated, and the green-glazed. Sharik said: And he mentioned things. A Bedouin said to him: We have no containers. He said: Drink what is lawful and do not get drunk. I repeated it to Sharik, and he said: Drink, and do not drink an intoxicant, and do not get drunk."
"6980","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah from Layth from Tawus from Ziyad Simin Kush from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be a tribulation cleansing the Arabs; its slain are in the Fire; the tongue therein is harsher than the blow of the sword."
"6981","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Ibn Lahiah from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day as if bidding farewell and said: I am Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, I am Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, three times, and there is no prophet after me. I was given the openings of speech and its comprehensive and its seals, and I knew how many are the keepers of the Fire and the bearers of the Throne, and passing was lightened for me, and I was spared and my nation was spared. So hear and obey while I am among you; and when I am gone, upon you is the Book of Allah: permit its lawful and forbid its unlawful."
"6982","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, haddathana Shubah from Ismail and Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar from al-Shabi from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"6983","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Zakariyya from al-Shabi who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"6984","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Ibn Abi Dhib from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Salamah from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The curse of Allah upon the briber and the bribed."
"6985","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Sufyan from Abu Hazim from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No servant believes until he believes in the decree, its good and its evil."
"6986","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana al-Amash from Amr ibn Murrah who said: We were sitting with Abu Ubaydah, and they mentioned showing off. A man called Abu Yazid said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make His creation hear of him on the Day of Resurrection, belittling him and diminishing him."
"6987","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, from Hilal ibn Khabbab Abu al-Ala who said: Haddathani Ikrimah, haddathani Abdullah ibn Amr who said: While we were around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they mentioned tribulation, or it was mentioned with him. He said: When you see people whose covenants are confused and whose trusts are diminished and they are like this, and he interlaced his fingers. So I stood to him and said to him: What shall I do then, may Allah make me ransom for you. He said: Stay in your house, control your tongue, take what you know, leave what you deny, attend to the affair of your own self, and leave from you the affair of the public."
"6988","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Sufyan from Habib from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He does not fast who fasts perpetually."
"6989","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith from Amr ibn Shuayb, if Allah wills, from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plucking white hair and said: It is the light of Islam."
"6990","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Bakr, haddathana Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas Abu Malik al-Azdi from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow nor oath in what the son of Adam does not own, nor in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, nor severing kinship. So whoever swears an oath then sees better than it, let him leave it and do what is better, for leaving it is its expiation."
"6991","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, akhbarana Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, haddathani Usamah ibn Zayd, haddathani Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying and selling in the mosque."
"6992","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata who said: And haddathana Husayn al-Muallim from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: When Makkah was opened to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Withhold weapons, and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Yahya and Yazid, and he said in it: And fulfill the oaths of the Jahiliyyah, for Islam only increased them in strength, and do not make a new alliance in Islam."
"6993","Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, haddathana Shubah from Qatadah: I heard Abu Ayyub al-Azdi narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: He did not raise it twice. He said: And I asked him the third time, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The time of Zuhr prayer is while Asr has not come; and the time of Asr prayer is while the sun has not yellowed; and the time of Maghrib prayer is while the light of twilight has not fallen; and the time of Isha prayer is till the middle of the night; and the time of Fajr prayer is while the sun has not risen."
"6994","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Talqani, haddathana Ibn Mubarak from Layth ibn Sad, haddathani Amir ibn Yahya from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, singles out a man of my nation before the creatures on the Day of Resurrection, and He spreads for him ninety-nine scrolls, every scroll the extent of sight. Then He says to him: Do you deny anything of this; did My recording guardians wrong you. He says: No, my Lord. So He says: Have you an excuse or a good deed. The man is bewildered and says: No, my Lord. So He says: Yes, you have with Us one good deed; no wrong today upon you. Then a card is brought out for him in it: I testify there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. So He says: Attend it. So he says: My Lord, what is this card with these scrolls. So it is said: You will not be wronged. He said: Then the scrolls are placed in a scale. He said: So the scrolls fly and the card is heavy; and nothing outweighs the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."
"6995","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Ishaq, haddathana Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak from Layth ibn Sad, haddathani Jafar ibn Rabiah from Bakr ibn Sawadah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to him who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: No man shall enter upon a woman whose husband is absent except with another. Abdullah ibn Amr said: After that station, I never entered upon such a woman except with one or two with me."
"6996","Haddathana Attab ibn Ziyad, haddathana Abdullah, meaning Ibn Mubarak, akhbarana Abdullah ibn Shawdhab who said: Haddathani Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid from Abdullah ibn Buraydah from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to distribute booty, he ordered Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, and he called thrice. Then a man came with a bridle of hair to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the booty was distributed and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is of booty I had taken. He said: Did you not hear Bilal call thrice. He said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from bringing it to me. So he made an excuse to him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will not accept it until you meet me with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"6997","Haddathana Attab, haddathana Abdullah, akhbarana Usamah ibn Zayd from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Conquest while in Makkah say: Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of wine, carrion, and pig. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the fats of carrion, for ships are caulked with them, skins are oiled with them, and people light with them. He said: No, it is forbidden. Then he said: May Allah destroy the Jews; when Allah forbade them fats, they melted them, then sold them and ate their prices."
"6998","Haddathana Attab ibn Ziyad, akhbarana Abdullah, akhbarana Usamah ibn Zayd, haddathani Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not shake hands with women at the pledge."
"6999","Haddathana Attab, haddathana Abdullah, akhbarana Usamah ibn Zayd from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a man to separate two except with their permission."
"7000","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Raja Abu Yahya, haddathana Musafi ibn Shaybah: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: So I adjure by Allah thrice, and he put his finger in his ears, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Corner and the Station are two rubies of the rubies of Paradise; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, effaced their light; and were Allah not to have effaced their light, they would have illuminated what is between the east and the west."
"7001","Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray related to me, Habib al-Muallim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have wealth and a father, and my father wants to take all my wealth. He said: You and your wealth belong to your father. Your children are among the purest of your earnings, so eat from the earnings of your children. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I was informed that Habib al-Muallim is said to be Habib ibn Abi Baqiyya."
"7002","Affan narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Habib narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Three attend Friday: a man who attends it engaged in idle talk, so that is his share of it; a man who attends it with supplication, so he is a man who supplicated Allah, mighty and majestic, and if He wills He gives him and if He wills He withholds from him; and a man who attends it listening attentively and silent, and does not step over the neck of a Muslim and does not harm anyone, so it is an expiation until the Friday that follows it plus three more days, for Allah says: whoever brings a good deed shall have ten like it."
"7003","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Shahr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; and whoever drinks a second time, flog him; then if he drinks a third time, flog him; then if he drinks a fourth time, kill him."
"7004","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Sad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the gravest of major sins is disobedience to parents. It was said: And what is disobedience to parents? He said: A man reviles a man, so he reviles his father, and he reviles his mother, so he reviles his mother."
"7005","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says in a day two hundred times: there is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise and He is over all things competent, no one before him surpassed him and no one after him will catch up with him except by better than his deed, meaning except one who does better than his deed."
"7006","Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyya narrated to me, he said: Abu Kabsha al-Saluli came while we were in the mosque, so Makhul and Ibn Abi Zakariyya and Abu Bahriyya stood up to him, and he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Convey from me even a verse, and narrate from the Children of Israel and there is no harm, and whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"7007","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala, from Amr ibn Shuayb, he said: I heard my father narrate from his father that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A lone rider is a devil, two riders are two devils, and three are a riding party."
"7008","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Raja ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musafi ibn Shayba narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to us, and he put his fingers in his ears, that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Stone and the Maqam are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise; Allah effaced their light, and were it not for that they would have illuminated what is between heaven and earth, or what is between the east and the west. Thus said Yunus: Raja ibn Yahya, and Affan said: Raja Abu Yahya. Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: Hudba ibn Khalid narrated it to us, he said: Raja ibn Subayh Abu Yahya al-Harashi narrated to us; and the correct view is Abu Yahya, as Affan and Hudba ibn Khalid said."
"7009","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Qawariri Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Raja Abu Yahya narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it."
"7010","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Musa ibn Ali ibn Rabah informed us, I heard my father narrate from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The people of the Fire are every coarse, swaggering, arrogant hoarder and withholder, and the people of Paradise are the weak and overpowered."
"7011","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Yunus ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only combined rites fearing he would be barred from the House, and he said: If it is not a Hajj then it is an Umra."
"7012","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed the people in the year of the Conquest upon the steps of the Kaba, and among what he said after praising Allah was: O people, every oath of alliance in the Jahiliyya, Islam only added to it in strictness; and there is no alliance in Islam, and no emigration after the Conquest; the hand of the Muslims is one against others besides them; their blood is equivalent; a believer is not killed for a disbeliever; the blood money of the disbeliever is like half the blood money of the Muslim; and there is no shighar in Islam, and no janab and no jalab; and their charities are taken in their own lands; the lowest of the Muslims grants protection on their behalf, and the farthest of the Muslims returns on their behalf. Then he descended. And Husayn said: He heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"7013","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Matar, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning exposed wounds: five, five camels; and the fingers are equal, all of them ten, ten camels."
"7014","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatada, from Shahr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"7015","Marwan ibn Shuja Abu Amr al-Jazari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla al-Uqayli of the people of Bayt al-Maqdis narrated to me, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As met on al-Marwa and conversed, then Abdullah ibn Amr went on and Abdullah ibn Umar remained weeping. A man said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: This one, meaning Abdullah ibn Amr, claims that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance, Allah will throw him down on his face into the Fire."
"7016","Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays Abu al-Jahm narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every prayer in which there is no recitation is defective, then defective, then defective."
"7017","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali informed me, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Do you know who the Muslim is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. He said: Do you know who the believer is? They said: Allah, meaning, and His Messenger know best. He said: One whom the believers trust with their selves and their wealth. And the emigrant is one who abandons evil and keeps away from it."
"7018","Ali ibn Asim informed us, Duwayd al-Khurasani informed us, while al-Zubayr ibn Adi was sitting with him, he said: Amr ibn Shuayb informed us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we hear narrations from you that we do not memorize; shall we not write them down? He said: Yes, so write them."
"7019","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Disbelief in Allah is disavowal of lineage, however slight, or claiming a lineage that is not known."
"7020","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I hear things from you; shall I write them down? He said: Yes. I said: In anger and in pleasure? He said: Yes, for I do not say in either except the truth."
"7021","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, he said, meaning Abd al-Wahhab, and I had heard it from him, meaning Husayn, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turn away from his right and from his left, and I saw him pray barefoot and wearing sandals, and I saw him fast while traveling and break his fast, and I saw him drink sitting and standing."
"7022","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have no wealth but I have an orphan. He said: Eat from the wealth of your orphan without extravagance, nor waste, nor accumulating wealth from it, and without shielding your wealth, or he said: ransoming your wealth with his wealth. Husayn doubted."
"7023","Ubayda ibn Humayd Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abdullah ibn Amr, in how many do you recite the Quran? He said: I said: In my day and my night. He said: He said to me: Sleep and pray, and sleep, and recite it in every month. He said: I kept bargaining with him and he kept bargaining with me until he said: Recite it every seven nights. My father said: And I did not understand, and a word escaped me, he said: Then he said. I said: I fast and do not break my fast. He said: He said to me: Fast and break your fast, and fast three days of every month. I kept bargaining with him and he kept bargaining with me until he said: Fast the most beloved fast to Allah, mighty and majestic, the fast of Dawud: fast a day and break a day. Then Abdullah ibn Amr said: That I had accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is dearer to me than red camels. I think Ubayda doubted."
"7024","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Amr ibn Shuayb ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no jalab and no janab, and their charities are not taken except in their homes."
"7025","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abu Sufyan al-Harashi narrated to me, and he was trustworthy in what the people of his land mentioned, from Muslim ibn Jubayr the freedman of Thaqif, and Muslim was a man from whom knowledge was taken, and he had met and heard, from Amr ibn Huraysh al-Zubaydi, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I said: O Abu Muhammad, we are in a land where we do not find dinars and dirhams, and our wealth is livestock, so we trade them among ourselves: we buy a cow for a sheep on credit to a term, and a camel for cows, and a horse for camels, all to a term; is there any harm upon us in that? He said: You have alighted upon one well informed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me to dispatch an army upon camels that were with me. He said: So I mounted the people upon them until the camels ran out while a remainder of the people remained. He said: So I said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O Messenger of Allah, the camels have run out and a remainder of the people remains with no mounts. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Buy for us camels in exchange for young she-camels from the charity camels due at their time, until you dispatch this expedition. He said: So I would buy a camel for two or three young she-camels from the charity camels due at their time until I dispatched that expedition. He said: Then when the charity fell due, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, paid it."
"7026","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Amr ibn Shuayb mentioned, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning the blood money of the fetus in its mother womb: a ghurra, a slave or a slave girl; so he ruled with that concerning the wife of Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabigha al-Hudhali; and that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"7027","Yaqub and Sad narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, meaning Muhammad, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled. He said: There is no shighar in Islam."
"7028","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: And Amr ibn Shuayb mentioned, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning the child of the two invoking mutual curses that he inherits his mother and his mother inherits him; and whoever accuses her through him is flogged eighty, and whoever calls him a child of fornication is flogged eighty."
"7029","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the gravest of major sins is that a man curse his parents. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how does a man curse his parents? He said: A man reviles a man, so he reviles his father, and a man reviles his mother, so he reviles his mother."
"7030","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn al-Muttalib al-Makhzumi, narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Amr ibn Shuayb al-Sahmi, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"7031","Yaqub narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hasan ibn Hasan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talha al-Taymi, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, the like of that."
"7032","Yaqub narrated to me, my father, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Isa ibn Talha ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood on the Day of Sacrifice upon his mount, and they began asking him. One of them would say: O Messenger of Allah, I did not realize that stoning comes before sacrifice, so I sacrificed before I stoned. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say: Stone, and there is no harm. And another would come and say: O Messenger of Allah, I did not realize that sacrifice comes before shaving, so I shaved before I sacrificed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say: Sacrifice, and there is no harm. He said: I never heard him that day asked about a matter of what a person forgets or is ignorant of, of advancing some rites before others and the like, except the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do it, and there is no harm."
"7033","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and he mentioned a narration. Ibn Ishaq said: And Amr ibn Shuayb ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As mentioned, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever kills a believer deliberately, he is handed over to the kin of the slain; if they wish they kill, and if they wish they take the blood money, and it is thirty hiqqa and thirty jadhaa and forty khalifa; so that is the blood money of deliberate killing; and whatever they agree upon of anything is theirs, and that is the severe blood money. And the blood money of quasi-deliberate killing is aggravated like the blood money of deliberate killing, but its perpetrator is not executed, and that is when Satan provokes among people so that bloodshed occurs without rancor and without bearing arms. For the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, meaning: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us, nor lies in wait by a road. So whoever is killed apart from that is quasi-deliberate, and its blood money is aggravated, but its perpetrator is not executed. And it is in the sacred month, and for the sanctity, and for kinship. And whoever is killed by mistake, his blood money is one hundred camels: thirty bint makhad and thirty bint labun and thirty hiqqa and ten young male camels, sons of labun. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would assess it upon the people of villages at four hundred dinars or its equivalent in silver, and he would assess it upon camel prices; when they rose he raised its valuation, and when they fell he reduced its valuation, according to the time as it was. So it reached in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, between four hundred dinars and eight hundred dinars, and its equivalent in silver was eight thousand dirhams. And he ruled that whoever owed blood money among the people of cattle, in cattle it is two hundred cows; and he ruled that whoever owed blood money among the people of sheep, it is two thousand sheep. And he ruled concerning the nose when cut off entirely: the full blood money; and when its tip is cut off, half the blood money. And he ruled concerning the eye: half the blood money, fifty camels or its equivalent in gold or silver, or one hundred cows or one thousand sheep. And the leg is half the blood money, and the hand is half the blood money. And the piercing head wound is a third of the blood money, thirty-three camels or its value in gold or silver or cattle or sheep. And the penetrating wound is a third of the blood money. And the bone-displacing wound is fifteen camels. And the bone-exposing wound is five camels. And the teeth are five camels."
"7034","He said: And Amr ibn Shuayb mentioned, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning a man who stabbed a man with a horn in his leg. He said: O Messenger of Allah, grant me retaliation. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Do not hasten until your wound heals. He said: But the man refused except to take retaliation, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted him retaliation against him. He said: So the one who took retaliation became lame while the one retaliated against healed. Then the one who took retaliation came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I became lame and my companion healed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Did I not command you not to take retaliation until your wound heals? So you disobeyed me. May Allah banish you, and your wound is void. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after the man who became lame, commanded whoever had a wound not to take retaliation until his wound heals; and when his wound heals, he may take retaliation."
"7035","Yaqub narrated to us, I heard him narrate, meaning his father, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in a gathering: Shall I not inform you of the most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in sitting on the Day of Resurrection, saying it three times. He said: We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then he said: The best of you in character."
"7036","Yaqub said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Yahya ibn Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Urwa, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I said to him: What is the most you saw Quraysh inflict upon the Messenger of Allah in what they displayed of enmity toward him? He said: I was present with them when their nobles gathered one day in al-Hijr and mentioned the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They said: We never saw the like of what we have endured from this man ever: he has belittled our minds, reviled our fathers, faulted our religion, split our unity, and cursed our gods. We have endured from him a grave matter, or as they said. He said: While they were thus, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appeared before them, walking until he touched the Corner, then passed by them circumambulating the House. When he passed by them they taunted him with some of what he says. He said: So I recognized that in his face. Then he went on. When he passed by them a second time they taunted him likewise, and I recognized that in his face. Then he went on. Then he passed by them a third time and they taunted him likewise, so he said: Do you hear, O company of Quraysh? By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I have indeed come to you with slaughter. So his word seized the people until there was not a man among them but as though a bird had fallen upon his head, until even the harshest of them toward him before that began to placate him with the best words he could find, until he would say: Go on, O Abu al-Qasim, go on rightly guided, for by Allah you were never ignorant. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left, until when it was the morrow they gathered in al-Hijr while I was with them. Some of them said to others: You mentioned what reached you from him until when he confronted you with what you dislike you left him alone. While they were in that, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appeared, so they leapt upon him with the leap of one man and surrounded him, saying to him: Are you the one who says such and such, of what had reached them from him of disparaging their gods and their religion? He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would say: Yes, I am the one who says that. He said: So I saw a man among them seize the juncture of his cloak. He said: And Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah تعالى be pleased with him, stood before him saying while weeping: Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah? Then they left him. That is indeed the severest I ever saw Quraysh inflict upon him."
"7037","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: And Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Amr, that the delegation of Hawazin came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at al-Jirana, and they had embraced Islam. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a root and a kin, and there has befallen us of calamity what is not hidden from you, so bestow favor upon us, may Allah bestow upon you. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Are your sons and your women dearer to you or your wealth? They said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave us choice between our honor and our wealth; rather return to us our women and our sons, for that is dearer to us. So he said to them: As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, it is yours. When I pray Zuhr with the people, stand and say: We seek the intercession of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the Muslims, and of the Muslims with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning our sons and our women; so I will give you at that time and ask for you. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed Zuhr with the people, they stood and spoke what he had commanded them. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Abd al-Muttalib, it is yours. The Emigrants said: And what belongs to us belongs to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And the Helpers said: And what belongs to us belongs to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Al-Aqra ibn Habis said: As for me and the Banu Tamim, no. And Uyayna ibn Hisn ibn Hudhayfa ibn Badr said: As for me and the Banu Fazara, no. Abbas ibn Mirdas said: As for me and the Banu Sulaym, no. The Banu Sulaym said: No, what belongs to us belongs to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Abbas says: O Banu Sulaym, you have weakened me. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for whoever among you holds to his right of these captives, for him for every person are six shares from the first spoils we take. So they returned to the people their sons and their women."
"7038","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Abu Ubayda ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir narrated to me, from Miqsam Abu al-Qasim the freedman of Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, he said: I went out, I and Talid ibn Kilab al-Laythi, until we came to Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As while he was circumambulating the House with his sandals hanging in his hand. We said to him: Were you present with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the Tamimi spoke to him on the day of Hunayn? He said: Yes. A man of the Banu Tamim called Dhu al-Khuwaysira came and stood before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was giving to the people. He said: O Muhammad, I have seen what you did this day. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, and how did you see it? He said: I did not see you act justly. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, became angry, then said: Woe to you, if justice is not with me, with whom would it be? So Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill him? He said: No, leave him, for he will have followers who go deep into religion until they exit from it as the arrow exits from the game: one looks at the head and finds nothing, then at the shaft and finds nothing, then at the notch and finds nothing; it has outstripped the dung and the blood. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Abu Ubayda, his name is Muhammad, trustworthy; and his brother Salama ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, none narrated from him except Ali ibn Zayd, and we do not know his standing; and Miqsam is unobjectionable; and this narration has other paths in this meaning, and other sound paths in this meaning; and Allah, glory and تعالى, knows best."
"7039","Muammal narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys, and the jallala, and riding it and eating its flesh."
"7040","Muammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Huwayrith, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The signs are beads strung in a thread; if the thread is cut, some of them follow others."
"7041","Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Harij, meaning Ibn Uthman al-Rahabi, narrated to us, from Hibban ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon his pulpit say: Show mercy and you will be shown mercy, and forgive and Allah will forgive you. Woe to the funnels of speech. Woe to the persisters who persist in what they did while they know."
"7042","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning Ibn Musa, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled that every one claimed as kin after his father to whom he is attributed, whom his heirs claim after him: he ruled that if he is from a slave girl he owned on the day he had intercourse with her, he is attached to the one who claimed him, but he has nothing of what was divided before of inheritance; and whatever of inheritance he finds not yet divided, he has his share; and he is not attached if his father to whom he is attributed denied him. And if he is from a slave girl he did not own or from a free woman with whom he fornicated, he is not attached and does not inherit, even if his father to whom he is attributed is the one who claimed him; and he is a child of fornication belonging to his mother people, whoever they are, free or slave."
"7043","Hashim narrated to us, Ishaq, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, Said ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr came to Ibn al-Zubayr while he was sitting in al-Hijr and said: O Ibn al-Zubayr, beware of deviation in the sanctuary of Allah, for I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: It shall be made lawful by a man of Quraysh, and a man of Quraysh shall violate it whose sins, were they weighed against the sins of the two worlds, would outweigh them. He said: So see that you are not he, O Ibn Amr, for you have read the books and accompanied the Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So I call you to witness that this face of mine is toward al-Sham striving."
"7044","Hasan, meaning al-Ashyab, narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said to them: The glad tidings in the life of this world, he said: are the righteous dream which the believer is given glad tidings of; it is a part of forty-nine parts of prophecy. So whoever sees that, let him report it; and whoever sees other than that, it is only from Satan to grieve him, so let him spit to his left three times and be silent and not inform anyone of it."
"7045","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Ibn Hubayra informed us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is turned back by omens from a need has associated partners. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the expiation of that? He said: That one of them say: O Allah, there is no good but Your good, and no omen but Your omen, and no god but You."
"7046","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Sallam informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from the report of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that when the sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, it was announced: Prayer in congregation. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bowed two bowings in a prostration, then the sun cleared. So Aisha, Mother of the Believers, said: I never prostrated a prostration longer than it, nor bowed a bowing longer than it."
"7047","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Sallam informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from the report of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that when the sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, it was announced: Prayer in congregation. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bowed two bowings in a prostration, then the sun cleared. So Aisha, Mother of the Believers, said: I never prostrated a prostration longer than it, nor bowed a bowing longer than it."
"7048","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahia informed us, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Isa ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The souls of two believers meet at a day and night journey, though neither of them has seen his companion."
"7049","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There will come upon people a time in which they are sifted as with a sieve; there shall remain of them dregs whose covenants and trusts are corrupted and who differ and become like this, and he interlaced his fingers. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the way out of that? He said: You take what you know and leave what you deny, and you attend to the affair of your own circle and leave the affair of the generality."
"7050","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Said al-Tujibi narrated to me, I heard Abu Qabil al-Misri say: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever dies on Friday or on Friday night is shielded from the trial of the grave."
"7051","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Mufaddal narrated to me, Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every sin of the martyr is forgiven except debt."
"7052","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Lahia informed us, al-Harith ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Hujayra the elder, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The upright Muslim indeed reaches the rank of the fasting, night-praying one by the verses of Allah, mighty and majestic, through nobility of his nature and good character."
"7053","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, and he is al-Harrani, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The One with two thin shanks from Abyssinia shall destroy the Kaba, and strip it of its ornaments, and divest it of its covering; and I can almost see him, bald and bow-legged, striking it with his shovel and his pick."
"7054","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Qaysar al-Tujibi, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a young man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may I kiss while fasting? He said: No. Then an old man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may I kiss while fasting? He said: Yes. So we looked at one another, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I knew you were looking at one another; the old man controls himself."
"7055","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth, wronged, is a martyr."
"7056","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, a house wider than it shall be built for him in Paradise."
"7057","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever withholds surplus water or surplus pasture, Allah, mighty and majestic, shall withhold His bounty from him."
"7058","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind and Habib al-Muallim, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Qays, from Mujahid, I think from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No disposal by a woman in her wealth is allowed when her husband owns her bond."
"7059","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man said: O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad alone. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have barred it from many people."
"7060","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man entered prayer and said: Praise be to Allah, and glorified. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who said it? The man said: I did. He said: I saw the angels receiving it from one another."
"7061","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Jews came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Death be upon you, and they said among themselves: Why does Allah not punish us for what we say? So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And when they come to you they greet you with what Allah did not greet you with, and he recited to His saying: So evil is the destination."
"7062","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, I heard Abu al-Abbas, and he was a poet, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked his permission for jihad. He said: Are your parents alive? He said: Yes. He said: Then in them strive."
"7063","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Umara ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People shall soon be sifted as with a sieve, and there shall remain dregs of people whose covenants and trusts are corrupted, and they become like this, and he interlaced his fingers. They said: What shall we do, O Messenger of Allah, if that happens? He said: You take what you know and leave what you deny, and you attend to your own circle and leave the generality of them. Qutayba ibn Said narrated it to us with its chain and meaning, except that he said: And there shall remain dregs of people, and you leave the affair of the generality of them."
"7064","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abdullah al-Maafiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, from al-Qasim ibn al-Barhi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever gives charity and finds only a Berber, let him return it."
"7065","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Huyayy ibn Abdullah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by Sad while he was performing ablution and said: What is this extravagance, O Sad? He said: Is there extravagance in ablution? He said: Yes, even if you are at a flowing river."
"7066","Qutayba narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Amir ibn Yahya, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The scales shall be set on the Day of Resurrection, and a man shall be brought and placed in a pan, and what was recorded against him shall be placed, and the scale shall tip against him. He said: So he shall be sent to the Fire. He said: Then when he is taken away, a crier shall cry from the Merciful saying: Do not hasten, do not hasten, for something remains for him. So a card shall be brought in which is: there is no god but Allah, and it shall be placed with the man in the pan until the scale tips in his favor."
"7067","Qutayba narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Wahib ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that he said: I saw in what the sleeper sees as though in one of my fingers was ghee and in the other honey, and I was licking them. When morning came I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: You read the two Books, the Torah and the Furqan. So he used to read them."
"7068","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the year of the Tabuk expedition, stood at night praying, and men of his companions gathered behind him guarding him, until when he prayed and turned to them he said to them: This night I have been given five that none before me was given: as for me, I was sent to all people generally, while those before me were sent only to their own people; and I was aided against the enemy with terror, and even were a month journey between me and them they would be filled with terror of me; and spoils were made lawful for me to eat, while those before me magnified eating them, they would burn them; and the earth was made for me mosques and a purification, wherever prayer overtakes me I wipe and pray, while those before me magnified that, they would pray only in their churches and synagogues; and the fifth, what a thing it is: it was said to me: Ask, for every prophet has asked, so I delayed my request until the Day of Resurrection, and it is for you and for whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah."
"7069","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, Rishdin informed us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Shaddad, from Abu Salih al-Ghifari, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The first to enter through this door shall be a man of the people of Paradise. Then Sad ibn Abi Waqqas entered."
"7070","Qutayba narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Thawban, from Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayya, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no contagion and no omen and no hama and no envy, and the evil eye is true."
"7071","Qutayba narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn al-Walid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you feel the revelation? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes, I hear clangings, then I become silent at that; there is no time revelation comes to me but I think my soul is overflowing."
"7072","Qutayba narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Jundub ibn Abdullah, from Sufyan ibn Awf, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when the sun rose, and he said: There shall come to Allah on the Day of Resurrection a people whose light is like the light of the sun. So Abu Bakr said: Are we they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but you have much good; rather they are the poor and the emigrants who are gathered from the ends of the earth. And he said: Blessed are the strangers, blessed are the strangers, blessed are the strangers. It was said: Who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Righteous people among many evil people; those who disobey them are more than those who obey them."
"7073","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, conveying to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever does not show mercy to our young and does not know the right of our elder is not of us."
"7074","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba, he said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: While a man was strutting in a suit, Allah, mighty and majestic, commanded the earth with him and it seized him, so he is sinking in it, or trembling in it, until the Day of Resurrection."
"7075","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usama informed me that Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to him, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I draw water into my basin until when I have filled it for my family a strange camel comes to me and I give it to drink; is there reward for me in that? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In every moist liver is a reward."
"7076","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Khattabi, narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Whoever touches his male organ, let him perform ablution; and whatever woman touches her private part, let her perform ablution."
"7077","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The time of Zuhr prayer is when the sun declines and the shadow of a man is like his height, as long as Asr has not come. And the time of Asr prayer is as long as the sun has not yellowed. And the time of Maghrib prayer is as long as the twilight has not set. And the time of Isha prayer is until midnight. And the time of Fajr prayer is from the rising of dawn as long as the sun has not risen; and when it rises, refrain, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, or with the two horns of a devil."
"7078","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awana informed us, from al-Amash, Uthman ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abu Harb al-Dayli, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Neither the green has shaded nor the dusty borne a man truer in speech than Abu Dharr."
"7079","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when deeds were mentioned, and he said: There are no days in which deeds are better than in these ten. They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad? So he magnified it. He said: Not even jihad, except that a man goes out with himself and his wealth in the path of Allah, then his lifeblood is shed in it."
"7080","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Saib ibn Malik, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died, the sun eclipsed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and prayed two bowings, prolonging the standing, then bowed like his standing, then prostrated like his bowing. So he prayed two bowings likewise, then saluted."
"7081","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Sharik al-Maafiri narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi al-Tanukhi, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I do not care what I take or what I ride if I drink theriac, or hang an amulet, or speak poetry from myself."
"7082","He said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Haywa narrated to us, he said: Rabia ibn Sayf al-Maafiri narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he saw Fatima, his daughter, and said to her: Whence have you come? She said: I have come from behind the bier of this man. He said: Did you reach al-Kuda with them? She said: No, and how would I reach it when I have heard from you what I heard? He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, had you reached al-Kuda with them you would not see Paradise until the grandfather of your father sees it."
"7083","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli say: We heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There shall be in the last of my nation men riding upon saddles like men, alighting at the doors of the mosque; their women clothed yet naked, upon their heads like the humps of lean camels. Curse them, for they are cursed. Had there been after you a nation among nations, your women would have served their women as the women of nations before you serve you."
"7084","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Ikrima the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is killed defending his wealth, wronged, for him is Paradise."
"7085","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah shall make the hearers of His creation hear of him, and belittle him and make him small."
"7086","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand people are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah forbade."
"7087","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Ibn Abi Rabia, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I mentioned fasting to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Fast one day of every ten days, and you have the reward of the nine. He said: So I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Then fast one day of every nine days, and you have the reward of the eight. He said: So I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Fast one day of every eight days, and you have the reward of those seven. He said: I said: I am stronger than that. He said: And he continued until he said: Fast a day and break a day."
"7088","Abu Said the freedman of the Banu Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The blood money of quasi-deliberate killing is aggravated like the blood money of deliberate killing, but its perpetrator is not executed. And whoever bears arms against us is not of us, nor lies in wait by a road."
"7089","Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Muthanna, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Allah, mighty and majestic, boasts to His angels on the evening of Arafa of the people of Arafa, saying: Look at My servants who have come to Me disheveled and dusty."
"7090","Abu Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is killed by mistake, his blood money is one hundred camels: thirty bint makhad, thirty bint labun, thirty jadhaa, and ten male sons of labun. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would assess it upon camel prices; when they fell he reduced its valuation, and when they rose he raised its valuation, according to the time as it was. So it reached in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, between four hundred dinars and eight hundred dinars, or its equivalent in silver, eight thousand."
"7091","Abu Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled that blood money is an inheritance among the heirs of the slain according to their shares."
"7092","Abu Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ruled concerning the nose when cut off entirely: the full blood money; and when its tip is cut off, half the blood money; and in the eye, half the blood money; and in the hand, half the blood money; and in the leg, half the blood money. And he ruled that the kin of a woman pay blood money on her behalf, whoever they are, but they do not inherit from her except what remains beyond her heirs; and if she is killed, her blood money is among her heirs, and they execute her killer. And he ruled that the blood money of the People of the Book is half the blood money of the Muslims, and they are the Jews and the Christians."
"7093","Abu Said the freedman of the Banu Hashim narrated to us, Shaddad Abu Talha al-Rasibi narrated to us, I heard Abu al-Wazi Jabir ibn Amr narrate from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No people sit in a gathering in which they do not remember Allah but they shall see it as regret on the Day of Resurrection."
"7094","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Amr, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a man who enters a garden. He said: He may eat without taking a pocketful."
"7095","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abdullah ibn Rafi narrated to me, Hanan ibn Kharija narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: A bold Alawi Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us about emigration to you: wherever you are, or to a particular people, or to a known land, or when you die is it cut off? He said: So he was silent a little, then said: Where is the asker? He said: Here he is, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Emigration is that you abandon indecencies, what is open of them and what is hidden, and establish prayer and pay zakat; then you are an emigrant even if you die in town. Then Abdullah ibn Amr said, beginning on his own: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us about the garments of the people of Paradise: are they created as creation or woven as weaving? So some of the people laughed. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why do you laugh at an ignorant one asking a learned one? Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bent down, then said: Where is the asker? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No, rather the fruits of Paradise shall split open from them, three times."
"7096","Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever is mutilated or burned with fire is free, and he is the client of Allah and His Messenger. He said: So a man was brought who had been castrated, called Sandar, and he freed him. Then he came to Abu Bakr after the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he did good to him. Then he came to Umar after Abu Bakr, and he did good to him. Then he wanted to go out to Egypt, so Umar wrote for him to Amr ibn al-As: Treat him well, or: Keep the charge of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning him."
"7097","Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man is absent and cannot find water; may he have intercourse with his wife? He said: Yes."
"7098","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, I heard Abu Iyad narrate from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Fast one day and you have the reward of what remains. He said: I can bear more than that. He said: Fast two days and you have the reward of what remains. He said: I can bear more than that. He said: Fast three days and you have the reward of what remains. He said: I can bear more than that. He said: Fast four days and you have the reward of what remains. He said: I can bear more than that. He said: Fast the best fast with Allah: fast the fast of Dawud; he would fast a day and break a day."
"7099","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: My father said: al-Hadrami narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a man of the Muslims asked permission of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning a woman called Umm Mahzul who used to commit fornication and stipulated that she would spend on him, and that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permission concerning her, or mentioned her affair to him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: The adulteress, none marries her but an adulterer or a polytheist. He said: There was revealed: The adulteress, none marries her but an adulterer or a polytheist. My father said: Arim said: I asked Mutamir about al-Hadrami, and he said: He was a storyteller, and I have seen him."
"7100","Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hadrami, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Amr, the like of it."
"7101","Haddathana Wahb ibn Jarir, haddathana my father, I heard al-Saqab ibn Zuhayr narrating from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a jubba of Tayalisah trimmed with dibaj or buttoned with dibaj, and he said: This companion of yours wants to raise every shepherd son of a shepherd and lower every horseman son of a horseman. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood angry and took hold of the folds of his jubba and pulled him and said: I do not see upon you the clothes of one who has sense. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and sat and said: Nuh (peace be upon him), when death came to him, called his two sons and said: I am shortening the will for you; I command you with two and forbid you two; I forbid you shirk and pride, and I command you with La ilaha illa Allah, for the heavens and the earth and what is in them, if placed in one pan of the scale and La ilaha illa Allah placed in the other pan, it would outweigh; and if the heavens and the earth were a ring and La ilaha illa Allah were placed upon it, it would break it or split it; and I command you with Subhan Allah wa bihamdihi, for it is the prayer of everything and by it everything is provided."
"7102","Haddathana Hashim and Husayn who said: Haddathana Muhammad ibn Rashid from Sulayman ibn Musa from Amr ibn Shuayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejected the testimony of the treacherous man and the treacherous woman and the one bearing rancor against his brother, and he rejected the testimony of the dependent for the people of the house, and he permitted it for others than them."
"7103","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Abu Awanah, haddathana Abu Bishr from Yusuf ibn Mahak from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed behind us on a journey we traveled; and he caught up with us when prayer, the Asr prayer, had pressed us, while we were performing ablution, and we began wiping over our feet, so he called out at the top of his voice two or three times: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
